\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 The  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  activists who say bringing back Roe is not enough\b0\par\par\uc2 Susan Rinkunas \par \uc2 1,156 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 January 2024\par 01:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups split with mainstream movement over support for former legal framework of \u8216\'20\'18viability\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Since the devastating loss of Roe v Wade, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement has seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/15/gallup-survey-abortion-support-united-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic levels}}}\uc2  of support for its cause, particularly through major victories on state ballot initiatives, with more expected this November. But as advocates move to re-enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the state level, a struggle has emerged over whether to reproduce Roe\u8217\'20\'19s legal framework \u8211\'20\'13 or go further.\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade, which was decided 51 years ago on Monday, protected the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability \u8211\'20\'13 the point at which a fetus can survive outside the uterus \u8211\'20\'13 which is widely accepted to be at roughly 24 weeks. A number of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2023/12/abortion-states-election-2024-ballot-measures/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ballot campaigns slated for November}}}\uc2  seek to bring back that standard \u8211\'20\'13 but a group of advocates is banding together to declare that the broader movement is engaging in harmful compromises when it could instead use the momentum to push for \u8220\'20\'1Cclean\u8221\'20\'1D policies that don\u8217\'20\'19t draw a strict limit to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is an enormous amount of pressure being put on leaders across states to run ballots whether they are good or bad,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bonyen Lee-Gilmore, vice-president of communications at the National Institute for Reproductive Health (NIRH), an advocacy group that is leading an effort to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement to go beyond the Roe framework.\par \par \uc2 The group has joined forces with several other organizations to create an entity called the Learning and Accountability Project (LAP), that fights for what they call \u8220\'20\'1Cclean\u8221\'20\'1D measures. The coalition plans to conduct polling and research to fight for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/demand-better-roe-v-wade-abortion-1850013645"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expansive policies}}}\uc2 , such as ensuring insurance coverage for abortions, and allowing minors to obtain abortions without parental consent. They also plan to create education campaigns about the problem with viability.\par \par \uc2 Pamela Merritt, executive director of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://msfc.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medical Students for Choice}}}\uc2 , said this was an opportunity to avoid past mistakes. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have to recreate [Roe],\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have to do this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The supreme court enshrined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wnycstudios.org/podcasts/radiolabmoreperfect/episodes/part-1-viability-line"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 viability as a legal compromise}}}\uc2  in Roe to balance the rights of pregnant women against the state\u8217\'20\'19s interest in potential life. But the viability line, advocates say, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2023/09/roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-amendment-missouri-pro-choice-ohio-arizona-planned-parenthood-viability-limits/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left behind}}}\uc2  people who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/activism/abortion-ballot-initiatives-viability/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 need later abortions}}}\uc2  and set the stage for Roe\u8217\'20\'19s downfall: anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/19/19-1392/184703/20210722161332385_19-1392BriefForPetitioners.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  it was an arbitrary standard in the case that overturned the seminal decision.\par \par \uc2 The project also includes the Society of Family Planning, Medical Students for Choice, Colorado Organization for Latina Opportunity and Reproductive Rights (Color), the advocacy group Patient Forward; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/01/11/abortion-rights-clashes-with-nimbyism-in-california-00135207"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DuPont Clinic}}}\uc2  ; and the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider Dr Colleen McNicholas.\par \par \uc2 Restrictions on reproductive healthcare have never been evidence-based, said Dr Jenni Villavicencio, interim director of public affairs and advocacy for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://societyfp.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Society of Family Planning}}}\uc2  and a later \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider. \u8220\'20\'1CHaving the government and politicians who are not scientific experts come in and tell us how to provide essential healthcare is inappropriate and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Local affiliates of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  are championing ballot measures with viability limits in states including Arizona, Florida and Nevada, while groups such as the Fairness Project and other consultants are involved behind the scenes on polling and ballot language. Often, advocates behind such measures argue that viability limits are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/08/08/arizona-abortion-ballot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 necessary}}}\uc2  to win, and these campaigns have been increasingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/11/09/democrats-abortion-election-plan-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 folded into Democratic electoral strategy}}}\uc2 . But members of the NIRH coalition are alarmed about the potential damage of inserting Roe\u8217\'20\'19s compromise into state constitutions.\par \par \uc2 People need abortions later in pregnancy for various reasons, including new medical diagnoses, delays in care caused by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and clinic closures, financial barriers such as a lack of paid time off or childcare, and simply discovering their pregnancies late.\par \par \uc2 Sarah Standiford, national campaigns director for \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 , said ballot measures were just one tool they plan to use to restore access in the years to come. Decisions around such measures are state-specific, she said, and groups must balance the competing needs of writing language that protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and also withstands legal challenges and wins a majority of voters. \u8220\'20\'1CThat may ultimately necessarily advance a policy that is far short of the ideal,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Aurea Bola\u241\'00\'F1os Perea, strategic communications director for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.colorlatina.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Color}}}\uc2 , said the reproductive rights movement had only progressed because groups like hers had pressured decision-makers to challenge the status quo.\par \par \uc2 As a Black woman in the movement, Merritt said she could not support proposals that trade away vulnerable people\u8217\'20\'19s access and affect future providers\u8217\'20\'19 training. \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Some rather than none\u8217\'20\'19 has always screwed over people who look like me,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, citing the 19th amendment, which formally granted American women the right to vote, but in practice kept that right out of reach for Black women. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is classic, second-wave feminist analysis that has historically hurt people who are marginalized,\u8221\'20\'1D she said of viability ballot campaigns.\par \par \uc2 For \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, the issue isn\u8217\'20\'19t theoretical. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I think about who\u8217\'20\'19s going to be harmed, I see specific patients. I see faces. I see the teddy bear and the 10-year-old and the tears of her mom,\u8221\'20\'1D said McNicholas, a later \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider.\par \par \uc2 Framing restrictions as a political necessity reflected the movement\u8217\'20\'19s internalized stigma around later \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Erika Christensen, co-founder of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.patientforward.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Patient Forward}}}\uc2 , which works to ensure access throughout pregnancy. Christensen, who had to travel out of state in 2016 for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/2022-interview-women-who-had-abortion-32-weeks-1848913142"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third-trimester \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after discovering a fatal fetal anomaly, said the push for viability was an especially flawed strategy in red and purple states like Arizona, where she lives, because it leaves the door open for hostile legislatures to pass bans criminalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in pregnancy. \u8220\'20\'1CThe stakes are higher in the so-called \u8216\'20\'18red\u8217\'20\'19 states. It\u8217\'20\'19s where so many people are suffering already,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy are you codifying the circumstances of the suffering into our constitution?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 LAP also believes current ballot campaigns are doubling down on harmful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stigma by conceding that banning later \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable\u8221\'20\'1D, rather than framing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a fundamental right, Merritt said. And they argue that permanently enshrining limits in state constitutions could deny people abortions and increase the risk of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ohio-miscarriage-prosecution-brittany-watts-b8090abfb5994b8a23457b80cf3f27ce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminalization}}}\uc2  for abortions and miscarriages later in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 As a tax-exempt non-profit, the coalition cannot oppose or endorse ballot measures, but they hope voters can make informed choices. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to be transparent and honest to pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  supporters in these campaigns. So if it\u8217\'20\'19s not perfect, we need to own that,\u8221\'20\'1D Lee-Gilmore said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery single right I have in this country as a Black woman \u8211\'20\'13 every single one \u8211\'20\'13 I have because people did not accept \u8216\'20\'18this is as good as it gets,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Merritt said. \u8220\'20\'1CI simply will not accept reproductive rights activists acting like we need to throw in the towel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240121ek1l000ul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
