\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Jury awards E Jean Carroll $83.3m in defamation case \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now); Chris Stein and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 5,397 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 January 2024\par 23:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest news on this verdict, you can read:Full report \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ordered to pay E Jean Carroll $83.3m in defamation trial\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The prospects of Congress voting on a deal to tighten immigration policy and approve military aid to Israel and Ukraine faced a new threat, in the form of Republican House speaker Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3cbf28f08f89f155ec32e#block-65b3cbf28f08f89f155ec32e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 objection}}}\uc2  to reported provisions in the deal. Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s opposition came a day after fury erupted when the top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , told his lawmakers behind closed doors that he may reject whatever deal is reached to allow \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to campaign on immigration. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3bff48f080601f6a47c04#block-65b3bff48f080601f6a47c04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McConnell reportedly later walked back}}}\uc2  those comments, but the prospects of a bargain to address one of the most intractable issues in American politics continue to look grim.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/26/e-jean-carroll-damages-trump-defamation-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  to pay $83.3m to author E Jean Carroll for defamation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3cbf28f08f89f155ec32e#block-65b3cbf28f08f89f155ec32e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also pledged}}}\uc2  to move forward with impeaching homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas on claims he is responsible for the surge in migrants crossing the southern border.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3de1a8f08f89f155ec477#block-65b3de1a8f08f89f155ec477"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paused approvals}}}\uc2  of new natural gas export terminals, citing their impact on the climate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-controlled state Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3f5838f08978231b974f8#block-65b3f5838f08978231b974f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 created a panel}}}\uc2  to investigate \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Fulton county district attorney whose election subversion case against Trump and 18 co-defendants has been rattled by allegations that she has a conflict of interest.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s spokeswoman, said Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s decision to execute a convicted murderer using nitrogen gas was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b408ad8f08978231b975d5#block-65b408ad8f08978231b975d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply troubling\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump owes Carroll a total of $88.3m between two trials. There\u8217\'20\'19s the $83.3m awarded today, and $5 million last year.\par \par \uc2 All in all, we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen a number of big defamation payouts recently, all involving players in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s orbit.\par \par \uc2 Right-wing figure Alex Jones was ordered to pay $1.5b to Sandy Hook parents, who suffered abuse and threats from believers of Jones\u8217\'20\'19s lies about the mass shooting. \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  was made to pay $148.1m to election workers for spreading lies about them.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alina Habba, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, called the trial a \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch hunt\u8221\'20\'1D, echoing the former president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am so proud to stand with President Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause he stood up, he took the stand, and he faced this judge.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Disgruntled Trump vows to appeal\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was, as one would expect, unhappy with this outcome.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI fully disagree with both verdicts, and will be appealing this whole Biden Directed Witch Hunt focused on me and the Republican Party,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on Truth Social. \u8220\'20\'1COur Legal System is out of control, and being used as a Political Weapon. They have taken away all First Amendment Rights. THIS IS NOT AMERICA!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is worth noting, among other things, that E Jean Carroll first sued Trump in 2019, before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was in office.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Carroll and her legal team were beaming as they left court in a black SUV. They did not answer questions immediately after court let out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge to jury: 'never disclose you were on this jury'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy advice to you is that you never disclose that you were on this jury, and I won\u8217\'20\'19t say anything more about it,\u8221\'20\'1D said judge Kaplan to jurors.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ordered to pay $83.3m\par \par \uc2 The former president must pay E Jean Carroll a total of $83.3m.\par \par \uc2 Carroll will receive $18.3m in compensatory damages and $65m in punitive retribution. Of the $18.3m in compensatory damages, $11m was awarded as part of the reputation repair program and $7.3m was awarded for other than the reputation repair program.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jury reaches decision in Carroll defamation trial vs Trump\par \par \uc2 The jury in E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s second defamation trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has reached a decision, court officials said. Carroll\u8211\'20\'13 who in a 2023 trial won a $5m verdict against Trump for sexual abuse, and defamation, over his denials\u8211\'20\'13is seeking damages to repair her reputation and deter Trump from continuing to defame her.\par \par \uc2 Carroll accused Trump of raping her in a department store dressing room around late 1995, when New York magazine in June 2019 published an excerpt of her then-forthcoming book, What Do We Need Men For? A Modest Proposal.\par \par \uc2 Trump subsequently went on the attack, calling Carroll a liar and a political operative who wanted to drum up book sales. He has continued to do so, despite the prior verdict, including throughout this trial.\par \par \uc2 The judge in this case, Lewis Kaplan, said that the jury\u8217\'20\'19s factual finding in that case would be accepted in this trial, meaning jurors were only charged with determining damages.\par \par \uc2 In her closing on Friday, Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s lead attorney, \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2  (no relation to the judge), asked jurors to award at least $24m.The decision is expected to be read in court soon.\par \par \uc2 E. Jean Carroll walks outside the Manhattan Federal Court, in New York City earlier today. Photograph: Brendan McDermid/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The family of Elizabeth Sennett, who was murdered by Kenneth Smith, spoke to the press following Smith\u8217\'20\'19s execution in Alabama on Thursday using an untested nitrogen gas method.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what they had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltrMichael Sennett, whose mother Elizabeth Sennett was murdered by Kenneth Smith, speaks after Alabama executed Smith by nitrogen gas Thursday:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNothing happened here today is gonna bring Mom back \u8230\'20\'26 Kenneth Smith made some bad decisions 35 years ago and his debt was paid tonight.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CWLp025Ncg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CWLp025Ncg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1750923843332419943?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Will we get a verdict in author E Jean Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s second defamation case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ? We are waiting to find out, but for those of you just joining us, here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/victoria-bekiempis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victoria Bekiempis}}}\uc2  of the day\u8217\'20\'19s proceedings, including Trump\u8217\'20\'19s abrupt storming out of the courtroom as Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers were talking:\par \par \uc2 As E Jean Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s second defamation trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  neared its final stage Friday morning in New York, proceedings quickly took a turn for the absurd with the judge threatening his lawyer with \u8220\'20\'1Clockup\u8221\'20\'1D and the ex-president leaving about 10 minutes into the former Elle writer\u8217\'20\'19s closing argument. Trump returned to court for his defense\u8217\'20\'19s closing.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s abrupt departure came as Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s lead attorney, \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2 , was delivering her closing argument \u8211\'20\'13 shortly after she noted that he had continued to defame the former Elle writer during this very trial. Trump left.\par \par \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2  had provided a chronology of the harm endured by Carroll due to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attacks in advance of the remark that appeared to trigger him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s denials and vicious accusations were all complete lies. That has already been proven, right in this courtroom, by a jury,\u8221\'20\'1D Kaplan said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s testimony was so short yesterday. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get a do-over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis case is also about punishing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for what he has done and for what he continues to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Kaplan said, adding shortly thereafter: \u8220\'20\'1CThis trial is about getting him to stop, once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/26/e-jean-carroll-defamation-trial-trump-closing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump abruptly leaves court during closing arguments in E Jean Carroll trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 One thing you can expect to hear a lot about from the White House in the months to come is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have put restoring nationwide access to the procedure at the center of their re-election campaign, but as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports, activists say they could be doing more to make that goal a reality:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign has made a big bet that outrage over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep the president in the White House come November.\par \par \uc2 Over the last several days, the Biden administration has unleashed a blitz of ads and events to spotlight the devastation wrought by the overturning of Roe v Wade. Biden met with a reproductive health task force, while his vice-president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who he has entrusted to lead this effort \u8211\'20\'13 embarked on a national tour to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They even devoted their first joint campaign stop of 2024 to the issue.\par \par \uc2 From the podium, Biden promised to sign any bill that would codify Roe\u8217\'20\'19s protections into law and to fight back efforts by Congress to diminish \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Maga Republicans, including the speaker of the House, are hellbent on going even further,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/30/opinion/abortion-pills-biden.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden said}}}\uc2 , a reference to the hard-right Republican speaker, Mike Johnson. \u8220\'20\'1CAs long as I have power of the presidency, if Congress were to pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, I would veto it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Congress is unlikely to ban or protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon. Not only is Congress largely frozen \u8211\'20\'13 it passed just 27 bills last year \u8211\'20\'13 but both political parties seem wary of tackling national legislation around a third-rail topic like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now that Roe is gone, the question of if and how to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is largely up to state governments to answer. But the executive branch of the \uc2 US government\uc2  still maintains several powers to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access \u8211\'20\'13 and undermine it.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/26/biden-abortion-rights-expand-protections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden hopes \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  will keep him in the White House. But has he done enough to protect rights?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House said that Texas governor Greg Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to defy federal government and supreme court assertions of federal control of the border are \u8220\'20\'1Cshameful\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The fight between Texas and the federal government is only intensifying, amid Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to put more razor wire on the border despite supreme court ruling that federal agents can remove it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll we are asking for is border patrol to have access to an area to enforce the law. That\u8217\'20\'19s what they are meant to do, that\u8217\'20\'19s what they are trying to do. We have a governor getting in the way of that,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/26/border-fight-texas-greg-abbott-razor-wire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fight over border intensifies as Texas governor pledges more razor wire}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House has declared the execution of Kenneth Smith last night using nitrogen \u8220\'20\'1Cvery troubling\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said at the west wing media briefing, now ongoing, on Friday afternoon that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has long had \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep concerns about the death penalty and whether it\u8217\'20\'19s consistent with our values\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s troubling to hear,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said of the news that despite appeals all the way up to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  and expert opinion that it was inappropriate to try out this unprecedented method on a human being, Smith {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/25/alabama-executes-kenneth-smith-nitrogen-gas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was executed}}}\uc2  in Alabama.\par \par \uc2 Smith, a convicted murderer, was 58 and his lawyers had argued the execution amounted to a form of cruel and unusual punishment banned under the US constitution.\par \par \uc2 Smith struggled as he was suffocated by forced breathing of nitrogen, eyewitnesses said. Alabama is now promoting the method to other states.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/25/alabama-executes-kenneth-smith-nitrogen-gas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama inmate executed with nitrogen gas was \u8216\'20\'18shaking violently\u8217\'20\'19 for 22 minutes, witnesses say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3cbf28f08f89f155ec32e#block-65b3cbf28f08f89f155ec32e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tense talks}}}\uc2  in the Senate and fierce chatter on Capitol Hill over a legislative deal linking new immigration regulations with funding for Ukraine, others are weighing in.\par \par \uc2 David Axelrod\uc2 , political consultant and former senior adviser to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  as president, said on X/\uc2 Twitter\uc2 , amid reports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/25/congress-mexico-border-ukraine-israel-aid-mcconnell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that pressure}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could derail bipartisan talks in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , that Trump would \u8220\'20\'1Crather exploit the problem for his own political profit than allow Republicans and Democrats to work together to solve it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump is a little like the "coyotes" who smuggle migrants across the border. He'd rather exploit the problem for his own poltical profit than allow Republicans and Democrats to work together to solve it. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eMykBU6yZK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/eMykBU6yZK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Axelrod\uc2  (@davidaxelrod) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidaxelrod/status/1750888933511286865?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Arizona congressman \uc2 Rub\u233\'00\'E9n Gallego\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/23/ruben-gallego-arizona-senate-kyrsten-sinema-democrat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who is running}}}\uc2  for the Senate seat held by \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  (who is in the thick of the border bill talks), told civil rights organizer \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2 , in a discussion on MSNBC, that the situation in relation to talks was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot ideal\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 given that Republican control of the House is pushing Democrats to the right on immigration issues \u8211\'20\'13 but that there had to be compromise to get a legislative deal.\par \par \uc2 enltrDiscussing Senate border talks with Arizona Rep. \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MorningJoe?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MorningJoe}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/T3aiB21h52"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/T3aiB21h52}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Reverend \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  (@TheRevAl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheRevAl/status/1750931341850313081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia Republican state senators are weighing in fiercely on Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  and her prosecution of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others for election interference, in a racketeering case, as they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3f5838f08978231b974f8#block-65b3f5838f08978231b974f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 form a committee}}}\uc2  to investigate her.\par \par \uc2 Republican state senator Brandon Beach of Alpharetta said that Willis\u8217\'20\'19 employment of [special prosecutor] Wade is a \u8220\'20\'1Cprosecution for personal profit scheme,\u8221\'20\'1D contending that she has stretched out the Trump inquiry to keep paying Wade and derive personal benefit, the Associated Press further reports.\par \par \uc2 I believe this scheme \u8212\'20\'14 prosecution for personal profit \u8212\'20\'14 was a fraud against the court and it was a fraud against you as a Georgia taxpayer,\u8221\'20\'1D Beach said.\par \par \uc2 The new panel would be able to issue subpoenas and require people to testify under oath \u8212\'20\'14 powers that no other Georgia legislative committee routinely uses.\par \par \uc2 People can already be prosecuted for making false statements to Georgia lawmakers. Those are among the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-georgia-election-investigation-grand-jury-willis-d39562cedfc60d64948708de1b011ed3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal charges}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and some others face for the false claims they made to Georgia lawmakers in late 2020. They claimed Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s election was marred by widespread fraud and that Trump and not Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was the rightful winner of the state\u8217\'20\'19s 16 electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 Georgia governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  has said he favors a revived prosecutor oversight board looking into whether Willis did anything wrong, instead of a legislative committee.\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Josh McLaurin accused Republicans of going down a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous path\u8221\'20\'1D by catering to Republicans who have shown themselves willing to threaten violence against Georgia lawmakers seen as insufficiently supportive of Trump.\par \par \uc2 If you guys think you can handle it \u8212\'20\'14 if you think you can inflame that base, and feed them more, feed them misinformation, or let them persist in their misinformation about the results of elections \u8212\'20\'14 and not face the consequences someday, I think you\u8217\'20\'19re mistaken,\u8221\'20\'1D McLaurin said.\par \par \uc2 Here is my colleague Sam Levine \u8217\'20\'19s latest analysis on Willis and the case.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/25/fani-willis-nathan-wade-georgia-election-interference-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How an alleged office romance could derail the Trump election interference case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia senate creates panel to investigate \uc2 Fani Willis\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s state senate has joined attempts to investigate Fulton county {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/25/fani-willis-nathan-wade-georgia-election-interference-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 District Attorney }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/25/fani-willis-nathan-wade-georgia-election-interference-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fani Willis}}}\uc2  , voting 30-19 on Friday to create a special committee that Republican senators say is needed to determine whether the prosecutor misspent state tax money in her ongoing prosecution of former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 This has to do with following state funds. We want to know where is our money going,\u8221\'20\'1D said Republican senator Matt Brass of Newnan.\par \par \uc2 The committee, which doesn\u8217\'20\'19t require approval by the state House or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/brian-p-kemp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Governor Brian Kemp}}}\uc2 , is tasked with making recommendations on state laws and spending based on its findings. But the committee can\u8217\'20\'19t directly sanction Willis, and Democrats denounced it as a partisan attempt to try to play to Trump and his supporters.\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19re talking about partisan politics. That\u8217\'20\'19s all you\u8217\'20\'19re talking about,\u8221\'20\'1D said Democratic senator. David Lucas of Macon.\par \par \uc2 Trump on Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/fani-willis-trump-election-case-georgia-race-c281a8ea34513dd597cdd3fa766341e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined an effort}}}\uc2  by co-defendant Michael Roman to have Willis, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-willis-wade-georgia-election-5d76abb5578308317306e7b2e610ac91"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 special prosecutor Nathan Wade}}}\uc2  and their offices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/willis-wade-affair-allegations-election-interference-trump-9a292135a319fd203190a107e3f4f4dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thrown off the case}}}\uc2 . Ashleigh Merchant, a lawyer for Roman, filed a motion Jan. 8 accusing Willis of having an inappropriate romantic relationship with Wade that resulted in a conflict of interest.\par \par \uc2 Willis has yet to respond publicly to the allegations of a romantic relationship between her and Wade. But she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/fani-willis-trump-georgia-election-indictment-prosecutor-6211c8f3b69c9ae37dee4218b5d8c71d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vigorously defended Wade and his qualifications}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A filing in Wade\u8217\'20\'19s divorce case includes credit card statements that show Wade \u8212\'20\'14 after he had been hired as special prosecutor \u8212\'20\'14 bought plane tickets in October 2022 for him and Willis to travel to Miami and bought tickets in April to San Francisco in their names.\par \par \uc2 District Attorney for Fulton County, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  speaks during an interview with The Associated Press on Dec. 12, 2023, in Atlanta. Photograph: Brynn Anderson/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Immigration officials did not document the medical necessity of at least two hysterectomies they authorized for women in their custody, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oig.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/assets/2024-01/OIG-24-16-Jan24.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new report}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Inspector General.\par \par \uc2 Investigators contracted with an OB/GYN to review six hysterectomies performed on migrant women who were in federal custody. The doctor found that in two of the cases, officials had failed to document whether it was medically necessary, the watchdog report states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur contracted OB/GYN concluded that for two of six hysterectomies performed, the detained non-citizens\u8217\'20\'19 IHSC medical files did not demonstrate that a hysterectomy was the most appropriate course of treatment and was medically necessary,\u8221\'20\'1D investigators wrote. \u8220\'20\'1C[Immigration health] officials agreed that their medical files did not contain the necessary documentation to demonstrate the medical necessity of these two hysterectomies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Office of the Inspector General (OIG) finding was part of a larger review that concluded \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) did not follow proper procedures to authorize dozens of such surgeries between fiscal years 2019 and 2021. Looking at a sample of 227 major surgeries, investigators found 72 of them \u8211\'20\'13 about a third \u8211\'20\'13 did not follow proper procedures.\par \par \uc2 While a clinical director is supposed to approve all major surgeries, investigators found these surgeries were approved by other healthcare personnel, like a nurse or nurse practitioner.\par \par \uc2 Based on that sample, OIG said it could infer with 95 percent confidence that between 137 and 217 of 553 major surgical procedures were not properly approved in the timeframe it studied.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  will have a fuller report on this on our website soon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The prospects of Congress voting on a deal to tighten immigration policy and approve military aid to Israel and Ukraine faced a new threat in the form of Republican House speaker Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3cbf28f08f89f155ec32e#block-65b3cbf28f08f89f155ec32e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 objection}}}\uc2  to reported provisions in the deal. Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s opposition came a day after fury erupted when the top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , told his lawmakers behind closed doors that he may reject whatever deal is reached to allow \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to campaign on immigration. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3bff48f080601f6a47c04#block-65b3bff48f080601f6a47c04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McConnell reportedly walked back}}}\uc2  those comments in another meeting with his party, but the prospects of a bargain to address one of the most intractable issues in American politics continue to look grim.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3c9ed8f08f89f155ec312#block-65b3c9ed8f08f89f155ec312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stormed out}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3c9ed8f08f89f155ec312#block-65b3c9ed8f08f89f155ec312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  of closing arguments}}}\uc2  in the New York City trial of author E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s defamation lawsuit against him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3cbf28f08f89f155ec32e#block-65b3cbf28f08f89f155ec32e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also pledged}}}\uc2  to move forward with impeaching homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas on claims he is responsible for the surge in migrants crossing the southern border.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/26/trump-republicans-ukraine-border-deal-support-latest-biden?page=with:block-65b3de1a8f08f89f155ec477#block-65b3de1a8f08f89f155ec477"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paused approvals}}}\uc2  of new natural gas export terminals, citing their impact on the climate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney Alina Habba has just wrapped up her closing arguments in the defamation lawsuit against him.\par \par \uc2 We are now hearing the rebuttal from author E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s attorney.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump attorney begins closing arguments in defamation case\par \par \uc2 In her closing arguments, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lead attorney Alina Habba said the former president was the real victim, because of the backlash caused by E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s defamation lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Carroll, she said, wasn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Caccepting any responsibility for the media and the press frenzy and the public profile that she wanted and still enjoys.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no one that can truly express the frustration of the last few years better than my client, the former president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Habba then played a video that had been introduced by Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers \u8211\'20\'13 because they considered it defamatory \u8211\'20\'13 in which Trump doubled down on his denials.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have absolutely no idea who this woman is. The verdict is a disgrace, a continuation of the greatest witch hunt of all time,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in the clip.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re right that\u8217\'20\'19s how he feels,\u8221\'20\'1D Habba continued. \u8220\'20\'1CThe president has been consistent, she\u8217\'20\'19s right, he has said this same thing over and over and over again and do you know why he has not wavered? Because it\u8217\'20\'19s the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D she said shortly thereafter, prompting an objection from Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s team.\par \par \uc2 Habba then started to attack Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s credibility, which appeared to edge toward breeching judge Lewis Kaplan \u8217\'20\'19s prohibition on litigating the facts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you violate my instructions again, Ms Habba, you may have consequences,\u8221\'20\'1D he warned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has meanwhile characterized his administration\u8217\'20\'19s decision to pause approval of new permits for natural gas export terminals as important to addressing the climate crisis. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about it, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/oliver-milman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Milman}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration has hit the brakes on the US\u8217\'20\'19s surging exports of gas, effectively pausing a string of planned projects that have been decried by environmentalists as carbon \u8220\'20\'1Cmega bombs\u8221\'20\'1D that risk pushing the world further towards climate breakdown.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the White House announced that it was pausing all pending export permits for liquified natural gas (LNG) until the Department of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/energy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Energy}}}\uc2  could come up with an updated criteria for approvals that consider the impact of climate change.\par \par \uc2 The pause, which will likely last beyond November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, could imperil the future of more than a dozen gas export terminals that have been planned for the Gulf of Mexico coast. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/23/louisiana-gas-export-hub-biden-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to one analysis}}}\uc2 , if all proposed LNG projects go ahead and ship gas overseas, it will result in 3.2bn tons of greenhouse gases \u8211\'20\'13 equivalent to the entire emissions of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A vigorous campaign by climate activists and local residents has pressed Biden to curb the rapid growth of LNG exports, pointing to its contribution to global heating and the direct pollution suffered by surrounding communities.\par \par \uc2 The US president said the pause will allow his administration to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake a hard look at the impacts of LNG exports on energy costs, America\u8217\'20\'19s energy security, and our environment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis pause on new LNG approvals sees the climate crisis for what it is - the existential threat of our time,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, adding that Republicans who support ever-expanding fossil fuel infrastructure \u8220\'20\'1Cwilfully deny the urgency of the climate crisis\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/26/biden-delays-cp2-louisiana-lng-export-project"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden hits pause on natural gas projects amid plans for carbon \u8216\'20\'18mega bombs\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson also objected to the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s decision to pause approval of liquid natural gas export permits, saying it undermined efforts to support Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Calling the decision \u8220\'20\'1Cas outrageous as it is subversive\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said:\par \par \uc2 Since Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine began, American petroleum producers have increased LNG shipments to our partners in Europe to prevent a catastrophic, continent-wide energy crisis and to provide an alternative to Russian energy exports.\par \par \uc2 It is outrageous that this administration is asking American taxpayers to spend billions to defeat Russia while knowingly forcing allies to rely on Russian energy, giving Putin an advantage. This policy change also flies in the face of the commitments made when the White House announced the joint US-EU Task Force less than two years ago to reduce Europe\u8217\'20\'19s dependence on Russia and strengthen energy security.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stormed out of the closing arguments of his defamation trial in New York City, judge Lewis Kaplan remarked: \u8220\'20\'1CExcuse me, the record will reflect that Mr Trump just rose and walked out of the courtroom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before the former president\u8217\'20\'19s abrupt departure, \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2 , an attorney for E Jean Carroll was providing a chronology of the harm endured by her client due to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attacks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s denials and vicious accusations were all complete lies. That has already been proven, right in this courtroom, by a jury,\u8221\'20\'1D Kaplan said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s testimony was so short yesterday. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get a do-over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis case is also about punishing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for what he has done and for what he continues to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Kaplan said, adding shortly thereafter, \u8220\'20\'1CThis trial is about getting him to stop, once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kaplan noted that Trump started to smear Carroll within a day of her last court victory, which found that he had defamed her. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , however, acts as if these rules and laws just don\u8217\'20\'19t apply to him,\u8221\'20\'1D and pointed out that he spent \u8220\'20\'1Cthis entire trial\u8221\'20\'1D attacking Carroll with nefarious posts.\par \par \uc2 It was right about this time that Trump walked out of court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CExcuse me,\u8221\'20\'1D judge Kaplan said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe record will reflect that Mr Trump just rose and walked out of the courtroom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Not long after \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2  said in her closing: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is required to follow the law, whether he likes it or not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Responding to Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s vow to impeach Alejandro Mayorkas, White House spokesman Ian Sams accused him of acting \u8220\'20\'1Cout of partisan political bloodlust\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrSuch a silly claim. There\u8217\'20\'19s no \u8220\'20\'1Cnecessity\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In fact\u8212\'20\'14since before they even took the majority, House Rs have been crowing about impeaching somebody\u8230\'20\'26anybody\u8230\'20\'26out of partisan political bloodlust\par \par \uc2 Totally baseless spin as House Rs refuse to even engage on bipartisan border solutions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lrQhuhYylJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/lrQhuhYylJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ian Sams (@IanSams46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IanSams46/status/1750899853956087993?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Johnson warns Ukraine-immigration deal likely 'dead on arrival' in House, pledges to impeach Mayorkas\par \par \uc2 In a letter to House Republicans, speaker Mike Johnson warned that the immigration deal under consideration in the Senate may be \u8220\'20\'1Cdead on arrival\u8221\'20\'1D in his chamber, while also vowing to move forward with plans to impeach homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 The Republican leader\u8217\'20\'19s statement bodes ill for the bargaining in the Senate, which is seen as crucial to unlocking GOP support for aid to Ukraine, as well as Israel and Taiwan. Democrats and Republicans in the upper chamber have been negotiating for months on an agreement to restrict immigration policy in a bid to keep undocumented migrants from entering the United States. While no compromise has yet been reached, Johnson said today that \u8220\'20\'1Cif rumors about the contents of the draft proposal are true, it would have been dead on arrival in the House anyway.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Johnson said he would support the effort to impeach Mayorkas, who Republicans have accused of mishandling border security.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we return next week, by necessity, the House Homeland Security Committee will move forward with Articles of Impeachment against Secretary Mayorkas. A vote on the floor will be held as soon as possible thereafter,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Impeachments of cabinet secretaries are exceedingly rare, and the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic majority will almost certainly refuse to convict Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump quickly departs defamation trial, judges threatens to jail his lawyer\par \par \uc2 As E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s second defamation trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  neared its final stage Friday morning in New York, proceedings quickly took a turn for the absurd with the judge threatening his lawyer with \u8220\'20\'1Clockup\u8221\'20\'1D and the ex-president leaving about 10 minutes into closing arguments.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s abrupt departure came as Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s lead attorney, \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2 , was speaking, and shortly after she noted that he had continued to defame the former Elle writer even during this very trial. At that point, Trump left.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 CNN heard from both Democratic and Republicans senators yesterday who were not interested in throwing out months of negotiations over the complex deal to change immigration policy and unlock aid to Ukraine and Israel, simply to help \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chris Murphy, the Connecticut Democrat who is a party to the talks, expressed dismay that Trump could wield so much power. Meanwhile, \uc2 James Lankford\uc2 , the Oklahoma Republican who is the party\u8217\'20\'19s lead on the issue, downplayed the former president\u8217\'20\'19s effect on the negotiations. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 enltrGOP Sen. \uc2 Kevin Cramer\uc2  on Rs who want to kill bipartisan immigration deal as Trump seeks to derail effort: "I reject the idea we should reserve a crisis for a better time to solve it... I don't see how we have a better story to tell when we miss the one opportunity to fix it." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YeJUjpanOR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YeJUjpanOR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1750646998301016393?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 McConnell's comments on Ukraine, border deal 'flipped around' \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 After meeting yesterday with their leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , Senate Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/01/25/congress/mcconnell-clarifies-00137879?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Politico}}}\uc2  that earlier comments he had made expressing opposition at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s urging to a deal to arm Ukraine and Israel while enacting conservative immigration policies were misunderstood.\par \par \uc2 McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s remarks were \u8220\'20\'1Cflipped around\u8221\'20\'1D, Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s Tommy Tuberville said, adding \u8220\'20\'1Che just tried to get it straight \u8230\'20\'26 some of the senators came out and got kind of misconstrued on what he was talking about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMcConnell has not changed his point of view,\u8221\'20\'1D according to Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s Roger Wicker, who said McConnell had earlier just been speaking plainly about the political calculations that would go into approving the deal. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I don\u8217\'20\'19t think anybody disagreed with him. We are at a particular set of crossroads and intersections,\u8221\'20\'1D Wicker said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican leader walks back Trump-driven opposition to Ukraine and border deal\par \par \uc2 Yesterday kicked off with the somewhat shocking news that Senate Republicans were, at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s behest, willing to walk away from a deal they had been negotiating with Democrats for months to implement some conservative immigration policies in exchange for approving new aid to Ukraine and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s militaries. The reason, the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  told his lawmakers in a private meeting, was that Trump wanted to be able to attack \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over immigration on the campaign trail, and passing the deal would undermine that. The comments unsurprisingly sparked outrage from Democrats and some Republicans, and later on Thursday, McConnell seems to have walked them back.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/01/25/congress/mcconnell-clarifies-00137879?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Politico}}}\uc2 , he again convened his party to tell them that he was still behind the deal. That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean it\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen \u8211\'20\'13 the odds of enacting legislation in an election year dealing with one of the most divisive issues in American politics, immigration, were also going to be long, but the parties seem resolved to at least try. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see what more is revealed about this kerfuffle over the course of the day.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump will once again be in a New York City courtroom for author E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s defamation trial against him, where closing arguments are expected today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The top \uc2 UN\uc2  court ordered Israel to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake all measures\u8221\'20\'1D to prevent genocide during its military campaign in Gaza, but did not order a ceasefire, as the country\u8217\'20\'19s critics had hoped. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jan/26/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-icj-genocide-case-ruling-israel-hamas-gaza-hostage-talks-cia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Follow our live blog}}}\uc2  for more on this developing story.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/26/biden-delays-cp2-louisiana-lng-export-project"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paused}}}\uc2  all pending natural gas export permits over concerns they\u8217\'20\'19d further fuel climate change.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240126ek1q0026d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
