\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Nearly 65,000 US rape victims could not get an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  in their state, analysis shows\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza in New York \par \uc2 723 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 January 2024\par 12:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Researchers estimated likely number of rape-related pregnancies in 14 states with near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans since Dobbs ruling\par \par \uc2 Nearly 65,000 rape-related pregnancies likely occurred in the 14 US states with near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans following the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2022 Dobbs decision \u8211\'20\'13 yet just 10 legal abortions are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://societyfp.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/WeCountReport_10.16.23.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 performed monthly on average}}}\uc2  in these states, researchers found in a new analysis.\par \par \uc2 The data demonstrates that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans likely make it impossible for most victims of rape to obtain abortions in their home states, even for the minority of people who live in states with exemptions for rape, researchers said.\par \par \uc2 The figures come as rape exemptions have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/06/no-exception-rape-incest-anti-abortion-laws-republicans-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fallen out of favor among anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  activists and politicians}}}\uc2 , despite the fact that most Americans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-election/vast-majority-republicans-support-abortion-exceptions-rape-incest-moth-rcna52237"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including Republicans}}}\uc2 , believe that victims of assault should have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that most Americans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/506759/broader-support-abortion-rights-continues-post-dobbs.aspx#:~:text=Trend%20from%201995%20to%202022,rising%20to%2055%25%20in%202022."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 morally acceptable}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe large number of estimated rape-related pregnancies in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban states compared with the 10 or fewer legal abortions per month occurring in each of those states indicates that persons who have been raped and become pregnant cannot access legal abortions in their home state, even in states with rape exceptions,\u8221\'20\'1D researchers wrote in a research letter in the journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamainternalmedicine/fullarticle/2814274?guestAccessKey=e429b9a8-72ac-42ed-8dbc-599b0f509890&utm_source=For_The_Media&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=ftm_links&utm_content=tfl&utm_term=012424"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JAMA Internal Medicine}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although the observational nature of the study might draw criticism, it is part of an important and growing number of analyses documenting the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans on women\u8217\'20\'19s lives, health and fertility. This growing body of evidence crosses disciplines, with contributions from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://societyfp.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/WeCountReport_10.16.23.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clinicians}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.iza.org/dp16608.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 economists}}}\uc2  and researchers.\par \par \uc2 In July 2022, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US supreme court overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , a nearly 50-year-old precedent that provided a constitutional right to terminate a pregnancy, in a case called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization}}}\uc2  (or simply \u8220\'20\'1CDobbs\u8221\'20\'1D).\par \par \uc2 The decision caused a seismic change in reproductive rights in the US \u8211\'20\'13 states were suddenly permitted to ban the procedure. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fourteen moved to do so immediately and almost totally}}}\uc2 , with five of those providing exemptions for victims of rape. Twenty-five million women of childbearing age now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/a-year-after-fall-of-roe-v-wade-25-million-women-live-in-states-with-abortion-bans-or-restrictions#:~:text=Twenty%2Dfive%20million%20women%20of,led%20states%20have%20restricted%20abortion."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live in states that ban the procedure}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In JAMA Internal Medicine, researchers estimated the number of women who are likely victims of \u8220\'20\'1Ccompleted\u8221\'20\'1D vaginal rape \u8211\'20\'13 forced and/or drug/alcohol\u8211\'20\'13facilitated vaginal penetration \u8211\'20\'13 using estimates from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  of intimate partner violence. They then determined the fraction that were likely to be of childbearing age (15-45) using \uc2 Bureau of Justice Statistics\uc2  data, arriving at a figure of roughly 520,000 total rapes. (Importantly, as noted by JAMA, data from \uc2 BJS\uc2  undercounts rapes.) Finally, they apportioned assaults to the 14 US states that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  using the Federal Bureau of Investigations\u8217\'20\'19 uniform crime statistics, which include rapes reported to law enforcement in 2019.\par \par \uc2 The estimate found that the overwhelming majority of rape-related pregnancies, 58,979, likely occurred in states without exceptions to their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Texas alone accounted for as much as 45% of that number (26,313) because of its large population and total ban without exceptions.\par \par \uc2 An estimated 5,586 rape-related pregnancies occurred in states with exceptions for victims of rape. Although not all women who become pregnant from a rape want an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , those who do are likely confronted with the reality that their state offers no access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Researchers found that even states with exemptions likely fail to provide any meaningful opportunity to terminate a pregnancy, given the low number of legal abortions per month in these states.\par \par \uc2 At least in part, researchers surmise this is driven by requirements for victims to report rape to law enforcement, which few feel comfortable doing. It would likely be worsened by the near total lack of providers who would be willing to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a state with severe criminal and professional penalties for doing so.\par \par \uc2 The analysis stops short of estimating the number of women who might have been forced to carry a rape-related pregnancy to term. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal in most circumstances in 30 US states, and nearly three-quarters of women seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have shown a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.iza.org/dp16608.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 willingness to travel to states}}}\uc2  where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal, recent research has found.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240125ek1p001s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\