\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New Hampshire primary: Biden warns US democracy at stake as Trump races closer to Republican presidential nomination \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Manchester, New Hampshire (now); L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Gloria Oladipo and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 18,186 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2024\par 04:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our latest reporting here:Follow our live results trackerTrump wins New Hampshire Republican primaryBiden wins New Hampshire Democratic primary\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made a huge step towards claiming the Republican presidential nomination for the third time since 2016 after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65b0619f8f08541705644c41#block-65b0619f8f08541705644c41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 winning New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s primary}}}\uc2  by a margin of, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65b083958f08af761dc32213#block-65b083958f08af761dc32213"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as of this writing}}}\uc2 , about 11 percentage points over \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 . Nonetheless, the former South Carolina governor says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65b067948f0898882cc4f4f2#block-65b067948f0898882cc4f4f2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the race isn\u8217\'20\'19t over yet}}}\uc2 , and plans to make a stand against Trump in her home state, even though polls there show her trailing him. The Democrats also held a primary, which reached an unsurprising result in a roundabout way. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65b063c08f08541705644c4f#block-65b063c08f08541705644c4f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the contest}}}\uc2  handily over long-shot candidates \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  and \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 , but only through a write-in campaign organized by outside groups, since his campaign honored recent Democratic rule changes and stayed away from the state. Following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65b085d08f08af761dc32222#block-65b085d08f08af761dc32222"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a statement}}}\uc2  saying he believed Trump would be the Republican nominee, and warned that the US economy and democracy are now \u8220\'20\'1Cat stake\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened tonight:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65b076278f0898882cc4f556#block-65b076278f0898882cc4f556"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued to insist}}}\uc2  victory in the 2020 election was stolen from him, even though it was not.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Phillips, who was walloped by New Hampshire Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65b073918f0898882cc4f550#block-65b073918f0898882cc4f550"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will continue}}}\uc2  campaigning for president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65b0701b8f0898882cc4f538#block-65b0701b8f0898882cc4f538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 encouraged}}}\uc2  his fellow Republicans to unite around Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 George Santos, the expelled former Republican congressman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65b05ec08f08541705644c2d#block-65b05ec08f08541705644c2d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned up}}}\uc2  at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election night watch party.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s electorate was quite different from Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65b054798f08541705644bef#block-65b054798f08541705644bef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  exit polls from CNN.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden says it's 'now clear' that Trump will be GOP nominee, warns US democracy, economy 'at stake'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said in a statement that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the Republican presidential nomination with his victory in New Hampshire tonight, and appealed to disaffected independents and Republicans to vote for him in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is now clear that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be the Republican nominee,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden wrote in a statement distributed by his campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd my message to the country is the stakes could not be higher. Our Democracy. Our personal freedoms \u8211\'20\'13 from the right to choose to the right to vote. Our economy \u8211\'20\'13 which has seen the strongest recovery in the world since COVID. All are at stake.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also weighed in on the write-in campaign held unofficially by his supporters in the state, which allowed him to win the New Hampshire Democratic primary even though his name was not on the ballot:\par \par \uc2 I want to thank all those who wrote my name in this evening in New Hampshire. It was a historic demonstration of commitment to our democratic process. And I want to say to all those Independents and Republicans who share our commitment to core values of our nation \u8212\'20\'14 our Democracy, our personal freedoms, an economy that gives everyone a fair shot \u8212\'20\'14 to join us as Americans.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 About 61% of the Republican primary vote has been counted, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a lead of about 10 percentage points over \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He has 54% of the vote, compared to Haley\u8217\'20\'19s 44.5%. That margin is substantial, but tighter than Iowa, where Trump triumphed with 51% of the vote, compared with runner-up \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 21.2%, and Haley\u8217\'20\'19s 19.1%.\par \par \uc2 We have a tracker updating with the latest results:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Hampshire primary 2024: live results tracker}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  opened her remarks on a conciliatory note, before hitting Trump in a way many Granite staters wished she had done much sooner on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI congratulate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his victory tonight. He earned it. And I want to acknowledge that,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, striking a starkly different tone from Trump, who attacked her right off the bat in his remarks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , you have one bout of chaos after another. This court case, that controversy, this tweet, that senior moment,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, in a reprisal of her stump speech rhetoric. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t fix \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chaos with Republican chaos.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She then questioned Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mental fitness.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve long called for mental competency tests for politicians over the age of 75. Trump claims he\u8217\'20\'19d do better than me on one of those tests. Maybe he would, and maybe he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, smiling. \u8220\'20\'1CBut if he thinks that, then he should have no problem standing on a debate stage with me!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crowd erupted in sustained applause. Later this evening, Haley\u8217\'20\'19s campaign sent out a press release accusing Trump of \u8220\'20\'1Cranting and raving about Haley\u8221\'20\'1D after his primary win, and asking: \u8220\'20\'1CIf Trump is in such good shape, why is he so angry?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  has a message for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 : see ya in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 In a speech following this evenings primary that was part concession, part rallying cry, Haley said her campaign had done what it set out to do: force a one-on-one showdown with the former president.\par \par \uc2 Vowing to stay in the race, she declared: \u8220\'20\'1CNew Hampshire is first in the nation. It is not the last in the nation. This race is far from over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a fighter and I\u8217\'20\'19m scrappy and now we\u8217\'20\'19re the last one standing next to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued.\par \par \uc2 She was sharper in her remarks than she had been on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost Americans do not want a rematch between Biden and Trump. The first party to retire its 80-year-old candidate is going to win this election,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI say it should be the Republicans!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also sounded confident that she could pull off the longed-for upset she sought in New Hampshire in her \u8220\'20\'1Csweet state\u8221\'20\'1D of South Carolina, which holds its primary on 24 February.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery time I\u8217\'20\'19ve run for office in South Carolina, I\u8217\'20\'19ve beaten the political establishment,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re lined up against me again. That\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise. But South Carolina voters don\u8217\'20\'19t want a coronation. They want an election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has wrapped up his speech, but before he did, he opined that if \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  had beaten him, she would find herself under investigation.\par \par \uc2 He, of course, knows a thing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 or four}}}\uc2  about that, since he has been indicted twice by federal prosecutors, and once each by district attorneys in Manhattan and Fulton county, Georgia, while also being the defendant in several civil suits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust a little note to Nikki. She\u8217\'20\'19s not going to win. But, if she did, she would be under investigation by those people in 15 minutes. And I could tell you five reasons why already. Not big reasons \u8211\'20\'13 a little stuff that she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to talk about. But she will be under investigation within minutes. And so would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/21/ron-desantis-drops-out-presidential-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron have been, but he decided to get out}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what \u8220\'20\'1Cstuff\u8221\'20\'1D he was referring to in relation to Haley.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 In 2013, then South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  appointed a congressman from the state, Tim Scott, to fill a vacant Senate seat \u8211\'20\'13 one he still holds to this day.\par \par \uc2 But the long history between the two Palmetto state politicians has led them on separate paths, and Scott is on stage right now with Trump, whom he endorsed after dropping out of the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 The former president remarked on this dynamic, saying to Scott: \u8220\'20\'1CYou must really hate her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The senator then came over the podium, to tell Trump: \u8220\'20\'1COh, I just love you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump is now casting his victory in the race for the GOP nomination as inevitable, pointing to his victory in the Iowa caucuses last week, and tonight in the New Hampshire primaries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you win both, they\u8217\'20\'19ve never had a loser. Let me put it that way. When you win Iowa, and you win in New Hampshire, they\u8217\'20\'19ve never had a loss,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Trump is the first Republican since then president \uc2 Gerald Ford\uc2  in 1976 to win both Iowa and New Hampshire. Ford indeed went on to win the nomination, but lost in the general election to Democrat \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump repeats 2020 election lie in victory speech\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  never misses an opportunity to repeat his false claim that he won the 2020 election, and today is no different.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe won in 2016. And if you really remember, if you want to play it straight, we also won in 2020, by more,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, to cheers from the crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we did much better in 2020 than we did in 2016.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  opened his speech with an attack on \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claim that she\u8217\'20\'19d be a better candidate against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve won almost every single poll in the last three months against crooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , almost, and she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t win those polls,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Trump is fibbing, as he often does. While some polls have shown him ahead of the president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 others have not}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump takes stage at watch party in Nashua, New Hampshire\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in Nashua, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has taken the stage at his watch party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGod Bless the USA\u8221\'20\'1D by Lee Greenwood was playing as he arrived to chants of \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D from the audience. It looks like Senator Tim Scott and entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 both Republicans who withdrew from the race and endorsed him \u8211\'20\'13 are by his side.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Long-shot Democratic candidate \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  vows to stay in race, despite loss to write-in Biden\par \par \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  took the stage at 8.30pm to congratulate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but said that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s margin of victory was \u8220\'20\'1Cby no means\u8221\'20\'1D what should be expected from an incumbent president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is a good man. He\u8217\'20\'19s a fine man \u8230\'20\'26 But I gotta tell you, everyone, he cannot win. The polls are saying he cannot win, his approval numbers are saying he can\u8217\'20\'19t win,\u8221\'20\'1D Phillips said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the fact that an unknown congressman from Minnesota, who two weeks before the election [Phillips actually entered the race in October] said \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna come up here and run for president\u8217\'20\'19 just got 21% that says something, too, my friends.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Flanked by supporters and campaign staff, Phillips gave out high fives from the stage. In the days before the vote, Phillips had suggested that winning 20% in New Hampshire would represent success, and he appeared delighted with the result.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve had so much darn fun I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what to do with myself,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Phillips urged his supporters to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo and have a little fun tonight\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 there\u8217\'20\'19s an open bar here. He said he will remain in the Democratic primary race, even though he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/politics/2023/12/08/dean-phillips-might-file-challenges-after-being-left-off-florida--n-c--ballots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 missed the filing deadline}}}\uc2  in states including Florida and North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to go to South Carolina, then we\u8217\'20\'19re going to Michigan, then we\u8217\'20\'19re going to 47 other states,\u8221\'20\'1D Phillips said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson calls on Republicans to get behind Trump\par \par \uc2 The Republican House speaker, Mike Johnson, has called on the GOP to support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after his victory in the New Hampshire primary tonight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur House Republican leaders and a majority of Republican Senators support his reelection, and Republican voters in Iowa and New Hampshire have strongly backed him at the polls. It\u8217\'20\'19s now past time for the Republican Party to unite around President Trump so we can focus on ending the disastrous Biden presidency and growing our majority in Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D the speaker said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not a hugely surprising statement from Johnson, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mike-johnson-donald-trump-2024-c0d8304f44bd7158415ac80673eb8c7f#:~:text=Johnson%2C%20an%20ally%20and%20defender,all%20in%20for%20President%20Trump.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed Trump}}}\uc2  in November, not long after Republicans elected him leader of the House of Representatives. After the 2020 election, he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/mike-johnson-trump-january-6-democracy-threat-election-denier"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an architect}}}\uc2  of a failed attempt by lawmakers to support Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to get the supreme court to disrupt \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Beyond just vowing to stay in the race, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  also made one more attempt to coax \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to the debate stage.\par \par \uc2 The former president has refused to debate any of the other Republicans who challenged him for the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, Haley included. That didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop her from challenging him to a parley, saying it would prove that he is fit to serve:\par \par \uc2 enltrNikki Haley: "The other day \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  accused me of not providing security at the Capitol on January 6th. Now, I've longed called for mental competency tests for politicians over the age of 75...he should have no problem standing on a debate stage with me." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LVbb9Hf7Ds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LVbb9Hf7Ds}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1749969836740853806?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign says New Hampshire results prove the 'Maga movement has completed its takeover' of GOP\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign appears to be welcoming a rematch with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a just-released statement, campaign manager Julie Ch \u225\'00\'E1vez Rodriguez said:\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s results confirm \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has all but locked up the GOP nomination, and the election denying, anti-freedom Maga movement has completed its takeover of the Republican party. Trump is offering Americans the same extreme agenda that has cost Republicans election after election: promising to undermine American democracy, reward the wealthy on the backs of the middle class, and ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  sees things differently. He\u8217\'20\'19s fighting to grow our economy for the middle class, strengthen our democracy, and protect the rights of every single American. While we work toward November 2024, one thing is increasingly clear today: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is headed straight into a general election matchup where he\u8217\'20\'19ll face the only person to have ever beaten him at the ballot box: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 A groan just went up at \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 election night party, after TV networks announced \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had won the Democratic primary.\par \par \uc2 Phillips wasn\u8217\'20\'19t expecting to win tonight. At campaign events, he had suggested that garnering 20% of the vote in New Hampshire would be a success.\par \par \uc2 His supporters will now be watching for more detailed results, after a write-in campaign for the president was clearly successful.\par \par \uc2 Bill Barry, a retired law enforcement officer, said Phillips, who entered the Democratic race in October 2023, just hasn\u8217\'20\'19t had time to reel in Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, he got in late,\u8221\'20\'1D Barry, 64, said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut, you know, you got to give the guy credit for three or four months. He\u8217\'20\'19s been out there on the campaign. He\u8217\'20\'19s been doing it the New Hampshire way: getting out there meeting the people, going into town halls, going to restaurants and shaking hands and meeting people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Phillips is showing no signs of dropping out of the race. A member of his campaign told the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  that tomorrow about 12 campaign staff are flying to South Carolina, which has its primary on 3 February.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Haley vows to stay in campaign despite Trump win\par \par \uc2 Speaking at her campaign headquarters in Concord, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his victory.\par \par \uc2 But she says she\u8217\'20\'19s staying in the race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNew Hampshire is first in the nation. It is not the last,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s win in New Hampshire has made one Republican senator who was holding out on endorsing him change his mind.\par \par \uc2 Texas Republican \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  had not weighed in on the presidential race, but made clear last year that he thought someone besides Trump should the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee. He has now endorsed the former president, after his win in New Hampshire this evening:\par \par \uc2 enltrI have seen enough. To beat Biden, Republicans need to unite around a single candidate, and it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that President Trump is Republican voters\u8217\'20\'19 choice. Four more years of failed domestic policies like the Biden Border Crisis and record-high inflation, and failed foreign\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  (@JohnCornyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnCornyn/status/1749961519343738885?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 24, 2024}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/news/politics/2023/05/18/cornyn-says-trump-cant-win-in-2024-gop-needs-someone-else-as-presidential-nominee/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Dallas Morning News reported}}}\uc2  that on a call with reporters last May, Cornyn said, \u8220\'20\'1CI think President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s time has passed him by and what\u8217\'20\'19s the most important thing to me is we have a candidate who can actually win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s watch party, the playlist is upbeat and supporters are dancing and cheering.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not the scene you\u8217\'20\'19d expect at the headquarters of a campaign that just lost in New Hampshire. But nevertheless, team Haley is jamming to \u8220\'20\'1CProud Mary\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CEye of the Tiger\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election night watch party in Nashua, several cheers went up in the crowded ballroom, and some hats were thrown in the air, when two big screens announced: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump wins New Hampshire!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, a candidate for Senate in Arizona, gleefully told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CMaga! Make America great again!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile the Beatles song \u8220\'20\'1CRevolution\u8221\'20\'1D is playing outside the ballroom for no obvious reason.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden wins New Hampshire primary, despite not campaigning in state\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has won New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic presidential primary, the Associated Press reports, despite the president not campaigning in the state.\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire had in years past held the first primary in the nation, and the second contest of the Democratic nomination calendar after Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses. But under Biden, the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  has changed its schedule, and South Carolina will be the first state to vote for the Democratic nominee on 3 February.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name did not appear on the ballot in New Hampshire, but his supporters organized a write-in campaign to show support for his presidency, and also to remind him of their desire to remain the first state to hold a primary. That campaign appears to have paid off.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 The biggest outstanding question now is how big \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in New Hampshire was.\par \par \uc2 The greater the gap between him and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , the more pressure the former South Carolina governor will be under to abandon the race \u8211\'20\'13 though she has previously said she will continue her campaign, no matter what.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins New Hampshire Republican primary\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s Republican presidential primary, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 This is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second victory in the two states that voted in the GOP nomination process. Last week, he won overwhelmingly in Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses.\par \par \uc2 The next state to vote is Nevada, where the Republicans will hold caucuses on 8 February. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/nevada/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polls show}}}\uc2  Trump is ahead there.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Voting concludes in New Hampshire presidential primary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s 8pm, and the final polling stations have just closed in New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s presidential primary. Now we await results.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 George Santos shows up at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  watch party\par \par \uc2 Disgraced ex-congressman George Santos has shown up at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election watch party.\par \par \uc2 Queuing at the bar, he denied that he is here as an official campaign surrogate. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just here to have fun,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a three-hour drive for me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Santos was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/01/george-santos-expelled-congress-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expelled last month}}}\uc2  from the House of Representatives. Asked what he is up to these days, Santos smiled: \u8220\'20\'1CHaving fun. I\u8217\'20\'19m enjoying my pink slip moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 George Santos arrives at an election night party for Trump in Nashua, New Hampshire, on 23 January. Photograph: Matt Rourke/AP\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election night party is at the Sheraton Nashua, where rooms start at $489 per night. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marriott.com/reservation/rateListMenu.mi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Its website}}}\uc2  states: \u8220\'20\'1CThe grand exterior of this castle-like hotel draws inspiration from medieval European castles, while the interior is built upon creating community-fluid spaces that feel warm and inviting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The hotel is buzzing ahead of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s expected victory in the New Hampshire primary election. People wearing Maga and USA hats, and stars and stripes scarves, are wandering about in the bar area. \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  popped into the hotel restaurant and was greeted by fans wanting handshakes.\par \par \uc2 The focal point is a fancy hotel ballroom where guests are gathering and making noise. The familiar Trump lectern and row of American flags is on stage. Trump surrogates such as Ramaswamy, Byron Donalds and Kari Lake are in the room doing media interviews.\par \par \uc2 But as the years go by and election cycles come and go, one thing doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change: journalists swapping tales about their lack of internet access on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  chases an upset in the Granite state, someone will be missing from her election night watch party: her husband.\par \par \uc2 Michael Haley is currently deployed on a yearlong mission in Africa with the South Carolina national guard. He previously deployed to Afghanistan in 2012, while she was governor of South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Haley references his service and her experience as the \u8220\'20\'1Cproud wife of a combat veteran\u8221\'20\'1D frequently in her stump speech. In it, she recalls dropping him off at \u8220\'20\'1C4am for another yearlong deployment\u8221\'20\'1D, watching her husband join hundreds of soldiers depart for a country they\u8217\'20\'19ve never been \u8220\'20\'1Call in the name of protecting America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re willing to sacrifice their lives and their families, because they still believe in this amazing experiment,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in Salem, New Hampshire, on Monday.\par \par \uc2 She uses this story as a segway to talk about her platform for veterans and criticize Biden\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the US withdrawal from Afghanistan. She also invoked Michael to respond to the interruptions by protesters during her events.\par \par \uc2 In Exeter, as security removed a protester holding a banner that said \u8220\'20\'1COil Sellout\u8221\'20\'1D, Haley said: \u8220\'20\'1CI am always happy to see a protester because my husband and many military men and women sacrifice every day for them to be able to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D It was one of her strongest applause lines of the evening.\par \par \uc2 Haley is not entirely without family on the trail. Her children, Rena and Nalin, and son-in-law, Josh Jackson, have been a constant presence at her campaign events in the final days before the primary.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Another batch of New Hampshire polls just closed at 7.30pm, per the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Voting in the last polling stations in the state still active will conclude at 8pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Cook Politics Report also believes \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s primary:\par \par \uc2 enltrI've seen enough: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  (R) wins the New Hampshire Republican presidential primary, defeating \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  (R).\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1749950152381493252?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 At the Guardian, we rely on the Associated Press to call these races, and they have not weighed in yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 While it\u8217\'20\'19s too soon to call the Republican primary, the Cook Political Report believes \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has won the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic primary, even though his name was not on the ballot and he did not campaign in the state:\par \par \uc2 enltrI've seen enough: Pres. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (D) wins the New Hampshire Democratic presidential primary.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1749949911796183372?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Supporters of the president nonetheless organized a write-in campaign, and it appears to have worked.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 CNN has done some exit polling in New Hampshire that underscore how the state is different from Iowa, whose caucuses \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won overwhelmingly last week.\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s electorate is known for being independent, and CNN\u8217\'20\'19s data shows a split over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims of fraud in the 2020 election, while his Maga philosophy has relatively few takers:\par \par \uc2 enltrFirst CNN exit polls from New Hampshire --\par \par \uc2 Do you think \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  legitimately won the 2020 election?\par \par \uc2 Yes: 49%\par \par \uc2 No: 49%\par \par \uc2 Are you a part of the MAGA movement?\par \par \uc2 Yes: 32%\par \par \uc2 No: 64% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YRUoJujXr8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/YRUoJujXr8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Wright\uc2  (@DavidWright_7) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidWright_7/status/1749920488816627926?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 There are also far more moderates in the Granite state than in Iowa:\par \par \uc2 enltrOther early findings --\par \par \uc2 Composition of the electorate:\par \par \uc2 Registered Republican: 49%\par \par \uc2 Registered undeclared: 47%\par \par \uc2 Ideology:\par \par \uc2 Very conservative: 24%\par \par \uc2 Somewhat Conservative: 39%\par \par \uc2 Moderate: 31%*\par \par \uc2 *was 9% in Iowa\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Wright\uc2  (@DavidWright_7) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidWright_7/status/1749920947937718308?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Perhaps unsurprisingly, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s voters sharply differ from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s over whether he should continue his campaign if convicted of one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the many things he has been accused of doing}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN exit poll of New Hampshire GOP primary voters:\par \par \uc2 Trump fit for presidency, if convicted of a crime?\par \par \uc2 Yes: 50%\par \par \uc2 No: 47%\par \par \uc2 AMONG TRUMP VOTERS\par \par \uc2 Yes: 86%\par \par \uc2 No: 11%\par \par \uc2 AMONG HALEY VOTERS\par \par \uc2 Yes: 12%\par \par \uc2 No: 85% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YRUoJujXr8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/YRUoJujXr8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Wright\uc2  (@DavidWright_7) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidWright_7/status/1749944525080990206?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll find out soon what this all means for Trump and Haley tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 First primary polls close in New Hampshire\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s 7pm, which means primary polling places in many parts of New Hampshire have closed. However, some sites are staying open until 8pm, so we won\u8217\'20\'19t have full results until after that.\par \par \uc2 Expect to see some results announced over the coming hour.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s allies are predicting victory by \u8220\'20\'1Ca big margin\u8221\'20\'1D in New Hampshire and are seeking to isolate \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  as the last Republican refusing to acknowledge that Trump will be the party nominee.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the Sheraton Nashua hotel ahead of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election watch party, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/kleavittnh/status/1749827759176663535?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Karoline Leavitt}}}\uc2 , a spokeswoman for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Super Pac, Make America Great Again Inc, said: \u8220\'20\'1CA win is a win and we\u8217\'20\'19re very confident that President Trump will win by a big margin here in New Hampshire. The polls have indicated that since the beginning of this race and the enthusiasm on the ground, you can tell. We have the best ground game in this state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Leavitt, who hails from New Hampshire and was a staffer in the first Trump administration, added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been saying for a long time that \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  does not have a pathway to this nomination, and it\u8217\'20\'19s been true for months. It certainly is true after Iowa, where she came in an embarrassing third place and it will be true again after tonight. That\u8217\'20\'19s a decision \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  has to make.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe seems to be the only Republican left in America who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t realise that President Trump is going to be the nominee and who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to start taking this fight to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D Leavitt added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took the stage after \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , but protesters upset at his administration\u8217\'20\'19s policy towards Israel interrupted his speech about 10 times.\par \par \uc2 Almost as soon as the president took the stage to begin speaking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a man carrying a Palestinian flag started to shout, \u8220\'20\'1CHow many kids have you killed?\u8221\'20\'1D After he appeared to have been escorted out, another woman interrupted Biden by shouting, \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael kills two mothers every hour!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During each interruption, the crowd on stage behind Biden started to chant, \u8220\'20\'1CFour more years!\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s go Joe!\u8221\'20\'1D Biden initially stood silently at the podium while the chants continued, but he later started to try to speak louder than the protesters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is going to go on for a while,\u8221\'20\'1D he said after numerous interruptions. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve got this planned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some of the protesters who interrupted \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during his speech in Virginia over his administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel. Photograph: Jim Lo Scalzo/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is under pressure from activists for its perceived support of \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s government in Israel, whose incursion into Gaza since the deadly 7 October attacks by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  has led to the deaths of an estimated 25,000 Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 In New Hampshire, a campaign has been launched to encourage people to write in the word \u8220\'20\'1Cceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D on their primary ballots in protest of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris attacks Trump for involvement in overturning Roe v Wade during campaign's first joint rally\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  kicked off their first joint campaign rally of 2024 in Manassas, Virginia today, with a plea for voters to send them back to the White House to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Harris took the stage before Biden and spoke in front of a group of primarily women, many of whom were carrying red and blue signs that read \u8220\'20\'1CDEFEND CHOICE.\u8221\'20\'1D She framed the fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access as being about freedom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CExtremists have proposed and passed laws that criminalized doctors and punished women. Laws that make no exception even for rape or incest,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd let us all agree: one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government should not be telling her want to do with her body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Virginia is a telling first stop for the 2024 campaign. In elections last year, Virginia Republicans failed to take control of the state legislature after campaigning on a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Seven other states have also voted directly on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot referendums since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade; in each case, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters won. Now, Biden and Harris are betting that outrage over Roe will send them back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Although the Republican primaries are still unfolding in New Hampshire, Harris took aim squarely at former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the Republican frontrunner. Trump appointed three of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices who overturned Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is the architect of this health care crisis, and he is not done, and the extremists are not done,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, warning of the possibility that a Republican administration may enact a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Haley Super Pac strategist vows to keep supporting her\par \par \uc2 A few hours before polls are to close in the Granite State, \uc2 Mark Harris\uc2 , a top strategist for a pro- Nikki Haley Super Pac, vowed to support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s main challenger for as long as she is in the race.\par \par \uc2 Speaking from the lobby of the \uc2 DoubleTree Hotel\uc2 , an election day gathering spot for politicians and journalists, Harris predicted Haley would far exceed her goal of doing better than she did in the Iowa caucuses, when she finished third with 20% of the vote. Like Haley, he refused to be specific about what a strong showing in New Hampshire would look like.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a clear path to victory,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, visibly frustrated by questions from reporters that suggested otherwise. \u8220\'20\'1CHer campaign [has] shepherded the resources to be able to fight a full fight in South Carolina. We\u8217\'20\'19re ready to fight that full fight with her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris pushed back on any suggestion that Haley would drop out before her home state primary late next month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter today, 1% of Republicans who are going to participate in this process will have participated \u8211\'20\'13 99% to go,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are focused on the 99% that are left to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA month is a long time in presidential politics,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, noting that there\u8217\'20\'19s more than a month until the South Carolina primaries on 24 February. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you think back a month ago, if you thought we would be here without \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in the race and all of those other variables and Nikki in the clear one-on-one fight, almost no one in this room would probably have thought that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhere we will be a month from now is, Nikki will be on the verge of doing very, very well in South Carolina and setting the table for a great Super Tuesday,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just political bigwigs like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  whose campaigns are counting on New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 Long-shot Democratic candidate Jason Palmer turned up today at Cat Alley Caf\u233\'00\'E9 in downtown Manchester, the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest city, where he told a group of intrigued college students that he was hoping to finish third in the party primary.\par \par \uc2 His candidacy was news to me. I had been working in the cafe, and unknowingly asked the entreprenneur-turned-presidential candidate to watch my bag when I went to get a coffee. I only learned he was a candidate when someone in the group he spoke to informed me.\par \par \uc2 Palmer, a venture capitalist who is serving on the board of numerous startups and was a former deputy director at the \uc2 Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation\uc2 , finished off his talk with the students by handing out free gloves that said, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen I\u8217\'20\'19m president in 2032, you can say you got the official gloves from 2024\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He then sauntered out of the caf\u233\'00\'E9 on his own.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Which is not to say that everyone in Laconia is on board with returning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to the White House.\par \par \uc2 As he waited outside the neighborhood church for his wife to finish voting inside, 73-year-old retiree Peter Spollett described himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig fan of not Trump\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s a fucking disaster. I love this country and I\u8217\'20\'19d never support someone who\u8217\'20\'19d undermine this country as he has,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Spollett had written in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to show support for the president, who he said has \u8220\'20\'1Cdone a great job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, he\u8217\'20\'19s not perfect, but things aren\u8217\'20\'19t as fucked up as when Trump was there,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding he wished he was a registered independent so he could have received a Republican ballot, as state law allows, and voted against Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 So friendly is Laconia to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that he chose it as the site of his last rally before the New Hampshire primaries.\par \par \uc2 The former president spoke at a resort in the city, which is at the heart of what is known in the state as its Lakes Region, for its many bodies of water:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speaks during his final rally before the New Hampshire primaries in Laconia last night. Photograph: Matt Rourke/AP\par \par \uc2 The rally was notable because three of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former rivals for the nomination \u8211\'20\'13 entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  and South Carolina senator Tim Scott \u8211\'20\'13 campaigned alongside him:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  (left) listens as senator Tim Scott speaks. \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , is behind him on the far right, next to North Dakota governor, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 . Photograph: Chip Somodevilla/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 One big name not in attendance was \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor who was at one point viewed as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s leading rival for the nomination, but dropped out on Sunday after a weak showing in Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses. He has endorsed Trump, but may still be smarting from his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/09/trump-attacks-desantis-no-personality-repeats-election-lies-nevada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign of insults}}}\uc2  against him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 When it comes to Trump country in New Hampshire, look no further than Belknap county, one of two that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won three years ago.\par \par \uc2 He lost the state overall, as every Republican candidate has since \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in 2000. But in the lakeside town of Laconia, where voters chose Trump in 2016 and 2020, the former president\u8217\'20\'19s faithful were making their way to a church in a quiet neighborhood to give him another shot at victory in November.\par \par \uc2 As she left the polling station, 52-year-old Denise Forgione recounted how she likes \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything\u8221\'20\'1D about Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a strong leader, and he will get (stuff) done,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s US politics live blog. She had voted for him previously, and the only other candidate she was considering this year was Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who on Sunday dropped out and endorsed Trump.\par \par \uc2 One candidate she had no interest in was \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe just isn\u8217\'20\'19t in my wheelhouse of what I\u8217\'20\'19m looking for in a president,\u8221\'20\'1D Forgione said. Why? \u8220\'20\'1CShe lies. A lot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t go into how she believed the former South Carolina governor had deceived voters, but she expected her to fail in her quest to win the state. \u8220\'20\'1CWith her, I still think it will be very close, but Trump will take it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Standing outside of a polling place in Derry, Michelle Moge held a sign urging voters to write \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s important that people know we support him even though we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have the delegates,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She understands why some New Hampshire Democrats are upset with the way the party reorganized its primary process, allowing South Carolina to upstage its first-in-the-nation primary status. But Moge understands why.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not a diverse state,\u8221\'20\'1D she said of the state\u8217\'20\'19s mostly white population. \u8220\'20\'1CI feel sad that we\u8217\'20\'19re not getting that woo-woo but at the same time, it makes sense. South Carolina is a lot more diverse than we are, they should be seen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an interesting idea to me to open it up and make the politics a little more diverse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve just got so many old white men \u8211\'20\'13 I love Joe, he\u8217\'20\'19s great. Wasn\u8217\'20\'19t my first choice in 2020 but I voted for him because it\u8217\'20\'19s the right thing to do,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Nodding to the Trump volunteers who were across the sidewalk, cheering and singing songs, she said she was baffled how so many of her fellow New Hampshire voters could still \u8220\'20\'1Cget behind a man who\u8217\'20\'19s a convicted criminal by a jury of his peers, who\u8217\'20\'19s been convicted as a rapist by a jury of his peers and people are still gonna vote for him\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Moge sighed heavily: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s important to me to say, hey, we\u8217\'20\'19re not doing that. We Democrats see that there is another choice who isn\u8217\'20\'19t a criminal. Vote for him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if she was worried Biden might be overshadowed by his nominal challengers \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  or \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 , Moge said it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a bad thing if the president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign felt a bit of pressure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBe warned,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. Let the results push Biden on policy, she said, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CMedicare for All is a wonderful thing. I wanted it before and I want it now. I want an extremely pro-choice candidate.. \u8230\'20\'26 I want all these things I don\u8217\'20\'19t have, but I\u8217\'20\'19m going to keep voting for the people who are going to get us closer and closer to that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 All eyes are on the results of the Republican primary tonight in New Hampshire, but we are also going to learn how the state\u8217\'20\'19s voters are feeling about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and the two long-shot candidates looking to unseat the president as the Democratic nominee. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  with a look at \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s and \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaigns in the state, and the write-in campaign in support of the president:\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Hampshire}}}\uc2  voters head to the polls on Tuesday, much attention will be paid to the Republican presidential primary, but another race could provide additional clues about the general election in November.\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  are moving forward with holding their presidential primary on Tuesday, despite warnings from the national party. The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  decided last year to make South Carolina the first voting state, a move that upended a century-old tradition of New Hampshire hosting the first primary.\par \par \uc2 Outraged over the voting calendar change, New Hampshire officials have chosen to hold an unsanctioned Democratic primary on Tuesday, although the DNC has said it will not award delegates based on the results. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name will not appear on the ballot, but his allies have launched a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bostonglobe.com/2024/01/19/metro/biden-wages-shadow-campaign-new-hampshire/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vigorous write-in campaign}}}\uc2  in support of his re-election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/democrat-candidates-biden-ballot-new-hampshire-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Long-shot Democratic candidates seek upset in New Hampshire primary}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire polls to begin closing at 7pm ET; results expected soon after\par \par \uc2 Polls in New Hampshire will begin closing at 7pm ET, and results will begin coming in shortly after that.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, the first results were reported at roughly 7.30pm ET, but Democratic ballots may take longer to tabulate this year because of the expected large number of write-in votes.\par \par \uc2 Historically, the Manchester and Concord areas have reported results faster, while northern New Hampshire has been slower to count ballots.\par \par \uc2 As we reported earlier, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  has already been declared the winner in Dixville Notch, where all six registered voters backed the former South Carolina governor.\par \par \uc2 Phil Stokel pets Finn at Christ the King Parish, during the New Hampshire presidential primary election, in Concord, New Hampshire. Photograph: Reba Saldanha/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Two prominent No Labels donors have sued the centrist political group for pulling a \u8220\'20\'1Cbait and switch\u8221\'20\'1D by preparing to back a third-party presidential candidacy after seeking donations to support \u8220\'20\'1Cbipartisan activism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Douglas and Jonathan Durst, cousins who are part of the powerful Durst real estate family in New York, allege that No Labels has \u8220\'20\'1Clost its way, abandoned its original mission, and fundamentally betrayed its donors\u8217\'20\'19 trust in the process\u8221\'20\'1D in their lawsuit, filed in the New York state supreme court on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The suit seeks damages and reimbursements for the $145,000 that the Dursts donated years ago, when No Labels was founded on the promise of finding governing solutions, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/23/us/politics/durst-no-labels-lawsuit-election-donors.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported.}}}\uc2  The suit reads:\par \par \uc2 This case seeks to hold No Labels accountable for the consequences of its misguided actions that have left its original benefactors like the Dursts feeling bewildered, betrayed and outraged.\par \par \uc2 No Labels has \u8220\'20\'1Cshifted seismically from its original mission\u8221\'20\'1D and its donors \u8220\'20\'1Cshould not have to stand idly by\u8221\'20\'1D, it continues.\par \par \uc2 Founded in 2009, No Labels is now on the ballot in 14 states and say it will decide in March whether to offer its ballot line to a unity presidential ticket.\par \par \uc2 Critics say if No Labels does mount a campaign, polling shows more voters likely to peel from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  than Trump, handing the latter the White House for a second term should he be the Republican nominee.\par \par \uc2 The Dursts\u8217\'20\'19 lawsuit continues:\par \par \uc2 A third ticket option is a clear break from No Labels\u8217\'20\'19 prior goal of uniting the two parties in Congress to pursue common sense solutions \u8212\'20\'14 instead, it incites division amongst Americans.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign raised $1.5m in the first two days after \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  dropped out of the Republican primary race on Sunday, her campaign told Fox News today.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the outlet, Haley said:\par \par \uc2 Everybody wants to talk about big dollar donations. These are all small donations. I mean, we\u8217\'20\'19ve received just in the last two days a million and a half dollars in small donations from all over the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he 'couldn't care less' if Haley stays or drops out of race\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , at a polling site in New Hampshire this afternoon, insisted \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a threat to his campaign and predicted a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig loss\u8221\'20\'1D for his rival in the state. He said:\par \par \uc2 I think she\u8217\'20\'19s worked very hard, but I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t care less, if she drops out that\u8217\'20\'19s fine.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t comment when asked if he had spoken with \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  since the Florida governor dropped out of the race on Sunday and endorsed him.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speaks to members of the press outside of Londonderry High School in Londonderry, New Hampshire. Photograph: Brandon Bell/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court on Tuesday rejected \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s request that it reconsider his appeal against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/donald-trump-election-interference-case-gag-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a gag order}}}\uc2  imposed against him in the criminal case over his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The move paves the way for a potential final challenge to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision by the US court of appeals to deny Trump an en banc rehearing \u8211\'20\'13 where the full bench of judges consider the matter \u8211\'20\'13 marks the latest setback for the former president after an earlier three-judge panel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/08/trump-special-counsel-federal-election-case-gag-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also rejected his appeal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For months, Trump has been attempting to free himself from a limited protective order entered by the US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/03/tanya-chutkan-trump-jan-6-case-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who is overseeing the criminal case}}}\uc2  in Washington. The order prohibits him from making inflammatory statements that could intimidate trial witnesses or poison the jury pool.\par \par \uc2 The gag order came after special counsel prosecutors complained that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s brazen public statements attacking them, court staff and potential trial witnesses could chill witness testimony and impede the fair administration of justice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/court-rejects-trump-gag-order-appeal-january-6-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Laconia, New Hampshire, on 22 January 2024. Photograph: Matt Rourke/AP\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/court-rejects-trump-gag-order-appeal-january-6-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Court rejects Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request to reconsider appeal against gag order in election interference case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Linda Gallant of Derry doesn\u8217\'20\'19t typically vote in the Republican primary. But the undeclared voter pulled a Republican ballot today. She said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll vote for anyone that has a chance to beat Trump.\par \par \uc2 Her support for Haley is mostly about denying Trump the nomination, but she said she could be persuaded to support her in a general election against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , whom she voted for in 2020.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s young, she\u8217\'20\'19s fresh. I think she brings a different energy.\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cbrings chaos wherever he goes, like she says. He\u8217\'20\'19s not a nice person. He\u8217\'20\'19s not an admirable person. She is and so is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but anybody other than Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congressman Byron Donalds, a Trump supporter, dropped by the polling place in Derry to thank campaign volunteers for their support. He posed for photos and thanked supporters who said they can\u8217\'20\'19t wait for him to run for president one day.\par \par \uc2 Donalds has called on Haley to drop out of the race if she loses to Trump in New Hampshire on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s got to show she can win a state. And this is the only one in my view that she\u8217\'20\'19s got a shot in,\u8221\'20\'1D he told yours truly. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the end of the line for her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donalds also insisted that Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Con it\u8221\'20\'1D mentally, after Haley questioned his mental acuity. Trump appeared to confuse her for \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  during a recent speech. Afterward, she added a segment of her stump speech raising the issue of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s age and fitness for office.\par \par \uc2 Donalds said he was with Trump on Monday night and found him unchanged mentally or physically.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know President Trump spent time with him, like saw him yesterday, saw him last night. It\u8217\'20\'19s not even the same situation, not even the same ballpark,\u8221\'20\'1D he told me.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jessica Bastien, an undeclared voter in Derry, showed up to cast her ballot for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wearing a top with the former president\u8217\'20\'19s mugshot and the words: \u8220\'20\'1CNOT GUILTY\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bastien is undaunted by the four criminal charges and 91 felony counts he\u8217\'20\'19s facing as he marches toward the Republican nomination. In her view, each count is baseless and she is hopeful he will ultimately be acquitted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI support his love for the country. His policies. His truthfulness and always sticking by what he says and protecting the US citizens first,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Asked what would happen if Trump loses, she said Biden was too weak to win and wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t contemplate any other outcome. In the unlikely event Trump is dethroned in the primary, she is not sure what she would do in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think both parties are corrupted and have their ways of lying to us,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s movement doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need the support of anti-Trump Republicans to win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not really worried about that,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think we lost anything. I think we lost the people that we should have lost a long time ago.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Voters arrived at a steady pace to cast their ballots in Derry, home to the largest polling place in the country. In a sign of the town\u8217\'20\'19s importance to Haley\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of a David v Goliath-sized upset on Tuesday night, the candidate dropped by to thank volunteers.\par \par \uc2 Steve Pearson, who represents Derry in the state legislature, was holding the lone Haley sign when I spoke to him outside of Pinkerton Academy high school. A raucous group of Trump campaign volunteers lined the sidewalk with signs next to a scattered group holding signs for Democratic candidates \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  and \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 . On the opposite side, a handful of people urged voters to \u8220\'20\'1Cwrite in\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name.\par \par \uc2 Just after midday, Jim MacEachern, a Republican who serves on the town council, said 3,700 people had already cast their ballots. Roughly 700 people chose a Democratic ballot while 3,000 took a Republican one.\par \par \uc2 If the pace keeps, and the weather keeps cooperating, he predicted the polling booth would see as many as 12,000 people by the end of the day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor a primary, that\u8217\'20\'19s pretty damn good,\u8221\'20\'1D MacEachern said. The secretary of state had predicted record-breaking turnout among Republicans, and Derry\u8217\'20\'19s strong participation is a sign New Hampshire might be on track to do that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA high turnout will bode well for her,\u8221\'20\'1D Pearson told me. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause the diehard Trump Trump folks are coming out either way. It\u8217\'20\'19s the independents, it\u8217\'20\'19s the Republicans who are looking to find a candidate that they think is electable\u8221\'20\'1D who will make the difference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor too long we\u8217\'20\'19ve treated the primary as the prize when the prize is the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou needed a candidate who is electable at a national scale.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump and Georgia representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  made an appearance at a polling place in Londonderry, New Hampshire, as voting is under way in the state\u8217\'20\'19s primary.\par \par \uc2 Greene helped stomp for Trump, declaring on social media that the primary was \u8220\'20\'1Cover\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is our nominee\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When asked if she had a final message for New Hampshire voters, Greene said, in part: \u8220\'20\'1CI think the big message is that this is a referendum on the Republican party and it\u8217\'20\'19s been coming. Republican voters\u8230\'20\'26are sick and tired of uni-party Republicans, the neo-con establishment wing of the party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMy message from Londonderry, New Hampshire!\par \par \uc2 Tonight, Republican voters are going to send a LOUD and CLEAR message:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is our nominee and the primary is OVER! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6M6r7gsl7R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6M6r7gsl7R}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  ???? (@mtgreenee) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mtgreenee/status/1749848372612055482?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Andres Hulfachor, 21, a student in Nashua, New Hampshire, voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He said:\par \par \uc2 He can bring a better America. I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t too happy with what \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did. I feel like honestly this country has gotten a little bit soft, and he can bring back that hard working culture. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of people that have that victim mindset now since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been president.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can give out that winning mindset that we need to be a country that other countries look at and don\u8217\'20\'19t really laugh at. On foreign relations, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  didn\u8217\'20\'19t do a good job at all. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  got a lot of respect from other countries. That\u8217\'20\'19s very important considering what\u8217\'20\'19s going on right now around the world.\par \par \uc2 Hulfachor would also be fine with \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  as the nominee:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think she\u8217\'20\'19s a bad candidate at all. If she ends up becoming president, I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be disappointed at all. She\u8217\'20\'19s a great lady, speaks well, has a lot of good ideas. I know my parents are fans of \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  too but I have Trump a touch in front of her. But like I said, if she wins, I won\u8217\'20\'19t be too disappointed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Law student AhLana Ames did not vote for a person, but for a word: \u8220\'20\'1Cceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She used her Democratic ballot to take part in a campaign to write in the term to protest the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19 support of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m against war in general. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think what\u8217\'20\'19s going on in Israel is particularly just,\u8221\'20\'1D the 23-year-old said.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not particularly pleased with how \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is handling it, but wanted to vote Democratic.\par \par \uc2 The president has been under increasing pressure from the left for his administration\u8217\'20\'19s defense of Israel, which staged a bloody invasion of Gaza following \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 7 October terrorist attack and mass kidnapping. An estimated 25,000 Palestinians have died in the incursion, but the Biden administration has generally refrained from openly criticizing \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government, and allowed Israel to buy US weapons, leading some progressives to say they will not vote for Biden again.\par \par \uc2 Ames plans to soon move to Pennsylvania, a swing state Biden will likely need to win to get a second term in office. While she may look into supporting a third party candidate, she concedes that would likely be pointless, and she will probably end up voting for Biden again. She added:\par \par \uc2 I just know I\u8217\'20\'19ll never vote for a Republican candidate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Martin Janoschek, 57, is a Republican-leaning independent who did not want to vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and thus voted for \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know she\u8217\'20\'19s a longshot,\u8221\'20\'1D said Janoschek, who is unemployed.\par \par \uc2 I think she\u8217\'20\'19s a pretty common-sensical person, from what I heard.\par \par \uc2 But if it comes down to Trump or \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the November general election, as polls indicate it most likely will, Janoschek will probably vote for the former president over the current one, even though he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like his style.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a little bit bombastic,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a die hard Republican, and I voted for president Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D declared 73-year-old Mark Gonyer as he left the polling station in downtown Concord.\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t like some of the things he did, but out of all the candidates, he\u8217\'20\'19s the best one.\par \par \uc2 There are, of course, far fewer candidates in the race than there were just a few months ago. Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  dropped out two days ago, former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  quit before the Iowa caucuses and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  exited after performing poorly in the Hawkeye state.\par \par \uc2 The one candidate left who could beat Trump in New Hampshire today \u8211\'20\'13 despite his big lead in recent polls \u8211\'20\'13 is former South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , but Gonyer wasn\u8217\'20\'19t interested.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s got some good points,\u8221\'20\'1D he conceded, but said, based on his experience with female politicians nationwide and in New Hampshire, he didn\u8217\'20\'19t think Haley was up to the task.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would give her a shot but look at Hillary Clinton, look at our vice-president we had now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gonyer, who delivers auto parts and rebuilds old tractors. \u8220\'20\'1CShe hasn\u8217\'20\'19t done anything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There wasn\u8217\'20\'19t much of a wait to vote at the old armory-turned-community center just steps from the New Hampshire statehouse that was one of the polling places for downtown Concord.\par \par \uc2 Voters got in and out quickly, passing supporters of Democrat \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 , Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and the write-in campaign for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on today\u8217\'20\'19s ballot.\par \par \uc2 Cinde Warmington, the lone Democrat on New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s executive council and a candidate for governor, was there to support the write-in effort for Biden. Holding a sign reading \u8220\'20\'1CWrite-in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, Warmington said:\par \par \uc2 It is so important that he comes out of here in New Hampshire, with the country knowing that we are 100% behind our president. We need to re-elect him, keep \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  out of the White House and to protect our fundamental freedom, like access to reproductive healthcare, which is under assault in the state as well as states across the country.\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire typically holds the first primary in the nation, but will now vote later after the \uc2 Democratic National Committee (DNC)\uc2  changed the schedule, and Biden has not endorsed the write-in campaign. Beyond being a show of support for him, Warmington said it was a way to remind Democratic leadership of the Granite state\u8217\'20\'19s importance. Warmington said:\par \par \uc2 We were first and we are still first, and regardless of what the DNC does, we will always be the first-in-the-nation primary.\par \par \uc2 The DNC rule change {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-presidential-primary-joe-biden-dean-phillips-marianne-williamson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 means Biden is not appearing on the Democratic ballot, }}}\uc2  though Williamson and Minnesota congressman \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  are. Nonetheless, reports emerged yesterday that New Hampshire voters were receiving robocalls in which a voice that sounded like the president told them not to vote today, prompting the Biden-Harris campaign to call for an investigation.\par \par \uc2 It is \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely disgraceful that anyone would try to suppress the vote\u8221\'20\'1D, Armington said.\par \par \uc2 I hope that they find out who it is and prosecute them to the full extent of the law.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls show \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  well ahead in New Hampshire. Even if \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  pulls off an upset here, there\u8217\'20\'19s a sense that the result would only prolong an inevitable Trump-Biden rematch.\par \par \uc2 There were no debates in the run-up to the primary. After Iowa, Haley refused to debate unless Trump was on stage. Two scheduled debates were dropped. If yard signs are a traditional measure of enthusiasm for a candidate about to break through, the conspicuous lack of them is telling.\par \par \uc2 In their absence, many voters here have complained that the battle for their vote is mostly playing out in ads. Tens of millions of dollars have been spent flooding the airwaves and filling their mailboxes. Some voters said they receive up to 10 pieces of campaign literature in the mailbox each day.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s enough to make any voter say good riddance.\par \par \uc2 Even Haley admitted as much in her primary eve remarks: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re excited because you won\u8217\'20\'19t have to watch any more commercials. You won\u8217\'20\'19t have to see the mail and the text messages will stop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A supporter of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  holds signs near a voting site at Londonderry high school in Londonderry, New Hampshire, on Tuesday. Photograph: Michael Reynolds/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire once again is at the center of the political universe, hosting a fiercely guarded \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst-in-the-nation\u8221\'20\'1D primary. But if you were here, as we are, something feels off in the Granite state.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just the warmer-than-usual weather.\par \par \uc2 Only one party is holding a seriously contested primary \u8211\'20\'13 not completely out of the ordinary when an incumbent is running, but the national Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65afcfda8f08541705644560#block-65afcfda8f08541705644560"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have effectively shived New Hampshire.}}}\uc2  The move infuriated local Democrats, who chose to move ahead with a Biden-free ballot knowing that, at least on their side of the aisle, the primary\u8217\'20\'19s glory days are in the past.\par \par \uc2 The Republican contest has at times felt as sleepy \u8211\'20\'13 even though \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is facing his first ever serious one-on-one challenge from his party.\par \par \uc2 Voters fill out their ballots at a polling location at Bedford high school in Bedford, New Hampshire. Photograph: Joe Raedle/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire voters, famously free-thinking and proud of their reputation for picking winners, haven\u8217\'20\'19t had much of the excitement they\u8217\'20\'19re used to. Only Haley has done the statewide blitz, shaking hands and answering interrogatories at diners, breweries and even a hockey game.\par \par \uc2 But the barn-storming came too late, veterans of New Hampshire politics told me. They faulted her for not opening herself up more frequently to voters. She didn\u8217\'20\'19t hold town hall style events that voters are accustomed to, a hallmark of past successful campaigns in the state and a way for voters to test a candidate\u8217\'20\'19s mettle.\par \par \uc2 Trump seems to be riding on the loyalty he inspires with the GOP base, dipping into the state between courtroom appearances and only for rallies at night.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In Nashua, New Hampshire, Vincent Ranucci, 78, a retired lawyer wearing a \uc2 Boston Red Sox\uc2  baseball cap, is an independent voter and wrote in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name. He explained: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a good president. He\u8217\'20\'19s got a good head on his shoulders and wants to do the right thing. No personality quirks.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve always liked him. He\u8217\'20\'19s not perfect like anybody else. I wish the border would be secured better than it is, and they\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to fix that. However, unfortunately, with our Congress and our parties, no matter what you want to do, you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to get it through them and they fuss and they try to tie different things together that shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be. They should take care of the border issue and do Ukraine separately. But that\u8217\'20\'19s what Joe\u8217\'20\'19s up against.\par \par \uc2 Ranucci, who has lived in New Hampshire since 1989, was untroubled by having to write Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name by hand on the ballot paper.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s fine. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care much about primaries or who\u8217\'20\'19s first and all that other stuff? It\u8217\'20\'19s all politics, it\u8217\'20\'19s all money. New Hampshire makes a lot of money on this, I\u8217\'20\'19m sure. Good for advertising New Hampshire so good for them. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care where we\u8217\'20\'19re first or second or whatever just as long as we have the system and we use it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris to hold \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights rally in Virginia\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will join forces at a rally in Virginia today as they campaign for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a likely top issue for Democrats in this year\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris will be joined by their spouses, first lady Jill Biden and second gentleman Doug Emhoff, the first time the four of them have appeared together since the 2024 campaign began.\par \par \uc2 At the rally, which comes a day after the 51st anniversary of the Roe v Wade ruling, Biden will address what he will describe as the \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating\u8221\'20\'1D impacts of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of the decision in June 2022. Afterward, Biden and Harris are expected to meet with healthcare providers and leaders of reproductive rights groups.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/kamala-harris-abortion-rights-wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kicked off her much-vaunted \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights nationwide tour }}}\uc2  in the battleground state of Wisconsin, which the president won in the 2020 presidential election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/general-news-7aef88488e4a801545a13cf4319591b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by just over 20,000 votes}}}\uc2 . Wisconsin is a notable starting point for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive freedoms tour. Last year, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights propelled a Democratic victory in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 critical election}}}\uc2  for the state supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade, the supreme court decision that enshrined the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned}}}\uc2  in June 2022 after the then president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  nominated three conservative justices to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court.\par \par \uc2 The decision was a major blow to supporters of reproductive rights, but since the ruling seven states \u8211\'20\'13 including the conservative strongholds of Kentucky, Kansas and Montana \u8211\'20\'13 have held ballot referendums where voters chose to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The issue also appeared to hurt Republicans in the 2022 midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump loses gag order request in January 6 case\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s request for the DC circuit to reconsider his gag order in the federal January 6 case has been denied, my colleague Hugo Lowell reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: US court of appeals for DC Circuit denies Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request for a panel rehearing over his gag order in the federal Jan. 6 case \u8212\'20\'14 sets up option for Trump to appeal to \uc2 SCOTUS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xeEYg0bkkq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xeEYg0bkkq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1749847159787196624?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mary Riddell, 64, a retired teacher, wrote in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name at the polls in Bicentennial elementary school in Nashua, New Hampshire. She said:\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s a good, strong Democrat with democratic ideals. America\u8217\'20\'19s already a fabulous country. We\u8217\'20\'19re doing great the way it is. I believe in public education, believe in teaching history correctly, believe in having access to books, believe in sharing the wealth to everyone in our country, believe in welcoming immigrants and, I just believe in doing what\u8217\'20\'19s right.\par \par \uc2 Riddell did not consider voting for \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  or \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re great people, they have good messages but we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to rally behind \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and make sure that Trump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t return for another four years because it was an angry, chaotic time in our country and we can\u8217\'20\'19t go back to that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 How did Riddell feel about having to write in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name rather than cast a traditional vote? \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pretty strong, I\u8217\'20\'19m pretty brave, I can write a name in. If that\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s expected of us to preserve our democracy, then we can rise to the challenge and do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Riddell said she understood the logic of moving New Hampshire down the primary electoral calendar. \u8220\'20\'1CI would like it to be more inclusive of different peoples, of different races, of different genders, of different ethnic groups, of different political persuasions. New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s a great state, a lovely state, but not representative of the rest of the country.\par \par \uc2 Sometimes things have to change. We\u8217\'20\'19ve gone through a lot of changes. The world\u8217\'20\'19s going through changes. We can write in somebody and it\u8217\'20\'19s time. It\u8217\'20\'19s good that South Carolina is going to have a chance. Let other states that are just more ethnically diverse have a chance because that\u8217\'20\'19s what our country is becoming and we welcome it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In Nashua, New Hampshire, Patricia Hemenway, 55, a production planner, is a registered independent and voted for \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  in the Republican race. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause I\u8217\'20\'19m voting against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said simply.\par \par \uc2 Asked about her objections to Trump, Hemenway summed up:\par \par \uc2 Everything. Absolutely everything. I\u8217\'20\'19m a military brat; my father served for 26 years. I will have to say the January 6 thing was absolutely revolting to me. I find him revolting. I find a lot of his followers scary.\par \par \uc2 If the presidential election is a Biden v Trump rematch, she would support the Democrat. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a bit old but, if that\u8217\'20\'19s the only alternative, I\u8217\'20\'19m voting for the lesser of two evils at this point.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There was a steady flow of voters at Bicentennial elementary school in Nashua, New Hampshire. At the snowy school entrance, a few people waved signs encouraging voters to write-in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name in the Democratic primary; there were also a couple of Trump supporters holding his signs on the Republican side.\par \par \uc2 Voters lined up inside a school hall decorated with the national flags of various countries as election officials and police looked on. A grey T-shirt draped over a partition said: \u8220\'20\'1CNH proudly voting first since 1920.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emerging from the hall Rita Case, 78, a retired IT worker, admitted that she had wanted to vote for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in the Republican primary. She said:\par \par \uc2 I like the things that DeSantis believes in and there would not be the chaos and division that might come with Bozo, whose mouth is his worst enemy.\par \par \uc2 But with the Florida governor having dropped out on Sunday, Case switched to Trump anyway. She explained:\par \par \uc2 He can keep people in their place and take care of the border and not let other countries walk all over us. The chaos and the \u8216\'20\'18uh, well\u8217\'20\'19 comes in second.\par \par \uc2 As for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , she offered: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s done a few good things but he\u8217\'20\'19s too weak. I don\u8217\'20\'19t like a lot of the Democrat beliefs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The New Hampshire attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office said on Monday that it was investigating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/biden-fake-robocalls-new-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reports of a robocall }}}\uc2  mimicking the voice of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and encouraging Democrats not to vote in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary election.\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire attorney general, John Formella, said the recorded message, which was sent to multiple voters on Sunday, appeared to be an illegal attempt to disrupt and suppress voting.\par \par \uc2 Voters should \u8220\'20\'1Cdisregard the contents of this message entirely\u8221\'20\'1D, he added.\par \par \uc2 A recording of the call, released by NBC, begins with: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat a bunch of malarkey,\u8221\'20\'1D, using a term so characteristic of the 81-year-old president it has been widely used in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/04/25/1171885259/dark-brandon-meme-makes-an-appearance-on-bidens-new-campaign-website"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 merchandising and meme-making}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know the value of voting Democratic,\u8221\'20\'1D the voice said. \u8220\'20\'1COur votes count. It\u8217\'20\'19s important that you save your vote for the November election. We\u8217\'20\'19ll need your help in electing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  up and down the ticket.\par \par \uc2 Voting this Tuesday only enables the Republicans in their quest to elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  again. Your vote makes a difference in November, not this Tuesday. If you would like to be removed from future calls, please press two now.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65afcfda8f08541705644560#block-65afcfda8f08541705644560"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will not be on the Democratic ballot}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, because New Hampshire went against an official reorganisation of the primary calendar which placed South Carolina first.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2 , the Democratic congressman from Minnesota who is mounting a long shot primary campaign against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , rocked up at the Windham high school polling location on Tuesday morning to shake the hands of some New Hampshire voters.\par \par \uc2 He was well received, even by a woman holding a \u8216\'20\'18Trump 2024\u8217\'20\'19 sign, and Phillips seemed unfazed when he saw a man holding a \u8216\'20\'18Write-in Biden\u8217\'20\'19 placard. After an internal Democratic party feud Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name is not on the ballot in New Hampshire, but a campaign has started to write the president\u8217\'20\'19s name anyway.\par \par \uc2 Inside, Phillips engaged with some volunteers from the Windham Lions, a charity organization which helps people in the community. The Lions are selling cookies \u8211\'20\'13 the molasses one is the bestseller so far \u8211\'20\'13 to raise money.\par \par \uc2 Democratic candidate for President and Minnesota Representative \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  greets voters during the New Hampshire Primary at a voting site at Windham High School in Windham, New Hampshire. Photograph: Amanda Sabga/UPI/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Phillips also stopped to chat with Theresa Arangio, who was on her way into the high school gym to vote. When she came out, she said she had been wavering between writing in Biden and voting for Phillips, but the latter had won her over.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis ads made a lot of sense when he was talking about Biden and Trump, and there\u8217\'20\'19s bad sides to both of them,\u8221\'20\'1D Arangio, 81, said.\par \par \uc2 And then just seeing him, he was just so personable. Not that Biden isn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8211\'20\'13 he is a very personable, very compassionate person. But yeah, maybe that was it, that just seeing Phillips here, him making the effort to come and meet people.\par \par \uc2 Arangio added:\par \par \uc2 President Biden, I really think he\u8217\'20\'19s done a great job. I really like him. But, you know, the age is a factor. And with Trump, I\u8217\'20\'19m just afraid. I don\u8217\'20\'19t want four more years of him, I just don\u8217\'20\'19t for our country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Three failed Republican candidates get behind Trump in New Hampshire\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  urged the crowd to end the primary right here. \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  told them to think of safety and prosperity. Tim Scott posed a series of questions that culminated with: \u8220\'20\'1CHow many y\u8217\'20\'19all want me to stop talking so you can hear from your next president, \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 ? \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the three failed US presidential candidates turned endorsers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JasonMillerinDC/status/1749618287309111648?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stood alongside}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on stage in Laconia, New Hampshire, on Monday, the crowd chanted \u8220\'20\'1CFour more years!\u8221\'20\'1D and the message to Republicans was clear: join us now or be cast into the political wilderness.\par \par \uc2 The show of unity exemplified the breakneck speed with which elected officials, rightwing media and mega-donors are consolidating around Trump as their seemingly inevitable nominee in 2024. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?c5103606/vivek-ramaswamy-doug-burgum-tim-scott-campaign-fmr-pres-trump-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump told the rally}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Now is the time for the Republican party to come together. We have to unify \u8230\'20\'26 We\u8217\'20\'19re all in the same team, 100% focused on [Joe] Biden and beating him in November.\par \par \uc2 Buoyed by a record win in last week\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa caucuses and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/21/ron-desantis-republican-presidential-candidate-dropped-out-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the exit of Florida governor Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , Trump heads into Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s New Hampshire primary election with only one opponent standing in his way: \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , a former US ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2 . If the former president wins convincingly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/nikki-haley-trump-polls-new-hampshire-republican-presidential-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as opinion polls suggest}}}\uc2 , Haley will face renewed pressure to end the anti-Trump resistance.\par \par \uc2 It is a striking contrast from the 2016 primary season, when multiple candidates continued to battle Trump into May. It is also very different mood music from a year ago when, in the wake of disappointing midterm elections, there were rumblings of discontent in the Republican party and a desire to turn the page.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/republican-donors-trump-new-hampshire-primary-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/republican-donors-trump-new-hampshire-primary-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Time to back Trump: Republican donors accept the inevitable}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/republican-donors-trump-new-hampshire-primary-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Time to back Trump: Republican donors accept the inevitable}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Diana Jeans voted for \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  this morning in Windham, a small town less than 10 miles from the New Hampshire-Massachusetts border.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe is down to earth. She\u8217\'20\'19s compassionate, and she\u8217\'20\'19s for the American people. Truly. It\u8217\'20\'19s not about Nikki, it\u8217\'20\'19s about the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D Jeans said.\par \par \uc2 She said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the opposite.\par \par \uc2 I think that he has a very large ego, and he is a little bit of a narcissist. And people like that have themselves as their best interest, more than the people. And \u8216\'20\'18Make America Great Again\u8217\'20\'19 didn\u8217\'20\'19t happen the first time. Why would it happen now?\par \par \uc2 If Trump does end up being the Republican nominee, Jeans said she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sure if she would vote for him, although she said she would \u8220\'20\'1Cdefinitely not\u8221\'20\'1D cast her vote for Biden.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Windham high school in Windham, New Hampshire, is a flurry of activity right now, with warmly dressed voters scurrying from their cars to the warmth of the voting booths inside.\par \par \uc2 Tina Lorenz, who is wearing a white puffer jacket with a series of red accessories \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m being patriotic,\u8221\'20\'1D she said \u8211\'20\'13 has been a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporter since 2016.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is representing the American people. He is not out for himself. He\u8217\'20\'19s not out for political gain. He\u8217\'20\'19s not out for financial reasons. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need money, he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need fame and fortune. He already has all of that,\u8221\'20\'1D Lorenz, 63, said.\par \par \uc2 He is out there for the average person. And that\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happening, we\u8217\'20\'19ve become so polarized, that there\u8217\'20\'19s nobody out there for just regular people.\par \par \uc2 Tina Lorenz, right, and Ed Schoen, behind, outside the polling place at Windham High School in Windham, N.H. Photograph: Michael Dwyer/AP\par \par \uc2 Immigration is a big issue for Lorenz, a retired nurse.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m all for people coming into this country legally and being helped. But just to have people come in and have people, regular American people, having to pay for more and more and more when they\u8217\'20\'19re having trouble just paying for themselves isn\u8217\'20\'19t right.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Asked if she would drop out should \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  beat her by double digits in New Hampshire, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  said that she has \u8220\'20\'1Cnever done what he tells me to do\u8221\'20\'1D. She added:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m running against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to talk about an obituary.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65afdd398f08af761dc31af2#block-65afdd398f08af761dc31af2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A memo by Haley\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager}}}\uc2  earlier today appeared to be a direct response to a Trump campaign memo on Sunday that suggested tonight\u8217\'20\'19s results could prompt her to exit the race.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign memo, written by the former president\u8217\'20\'19s advisers Chris LaCivita and Susie Wiles, argued that Haley faces only two options if she loses in New Hampshire: to drop out and back Trump, or to be prepared to be \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely DEMOLISHED and EMBARASSED in her [] home state of South Carolina\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'See y'all in South Carolina': Haley campaign says she's 'not going anywhere'\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has insisted she isn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing anywhere\u8221\'20\'1D in a memo on Tuesday that appeared to push back against suggestions that she could drop out of the Republican primary race if she loses in New Hampshire tonight.\par \par \uc2 The memo by Haley\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager, Betsy Ankney, accuses the \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical class and the media\u8221\'20\'1D of wanting to \u8220\'20\'1Cthrow up their hands\u8221\'20\'1D and to give \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ccoronation\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CThat isn\u8217\'20\'19t how this works,\u8221\'20\'1D she writes.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve heard multiple members of the press say New Hampshire is \u8216\'20\'18the best it\u8217\'20\'19s going to get\u8217\'20\'19 for Nikki due to Independents and unaffiliated voters being able to vote in the Republican primary. The reality is that the path through Super Tuesday includes more states than not that have this dynamic.\par \par \uc2 She notes that South Carolina has no party registration, meaning that anyone can vote in the Republican primary if they have not already voted in the Democrat primary on 3 February.\par \par \uc2 Eleven of the 16 Super Tuesday states have \u8220\'20\'1Copen or semi-open primaries\u8221\'20\'1D, she says, adding that after Super Tuesday, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe will have a very good picture of where this race stands \u8230\'20\'26 Until then, everyone should take a deep breath.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  made her closing pitch in Salem last night, she was interrupted by a heckler.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWill you marry me?\u8221\'20\'1D a young man shouted. Haley laughed, and without missing a beat pointed at him: Will you vote for me?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said no, he was voting for Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGet outta here,\u8221\'20\'1D she said as the crowd booed and security moved to escort him out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls open in New Hampshire as Trump looks to drive Haley out of the race\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  are facing off in New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s first-in-the-nation primary as voters head to the polls to select a Republican nominee to take on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in November.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65af98d68f089c7f255c27da#block-65af98d68f089c7f255c27da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 With polls open,}}}\uc2  New Hampshire voters are set to determine the course of the GOP primary: will they stand by Trump, delivering him a decisive sweep of the first contests, or will enough of them choose to turn the page, putting Haley in striking distance of her former boss or possibly even handing her an upset outright.\par \par \uc2 Trump leads in New Hampshire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65afba358f086ad0fadb06e6#block-65afba358f086ad0fadb06e6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  by double-digit margins}}}\uc2  but is considered more vulnerable in the state, where independent voters make up nearly 40% of the electorate and can choose to vote in either party\u8217\'20\'19s primary. The former president is aiming to secure a commanding victory in New Hampshire, the state that propelled him to the nomination in 2016 and where he continues to hold strong sway among the Republican base.\par \par \uc2 A large enough win would effectively extinguish Haley\u8217\'20\'19s presidential ambitions, eight days after the former president\u8217\'20\'19s record-setting victory in the Iowa. Haley has staked her candidacy on a strong showing in New Hampshire, investing time and resources into persuading the state\u8217\'20\'19s famously free-thinking electorate that she is the candidate best positioned to beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in November. In the first official results, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65af865f8f081fd80444fbd9#block-65af865f8f081fd80444fbd9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all six registered voters of Dixville Notch cast their ballots for Haley}}}\uc2  in the tiny township\u8217\'20\'19s midnight primary.\par \par \uc2 Democrats will also hold a primary on Tuesday, but \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s name {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-presidential-primary-joe-biden-dean-phillips-marianne-williamson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won\u8217\'20\'19t be on the ballot}}}\uc2 . Though turnout is expected to be low, Democrats will have the choice between voting for \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2 , a Democratic congressman from Minnesota, and \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 , an author and self-help guru who ran for president in 2020. Meanwhile, some of the president\u8217\'20\'19s supporters in the state have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65afcfda8f08541705644560#block-65afcfda8f08541705644560"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged Democrats to write in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name }}}\uc2  on their ballots.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In the final hours before polls opened, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  held a rally with supporters at a swanky new hotel in Salem, a suburb in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got a lot on the line here,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley told the crowd, which packed a chandeliered ballroom, and spilled into the lobby. Making her closing pitch, she told supporters:\par \par \uc2 If you go to the polls tomorrow \u8211\'20\'13 and take five people with you \u8211\'20\'13 and you commit to getting us back on track, I will spend every single day proving to you that you made a good decision.\par \par \uc2 In her remarks, Haley attempted to showcase the breadth of her appeal, pushing back on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s accusations that she\u8217\'20\'19s relying on moderates and liberals to boost her campaign.\par \par \uc2 Republican candidate \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  addresses a crowd of supporters in Salem, New Hampshire, on Monday. Photograph: Cj Gunther/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 She pointed into the crowd at \uc2 Don Bolduc\uc2 , a combat veteran who backed Haley after losing a Trump-endorsed bid for Senate in 2022 during which he claimed the 2020 election had been stolen. He later tried to reverse those claims in the general election, but it was seen as a factor in his loss to Democratic senator, \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s as conservative as they get,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley beamed. And then she pointed to the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2 , who has escorted her across the state for the last week. He\u8217\'20\'19s a \u8220\'20\'1Cmoderate\u8221\'20\'1D, she noted. Left unsaid was that he is one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s few prominent Republican critics.\par \par \uc2 Introducing Haley in Salem, Sununu reminded the crowd that since Trump was elected in 2016, Republicans had lost the House, Senate and the White House. He said New Hampshire Republicans had fared poorly too, with several of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies in the state losing their elections in the 2022 midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHey Donald Trump, where the F is the \u8216\'20\'18red wave,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CGive me a break.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Why Biden's name isn't on the New Hampshire primary ballot\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  might draw focus, a shadow presidential primary is taking place in New Hampshire, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  could stumble at the first hurdle of his bid to run for president again in 2024 following an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/17/democratic-primaries-2024-new-hampshire-south-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 internal Democratic party feud}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As a consequence of the party scrap, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name will not even appear on the ballot in the Granite state on Tuesday. While the president remains the favorite to win his party\u8217\'20\'19s overall nomination, his absence here has opened a window for \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2 , a Democratic congressman from Minnesota, and \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 , an author and self-help guru who ran for president in 2020, to mount longshot presidential bids.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks during a meeting in the State Dining Room of the White House on Monday. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 The unusual situation stems from the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to ditch decades of tradition this year in designating South Carolina, a much more racially diverse state, to host the first presidential primary. The decision outraged New Hampshire Democrats, who insisted they would not go along with the national party\u8217\'20\'19s plan to rob them of their \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst-in-the-nation\u8221\'20\'1D status. As a result, the New Hampshire Democratic party decided to hold its primary the same day as the Republican primary, in defiance of the DNC\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 The DNC has criticized the New Hampshire primary as a sham, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/01/08/nh-attorney-general-cease-and-desist-dnc-meaningless-election/72153273007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  on the state party to \u8220\'20\'1Ceducate the public\u8221\'20\'1D that the contest \u8220\'20\'1Cis a non-binding presidential preference event and is meaningless\u8221\'20\'1D. The New Hampshire attorney general, Republican John Formella, in turn sent a cease-and-desist letter to the DNC to compel the organization to stop making \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse, deceptive and misleading\u8221\'20\'1D claims about the primary.\par \par \uc2 Biden might be absent from the state, but a movement has emerged encouraging people to write his name on voting slips, and in a sign that the Biden campaign sees the potential for embarrassment, a series of high-profile Biden supporters have been dispatched to New Hampshire in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Voters are queueing up at polling places across New Hampshire this morning for the first-in-the nation primary.\par \par \uc2 Most polling sites in the state will close at 7pm ET, with results beginning to come shortly after that, but some will be open until 8pm.\par \par \uc2 Voters line up for the polls to open to cast their ballots in the New Hampshire Republican presidential primary in Manchester, New Hampshire. Photograph: David Goldman/AP Voters line up to cast their ballots in the New Hampshire primary at Pinkerton Academy in Derry, New Hampshire. Photograph: Brandon Bell/Getty Images Volunteers check voters identification at the St Anthony\u8217\'20\'19s Community Center during voting in the New Hampshire presidential primary election in Manchester, New Hampshire. Photograph: Mike Segar/Reuters Voters check in to vote at a polling location setup at Winnacunnet high school in Hampton, New Hampshire. Photograph: Joe Raedle/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  isn't backing down from challenging Biden\par \par \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2 , the long-shot Democratic challenger to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , has refused to back down from attacking the president as he vowed to stay in the race \u8220\'20\'1Cas long as it takes to get a head-to-head matchup with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota Democrat, in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EarlyStart/status/1749775768207360230"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview }}}\uc2  with CNN this morning, criticized his party for being \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely delusional\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that he has \u8220\'20\'1Ca conviction that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is going to lose\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m trying to shake it up,\u8221\'20\'1D Phillips said.\par \par \uc2 We need to. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is going to win. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is a fine man, but he\u8217\'20\'19s going to lose.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was joined by three of his former GOP primary rivals last night at his final rally before the New Hampshire primary.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , Tim Scott and \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  joined Trump onstage in Laconia, New Hampshire, where they briefly addressed the crowd to reiterate their support for the former president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a group of great people,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ll be seeing a lot of them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senator Tim Scott (2nd-R), \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  (L), \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  (2nd-R) and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  (R) at a campaign rally in the basement ballroom of The Margate Resort in Laconia, New Hampshire. Photograph: Chip Somodevilla/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The rally was interrupted several times by fossil fuel protesters, who shouted out \u8220\'20\'1Cblood on his hands\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Coil sellout\u8221\'20\'1D before being kicked off the resort where the event was held.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump widens lead over Haley in New Hampshire poll\par \par \uc2 A tracking poll released this morning shows \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has widened his lead over \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  in recent days, following the withdrawal of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  from the GOP race.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcboston.com/news/local/with-desantis-out-trump-widens-lead-over-haley-in-nh-new-tracking-poll-shows/3255217/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  poll}}}\uc2  by NBC News, the \uc2 Boston Globe\uc2  and \uc2 Suffolk University\uc2  shows Trump at 60% among likely Republican primary voters, compared with Haley at 38%.\par \par \uc2 The results also show that most of likely New Hampshire voters have already made up their minds about who they\u8217\'20\'19re voting for today. More than 89% said they are either \u8220\'20\'1Cnot at all likely\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cnot very likely\u8221\'20\'1D to change their minds.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some early risers in New Hampshire, already up and queueing to cast their votes today.\par \par \uc2 People line up to vote during the 2024 Republican presidential primary at Pinkerton Academy in Derry, New Hampshire. Photograph: Reba Saldanha/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The state Democratic party in New Hampshire is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-presidential-primary-joe-biden-dean-phillips-marianne-williamson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plowing ahead with a primary}}}\uc2 , even though the national party has said it will not honor the results. There is a sense that politicians, journalists and voters could be witnessing the end of an era.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNew Hampshire is a very white area with an average age that\u8217\'20\'19s a bit on the older side, so I do understand that it\u8217\'20\'19s maybe not the best group of voters to represent the entire country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jamie Setzler, 20, from New Boston, New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut from a selfish standpoint it is disappointing. I used to be able to look forward, every four years, to something interesting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This graphic shows how the demographics in New Hampshire compares to the rest of the US.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/01/archive-zip/giv-13425Y8A9sBreMN2I/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 The change to the calendar came after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who came fifth in the 2020 New Hampshire Democratic primary before reviving his campaign with a win in South Carolina, wrote to the DNC in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor decades, Black voters in particular have been the backbone of the Democratic party but have been pushed to the back of the early primary process,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe rely on these voters in elections but have not recognized their importance in our nominating calendar. It is time to stop taking these voters for granted, and time to give them a louder and earlier voice in the process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more from Adam Gabbatt in Manchester, New Hampshire here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primaries-elections-democrats-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19ve dug our heels in\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 is this the end of New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s election clout?}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primaries-elections-democrats-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19ve dug our heels in\u8217\'20\'19: is this the end of New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s election clout?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 One of the big questions today is if a big win for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will effectively end the race to be the Republican nominee. Over at CNN Eric Bradner and Gregory Krieg {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/01/23/politics/what-to-watch-new-hampshire-primary/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 write}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 If Trump wins, he would make history: In modern presidential campaign history \u8211\'20\'13 since the Iowa caucuses began serving as the official kickoff, followed by the New Hampshire primary \u8212\'20\'14 no non-incumbent Republican has won both states.\par \par \uc2 And in doing so, he would make it much tougher for Haley to convince donors to pour money into her campaign and voters to stick with her for the month until the South Carolina primary. She\u8217\'20\'19ll miss her only shot at another win before then because Haley filed to run in Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s state-run primary, instead of competing in the state GOP-run caucuses. Delegates are awarded through the Nevada caucuses.\par \par \uc2 Some in the party are already eager to see the nominating race reach its end eight days after it started.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden still expected to win Democratic primary despite not being on ballot\par \par \uc2 Even without a formal campaign presence in New Hampshire, and without Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name on the ballot paper, the US president is still expected to receive the most votes in the Democratic primary by a wide margin.\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emersoncollegepolling.com/new-hampshire-2024-poll-trump-leads-haley-in-primary-by-15-points/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emerson College/WHDH poll}}}\uc2  conducted last week showed Biden winning the support of 61% of likely Democratic primary voters, compared to 16% for Phillips and 5% for Williamson.\par \par \uc2 But a disappointing performance could point to decreased enthusiasm among the Democratic base, which would be a worrisome sign for Biden heading into the general election. Polls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already show}}}\uc2  Biden running neck and neck with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is widely expected to win the Republican presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 In an indication of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s potential vulnerabilities, some of the president\u8217\'20\'19s prominent allies, including congressman \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2  of California, have spent time campaigning on his behalf in New Hampshire. Speaking at a house party in support of the write-in campaign on Saturday, Khanna predicted a \u8220\'20\'1Cdecisive win\u8221\'20\'1D for Biden in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s going to propel him to have a big win in November,\u8221\'20\'1D Khanna said. \u8220\'20\'1CAt the end of the day, I am a believer that Americans love this country and love our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some voters, however, outraged over the war in Gaza, are expected to write in \u8220\'20\'1Cceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D to the ballot paper today to criticize US support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 We are a ways out from the 5 November election itself, but after today\u8217\'20\'19s primary in New Hampshire the election events start coming thick and fast until we reach Super Tuesday on 5 March. If you need it, here is a handy timeline of how the process unfolds throughout the year.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/12/us-elections-2024-calendar-key-events"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US elections 2024: a calendar of the key events}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Former US secretary of labor Robert Reich has written for the Guardian today, and is scathing about what he says is the way that the media are making a big deal of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s performance in the campaign so far:\par \par \uc2 Headline after headline offers the same breathless, spellbound story: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is dominating.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CDisciplined.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CRuthless.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CHugely effective.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CRemarkable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earth to the mainstream media: this is dangerous nonsense.\par \par \uc2 Why should Trump\u8217\'20\'19s dominance be surprising? He\u8217\'20\'19s dominated the Republican party since 2016. He dominates by ridiculing opponents, blasting anyone who stands in his way, bullying, browbeating, and bellowing. The media eats it up. He\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous and entertaining.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s success in last week\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa caucuses wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning show of strength\u8221\'20\'1D. It was a display of remarkable weakness. He got just 56,260 votes. There are 2,083,979 registered voters in Iowa. Fewer than 3% of Iowans voted for him.\par \par \uc2 The danger in the mainstream media\u8217\'20\'19s awestruck coverage of Trump right now \u8211\'20\'13 making a big deal out of his winning the Iowa caucuses, dominating the polls, pushing out all rivals except Haley, and almost surely winning today\u8217\'20\'19s New Hampshire primary \u8211\'20\'13 is that it creates a false impression that Trump is unstoppable, all the way through the general election.\par \par \uc2 But no one should confuse Trump\u8217\'20\'19s performance in the Republican primaries for success in the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Read more of this opinion piece here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/jan/23/trump-primaries-election-biden-robert-reich"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Reich \u8211\'20\'13 Yes, Trump is dominating the primaries. That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean he\u8217\'20\'19ll beat Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/jan/23/trump-primaries-election-biden-robert-reich"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Of course Trump is dominating the primaries. That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean he\u8217\'20\'19ll beat Biden | Robert Reich}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Mike Allen at Axios has this on why some Biden supporters are, perhaps unexpectedly, hoping for a big \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  win in New Hampshire today that knocks \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  out of the race. He writes:\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s backers see New Hampshire as a win-win: either Trump wins huge and a 286-day general election campaign begins tomorrow or Trump gets caught in a drawn-out primary until at least South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s contest on 24 February.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has internal data indicating that most of the undecided voters Biden is targeting don\u8217\'20\'19t think Trump will be the Republican nominee. They haven\u8217\'20\'19t tuned in to an election that\u8217\'20\'19s more than nine months away.\par \par \uc2 That leads Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team to believe the dynamics of the campaign will change significantly once those voters realize it really will be a Biden-Trump matchup in November.\par \par \uc2 Allen does point out one trend in recent polling data though that could prove a worry to the president:\par \par \uc2 A USA Today/Suffolk university poll found 44% of Republican primary voters were \u8220\'20\'1Cvery enthusiastic\u8221\'20\'1D about Trump. Only 18% of Democratic primary voters said the same about Biden.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Most places in New Hampshire \u8211\'20\'13 if they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-live-donald-trump-nikki-haley-republican-vote?page=with:block-65af865f8f081fd80444fbd9#block-65af865f8f081fd80444fbd9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aren\u8217\'20\'19t called Dixville Notch}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 will open their polls at 7am EST (noon GMT), although a few places will open an hour earlier than that. Most polls will close at 7pm EST (midnight GMT), and the results in the Republican primary will probably get called about an hour after that.\par \par \uc2 There will be 24 names on the Republican ballot paper, which obviously has to be printed well ahead of the election, and so doesn\u8217\'20\'19t take into account the fact that a lot of the candidates have already pulled out of the campaign.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats have 21 names to choose from on their ballots, but not \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . As my colleague Adam Gabbatt explained:\par \par \uc2 The unusual situation stems from the Democratic national committee\u8217\'20\'19s decision to ditch decades of tradition this year in choosing South Carolina, a much more racially diverse state, to host the first presidential primary. When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Hampshire}}}\uc2  said it would host its primary first anyway \u8211\'20\'13 South Carolina will vote next week \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  essentially said it would ignore the state\u8217\'20\'19s results.\par \par \uc2 This may, however, end up delaying the results of the vote in New Hampshire. Some Biden supporters have been encouraging voters to write in his name on the ballot, which will complicate the counting.\par \par \uc2 The move hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been universally popular. CBS News reports that yesterday New Hampshire Democratic Sen \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2  told reporters:\par \par \uc2 The DNC made a terrible decision not to have New Hampshire go first. We care about our country in New Hampshire. We care about democracy in New Hampshire. And we know what the stakes are here. We know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is going to be the Republican nominee. And we know the threat that that poses to our democracy.\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire is so wedded to being the first primary in an election campaign that in 1975 the state passed a law requiring its primary date to be set not by the parties themselves, but by the secretary of state. The law also requires the vote to take place seven days or more ahead of any other.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Haley: this vote is 'not a coronation' for Trump\par \par \uc2 Campaigning last night, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  insisted that today\u8217\'20\'19s vote was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a coronation\u8221\'20\'1D for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the Republican nominee.\par \par \uc2 Interviewed by Leland Vittert, Haley said viewing her performance in New Hampshire as make or break for her campaign had never been fair. She told him:\par \par \uc2 It has never been fair. I said I needed to be strong in Iowa. We started at 2%. We ended at 20%. I need to be stronger in New Hampshire. I think we\u8217\'20\'19ll do that tomorrow. And then I need to be stronger than that in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 The one thing we have to remember is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  only won with one and a half percent of the vote in Iowa, 56,000 people voted for him out of a state of three million people. That is not representative of the country.\par \par \uc2 And you\u8217\'20\'19ve got the political class saying, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, it\u8217\'20\'19s got to be him. No. This is not a coronation. This is an election.\par \par \uc2 You go state by state. You are trying to get representation of real normal people. And that is what we are focused on. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to take it one step at a time.\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina primary, in Haley\u8217\'20\'19s home state, is scheduled for 24 February.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Two New Hampshire polls released in the lasat couple of days didn\u8217\'20\'19t carry as much encouragement for \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  as she might have hoped, although with Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  ending his presidential campaign at the last minute, there may be some wriggle room in the numbers.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday NBC News, the \uc2 Boston Globe\uc2  and \uc2 Suffolk University\uc2  put \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  19 points clear of Haley, at 55% to 36% support. On Monday, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  and \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2  put Trump at 52% support in New Hampshire, to 34% for Haley.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 If you fancy something audio to set the scene, then today\u8217\'20\'19s episode of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/series/todayinfocus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Today in Focus}}}\uc2  is about the New Hampshire primary and the 2024 US election race.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Washington bureau chief, \uc2 David Smith\uc2 , speaks to Michael Safi, and explains how New Hampshire could deliver a win that helps \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  seal up the votes he needs for the nomination before his numerous court appearances can seriously dent his candidacy.\par \par \uc2 You can listen to it here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-the-last-chance-to-stop-trump-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Today in Focus \u8211\'20\'13 New Hampshire primary: the last chance to stop Trump?}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-primary-the-last-chance-to-stop-trump-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Hampshire primary: the last chance to stop Trump? - podcast}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  wins all six votes in small New Hampshire town\par \par \uc2 Voting has actually begun in New Hampshire, because Dixville Notch traditionally opens its polls at midnight and declares the result as quickly as possible afterwards. It is a tiny electorate \u8211\'20\'13 just six people voted. They all went for \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/23/us/politics/dixville-notch-new-hampshire-haley-2024.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notes}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe event is as much a press spectacle as it is a serious exercise in democracy\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere were more than ten journalists for every voter, including representatives from major TV networks, newspapers, wire services and foreign press from over a dozen countries.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cory Pesaturo plays the national anthem on accordion to start voting after midnight on the day of the US presidential primary election in Dixville Notch, New Hampshire. Photograph: Faith Ninivaggi/Reuters\par \par \uc2 78-year-old Tom Tillotson told the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CThe real message here is \u8216\'20\'18get off your butts, get out there and vote.\u8217\'20\'19 Everybody. Republicans and Democrats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And no election is complete without pictures of dogs taking part in the democratic process, and thankfully Dixville Notch delivered on that score already.\par \par \uc2 A dog with an American flag tie walks in the room before the First-in-the-Nation midnight vote for the New Hampshire primary elections in Dixville Notch. Photograph: S\u233\'00\'E9bastien St-Jean/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley chases an upset in bitter New Hampshire face-off with Trump\par \par \uc2 Lauren Gambino is in Manchester, New Hampshire for the Guardian\par \par \uc2 Republicans are predicting record turnout \u8211\'20\'13 and good weather, seen as a possible boon to Nikki Haley who is relying more heavily on voters who don\u8217\'20\'19t typically participate in the party\u8217\'20\'19s primary.\par \par \uc2 The stakes could not be higher for Haley. She is barnstorming the state, from the \u8220\'20\'1Csuburbs to the seacoast\u8221\'20\'1D, trying to persuade anti-Trump independents and open-minded conservatives to back her long-shot bid.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump by contrast has been in and out of the state, holding raucous evening rallies between appearances in court. New Hampshire propelled Trump to the Republican nomination in 2016 after he came in second in the Iowa caucuses. This year, Trump hopes to notch a victory large enough to effectively extinguish Haley\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 For much of her nearly year-long campaign, Haley carefully avoided Trump, instead drawing implicit contrasts with calls for a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew generation\u8221\'20\'1D of leaders in Washington and a proposal to instate cognitive tests for older politicians. But in the final days before New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s primary, she went after him more aggressively, questioning his mental fitness and accusing him of cozying up to dictators and autocrats.\par \par \uc2 Trump responded with insults and misrepresentations while accusing her campaign of relying on the support of \u8220\'20\'1Cglobalists\u8221\'20\'1D and liberals to win. In an ugly series of social media posts, he revived the birtherism conspiracy that she was ineligible to be president because her parents were not US citizens when she was born. This is false; Haley, the South Carolina-born daughter of immigrants from India, is eligible. Trump also appeared to mock her Indian ancestry by referring to \u8211\'20\'13 and mispelling \u8211\'20\'13 her given name, Nimarata. Haley has always gone by her middle name, Nikki.\par \par \uc2 Haley and her allies insist she has a path forward even if she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t pull off an upset. Improving on her third-place finish in Iowa would be enough. But if she can\u8217\'20\'19t win in New Hampshire, with an electorate seen as far more friendly to her brand of Republicanism, analysts said it will be hard to make the pitch to voters \u8211\'20\'13 and donors \u8211\'20\'13 that she can win anywhere else.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Lauren Gambino\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-presidential-primary-nikki-haley-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley chases an upset in bitter New Hampshire face-off with Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-presidential-primary-nikki-haley-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley chases an upset in bitter New Hampshire face-off with Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Welcome and opening summary \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our live US politics coverage on a milestone day in the race for the 2024 US presidential election, with the opening day of the primary season. Here are the headlines \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire will hold its first-in-the nation primary in what may be the last chance Republicans have to stop Donald Trump from running away with the nomination, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-presidential-primary-nikki-haley-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-presidential-primary-nikki-haley-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  chases an upset}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Just over a week after the former president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/16/donald-trump-iowa-caucus-victory-new-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record-setting victory in the Iowa caucuses}}}\uc2 , he is now locked in an increasingly bitter showdown with Haley, who has staked her candidacy on a strong showing in the more moderate New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump leads by double-digit margins but is considered more vulnerable in the state, where independent voters make up nearly 40% of the electorate and can choose to vote in either party\u8217\'20\'19s primary.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A shadow presidential primary is also taking place. Dean Phillips, a Democratic congressman from Minnesota, and Marianne Williamson, an author and self-help guru who ran for president in 2020, are mounting longshot presidential bids. Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s name {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-presidential-primary-joe-biden-dean-phillips-marianne-williamson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won\u8217\'20\'19t feature on the ballot paper}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The primary comes with the background noise of intervention against Yemen\u8217\'20\'19s Houthis in the Red Sea rumbling on. The US has carried out its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/22/us-uk-continue-strike-houthi-yemen-military-biden-sunak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eighth round of airstrikes}}}\uc2 . A Pentagon statement said the bombing was \u8220\'20\'1Cproportionate and necessary\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 I am Martin Belam, and I will be with you for the next few hours. You can contact me at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:martin.belam@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 martin.belam@theguardian.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240123ek1n0018w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
