\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris attacks Trump over Roe v Wade at first campaign rally with Biden\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 742 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2024\par 00:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president appeared Tuesday in Virginia with president, who warned \u8216\'20\'18Maga Republicans \u8230\'20\'26 are hellbent on going even further\u8217\'20\'19New Hampshire primary \u8211\'20\'13 live updatesFollow our live results tracker\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  kicked off their first joint campaign rally of 2024 in Manassas, Virginia, on Tuesday, with a focused plea for voters to send them back to the White House on one key issue: protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 This fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said, is about freedom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CExtremists have proposed and passed laws that criminalized doctors and punished women. Laws that make no exception even for rape or incest,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris, who spoke first, before the US president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd let us all agree: one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government should not be telling her what to do with her body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Virginia was a telling first stop for the 2024 campaign, where Biden and Harris were accompanied by first lady, Jill Biden, and the second gentleman Doug Emhoff. Last year, during the state\u8217\'20\'19s elections, Virginia Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/virginia-election-voting-results-house-delegates-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to take control}}}\uc2  of the state legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/20/democrats-virginia-abortion-strategy-roe-v-wade-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after campaigning}}}\uc2  on a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Seven other states have also voted directly on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot referendums since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-cour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe fell}}}\uc2  at the hand of the right-leaning \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in 2022; in each case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including in}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 red states}}}\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters won.\par \par \uc2 Now, Biden and Harris are betting that outrage over the decision to overturn Roe \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the result of}}}\uc2  the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization case out of Mississippi \u8211\'20\'13 will send them back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think this court and the Maga Republicans have any clue about the power of women in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told the crowd, referring to the loyal base of supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his Make America Great Again election slogan. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think they have any clue. But they\u8217\'20\'19re about to find out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stories of women who say they were denied medically necessary abortions have been particularly powerful in sustaining post-Roe outrage. One of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/20/texas-women-pregnancy-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 those women}}}\uc2 , Amanda Zurawski, took the stage to introduce Biden. Zurawski is the lead plaintiff in a lawsuit in Texas that now involves dozens of women who say the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban blocked them from getting abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I went through was nothing short of barbaric,\u8221\'20\'1D Zurawski told the crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it didn\u8217\'20\'19t need to happen. But it did, because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Over and over again, \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/donald-trump-abortion-election-republicans-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brags about}}}\uc2  killing Roe v Wade. It is unthinkable to me that anyone could cheer on these \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that nearly took my life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although the Republican primary was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/23/new-hampshire-presidential-primary-nikki-haley-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still unfolding}}}\uc2  in New Hampshire on Tuesday, Trump was the clear and repeated target of the rally, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/16/donald-trump-iowa-caucus-victory-new-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the frontrunner}}}\uc2  for the Republican nomination. Trump appointed three of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices who overturned Roe. While he was first running for president in 2016, he also suggested that women who get abortions should be punished in some way \u8211\'20\'13 a stance that he later walked back, but was repeatedly mentioned at Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Maga Republicans, including the speaker of the House, are hellbent on going even further,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said , referring to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/22/speaker-mike-johnson-holocaust-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hard-right}}}\uc2  Republican speaker, Mike Johnson. He added: \u8220\'20\'1CAs long as I have power of the presidency, if Congress were to pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, I would veto it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Further \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are not the only threats on the table, Biden said. Because the Roe decision descends from a line of supreme court decisions that protect the right to privacy, overturning that decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/clarence-thomas-roe-gay-marriage-contraception-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also threatens}}}\uc2  access to birth control and same-sex marriage. He promised to codify the protections of Roe into law, as he has said in the past.\par \par \uc2 However, that promise is unlikely to come true anytime soon, given that Congress has shown little interest in moving substantively forward on bills that would enshrine similar protections as those that were in Roe.\par \par \uc2 Protesters interrupted Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech eight times. One man, who was carrying a Palestinian flag, shouted: \u8220\'20\'1CHow many kids have you killed?\u8221\'20\'1D A woman later interrupted Biden by shouting: \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael kills two mothers every hour.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They were escorted out of the crowd. During each interruption, the crowd behind the speakers started to chant \u8220\'20\'1CFour more years!\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s go, Joe!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240124ek1n00005\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
