\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Democrats condemn \u8216\'20\'18cruel\u8217\'20\'19  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans ahead of 51st anniversary of Roe\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 868 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 January 2024\par 16:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Extreme\u8217\'20\'19 Republican-backed bans have caused untold \u8216\'20\'18suffering\u8217\'20\'19 for women, senators say, and vow to restore federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats underscored their commitment to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yGnc8JkaUII"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press conference on Wednesday}}}\uc2 , ahead of the 51st anniversary of Roe v Wade. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now-overturned supreme court case}}}\uc2  provided American women with a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for nearly 50 years.\par \par \uc2 Experts at the briefing described {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican-backed \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2  across the country as \u8220\'20\'1Ccruel\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme\u8221\'20\'1D and causing untold \u8220\'20\'1Csuffering\u8221\'20\'1D for American women, thousands of whom are forced to travel across state lines for abortions or be forced to remain pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenate Democrats will not let anyone turn away from the devastation Republicans have caused,\u8221\'20\'1D said Senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , a Washington state Democrat. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we will not stop pushing to restore the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The briefing comes at the start of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 presidential election}}}\uc2  cycle, in which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are expected to be a defining issue. Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , called the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pro-life president\u8221\'20\'1D by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists and national organizations alike, has already won the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/16/iowa-caucuses-key-takeaways-trump-desantis-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa Republican caucuses handily}}}\uc2 , and is widely expected to become the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee.\par \par \uc2 Trump nominated and the Senate confirmed three right-leaning supreme court justices, all of whom voted to overturn Roe v Wade in the case that now governs federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Even so, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws have become a politically poisonous issue for Republicans. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have won at the ballot box again and again, as in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/28/abortion-rights-michigan-roe-wade-ballot-initiative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas}}}\uc2 . Polls show {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/506759/broader-support-abortion-rights-continues-post-dobbs.aspx#:~:text=Trend%20from%201995%20to%202022,rising%20to%2055%25%20in%202022."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more Americans than ever}}}\uc2  support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Even Republicans in the House, where caucus members have repeatedly signed on to federal legislation that would amount to a total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, are now backing away from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/12/us/politics/house-republicans-abortion-ban.html#:~:text=Still%2C%20even%20with%20the%20retreat,the%20national%20abortion%20ban%20bill."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  messaging bills}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe anniversary of Roe v Wade should be a joyous day for our country, a day when the supreme court decided to value a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to privacy and autonomy,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Democratic Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2022, tragically, alarmingly and outrageously they succeeded when a hard-right majority voted to overturn Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the anniversary of Roe, the briefing also comes ahead of the March for Life, the largest gathering of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists of the year. Before the Dobbs decision, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/jan/24/march-for-life-anti-abortion-rally-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marched in protest of Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 . Today, activists strategize about further \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans \u8211\'20\'13 including a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/pence-calls-for-2024-gop-candidates-to-back-a-15-week-federal-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal 15-week ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dr Austin Dennard is an obstetrician and gynecologist who said she was forced to \u8220\'20\'1Cflee\u8221\'20\'1D her state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after her fetus was diagnosed with anencephaly, a severe and fatal condition where a fetus develops without parts of the brain or skull.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to flee the state,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy state\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 she is a sixth-generation Texan \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere I practice medicine, where I\u8217\'20\'19m raising my family,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dennard. \u8220\'20\'1CThen my doctor gave me a hug. \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m so sorry,\u8217\'20\'19 was all she was able to say.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2023/08/21/1194482842/texas-pregnant-doctor-abortion-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dennard was forced to travel east}}}\uc2 , but said she was afraid to use credit cards or tell people where she was going for fear she would be criminally prosecuted under Texas\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was absolutely humiliating and I felt physically and emotionally broken,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dennard.\par \par \uc2 Dr Serina Floyd, an OB-GYN in Washington DC and the chief medical officer of Planned Parenthood of Metropolitan Washington DC, Inc, said only last week she provided an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a woman, who she referred to under the pseudonym \u8220\'20\'1CNina\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Nina traveled by bus from North Carolina, where a 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban recently went into effect. She missed her first bus, was able to board a second but arrived too late for her scheduled appointment. Nina was rescheduled for the next day. When Floyd asked Nina where she would stay the night, Nina said she had found a homeless shelter 15 minutes from the clinic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNina had no money \u8211\'20\'13 not for a hotel, not for food, not for nothing. All she had was a bus ticket home,\u8221\'20\'1D said Floyd.\par \par \uc2 Another expert, feminist and columnist Jessica Valenti, said she regularly documented \u8220\'20\'1Csuffering\u8221\'20\'1D, and received more messages from women than she could ever respond to.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Republicans feign surprise or compassion over post-Roe horror stories \u8211\'20\'13 they are lying,\u8221\'20\'1D said Valenti. She said she has documented a \u8220\'20\'1Cquiet campaign\u8221\'20\'1D by national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jessica.substack.com/p/calculated-cruelty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 undermine prenatal testing}}}\uc2  that reveals fetal abnormalities and to sow doubt about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2022/11/bill-dean-ohio-maternal-mortality-rate-obese-people"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accuracy of maternal mortality numbers}}}\uc2  (the US has among the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonwealthfund.org/blog/2022/us-maternal-mortality-crisis-continues-worsen-international-comparison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worst in the developed world}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe question I get asked most often is, \u8216\'20\'18Why?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Valenti. Republicans, she said, are trying to enforce, \u8220\'20\'1Ca world view that it is women\u8217\'20\'19s job to be pregnant and stay pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 no matter the cost or consequence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 22 January 2024 to correct the title of Dr Serina Floyd. An earlier version said she is the chief medical officer of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 . To clarify: she holds that role for the organization\u8217\'20\'19s local affiliate of Metropolitan Washington DC, Inc.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240117ek1h00336\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
