\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Biden  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ad marks campaign shift to emphasize reproductive rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore \par \uc2 611 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 January 2024\par 21:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Campaign ad, titled Forced, is designed to tie \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  directly to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue\par \par \uc2 The Biden re-election campaign rolled out a new campaign ad on Sunday, signaling a shift in emphasis to reproductive rights that the White House hopes will carry and define Democrats through the 2024 election cycle.\par \par \uc2 The campaign ad, titled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/vrtvE4bSwKY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Forced }}}\uc2 , is designed to tie \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  directly to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue almost 18 months after his nominees to the supreme court helped to overturn a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  enshrined in Roe v Wade, which would have turned 51 this week.\par \par \uc2 Dr Austin Dennard, a Texas OB-GYN and mother of three tells the camera her story about traveling out of her state to terminate her pregnancy after learning her fetus had a fatal condition, calling her situation \u8220\'20\'1Cevery woman\u8217\'20\'19s worst nightmare\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In Texas, she said, her choice \u8220\'20\'1Cwas completely taken away and that\u8217\'20\'19s because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  overturning Roe v Wade\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The launch of the ad comes as anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists descended on Washington DC this weekend. One event, the National Pro-Life Summit, activists came to celebrate anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activism in the US. At another, the March for Life, marchers called for advocacy against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is now being placed to the forefront of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s messaging on reproductive rights, a position Biden has said he is not \u8220\'20\'1Cbig on\u8221\'20\'1D because of his Catholic faith, though he believes the landmark 1973 decision \u8220\'20\'1Cgot it right\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Harris will embark on a nationwide tour to focus attention on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to protect the right of women to choose. Her tour will start in Wisconsin, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights propelled a Democratic victory in a key state supreme court election.\par \par \uc2 A statement from Harris\u8217\'20\'19s office said the vice-president will \u8220\'20\'1Chighlight the harm caused by extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and share stories of those who have been impacted in Wisconsin and across the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe will also hold extremists accountable for proposing a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, call on Congress to restore the protections of Roe, and outline steps the Administration is taking to protect access to health care,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement added.\par \par \uc2 Democrats this year are hoping to emphasize that a second Trump presidency would establish new personal health restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the reason that more than 1 in 3 American women of reproductive age don\u8217\'20\'19t have the freedom to make their own health care decisions. Now, he and MAGA Republicans are running to go even further if they retake the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D Julie Chavez Rodriguez, Biden-Harris 2024 campaign manager, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/4418543-harris-takes-center-stage-in-2024-abortion-fight/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement to The Hill. }}}\uc2  is the reason that more than 1 in 3 American women of reproductive age don\u8217\'20\'19t have the freedom to make their own health care decisions. Now, he and MAGA Republicans are running to go even further if they retake the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D Julie Chavez Rodriguez, Biden-Harris 2024 campaign manager,\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, the Michigan governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  , told \uc2 CBS\uc2  Face the Nation that \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be good\u8221\'20\'1D if Biden talked about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than he does. \u8220\'20\'1CI know that one tenet of his belief system is that women and only women with their families and healthcare professionals are the one who know what decision is right for them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if the president needs to take up that message more forcefully, Whitmer said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it would hurt. I think people want to know that this is president that is fighting \u8230\'20\'26 but maybe to use more blunt language would be helpful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240121ek1l001pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
