\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  kicks off  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights tour on 51st anniversary of Roe v Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 Erum Salam \par \uc2 638 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 January 2024\par 22:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president is expected to announce support for more access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as she begins tour in battleground state of Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  kicked off her much-vaunted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide tour in Wisconsin on Monday as Joe Biden convened a meeting of his taskforce on reproductive healthcare access, in a tag-team effort to double down on what is likely to be a key campaign issue this year.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president chose the 51st anniversary of the Roe v Wade ruling to begin the Reproductive Freedoms Tour, announced in December, in the battleground state of Wisconsin, which the president won in the 2020 presidential election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/general-news-7aef88488e4a801545a13cf4319591b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by just over 20,000 votes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade, the supreme court decision that enshrined the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned}}}\uc2  in June 2022 after the then president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  nominated three conservative justices to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court.\par \par \uc2 The decision was a major blow to supporters of reproductive rights, but since the ruling seven states \u8211\'20\'13 including the conservative strongholds of Kentucky, Kansas and Montana \u8211\'20\'13 have held ballot referendums where voters chose to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The issue also appeared to hurt Republicans in the 2022 midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin is a notable starting point for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive freedoms tour. Last year, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights propelled a Democratic victory in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 critical election}}}\uc2  for the state supreme court.\par \par \uc2 In the first of many similar scheduled events, Harris is expected to announce support for increased access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraceptives through the new emergency care law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/09/emergency-abortion-supreme-court-case-emtala-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act}}}\uc2  (Emtala).\par \par \uc2 She will also denounce Trump, the runaway frontrunner for the Republican presidential nomination, for his hand in overturning the federally protected right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProud that women across our nation are suffering?\u8221\'20\'1D Harris will say, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/kamala-harris-abortion-biden-2024-election-560bc2bbdf036c18b6601ced44a62b50"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 excerpts}}}\uc2  from her speech obtained by the Associated Press. \u8220\'20\'1CProud that women have been robbed of a fundamental freedom? That doctors could be thrown in prison for caring for patients? That young women today have fewer rights than their mothers and grandmothers?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The following day, Harris will be joined by Biden for another \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -focused event, along with their spouses, Jill Biden and Doug Emhoff.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/21/biden-abortion-ad-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rolled out a new campaign ad}}}\uc2  on Sunday, titled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/vrtvE4bSwKY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Forced}}}\uc2 , which aims to tie \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  directly to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue.\par \par \uc2 In Dobbs v Jackson, the 2022 supreme court case that overturned Roe, a Mississippi law that banned most abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy with certain medical exceptions was upheld, negating the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and overruling the precedent set by Roe more than half a century ago.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/01/22/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-the-51st-anniversary-of-roe-v-wade/#:~:text=Then%2C%20a%20year%20and%20a,and%20lives%20are%20at%20risk."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on the 51st anniversary of Roe v Wade, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CFifty-one years ago today, the supreme court recognized a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to make deeply personal decisions with her doctor \u8211\'20\'13 free from the interference of politicians. Then, a year and a half ago, the court made the extreme decision to overturn Roe and take away a constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result, tens of millions of women now live in states with extreme and dangerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Because of Republican elected officials, women\u8217\'20\'19s health and lives are at risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/12/19/vice-president-kamala-harris-launches-reproductive-freedoms-tour/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcing}}}\uc2  her tour in December, Harris said: \u8220\'20\'1CExtremists across our country continue to wage a full-on attack against hard-won, hard-fought freedoms as they push their radical policies \u8211\'20\'13 from banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all 50 states and criminalizing doctors, to forcing women to travel out of state in order to get the care they need.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will continue to fight for our fundamental freedoms while bringing together those throughout America who agree that every woman should have the right to make decisions about her own body \u8211\'20\'13 not the government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240122ek1m003bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
