\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden campaign calls for investigation of New Hampshire robocalls impersonating US president \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Manchester, New Hampshire (now) and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 5,517 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 January 2024\par 21:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our full report here:Democrats sound alarm over AI robocall to voters mimicking Biden\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  made the most of the hours remaining before tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s primary in New Hampshire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae9f978f0835e980a416ba#block-65ae9f978f0835e980a416ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crisscrossing the Granite state}}}\uc2  alongside governor \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2  in a bid to lure votes away from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae96e18f08b5ba94ebfae4#block-65ae96e18f08b5ba94ebfae4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls continue to show}}}\uc2  the former president with a big lead, underscoring the difficulty Haley will have in overcoming his status as the frontrunner for the Republican presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected in New Hampshire later today, after appearing this morning in a New York City courtroom for a hearing in author E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s defamation lawsuit against him, where he was set to testify. The session {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae89c88f0819b86aadad5e#block-65ae89c88f0819b86aadad5e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was unexpectedly adjourned}}}\uc2  after a juror felt ill, and one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers was exposed to Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65aeccd68f081fd80444f660#block-65aeccd68f081fd80444f660"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assailed}}}\uc2  Trump for his role in overturning Roe v Wade on the 51st anniversary of the supreme court decision that allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  has avoided talking much about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though she has signalled she would be fine with restricting the procedure federally. Some voters who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65aed5be8f0835e980a41940#block-65aed5be8f0835e980a41940"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fine with that}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Judge Judy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae93548f08b5ba94ebfac6#block-65ae93548f08b5ba94ebfac6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delivered her verdict}}}\uc2  on the presidential race by stumping for Haley in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , who is seen as potential running mate for Trump, said the adjournment of his defamation trial was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae9d2d8f0805c8927543f3#block-65ae9d2d8f0805c8927543f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cblatant election interference\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . In reality, it was requested by the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Someone is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae81168f08fb2972a012e9#block-65ae81168f08fb2972a012e9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 making robocalls}}}\uc2  to New Hampshire voters that sound like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and encourage them not to vote in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65aec7c18f0835e980a418be#block-65aec7c18f0835e980a418be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prompting}}}\uc2  the president\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign to call for an investigation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As she blitzes the state, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  talks about keeping taxes low, the military strong and the border secure. One issue she does not mention: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On the 51st anniversary of Roe v Wade, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Democrats across the country are railing against Republicans, calling them \u8220\'20\'1Canti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists\u8221\'20\'1D who would impose a federal ban on the procedure if they win back power this fall.\par \par \uc2 Haley calls herself \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D but has promised to seek consensus as president. In Iowa, where evangelical Christians dominate the caucuses, Haley signaled her willingness, if elected, to sign any restrictions that reached her desk.\par \par \uc2 But in comparatively moderate New Hampshire, she has mostly shut down inquiries about what kind of federal limit she would support, insisting that any legislation is purely theoretical without 60 votes in the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 as she told one curious onlooker at a stop in Epping on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Across the state, several pro-choice independent voters said the risk of a Trump presidency worried them more than Haley\u8217\'20\'19s views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve long ago accepted that I can\u8217\'20\'19t agree with a candidate on everything,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carole Alfano, an independent who met Haley at the campaign stop in the town of Epping. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll part ways on that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alfano backed Biden in 2020, but plans to support Haley in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary.\par \par \uc2 In Derry, Marie Mulroy is ecstatic about the prospect of a Haley nomination even though she believes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should remain legal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll agree to disagree on that,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Can \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  pull a shock win in New Hampshire out of the bag?\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s the last candidate standing against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , after Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  exited the race and endorsed the former president on Sunday. Host of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Politics Weekly America podcast Jonathan Freedland headed out on the campaign trail in the Granite state to find out the answer:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign marked Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19s 51st anniversary by debuting an advertisement in which Texas obstetrician-gynecologist Austin Dennard discusses how she had to leave the state to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after finding out that her fetus would not survive.\par \par \uc2 Who\u8217\'20\'19s to blame? \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , as Dennard makes clear. Expect to see tons of this sort of messaging coming from the campaigns of the president and other Democrats over the coming months:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'How dare he?': Harris attacks Trump on Roe v Wade anniversary\par \par \uc2 On the 51st anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Roe v Wade decision, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  attacked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his role in appointing justices who overturned the precedent and allowed states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The vice-president spoke during a visit today to Wisconsin, a battleground state that will be crucial to deciding the outcome of the November election. Democrats plan to campaign on restoring access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the 2022 decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization that curtailed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in many states.\par \par \uc2 Harris did not hold back from assailing the former president, citing his comments that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D of his role in getting three justices confirmed to the court, all of whom voted to overturn Roe. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what she had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltrVP Harris on Trump saying he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D for his role in ending Roe:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProud that women across our nation are suffering? Proud that women have been robbed of a fundamental freedom? Proud that... young women today have fewer rights than their mothers and grandmothers? How dare he?\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LvmpYYkIdo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LvmpYYkIdo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1749514279240561046?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign calls for investigation of New Hampshire robocalls impersonating president\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign has called on New Hampshire authorities to investigate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae81168f08fb2972a012e9#block-65ae81168f08fb2972a012e9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a spate of robocalls}}}\uc2  to voters in which a voice that sounds like the president encourages them not to participate in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name is not appearing on the primary ballot, since Democrats have decided to hold their first nominating contest in South Carolina next month. But some in the party are encouraging their voters to write in the president\u8217\'20\'19s name, both as a show of support and to pressure the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  to give New Hampshire, which has historically been the second state to vote, a more prominent role in the nominating process.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Biden-Harris campaign manager Julie Chavez Rodriguez said:\par \par \uc2 This matter has already been referred to the New Hampshire Attorney General, and the campaign is actively discussing additional actions to take immediately. Spreading disinformation to suppress voting and deliberately undermine free and fair elections will not stand, and fighting back against any attempt to undermine our democracy will continue to be a top priority for this campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 David Scanlan, the New Hampshire secretary of state, predicted Republican voter participation in the primaries will reach 322,000, eclipsing 2016\u8217\'20\'19s total, when Republicans set a record of 287,652 votes.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, it was Democrats who saw record turnout for their competitive primary, with 300,368 votes cast.\par \par \uc2 Before a deadline in October, as many as 4,000 registered Democrats changed their party affiliation to \u8220\'20\'1Cundeclared,\u8221\'20\'1D suggesting some plan to vote in the Republican primary.\par \par \uc2 A Monmouth University Poll-Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/01/22/trump-leads-new-hampshire-post-monmouth-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll released today}}}\uc2  found that the number of registered New Hampshire independents who plan to vote in the Republican primary increased from 52% in November to 63%.\par \par \uc2 More than a third of these voters said they voted for Biden in 2020, suggesting there could be a \u8220\'20\'1Cmeasurable influx of Democratic-leaning independents\u8221\'20\'1D who will participate in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a conversation on Friday, Fergus Cullen, a former New Hampshire GOP chairman and prominent Trump opponent, said he did not see evidence that Haley had \u8220\'20\'1Clit a spark\u8221\'20\'1D among these voters in the way that might foretell \u8220\'20\'1Csome kind of surge coming her way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople turn out when they are inspired, or they\u8217\'20\'19re pissed off,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cullen, who had seen Haley on the campaign trail four times. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing is that people are not inspired, and they\u8217\'20\'19re apathetic. And that means that they don\u8217\'20\'19t show up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state David Scanlan is predicting record turnout in the Republican primary, while governor \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2  is joking that he is cashing in all of his political capital to ensure balmy weather for voters headed to the polls on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 That would be a stark contrast from Iowa, where arctic temperatures were blamed for the low turnout last week.\par \par \uc2 Recent polling has shown Trump with a double digit lead in the state. But New Hampshire has a record of unpredictability, thanks to the large number of voters who proudly belong to neither party. They are not a monolith, but analysts believe that the more of them who choose to vote in the Republican primary, the better for Haley.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only big X factor I see: how big is turnout?\u8221\'20\'1D said Dante Scala, a professor of Political Science and International Affairs at the \uc2 University of New Hampshire\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to Scala, Haley is attempting something novel in New Hampshire. Republican presidential candidates who have pulled off wins in New Hampshire \u8211\'20\'13 such as \uc2 John McCain\uc2  in 2008 and \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  in 2012 \u8211\'20\'13 managed to appeal to the state\u8217\'20\'19s independents while still pulling in a sizable chunk of the party faithful. (Independents, called \u8220\'20\'1Cundeclared\u8221\'20\'1D voters in New Hampshire, can vote in either party\u8217\'20\'19s primary.)\par \par \uc2 This year, Trump has a lock on Republican base voters. To win, or even to come within striking distance of Trump, Scala said Haley will need to run up the score with these independent voters, some of whom could choose to vote in the sleepy Democratic primary or not at all if they feel the contest is a foregone conclusion.\par \par \uc2 Scala said Haley\u8217\'20\'19s test is whether she \u8220\'20\'1Cinspired enough people to show up, who don\u8217\'20\'19t normally show up, to get a turnout big enough that it swamps the Trump people and your mainstream Republican in New Hampshire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke to UK prime minister Rishi Sunak on Monday about Gaza, Ukraine, and the Houthi attacks in the Red Sea, White House spokesperson John Kirby said, AFP reported.\par \par \uc2 From White House correspondent for AFP Danny Kemp:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden just spoke on the phone with British PM Rishi Sunak on Red Sea, Gaza and Ukraine, White House's John Kirby. UK and US have both struck Houthi sites in past days\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Danny Kemp (@dannyctkemp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dannyctkemp/status/1749499040188842070?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrKirby confirms Biden's Middle East advisor \uc2 Brett McGurk\uc2  is in the region for fresh talks, after reports he's there to discuss hostages and future Gaza plans with Egypt, Qatar and others\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Danny Kemp (@dannyctkemp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dannyctkemp/status/1749503333654540382?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judy Sheindlin, widely known as Judge Judy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/DanaBashCNN/status/1749493842372333884?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  on Monday that she would endorse \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  if she \u8220\'20\'1Cwere a frog\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During the interview with CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Bash, Judge Judy was asked if the reason she endorsed Haley was because Haley is a woman.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo, I would support her if she were a frog,\u8221\'20\'1D said the ever-colorful Sheindlin .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s capable. She\u8217\'20\'19s poised,\u8221\'20\'1D Sheindlin added.\par \par \uc2 Sheindlin said that neither Trump nor Biden have the \u8220\'20\'1Cintellectual gravitas\u8221\'20\'1D to be US president.\par \par \uc2 According to Sheindlin, she has only endorsed one presidential candidate before \u8211\'20\'13the former New York mayor, \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2 , during the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Sheindlin has campaigned for Haley ahead of the highly watched New Hampshire primary on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  is making the most of the hours remaining before tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s primary in New Hampshire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae9f978f0835e980a416ba#block-65ae9f978f0835e980a416ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crisscrossing the Granite state}}}\uc2  alongside governor \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2  in a bid to lure votes away from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae96e18f08b5ba94ebfae4#block-65ae96e18f08b5ba94ebfae4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls continue to show}}}\uc2  the former president with a big lead, underscoring the difficulty Haley will have in overcoming his status as the frontrunner for the Republican presidential nomination. Trump is expected in New Hampshire later today, after appearing this morning in a New York City courtroom for a hearing in author E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s defamation lawsuit against him, where he was set to testify. The session {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae89c88f0819b86aadad5e#block-65ae89c88f0819b86aadad5e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was abruptly adjourned}}}\uc2  after a juror felt ill, and one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers was exposed to Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Judge Judy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae93548f08b5ba94ebfac6#block-65ae93548f08b5ba94ebfac6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delivered her verdict}}}\uc2  on the presidential race by stumping for Haley in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , who is seen as potential running mate for Trump, said the adjournment of his defamation trial was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae9d2d8f0805c8927543f3#block-65ae9d2d8f0805c8927543f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cblatant election interference\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . In reality, it was requested by the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Someone is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-trump-haley-primary-election-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-65ae81168f08fb2972a012e9#block-65ae81168f08fb2972a012e9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly making robocalls}}}\uc2  to New Hampshire voters that sound like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and encourage them not to vote in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary. Supporters of a campaign to write in his name \u8211\'20\'13 he is not appearing on the ballot, in line with \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  rules \u8211\'20\'13 say the calls are meant to undermine them.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is clearly smarting from the ongoing defamation lawsuit against him by author E Jean Carroll, and a jury\u8217\'20\'19s verdict last year that he sexually abused her. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports, his campaign yesterday barred a NBC News reporter who had pressed his ally \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  for her thoughts on the verdict:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2024/01/donald-trumps-campaign-cuts-off-access-after-refusing-to-allow-nbc-news-vaughn-hillyard-as-designated-pool-reporter-1235799928/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly blocked}}}\uc2  an NBC News journalist from covering campaign events in New Hampshire on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s exclusion of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/nbc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC}}}\uc2  News correspondent Vaughn Hillyard came when he was set to serve as a pool reporter. Instead of having a pack of reporters follow a candidate everywhere, campaigns will often allow television, print, and radio news organizations to send a single pool reporter to travel with them \u8211\'20\'13 and those reporters in turn then send a readout to other news outlets.\par \par \uc2 But on Sunday, Hillyard wrote in an email to the pool: \u8220\'20\'1CYour pooler was told that if he was the designated pooler by NBC News that the pool would be cut off for the day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The email, which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2024/01/donald-trumps-campaign-cuts-off-access-after-refusing-to-allow-nbc-news-vaughn-hillyard-as-designated-pool-reporter-1235799928/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  subsequently published}}}\uc2  by several news organizations, added: \u8220\'20\'1CAfter affirming to the campaign that your pooler would attend the events, NBC News was informed at about 2.20pm that the pool would not be allowed to travel with Trump today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hillyard a day earlier {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/politics/its-not-me-its-a-jury-vaughn-hillyard-snaps-back-at-elise-stefanik-blaming-media-for-trump-sexual-assault-trial/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had pressed}}}\uc2  New York congresswoman \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 said to be a potential Trump running mate \u8211\'20\'13 on whether she believed the ex-president had sexually assaulted E Jean Carroll.\par \par \uc2 NBC News and Steven Cheung, a Trump campaign spokesperson, did not immediately return a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/trump-campaign-blocks-nbc-reporter-vaughn-hillyard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump campaign blocks NBC journalist from New Hampshire event}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 You don\u8217\'20\'19t have to be \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for someone to make a robot of your likeness. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/danmilmo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dan Milmo}}}\uc2  reports, Democratic congressman and presidential candidate \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  has his own AI impersonator:\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  has removed the account of the developer behind an artificial intelligence-powered bot impersonating the US presidential candidate \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2 , saying it violated company policy.\par \par \uc2 Phillips, who is challenging \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for the Democratic party candidacy, was impersonated by a ChatGPT-powered bot on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dean.bot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dean.bot}}}\uc2  site.\par \par \uc2 The bot was backed by Silicon Valley entrepreneurs Matt Krisiloff and Jed Somers, who have started a Super Pac \u8211\'20\'13 a body that funds and supports political candidates \u8211\'20\'13 named We Deserve Better, supporting Phillips.\par \par \uc2 San Francisco-based \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  said it had removed a developer account that violated its policies on political campaigning and impersonation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe recently removed a developer account that was knowingly violating our API usage policies which disallow political campaigning, or impersonating an individual without consent,\u8221\'20\'1D said the company.\par \par \uc2 The Phillips bot, created by AI firm Delphi, is now disabled. Delphi has been contacted for comment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/jan/22/openai-bans-bot-impersonating-us-presidential-candidate-dean-phillips"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 OpenAI bans bot impersonating US presidential candidate Dean Phillips}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A factor working against \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  in her quest to win the New Hampshire Republican primary is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s resounding victory in last week\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa caucus.\par \par \uc2 His triumph in the first state to vote in the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s nomination process confirmed his status as the frontrunner for the nomination. But election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/17/trump-2020-lies-voter-impact-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turnout was low}}}\uc2  in the Hawkeye state, a fact Haley was keen to remind voters of in New Hampshire:\par \par \uc2 enltrNikki Haley in New Hampshire hits the \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical elite\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmedia elite\u8221\'20\'1D that she says want her to drop out and support Trump:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me get this straight: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won 56,000 votes out of 3 million in Iowa. He got 1.5% of the vote in Iowa. America doesn't do coronations.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HOY29xNoor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HOY29xNoor}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1749473729741230350?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire governor campaigns for Haley ahead of must-win primary\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  is spending the final moments before New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s make-or-break primary getting out the vote with the state\u8217\'20\'19s popular Republican governor, \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2  by her side.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is it. Twenty-four hours to go,\u8221\'20\'1D Sununu told the crowd at a packed, dimly lit veteran\u8217\'20\'19s hall in Franklin. \u8220\'20\'1CAll the momentum is at \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He told the voters not to pay any mind to the polls \u8211\'20\'13 unless it\u8217\'20\'19s the ones showing Haley trouncing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in a general election \u8211\'20\'13 and reminded them of their fiercely guarded reputation as the state that delivers political upsets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe always buck the trend in New Hampshire,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to start tomorrow.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haley reminded voters of the stakes of tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s primary \u8211\'20\'13 not that they needed any reminding, since some say they\u8217\'20\'19ve received upwards of 10 campaign mailers a day in recent weeks, in addition to the political ads flooding the airwaves.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t complain about what happens in a general election if you don\u8217\'20\'19t play in this primary tomorrow,\u8221\'20\'1D she charged. \u8220\'20\'1CIt matters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Just about every time she speaks these days, \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  reminds everybody how badly she wants to be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s example is the New York Republican congresswoman calling the adjournment in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defamation trial in New York City today \u8220\'20\'1Cblatant election interference\u8221\'20\'1D because it could mean the former president has to testify tomorrow, the day of the New Hampshire primary.\par \par \uc2 In reality, the postponement was agreed to by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, who has also requested his testimony take place Wednesday, to accommodate for the primary:\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is blatant election interference!\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his Democrat cronies are the true threats to democracy!\par \par \uc2 TRUMP 2024! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LnBmYxa5ud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/LnBmYxa5ud}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  (@EliseStefanik) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EliseStefanik/status/1749454981617394015?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump maintains big lead over Haley in New Hampshire, poll finds\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire voters may not give \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  what she wants on Tuesday, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/01/22/trump-leads-new-hampshire-post-monmouth-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Washington Post-Monmouth University poll}}}\uc2  released today that finds her trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the state by 18 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 Trump is the clear frontrunner, with 52% support, compared to Haley\u8217\'20\'19s 34%. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  polled at 8% in the survey completed before he withdrew from the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 The Post notes that Haley\u8217\'20\'19s support has doubled from November, largely due to her attracting voters that supported former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , who exited the race earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The survey offers a snapshot of the types of voters who are supporting Trump and Haley, with 71% of the former South Carolina governor\u8217\'20\'19s supporters believing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the 2020 election fairly, and 48% registered with neither party. Forty-nine percent say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, and 56% described themselves as moderate or liberal.\par \par \uc2 Among Trump voters, only 14% believe Biden won fairly, 38% were not registered with a party, 29% said they were moderate or liberal and 38% thought \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judy Sheindlin \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judgejudy.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge Judy}}}\uc2  to you \u8211\'20\'13 is famous for weighing on things, and she recently reached her own verdict on this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential race: \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  is the best candidate for the job.\par \par \uc2 She campaigned with the former South Carolina governor in New Hampshire yesterday, urging voters to, \u8220\'20\'1Cbring her home on Tuesday\u8221\'20\'1D. Sheindlin\u8217\'20\'19s political allegiances have shifted over the years, and in 2020, she endorsed former New York mayor \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2  for the Democratic presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll find out soon enough if her verdict on Haley is enough to push her over the top in New Hampshire. If it is not, Sheindlin does not seem ready to campaign for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 she went on CNN to say that she thinks he is too old:\par \par \uc2 enltrJudge Judy, when asked Sunday about endorsing \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  for president:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now older. \u8230\'20\'26 He's my age. \u8230\'20\'26 I need a nap in the afternoon. So does \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 probably two.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/usOAGJ0jSE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/usOAGJ0jSE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1749459167784636534?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s exit, former South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  has the two-person race she wants in New Hampshire, the state she has bet her campaign on. But will it be enough to beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Tuesday? The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  took a look at Haley\u8217\'20\'19s pitch to voters, and if it\u8217\'20\'19s working:\par \par \uc2 Plodding across frigid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Hampshire}}}\uc2  ahead of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  offered the state\u8217\'20\'19s proudly freethinking voters a tantalizing proposal: choose her and save America from the presidential rematch seemingly nobody wants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSeventy percent of Americans have said they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to see a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 -\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  rematch,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley exclaimed on Sunday, drawing head nods and murmurs of agreement from attendees packed into a middle school library in Derry. Haley leaned in: \u8220\'20\'1CDo we really want to have two presidential candidates in their 80s?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden, the 81-year-old Democratic president, is coasting to his party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination and Trump, the 77-year-old former president, is marching toward the Republican one as the field narrows and he consolidates support from across the party. But Haley, who celebrated her 52nd birthday hopscotching the state on Saturday, insisted there was a different \u8211\'20\'13 viable \u8211\'20\'13 path.\par \par \uc2 Haley, the former \u8220\'20\'1CTea Party governor\u8221\'20\'1D of South Carolina who served as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first United Nations ambassador, has staked her presidential aspirations on a strong showing in the first-in-the-nation primary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNew Hampshire is do-or-die for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mike Dennehy, a veteran Republican strategist in New Hampshire who worked on \uc2 John McCain\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s winning presidential primary campaigns in the state in 2000 and 2008 and is unaffiliated. \u8220\'20\'1CShe needs to go all in and speak specifically to independent voters who want change in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/nikki-haley-new-hampshire-primary-independent-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley bets on New Hampshire as best chance of wresting nomination from Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge postpones Trump defamation trial till Tuesday\par \par \uc2 Change of plans for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  : today\u8217\'20\'19s hearing in New York City of the defamation lawsuit brought against him by author E Jean Carroll has been postponed till Tuesday after a juror felt ill, and an attorney for the former president said one of her parents had been exposed to Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Trump was expected to testify today, but that will now also take place another time. Follow our live blog for the latest on this story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/22/trump-e-jean-carroll-defamation-trial-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump defamation trial postponed until tomorrow due to illness \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t be on the ballot in New Hampshire, but two long-shot Democratic candidates will be, while opponents of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza are encouraging voters to write in \u8220\'20\'1Cceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D as a show of protest. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  on some of the lesser-known aspects of the state\u8217\'20\'19s primary tomorrow:\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  might draw focus, a shadow presidential primary is taking place in New Hampshire, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  could stumble at the first hurdle of his bid to run for president again in 2024 following an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/17/democratic-primaries-2024-new-hampshire-south-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 internal Democratic party feud}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As a consequence of the party scrap, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name will not even appear on the ballot in the Granite state on Tuesday. While the president remains the favorite to win his party\u8217\'20\'19s overall nomination, his absence here has opened a window for \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2 , a Democratic congressman from Minnesota, and \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 , an author and self-help guru who ran for president in 2020, to mount longshot presidential bids.\par \par \uc2 The pair have spent weeks campaigning in the state, pitching different visions for the future. Phillips, 55, has touted his reputation as a centrist; his record of working with Republicans to get things done; and the fact that he is 26 years younger than Biden.\par \par \uc2 Williamson, who withdrew from the 2020 race before the Iowa caucuses, is selling more of a deviation from the current administration. A progressive, she would introduce free college tuition, declare a climate emergency and Department of Peace which would be tasked with avoiding war abroad and tackling white supremacy at home.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/new-hampshire-presidential-primary-joe-biden-dean-phillips-marianne-williamson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name won\u8217\'20\'19t appear on New Hampshire ballots \u8211\'20\'13 where does that leave Democrats?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There are reportedly some shenanigans happening in New Hampshire ahead of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary, though what they amount to is unclear.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/fake-joe-biden-robocall-tells-new-hampshire-democrats-not-vote-tuesday-rcna134984"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2  that Granite state residents are getting robocalls from a fake voice that sounds like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and encourages them not to vote tomorrow. The president\u8217\'20\'19s name is not appearing on the ballot in New Hampshire, after the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  opted to make South Carolina the first state in its nominating process.\par \par \uc2 However supporters of the president are encouraging people to write in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name on their ballots, as a way to show their support and try to win back the state\u8217\'20\'19s spot in the nominating process. In previous years, New Hampshire was the second state to vote after Iowa for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The robocalls concluded by giving people the phone number for Kathy Sullivan, a former state Democratic party chair who is supporting the write-in campaign. She believes the calls\u8217\'20\'19 intention is to hurt Biden, NBC News reports, and that they are illegal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want them to be prosecuted to the fullest extent possible because this is an attack on democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D she told NBC. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to let it go. I want to know who\u8217\'20\'19s paying for it? Who knew about it? Who benefits?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Money, endorsements, poll numbers: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  had it all, and then he lost it. Was it taken from him by the 800lb gorilla of the Republican party \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , or did he cause his own downfall? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  untangles the question, and finds that it\u8217\'20\'19s a little bit of both:\par \par \uc2 It began in a glitch-filled disaster on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . It ended with a misattributed quotation on X. Just like \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s social media platform, efforts to rebrand \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US presidential election campaign could not mask its fundamental flaws.\par \par \uc2 When in May the Florida governor announced his run during a chat with Musk on Twitter Spaces, the platform\u8217\'20\'19s audio streaming feature, there were technical breakdowns that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-elon-musk-twitter-campaign-launch-glitch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drew comparisons}}}\uc2  with one of Musk\u8217\'20\'19s space rockets blowing up on the launchpad.\par \par \uc2 Eight months, dozens of staff departures, tens of millions of dollars and one crushing defeat in Iowa later, DeSantis announced he was dropping out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RonDeSantis/status/1749159384112845285?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a video}}}\uc2  posted on the renamed X that quoted Winston Churchill as saying: \u8220\'20\'1CSuccess is not final, failure is not fatal \u8211\'20\'13 it is the courage to continue that counts.\u8221\'20\'1D According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://winstonchurchill.org/publications/finest-hour/finest-hour-136/media-matters/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 International Churchill Society}}}\uc2 , the British wartime prime minister never said that.\par \par \uc2 Two days before the New Hampshire primary election, DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s humiliation was complete. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is probably the biggest collapse of a presidential campaign in modern American history, if not all American history,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://davidjolly.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Jolly}}}\uc2 , a former Republican congressman from Florida, told the MSNBC network on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  had everything going for him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/21/ron-desantis-republican-presidential-candidate-dropped-out-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis put nearly all his eggs in the basket of a \u8216\'20\'18war on woke\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 DeSantis's exit winnows Republican race down to just two candidates\par \par \uc2 It was only a few weeks ago that Republicans looking for an alternative to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jan/21/presidential-election-candidates-biden-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a veritable cornucopia of big-league politicians}}}\uc2  to choose from. But, with the exception of \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , all of them have dropped out, and yesterday, a big name announced his exit: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor who once seemed like the best bet to unseat Trump from the helm of the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 His downfall was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/16/ron-desantis-second-place-iowa-caucus-whats-next-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a mediocre second-place showing}}}\uc2  in Iowa last Monday, despite pouring everything his campaign had into winning the first state to vote in the GOP nomination process. There was clearly not backup plan for DeSantis, and yesterday, he announced his exit from the race with a video posted on X that included a fabricated Winston Churchill quote.\par \par \uc2 In it, the Florida governor takes one last jab at Trump, who has spent the past months pummeling him with insults, most notably the nickname \u8220\'20\'1CRon DeSanctimonious\u8221\'20\'1D. DeSantis nonetheless endorsed Trump as he exited the race, and later on Sunday, the former president said the nickname was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ShelbyTalcott/status/1749193962236092883"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being retired}}}\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s what DeSantis had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CSuccess is not final, failure is not fatal: it is the courage to continue that counts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 - Winston Churchill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ECoR8YeiMm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ECoR8YeiMm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (@RonDeSantis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonDeSantis/status/1749159384112845285?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Haley scrambles to overtake Trump ahead of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s must-win New Hampshire primary vote\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics live blog readers. We are coming to you today from Manchester, New Hampshire, the state where former South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  is making what may well be her last stand to seize the Republican presidential nomination from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The race winnowed down to two main candidates yesterday, when Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  dropped out after his disappointing second-place finish in last week\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa caucus. Haley has staked it all on winning in New Hampshire, which will vote in primaries tomorrow, and today, she has five publicly announced campaign events on her schedule. Trump, meanwhile, has one speech planned for 9pm eastern time, and may {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-carroll-defamation-lawsuit-trial-1e5420d5b28c857220429275ab901a34"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  spend today testifying to the New York City jury hearing the defamation lawsuit brought against him by author E Jean Carroll.\par \par \uc2 Trump has functioned as a juggernaut in the race for the GOP nomination for more than a year, with polls showing him the frontrunner among Republicans both nationally and in most early voting states, New Hampshire included. While Haley has seen some momentum in polling recently, the gap between her and the former president remains significant. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/21/politics/new-hampshire-primary-poll-trump-haley-desantis/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a survey}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 University of New Hampshire\uc2  released by CNN yesterday, she\u8217\'20\'19s running 11 percentage points behind Trump, who is polling at 50%. It\u8217\'20\'19s quite the deficit to make up, and we expect to hear her give her closing arguments throughout the course of today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Today is the 51st anniversary of Roe v Wade, the supreme court decision that allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, which was overturned by conservative justices in 2022. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is traveling to Wisconsin for a speech to mark the start of what the Biden administration is calling its \u8220\'20\'1CFight for Reproductive Freedoms\u8221\'20\'1D tour.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senators have for weeks been negotiating a deal to tighten immigration restrictions in order to win the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s support for aid to Israel and Ukraine. If an agreement has been reached, it could theoretically be announced today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats making a quixotic effort to unseat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee will also be campaigning in New Hampshire today, including Minnesota congressman \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  and \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240122ek1m002ej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
