\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They hate God\u8217\'20\'19: US anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  activists aim to fight back on 51st Roe anniversary\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,636 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 January 2024\par 19:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As Biden unveils blitz of events to mark 1973 ruling, conservatives try to stage comeback after key ballot failures\par \par \uc2 Within the subterranean levels of a fancy hotel in downtown Washington, just a few days before the 51st anniversary of Roe v Wade, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement was trying to mount a comeback.\par \par \uc2 Kevin Roberts\uc2  stood on stage in a cavernous ballroom aglow with neon shades of blue, purple and pink. As president of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , Roberts leads one of the main thinktanks behind recent conservative attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And he is not happy with how things are going.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe meet today amid a pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  media narrative of smug triumphalism,\u8221\'20\'1D Roberts told hundreds of young \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes, who had gathered in the ballroom from across the country to hear him and other anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaders speak.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve heard the story. Less than two years after the supreme court overturned Roe, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -industrial complex is celebrating an unprecedented political winning streak. Across the country, pro-life bills have failed. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referenda have passed. Democrat leaders are crowing while too many Republican leaders are cowering from the fight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Roberts was speaking at the annual National Pro-Life Summit, a one-day organizing camp for high school- and college-aged anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists. This year, the summit faced a monumental task: organizers and attendees alike hoped to reinvigorate a movement that, 18 months ago, soared to the height of its power with the overturning of Roe \u8211\'20\'13 and then, in the months that followed, has repeatedly crashed-landed back on earth.\par \par \uc2 Since Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, seven states have voted on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot referendums. In each case, voters have decisively moved to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, even in ruby-red states like Kentucky, Kansas and Montana.\par \par \uc2 The stakes are even higher in 2024. Not only are roughly a dozen more states gearing up to potentially vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related referendums, but the future of the White House is on the line. If \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurts Republicans the election \u8211\'20\'13 as it\u8217\'20\'19s widely thought to have done in the 2022 midterms \u8211\'20\'13 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists may see the GOP brand their movement as ballot-box poison.\par \par \uc2 The National Pro-Life Summit is generally a peek into what the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is telling itself about itself \u8211\'20\'13 and at present, it is not happy with Republicans. For years, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has corralled voters for Republicans. On Saturday, they repeatedly condemned the GOP for failing to adequately support their cause.\par \par \uc2 The last Republican president appointed the justices who overturned Roe, while red states have enacted more than a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozen near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2  since the ruling fell. But many Republicans have begun to back away from the issue. Before the 2022 elections, several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/08/30/republican-abortion-positions-midterm-elections-00054128"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quietly downplayed their stances}}}\uc2 , while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/12/us/politics/house-republicans-abortion-ban.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozens of House Republicans have delayed}}}\uc2  signing onto a bill to nationally ban abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur friends in the Republican party need to touch some grass,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , the president of Students for Life of America, the organization behind the summit. \u8220\'20\'1CThose who say now that we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be talking, that Republican candidates, those seeking for office, should hide from the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue \u8211\'20\'13 they continue to be wrong. We won\u8217\'20\'19t win if we put our head in the sand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats are already attempting to use Roe\u8217\'20\'19s impact on doctors to win votes, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign has launched a blitz of events and ads timed to the Roe anniversary on Monday. Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will kick off a tour devoting to spotlighting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, while Biden will assemble a meeting of his reproductive health taskforce.\par \par \uc2 His administration has also announced plans to expand access to contraception under the Affordable Care Act as well as an initiative to spread information about a law that, the administration says, guarantees Americans\u8217\'20\'19 legal rights to emergency abortions, even in states that ban the procedure.\par \par \uc2 A thin line\par \par \uc2 The mood on Saturday wasn\u8217\'20\'19t totally dour.\par \par \uc2 Attendees could buy baseball caps that read \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just out here saving babies,\u8221\'20\'1D sweatshirts that bore an image of a newspaper front page that proclaimed \u8220\'20\'1CROE REVERSED\u8221\'20\'1D, as well as red hats adorned with the words \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Pro-Life Again\u8221\'20\'1D in the unmistakable style of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Maga hats. Young people excitedly posed for group photos in front of a backdrop that read, \u8220\'20\'1CEQUAL RIGHTS FOR THE PREBORN!\u8221\'20\'1D An illustrated fetus was curled up in one corner.\par \par \uc2 Yet, in speech after speech, activists told young people that they were the victims of vast forces arrayed against them. They accused \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters of spreading misinformation about ballot referendums and said they were simply outspent by the opposition. In Ohio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/07/ohio-vote-abortion-rights-ban-what-is-issue-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights supporters reported receiving}}}\uc2  about three times as much money as a coalition that opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese people love chaos. That is the left. The left is inherently chaotic at its core,\u8221\'20\'1D said Will Witt, a conservative influencer who, like Roberts, spoke at the morning address to all attendees.\par \par \uc2 After quoting from the Bible in an effort to demonstrate that God originated order, Witt continued: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is why the left, this is why these pro-choicers, this is why they hate God. Because God represents order in the world, whereas they love chaos.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The summit speakers were attempting to walk a fine line. At the same time that they were attempting to convince attendees that they were the victims of a world turned against them, they also had to make the case that opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a majority view \u8211\'20\'13 and one issue that can get Republicans elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur opinion on this issue, the issue, is not outside of the mainstream, no matter how many times ABC wants to try to tell me it is,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawkins told attendees at a workshop dedicated to understanding what went wrong with the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendums. Most millennials and members of Gen Z, she added, \u8220\'20\'1Cwant some sorts of limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Polling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is complex, since respondents\u8217\'20\'19 answers can vary widely depending on how a question is asked or how much context is provided. Most Americans believe that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be restricted after the first trimester of pregnancy, according to polling from Gallup. However, over the last two decades, more and more people have become open to keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal later into pregnancy. Republicans in Virginia failed to take control of the state legislature last year after they ran on a promise of banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Gallup has also found that, since 2020, more Americans identify as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D than \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D. More people have started to call themselves \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Hawkins is not in favor of only \u8220\'20\'1Csome sorts of limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to see no abortions be legal, ever,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in an interview. She rejected the notion that abortions performed to save women\u8217\'20\'19s lives qualify as abortions. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you\u8217\'20\'19re looking at a case where a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life is at risk, where the physician believes that she can no longer safely carry her child in her womb, or she may lose her life \u8211\'20\'13 we wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t consider that an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the abortionist goes in with the intention to killing the child.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Instead, she said, it\u8217\'20\'19s a \u8220\'20\'1Cmaternal-fetal separation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hawkins\u8217\'20\'19 point was an effort to contend with a phenomenon that has been particularly damaging for the movement: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/16/abortion-ban-lawsuits-pregnancy-complication-emergency-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stories from women}}}\uc2  who have sued after they said they were denied medically necessary abortions.\par \par \uc2 Every state with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has some kind of exception for cases of medical emergencies, but doctors in those states have widely said that the exceptions are so vague as to be unworkable. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamanetworkopen/fullarticle/2814017"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent study}}}\uc2  of 54 OB-GYNs in states with post-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, more than 90% said that the law prevented them from adhering to the best clinical standards of care.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18You vote pro-life\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Last year, when the National Pro-Life Summit held a straw poll asking attendees about their preferred 2024 president candidate, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  won. This year, with DeSantis a day away from dropping out of the presidential primary, Hawkins cheerfully proclaimed the latest straw poll victor: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As much as their leaders may lock heads with Republicans or Trump \u8211\'20\'13 who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/donald-trump-abortion-election-republicans-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2  that hardline \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stances hurt Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 they are ultimately unlikely to withhold votes from the GOP. Even Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , who was a target of the January 6 riot and who spoke at the summit, indicated that people need to simply get on with it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why we have primaries. We sort \u8217\'20\'19em out at every level. But after the primary\u8217\'20\'19s over, you vote pro-life,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou go get behind men and women who are going to stand for the right to life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A booth for \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  was emblazoned with logos for its \u8220\'20\'1CProject 2025\u8221\'20\'1D, which includes a playbook for the next conservative president. It recommends that the \uc2 US government\uc2  stop funding or promoting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in international programs, turbocharge the government\u8217\'20\'19s existing \u8220\'20\'1Csurveillance\u8221\'20\'1D efforts to collect data about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and enforce the 19th-century Comstock Act to ban the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. That would effectively result in the removal of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills from the market, which Hawkins said is a policy goal of hers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would be elected again, the people he would appoint to his presidential administration would not be \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawkins said in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CHands down, that\u8217\'20\'19s a guarantee. And they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be coming to Washington to protect the people and the people includes the pre-born children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240122ek1m002ee\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
