\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We will never go away\u8217\'20\'19: anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  activists meet in Washington to plan further bans\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman in Washington DC \par \uc2 781 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 January 2024\par 17:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are emboldened by the fall of Roe, but many states have enacted protections after ruling\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  had a message: always vote against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 even if, he suggested, that means voting for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why we have primaries. We sort \u8217\'20\'19em out at every level. But after the primary\u8217\'20\'19s over, you vote pro-life,\u8221\'20\'1D the former Republican vice-president to Trump told a downtown Washington DC ballroom of young, diehard anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists on Saturday. \u8220\'20\'1CYou go get behind men and women who are going to stand for the right to life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The room erupted into applause.\par \par \uc2 The activists had gathered in the ballroom for the National Pro-Life Summit, the conclusion of a two-day extravaganza of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activism in the US capital. On Friday, many had walked through the snowy streets of Washington to support the March for Life, the largest annual anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  event in the United States.\par \par \uc2 But while the March for Life is a mass show of force, the National Pro-Life Summit is far more focused. It aims to arm the foot soldiers of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, high school- and college-aged activists, with the education and energy they need to effectively advocate against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 especially in an election year.\par \par \uc2 In the months since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters have repeatedly defeated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes in ballot referendums, even in conservative strongholds such as Kansas, Kentucky and Ohio.\par \par \uc2 This string of losses, though, has seemingly hardened the stance of summit attendees and speakers. Rather than compromising, summit speakers urged young people: don\u8217\'20\'19t give up. Do more.\par \par \uc2 I want to see no abortions be legal, ever\par \par \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of Students for Life of America\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to be bolder. We need to be louder,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of Students for Life of America, the organization behind the Pro-Life Summit, said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re working in 10 to 17 states this year, introducing various pro-life laws, doing as much as we can to save as many lives. So I want to see no abortions be legal, ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the morning, summit attendees gathered in a massive ballroom lit in shades of purple, purple and pink. Speakers spoke against a teal backdrop emblazoned with logos for groups such as \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  and the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , two powerful organizations that are spearheading much of the conservative political and legal charge against causes like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ+ rights.\par \par \uc2 The speakers\u8217\'20\'19 talks portrayed the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes in the room as the descendants of freedom fighters such as soldiers in the US revolutionary war and the second world war. The historical analogies did not stop there: they also drew comparisons between \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Holocaust and the 7 October attack in Israel.\par \par \uc2 The fight against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they suggested, was no less than righteous spiritual warfare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake: this idea of human inequality, that some people count and some people don\u8217\'20\'19t, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t come from the media, or the government, or the elite, or even \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Kevin Roberts\uc2 , president of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt comes straight from hell.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Attendees cheered wildly \u8211\'20\'13 even more than they had for Pence\u8217\'20\'19s remarks.\par \par \uc2 This weekend marked a kind of official kick-off around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organizing, for both sides of the aisle, since the would-be 51st anniversary of Roe is on Monday. While anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists amassed in Washington, Joe Biden and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have announced that they are launching a new blitz of ads and events to spotlight the impact of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise.\par \par \uc2 That strategy seems well placed. Polling in the US still suggests strong support for a legal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite an intense wave of crackdowns and restrictions by Republican-run state legislatures. That also has translated at the ballot box, where Republican losses in the 2022 midterms and Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s elections last year were partly blamed on anger over Republican extremism on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But if Democrats are hoping that outrage over Roe will lead them to victory in the 2024 elections, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents remain equally as determined to stay strong.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn every struggle between good and evil, we know the enemy\u8217\'20\'19s outrage can be wielded as a powerful weapon. However, the key to victory always lies in those who persist,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawkins told attendees in a speech, a cross swinging from glittery beads looped around her neck. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that\u8217\'20\'19s what those on the other side just don\u8217\'20\'19t understand about us. That we will never go away.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240120ek1k0025t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
