\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We don\u8217\'20\'19t want to be the bad guys\u8217\'20\'19: anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  marchers seek post-Roe stance\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 916 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 January 2024\par 23:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 On the 51st anniversary of Roe v Wade, a sparse crowd of activists brave snow on March for Life in Washington DC\par \par \uc2 While Joe Biden and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are planning a cascade of ads and events to coincide with the 51st anniversary of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , hundreds of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists gathered on the National Mall in Washington DC on Friday in hopes of re-energizing a movement that has repeatedly stumbled since Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturning.\par \par \uc2 Originally organized around the goal of overturning the Roe precedent that established federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the March for Life has seen what was once its greatest victory become a political liability. In the 18 months since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/dec/15/neil-gorsuch-us-supreme-court-dobbs-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise}}}\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters have trounced anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in state-level ballot referendums. Yet the march\u8217\'20\'19s message was largely similar to past years: speakers and attendees alike talked about the need to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cunthinkable\u8221\'20\'1D rather than just illegal \u8211\'20\'13 with scant details on how to make that happen.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want to just go in and be the bad guys,\u8221\'20\'1D said Elijah Persinger, a 19-year-old from Fort Wayne, Indiana. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to make make people understand and help them understand the science behind things and the logic that we\u8217\'20\'19re going by as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As in years past, march attendees skewed young. Schools and universities organize trips for students to attend the march, and groups often carry banners and flags with their schools\u8217\'20\'19 names. Some groups all wear bright-colored, matching hats in order to keep from getting lost in the crowd.\par \par \uc2 Persinger took a 12-hour, overnight bus ride to attend Friday\u8217\'20\'19s March for Life. His group planned to leave DC after the event.\par \par \uc2 But the crowd on Friday seemed relatively sparse. When the US House speaker, Mike Johnson, stood on a podium to speak, he was met with only muted applause \u8211\'20\'13 despite being a high-profile attendee for the march. The greatest response came when he mentioned Biden: when he said that the president\u8217\'20\'19s administration planned to restrict funding to crisis pregnancy centers, the crowd booed loudly.\par \par \uc2 Organizers also spoke from the stage about the need to support maternity homes and crisis pregnancy centers, facilities that aim to convince people to keep their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChristians don\u8217\'20\'19t mean to impose what we believe on anyone. But this nation was founded as a Christian nation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Laurel Brooks, a march attendee from North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Brooks works for an organization called My Faith Votes, which aims to mobilize Christian voters, but she clarified that she was sharing her own views, not her organization\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe foundation of America is truly Christian,\u8221\'20\'1D Brooks remarked. \u8220\'20\'1CThat doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean we reject, hate, dislike anyone who does not believe as we do. That\u8217\'20\'19s not who Christians are. We accept people for their free will. God honors free will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the speakers finished, marchers spent three hours slowly walking from the National Mall to the steps of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 . The weather was unusually wintry, with marchers braving wind and several inches of snow.\par \par \uc2 To keep from getting cold, some marchers danced to the Cha Cha Slide. Others started a call-and-response chant of, \u8220\'20\'1CWe are pro-life, marching for life, saving the babies, one at a time!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Icons of fetuses and babies dominated the march. Many carried signs with ultrasound images above phrases such as \u8220\'20\'1CFuture Doctor\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CFuture Dancer\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1CFuture Wife\u8221\'20\'1D. Others had signs with images of babies above the conservative slogan \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t Tread on Me\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are no mistakes, just happy accidents,\u8221\'20\'1D read another sign, complete with a hand-drawn beaming baby and portrait of the painter Bob Ross. One young woman even carried a baby made out of snow.\par \par \uc2 At least one man was trying to sell Trump 2024 merchandise to marchers. But overall, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had a minimal presence at the march despite being the frontrunner for the Republican White House nomination as he seeks a second presidency.\par \par \uc2 Trump has waffled on his stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : while he has taken credit for installing supreme court justices who helped overturn Roe, he has also suggested that hardline stances on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can backfire on Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not voting for Trump, I know that much,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ali Mumbach, 26. She carried a sign listing police brutality, gun violence and other issues that should matter to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists who call themselves \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is anti-life, especially in regards to Black lives and the lives of immigrants. So, yeah, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that he is pro-life. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that he cares about people who live in poverty. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he has the best interests of the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D Mumbach said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, meanwhile, are hoping sustained outrage over Roe will propel them to victory up and down the general election ballot.\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign is now launching a paid media campaign, timed to Roe\u8217\'20\'19s anniversary, to target women and swing voters in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 Harris plans to appear on Monday in Wisconsin to spotlight post-Roe attacks on reproductive rights before holding a campaign rally alongside Biden in Virginia.\par \par \uc2 In the November 2023 state elections, Virginia Republicans tried to take control of the state legislature by promising to enact a \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable\u8221\'20\'1D ban on terminating pregnancies that were 15 weeks or beyond \u8211\'20\'13 an effort that failed.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240120ek1j00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
