\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge threatens to exclude Trump from court for loud complaints as E Jean Carroll testifies \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 5,098 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 January 2024\par 21:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For more on the trial, you can read our latest:Full report: E Jean Carroll testifies \u8216\'20\'18to get my reputation back\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to Trump on Trial: a newsletter on all the latest court developments\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today's recap\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 E Jean Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s testimony in the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  defamation trial prompted outbursts from the former president in court.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/17/trump-carroll-lawsuit-testify-defamation-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  a full picture of the day\u8217\'20\'19s proceedings.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  continued to lead in the race for the Republican presidential nomination, enjoying a 16-point lead in New Hampshire, per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/17/trump-new-hampshire-poll-lead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a major new poll}}}\uc2 . Former South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  came in second, and Florida \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was a distant third, days before the state\u8217\'20\'19s primary. DeSantis, said the US was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a racist country\u8221\'20\'1D, echoing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/16/politics/nikki-haley-says-us-not-racist-country/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a controversial claim by Haley}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A top aide for president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  to apologize. White House chief of staff Jeff Zients apologized a mocking statement released by the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  regarding Hutchinson\u8217\'20\'19s decision to drop out of the 2024 presidential race.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Guardian staff\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Cross-examination of E Jean Carroll in Trump defamation case has concluded\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lead attorney in the case, Alina Habba, tried to discredit Carroll by noting that the gun she has kept for protection isn\u8217\'20\'19t registered.\par \par \uc2 Habba also inquired about Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s deletion of threatening texts and emails. \u8220\'20\'1CSo as [you] sit here today, I have no way of knowing how many death threats you have received, nor do the police?\u8221\'20\'1D Habba asked.\par \par \uc2 Carroll is suing Trump over his June 2019 denials of her rape claim against him, maintaining that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s denials smeared her reputation, sparking online abuse and serious threats. This trial will determine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/16/jury-selection-e-jean-carroll-defamation-trial-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 damages}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US has put Yemen\u8217\'20\'19s Houthi rebels back on its list of global terrorists as the group warned it would view any such move by Britain or America as a declaration of war.\par \par \uc2 Houthi leaders said their attacks on commercial shipping in the Red Sea would stop as soon as the \u8220\'20\'1CIsraeli aggression\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza stopped, a point underlined by what appeared to be a fresh attack on a ship near Aden late on Wednesday. The United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations (UKMTO) organisation said that a vessel had reportedly been struck by an \u8220\'20\'1Cuncrewed aerial system,\u8221\'20\'1D causing a fire onboard that was later extinguished.\par \par \uc2 The Houthi deputy foreign minister, Hussein Alezzi, said before the US decision: \u8220\'20\'1CAny measure that harms Yemen\u8217\'20\'19s interests will be considered a declaration of war, and preventing Israeli ships will not be confined to the Bab el-Mandeb Strait alone.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere are others who will obstruct them through different means, and our coordination in this matter is advanced. The aggression by America and Britain and their shedding of Yemeni blood was unnecessary and will become a lifetime mistake unless they accept Yemen\u8217\'20\'19s forthcoming response and cease their crimes against Gaza.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mohammad al-Houthi, a member of the Houthi supreme political council, said: \u8220\'20\'1CDirect confrontation with America is a positive thing because it is the US that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/sep/30/yemenis-living-under-the-shadow-of-death-by-airstrike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brought destruction, siege, and poverty to our country}}}\uc2 . America, which said it had a bank of targets, targeted everything in the Republic of Yemen \u8211\'20\'13 hospitals, roads, schools, markets, prisons, and gatherings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Follow along with the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s coverage of the unfolding situation here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jan/17/middle-east-crisis-live-news-updates-israel-gaza-palestine-hamas-war-iran-strike-pakistan-sunni-us-red-sea-crisis-houthi-missile-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Middle East crisis live: Houthis say they targeted US ship in Gulf of Aden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A top aide for president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has called former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  to apologize for a mocking statement released by the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  regarding Hutchinson\u8217\'20\'19s decision to drop out of the 2024 presidential race.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released on Tuesday, DNC press secretary Sarafina Chitika said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis news comes as a shock to those of us who could\u8217\'20\'19ve sworn he had already dropped out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said that Biden directed White House chief of staff Jeff Zients to call Hutchinson and apologize for the statement, saying that it did not reflect his views.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden has respect for governor Hutchinson and admires the race that he ran. The president knows him to be a man of principle who cares about our country and has a strong record of public service,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the 51st anniversary of Roe v Wade, Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has condemned anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republicans over their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Wednesday, Schumer said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor decades, the far-right has led a campaign to systematically dismantle a woman\u8217\'20\'19s fundamental right to choose. The most extreme elements of the Republican party have made it their mission to eliminate this freedom of choice. Republican \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans across the country have led to chaos, irreperable harm\u8230\'20\'26 We will never, never stop fighting for a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, ahead of the 51st anniversary of Roe v. Wade, Senate Democrats heard from witnesses at the forefront of fighting for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 MAGA Republicans are still pushing for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Democrats will never relent in fighting for a woman's right to choose. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HWbUFOANeh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HWbUFOANeh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1747708047160492173?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some courtroom sketches coming through the newswires of E Jean Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s defamation trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 E. Jean Carroll testifies before Judge Lewis Kaplan as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  watches. Photograph: Jane Rosenberg/Reuters E Jean Carroll reacts during questioning by her lawyer \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2 . Photograph: Jane Rosenberg/Reuters In this courtroom sketch, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sits with arms folded beside his attorney, Alina Habba. Photograph: Elizabeth Williams/AP In this courtroom sketch, E Jean Carroll, right, is questioned by her lawyer \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2 , center. Photograph: Elizabeth Williams/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Less than a week before the New Hampshire primary, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  enjoys a 16-point lead in the north-eastern state, according to a major poll.\par \par \uc2 The poll, from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bostonglobe.com/2024/01/17/metro/boston-globe-new-hampshire-tracking-poll/?event=event12"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Suffolk University, the Boston Globe and NBC}}}\uc2 , gave the former president 50% support, to 34% for the former South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 . \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the hard-right governor of Florida who edged out Haley for second in Iowa this week, was a distant third on 5%.\par \par \uc2 In New Hampshire, voters who are not registered Democrats can take part in the Republican primary.\par \par \uc2 In the new poll, Trump dominated among registered Republicans and voters who called themselves conservatives. Haley led among moderates and independents.\par \par \uc2 David Paleologos, director of the Suffolk University Political Research Center, told the Globe: \u8220\'20\'1CHaley\u8217\'20\'19s had a tough week: underperforming in Iowa, trying to answer Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on her positions on social security and immigration, and the recent [Vivek] Ramaswamy endorsement of Trump helping him with younger GOP voters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy, a biotech entrepreneur with whom Haley frequently clashed in debates, dropped out of the race after finishing fourth in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 For Haley, Paleologos said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is time to at least close the gap with undecided voters or even with some Trump voters, and pull Trump below 50.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other polls have shown Haley closing the gap in New Hampshire. Also on Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://americanresearchgroup.com/pres2024/rep/nhrep.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American Research Group}}}\uc2  put Haley and Trump tied on 40% each.\par \par \uc2 The polling analysis site FiveThirtyEight.com gives ARG a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/pollster-ratings/american-research-group/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 C+ rating}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Suffolk University{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/pollster-ratings/suffolk-university/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gets}}}\uc2  an A-.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Cross-examination in E Jean Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s defamation trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is starting now.\par \par \uc2 The cross-examination follows Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s testimony which Trump loudly complained throughout.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Carroll tells trial Trump's statement after her first win made her feel 'worthless'\par \par \uc2 Much of E Jean Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s testimony detailed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s continued statements about her after he was found liable of sexual abuse and defamation. This relates to jurors\u8217\'20\'19 decision on damages, as they must determine a sum that would deter him from making similar statements.\par \par \uc2 Her attorney played a portion of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/05/11/politics/transcript-cnn-town-hall-trump/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s CNN town hall}}}\uc2 , which took place one day after Carroll won her first trial. Asked about the verdict, Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I swear and I\u8217\'20\'19ve never done that, and I swear to \u8211\'20\'13 I have no idea who the hell \u8211\'20\'13 she\u8217\'20\'19s a whack job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s doing it to a large crowd and drawing laughs about sexual assault,\u8221\'20\'1D Carroll noted.\par \par \uc2 When asked how this made her feel, Carroll choked up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI felt worthless,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Guardian US is launching a new newsletter, focusing on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s many legal travails.\par \par \uc2 Will the former US president (and leading Republican candidate in this one) be a convicted felon by the time of this November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election?\par \par \uc2 Will the multiple cases against him actually conclude in time? Will he be allowed to stay on the ballot? Could he pardon himself?\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is launching a newsletter to help readers keep track of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s myriad legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 Cameron Joseph, a politics reporter with 15 years of experience in Washington, will help readers stay on top of different cases, offering guidance on the big legal questions facing Trump and the American judicial system.\par \par \uc2 The newsletter will go out every Thursday \u8211\'20\'13 plus bonus editions on days with major Trump trial news.\par \par \uc2 You can sign up for the news letter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/18/sign-up-for-the-trump-on-trial-newsletter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HERE}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York writer E Jean Carroll fought back tears on the stand in court in Manhattan earlier today, when shown a message by her lawyer \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2 , who is not related to the judge in the case, Lewis Kaplan, that had suggested that she stick a gun in her mouth and pull the trigger, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was attacked on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , I was attacked on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , I was attacked on news blogs, I was brutally attacked in messages,\u8221\'20\'1D Carroll said, about what happened to hear after she accused Trump of sexual assault in the past. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a new world.\u8221\'20\'1D\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Carroll said she once got 200 letters a month from readers seeking advice, and now gets eight. She was best known as an advice columnist at Elle magazine.\par \par \uc2 She also said the attacks hadn\u8217\'20\'19t let up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYesterday I opened up \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , and it said \u8216\'20\'18hey lady, you\u8217\'20\'19re a fraud,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Carroll said. \u8220\'20\'1CNow I\u8217\'20\'19m known as a liar, a fraud and a whack job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  is now known as X. Trump has also called Carroll a whack job.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, when asked by her lawyer if she regretted coming forward, Carroll said: \u8220\'20\'1COnly momentarily. I am very glad I took action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The defamation trial of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is about to resume, amid high drama, in court in New York, where plaintiff E Jean Carroll has been testifying, and the former US president is present.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some useful background context from Reuters:\par \par \uc2 Last May, a different jury ordered Trump to pay Carroll $5m, finding he had sexually abused in a \uc2 Bergdorf Goodman\uc2  department store dressing room in New York, and defamed her in 2022 by denying that anything happened.\par \par \uc2 In Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s trial, Carroll is seeking another $10m in compensatory damages, plus punitive damages.\par \par \uc2 Judge Lewis Kaplan has already ruled that Trump sexually abused Carroll in the dressing room by forcing his fingers into her vagina, and defamed her for two statements he made in 2019 when he was president.\par \par \uc2 Trump had claimed that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t know Carroll, and that she branded him a rapist to boost sales of her then-new memoir.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The court in New York is on break amid the trial in which writer E Jean Carroll has sued \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for defamation for remarks he made while president after she alleged publicly that he had raped her in the past.\par \par \uc2 One of Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers, Shawn Crowley, has had to complain twice to the judge, Lewis Kaplan, about Trump complaining about the case so loudly in court, while Carroll was testifying, that at least some of jury can probably hear him.\par \par \uc2 Before the break, Crowley said: \u8220\'20\'1CJust asking your honor to remind the parties that they\u8217\'20\'19re not supposed to make statements to or indirectly \u8211\'20\'13 the defendant has been making statements again [that] we can hear at counsel table\u8221\'20\'1D and added that jurors were sitting closer to Trump than the plaintiff\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge in E Jean Carroll case threatens to exclude Trump from court\par \par \uc2 Judge Lewis Kaplan has warned \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that his right to attend court in the defamation trial under way in New York, where the former president is the defendant in a civil case brought by writer E Jean Carroll, can be forfeited if he continues to disrupt proceedings.\par \par \uc2 Carroll has been testifying this morning and Trump, sitting with his lawyer, has been grumbling about the case, loudly enough that the jury can probably hear his remarks, Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s legal team has said.\par \par \uc2 The judge had already warned Trump to pipe down. Just before the court broke for lunch, Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s team complained to Judge Kaplan again. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CMr Trump has the right to be present here \u8211\'20\'13 that right can be forfeited and it can be forfeited if he is disruptive which is what has been reported to me and if he disregards court orders.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Addressing Trump, the judge said: \u8220\'20\'1CMr Trump, I hope I don\u8217\'20\'19t have to consider excluding you from the trial \u8230\'20\'26 I understand you are probably very eager for me to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump responded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would love it, I would love it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said and gestured.\par \par \uc2 The judge replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI know you would, you just can\u8217\'20\'19t control yourself in this circumstance apparently.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shawn Crowley, one of Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers, had said to the judge: \u8220\'20\'1CThe defendant has been making statements again [that] we can hear at counsel table.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She noted that some jurors are seated even closer to Trump than she is.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe said it is a \u8216\'20\'18witch-hunt,\u8217\'20\'19 it really is a \u8216\'20\'18con-job\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Crowley told the judge.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on another Trump presidency: 'I am scared as heck'\par \par \uc2 Speaking to The View, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said she is \u8220\'20\'1Cscared as heck\u8221\'20\'1D about another \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  presidency.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am scared as heck, which is why I\u8217\'20\'19m traveling our country. We should all be scared. But as we know, we don\u8217\'20\'19t run away from something when we\u8217\'20\'19re scared. We fight back against it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrVP \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on \u8220\'20\'1CThe View,\u8221\'20\'1D when asked if she\u8217\'20\'19s scared of another Trump presidency:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am scared as heck, which is why I'm traveling our country \u8230\'20\'26 We should all be scared. But as we know \u8230\'20\'26 we don't run away from something when we're scared; we fight back against it.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UYXfcIvAyj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UYXfcIvAyj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1747668216225177763?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With the E. Jean Carroll defamation trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  underway in a Manhattan courthouse, vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also made an appearance in the city where she took to The View\u8217\'20\'19s studios to comment on \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s remarks that the US has \u8220\'20\'1Cnever been a racist country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe issue of race in America is not something that should be the subject of a soundbite. The history of racism in America should never be the subject of a soundbite or a question that is meant to elicit a one sentence answer. But there is no denying that we have, in our history as a nation, racism, and that racism has played a role in the history of our nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrVP \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on \u8220\'20\'1CThe View\u8221\'20\'1D reacts to \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  saying that the United States has \u8220\'20\'1Cnever been a racist country\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no denying that we have, in our history as a nation, racism, and that racism has played a role in the history of our nation.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/s82KEq4SvJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/s82KEq4SvJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1747666869404766614?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 E Jean Carroll described the barrage of threats she has received in the years since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope you die soon. I hope someone really does attack, rape and murder you,\u8221\'20\'1D one missive presented in court stated. \u8220\'20\'1CYou deserve it all, you c--t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another simply said: \u8220\'20\'1CRape Jean rape Jean.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carroll described methods she has taken to protect herself at home in upstate New York. She bought a pitbull who goes leash-less on her property.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe now patrols very eagerly and enthusiastically,\u8221\'20\'1D Carroll said. She also purchased bullets for the gun that had belonged to her father.\par \par \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2  asked Carroll where she kept the gun.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy my bed,\u8221\'20\'1D Carroll said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge tells Trump to keep his voice down so the jury can't hear him\par \par \uc2 Before court resumed after the break, Judge Lewis Kaplan cautioned:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just going to ask Mr Trump to take special care to keep his voice down when conferring with counsel, so that the jury does not overhear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump loudly complains as Carroll testifies\par \par \uc2 As E Jean Carroll testified, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  complained audibly and appeared to double down on defamatory denials, her lawyer said during a morning break in the proceedings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr Trump has been sitting at the back table and has been loudly saying things throughout Ms Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s testimony,\u8221\'20\'1D said attorney Shawn Crowley.\par \par \uc2 They included claims that her comments were false and the statement, \u8220\'20\'1CShe now seems to have gotten her memory back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s loud enough for us to hear it,\u8221\'20\'1D Crowley said, so \u8220\'20\'1CI imagine it\u8217\'20\'19s loud enough for the jury to hear it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s public remarks about E Jean Carroll \u8220\'20\'1Cended the world I had been living in \u8221\'20\'1D, Carroll said in court, MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Kyle Griffin reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo have the president of the United States, one of the most powerful persons on earth, call me a liar for three days and say it 26 times \u8211\'20\'13 I counted them. It ended the world I had been living in and I lived in a new world,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carroll.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Carroll: 'I've paid just about as dearly as is possible to pay'\par \par \uc2 During her testimony, E Jean Carroll explained the chain of events that unfolded after the excerpt ran. Carroll said she had never told anyone publicly about the incident.\par \par \uc2 She said that the fact that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was president did factor into her decision to go public. \u8220\'20\'1CI took the responsibility and went ahead and did it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Carroll said she expected him to respond but not in the way that he did. \u8220\'20\'1CI expected him to deny it, but to say it was consensual, when it was not, but that\u8217\'20\'19s what I expected him to say,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIs that what Trump did?\u8221\'20\'1D asked Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s counsel, \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2 , who has no relation to Judge Lewis Kaplan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo,\u8221\'20\'1D Carroll said.\par \par \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2  referred to the language in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s denials.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe thing that really got me about this was, from the White House, he asked if anyone had any information about me and if they did, to please come forward as soon as possible, because he wanted the world to know what\u8217\'20\'19s really going on \u8211\'20\'13 and that people like me should pay dearly,\u8221\'20\'1D Carroll recalled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHave you paid dearly, Ms Carroll?\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve paid just about as dearly as is possible to pay,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carroll.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lead attorney in the case, Alina Habba, does not appear to be doing him any favors, repeatedly angering Judge Lewis Kaplan \u8211\'20\'13 a no-nonsense jurist who does not hold back in voicing his displeasure.\par \par \uc2 Habba irked Kaplan by once again asking for proceedings to be adjourned on Thursday, which is the scheduled date for his mother-in-law\u8217\'20\'19s funeral. Kaplan has denied this request on several occasions.\par \par \uc2 Kaplan said he would not hear another argument on it, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CNone, none, do you understand that word, none?\u8221\'20\'1D and told her to sit. Habba did not. \u8220\'20\'1CI said sit down,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kaplan.\par \par \uc2 She did not and said she wanted to discuss another thing. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t like to be spoken to that way, your honor,\u8221\'20\'1D Habba said. \u8220\'20\'1CI will ask you to refrain from speaking to me that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kaplan again said her request for an adjournment was denied. \u8220\'20\'1CSit down,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, his voice growing very stern.\par \par \uc2 Another time, Habba started to address the court while seated. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you speak in this courtroom or any other courtroom in this building, you stand up,\u8221\'20\'1D Kaplan warned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 When E Jean Carroll first took the stand, Trump could be seen whispering to his lead attorney, Alina Habba. He sat with slightly hunched shoulders as Carroll testified.\par \par \uc2 Following Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s initial remarks, one of her attorneys, \uc2 Roberta Kaplan\uc2 , asked the former Elle columnist questions about her career. Jurors heard how Carroll ascended from writing articles for high-profile publications to landing the columnist position, as well as a talkshow and authoring multiple books.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some images coming through the newswires of E Jean Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s defamation case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 E Jean Carroll, left, arrives at Manhattan federal court in New York on Wednesday. Photograph: Angela Weiss/AFP/Getty Images \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  leaves Trump Tower for Manhattan federal court for the second defamation trial against him on Wednesday. Photograph: Charly Triballeau/AFP/Getty Images The motorcade of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  arrives at Manhattan federal court in New York. Photograph: Angela Weiss/AFP/Getty Images \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Alina Habba, leaves Trump Tower for Manhattan federal court. Photograph: Charly Triballeau/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 E Jean Carroll: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  'lied and it shattered my reputation'\par \par \uc2 E Jean Carroll took the witness stand Wednesday morning in her defamation trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , marking the first time she confronted the ex-president in a courtroom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  assaulted me and when I wrote about it, he said it never happened,\u8221\'20\'1D Carroll testified. \u8220\'20\'1CHe lied, and it shattered my reputation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here to get my reputation back and to stop him from telling lies about me,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 E Jean Carroll is now on the stand, Victoria Bekiempis reports for the Guardian from the Manhattan courthouse.\par \par \uc2 We will bring you the latest updates from the trial.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  walked into the courtroom just before 10am in E Jean Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s second defamation trial against him.\par \par \uc2 The trial is in its second day and Carroll is expected to testify about how Trump\u8217\'20\'19s denials of her rape claim destroyed her reputation and resulted in threats. Carroll is expected to testify.\par \par \uc2 If Trump does stay for Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s testimony, this will mark the first time she will confront him in open court.\par \par \uc2 People hold signs outside the Manhattan federal court in New York for the second defamation trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Photograph: Angela Weiss/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  echoed \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s remarks of the US having \u8220\'20\'1Cnever been a racist country\u8221\'20\'1D, saying at Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s town hall, \u8220\'20\'1CThe US is not a racist country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, who is engaged in a self-described war on \u8220\'20\'1Cwokeness\u8221\'20\'1D involving LGBTQ+ communities, education and race, added, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve overcome things in our history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Republican governor of Florida also cited his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/02/ron-desantis-block-dei-program-state-colleges-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempts}}}\uc2  to ban diversity, equity and inclusion programs in his state, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThey say it\u8217\'20\'19s diversity, equity and inclusion, but it\u8217\'20\'19s really very ideological, and they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to impose an agenda\u8230\'20\'26 I think the way it\u8217\'20\'19s actually practiced, it stands for discrimination, exclusion and indoctrination, and it\u8217\'20\'19s wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Despite his legal woes, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his potential comeback as president remains at the forefront of discussions at the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  in Davos, Switzerland.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2024/01/17/davos-trumps-potential-return-to-white-house-is-dominating-small-talk.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speaking to}}}\uc2  CNBC, \uc2 Tim Adams\uc2 , president of the Institute of International Finance said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery question I\u8217\'20\'19ve gotten as I\u8217\'20\'19ve walked up and down the [Davos] Promenade today is, \u8216\'20\'18Is he coming back?\u8217\'20\'19\u8230\'20\'26 So I think there is a lot of interest in that question and what does that mean and who would be in the key positions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bill Winters\uc2 , CEO of \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe slight re-engagement that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing through the [Joe] Biden administration are an indication to me that the US is looking to stabilize [relations with China]\u8230\'20\'26 If Trump becomes president, we know that he\u8217\'20\'19s a transactional president, and there\u8217\'20\'19s probably a transaction in there someplace, that keeps the economy on an even keel, without fundamentally disrupting that relationship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Vera Jourova\uc2 , \uc2 European Commission\uc2  vice president, told CNBC:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Mr. Trump will become the president... we might see a strengthening of Russia and increasing of appetite of [Vladimir] Putin to grab more territory, and this directly endangering the security of our member states,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have concerns, we are preparing for any option.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 : US has 'never been a racist country'\par \par \uc2 The US has \u8220\'20\'1Cnever been a racist country,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  said in a recent Fox News interview.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Fox host Brian Kilmeade who asked the Republican presidential candidate whether the Republican party is racist, Haley responded, \u8220\'20\'1CNo. We\u8217\'20\'19re not a racist country. We\u8217\'20\'19ve never been a racist country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She went on to add, \u8220\'20\'1COur goal is to make sure that today is better than yesterday. Are we perfect? No. But our goal is to always make sure we try and be more perfect every day that we can.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haley also said, \u8220\'20\'1CI know, I faced racism when I was growing up. But I can tell you, today is a lot better than it was then.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNikki Haley: "We've never been a racist country" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qcB0wTjvJS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qcB0wTjvJS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1747275515789287839?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 A few weeks ago at a campaign event, Haley {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/28/nikki-haley-civil-war-slavery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined}}}\uc2  to say that slavery was the cause of the US civil war, instead saying that the war involved \u8220\'20\'1Cbasically how the government was going to run\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe freedoms of what people could and couldn\u8217\'20\'19t do\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Haley later walked back on her remarks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_iWLPUS7wq4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying,}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1COf course\u8221\'20\'1D the US civil war was about slavery.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 During his town hall on Tuesday with CNN, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  also questioned his opponent \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ability to bring Republicans together.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/01/16/politics/takeaways-town-hall-ron-desantis/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speaking to}}}\uc2  CNN host Wolf Blitzer, DeSantis said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s great in a general election to build a big tent\u8230\'20\'26but to win a Republican primary\u8230\'20\'26you gotta be able to win core Republicans, you gotta be able to win conservatives, and she can\u8217\'20\'19t do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to add:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe does not have the ability to win the kind of coalition that you need to win a Republican primary \u8211\'20\'13 period, much less take on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  says Republicans will lose election with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as nominee\par \par \uc2 Florida governor and Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Ron DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/01/16/politics/takeaways-town-hall-ron-desantis/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  warned}}}\uc2  that if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  becomes the Republican presidential nominee, then Republicans are \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to lose\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis cited Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mounting legal issues as distraction to the election, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the nominee, the election will revolve around all these legal issues, his trials, perhaps convictions if he goes to trials and loses there and about things like January 6.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a CNN town hall on Tuesday, he added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to lose if voters are making a decision based on that. We don\u8217\'20\'19t want it to be a referendum on those issues. We want it to be a referendum on the country going in the wrong direction and a candidate like me being a president that can reverse the decline.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s comments follow his second-place finish at the Iowa caucuses earlier this week, where he landed 30 percentage points behind Trump and two points ahead of \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , former South Carolina governor and the US ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  under Trump.\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House is set to convene at 10am on border security legislation with first votes expected at 1.30pm ET, Politico Playbook {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/playbook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 ABC News has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/16/new-hampshire-debate-trump-nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancelled}}}\uc2  the next Republican presidential debate after Haley said she would not participate without Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An aide to defense secretary Lloyd Austin who called 911 for an ambulance asked the ambulance to \u8220\'20\'1Cnot show up with lights and sirens\u8221\'20\'1D, a newly unveiled recording has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/01/16/politics/austin-911-audio-walter-reed/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240117ek1h0028q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
