\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Iowa caucuses 2024: Trump wins state as DeSantis projected to win second place \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh, Rachel Leingang, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Yohannes Lowe \par \uc2 20,011 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 January 2024\par 02:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ex-president beats Republican rivals as DeSantis finishes a distant second, Haley slides into third place and Ramaswamy drops outIowa results tracker: how the candidates rankTrump wins in Iowa as contest kicks off 2024 election race\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Iowa caucus recap\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won by a landslide in Iowa Monday, with \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  trailing in a distant second and third place, respectively. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s victory was so clear and decisive that the Associated Press projected his win just 30 minutes after the caucuses began \u8211\'20\'13 much to the ire of DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A jubilant Trump offered an unusually conciliatory call for unity in his speech Monday night. \u8220\'20\'1CI really think this is time now for everybody, our country, to come together,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. He also celebrated poll findings that the majority of Iowa Republics did not accept the validity of the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Delegates will be allocated proportionally, once all the votes from across the state have been tabulated. But the night\u8217\'20\'19s results are a big blow to both DeSantis and Haley. The former, especially, invested massive amounts of time and effort in the state, visiting all 99 of Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s counties.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 DeSantis told supporters at his watch party Monday night, \u8220\'20\'1CI can tell you because of your support, in spite of all of that, that they threw at us \u8211\'20\'13 everyone against us \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19ve got our ticket punched out of Iowa.\u8221\'20\'1D Haley, meanwhile, insisted that this was a \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo-person race\u8221\'20\'1D between her and Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  finished fourth and ended his campaign, endorsing Trump as he bowed out.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Frigid conditions and chilly winds, which the National Weather Service said made for dangerous conditions across the state, may have impacted turnout, which is estimated to be notably lower than 2016.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/15/donald-trump-wins-iowa-caucus-republicans-nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump wins in Iowa as Republican contest kicks off 2024 presidential race}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 When he arrived on stage to chants of \u8220\'20\'1CRon, Ron, Ron\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  cast the night as a successful stand against an array of forces his enemies had deployed against him.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis greets supporters at his caucus night event. Photograph: Anna Moneymaker/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey threw everything but the kitchen sink at us,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, pointing to his opponents\u8217\'20\'19 spending on ads targeting him, and negative coverage his campaign received from news outlets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut they were just so excited about the fact that they were predicting that we wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be able to get our ticket punched here out of Iowa. But, I can tell you because of your support, in spite of all of that, that they threw at us \u8212\'20\'14 everyone against us \u8212\'20\'14 we\u8217\'20\'19ve got our ticket punched out of Iowa.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Finishing second in the state is the best result DeSantis could realistically hope for, and will keep his campaign alive going into New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s primary on 23 January. However, it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if he can replicate that result in the Granite State, where \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  has seen a polling surge recently that may have put her within striking distance of Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a striking visual from NBC election tabulator Steve Kornacki, who points out that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has virtually accomplished a sweep of Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s 99 counties.\par \par \uc2 enltrAnd by a margin of 1 vote \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  appears to have won Johnson County (Iowa City), leaving \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that close to a 99-county sweep: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MI5bearyPx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MI5bearyPx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Kornacki (@SteveKornacki) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SteveKornacki/status/1747118323785932839?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  addressed her supporters as well, thanking Iowans, who she called \u8220\'20\'1Cfaithful and patriotic Americans\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Haley speaks at her caucus night event. Photograph: Joe Raedle/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can safely say, tonight Iowa safely made this Republican primary a two person race,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe question before Americans now is very clear \u8211\'20\'13 do you want more of the same, or do you want a new generation of conservative leadership.\par \par \uc2 Haley appears to be referencing to a race between her and Trump \u8211\'20\'13 but her path ahead after sliding into a distant third tonight remains unclear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur campaign is the last best hope of stopping the Trump-Biden nightmare,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey threw everything but the kitchen sink at us,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , speaking to supporters in Des Moines.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis speaks at his caucus night event on in West Des Moines. Photograph: Scott Olson/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 After all the time and funds his campaign poured into Iowa, his performance tonight will be a disappointment. But his candidacy has survived to fight another day. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got our ticket punched out of Iowa,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  cinches second place, AP projects\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor has finished a \u8220\'20\'1Cdistant second\u8221\'20\'1D to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the Associated Press projects. \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  is expected to come third.\par \par \uc2 enltrFlorida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has finished a distant second to former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Iowa's leadoff Republican caucuses. Former \uc2 U.N.\uc2  Ambassador \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  came in third. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yjeQ0DE6WV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/yjeQ0DE6WV}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9qhTgBX1yF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9qhTgBX1yF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Associated Press (@AP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1747112357317202425?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  drops out\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no path for me to be the next president absent things that we don\u8217\'20\'19t want to see happen in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  told supporters in Des Moines.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy speaks at his caucus night event at the Surety Hotel in Des Moines, Iowa. Photograph: Kevin Dietsch/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 He reflected on his candidacy. \u8220\'20\'1CNobody knew who we were, nobody knew what we were up to, but together, we have created a movement that I think is going to carry our nation to the next level,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 He endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s watch party is getting underway, with social conservative activist Bob Vander Plaats pitching the Florida governor as the right candidate to beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Supporters of Republican presidential candidate Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  wait for him to walk out to speak during a caucus night party, Monday, Jan. 15, 2024, in West Des Moines, Iowa. (AP Photo/Charlie Neibergall) Photograph: Charlie Neibergall/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow we will have a real fight between whether or not we\u8217\'20\'19re going to return to someone who has proven all he knows how to do is lose to Democrats. Him and his candidates, for the last three cycles, that\u8217\'20\'19s all they\u8217\'20\'19ve done. For the rest of the country, tired of losing to these guys, let\u8217\'20\'19s go with the guy who beat them and that is \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Vander Plaats said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nearly two-thirds of Iowa Republicans polled while entering the caucuses on Monday evening by Edison Research said they did not believe \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  legitimately won the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 A majority of the 1,577 caucus-goers the firm questioned said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would be fit to return to the presidency even if he were convicted of a crime. And nearly half of the respondents said they considered themselves part of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s MAGA movement.\par \par \uc2 The results underline Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hold on the Republican party in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Reuters on the results:\par \par \uc2 Following are highlights from the Edison Research poll based on interviews with 1,577 Iowa Republicans. The results will be updated as more interviews are collected.\par \par \uc2 * 65% said they did not think Biden legitimately won the presidency in 2020.\par \par \uc2 * 64% said they decided who to support in the presidential nomination contest before this month.\par \par \uc2 * 63% said Trump would still be fit to be president if he were convicted of a crime. 32% said he would be unfit if convicted.\par \par \uc2 * 59% said they favor a federal law that would ban abortions nationwide.\par \par \uc2 * 51% of white caucus-goers who considered themselves evangelical or born-again Christians supported Trump, while 29% backed DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 * 44% of voters said they considered themselves part of the MAGA movement, a reference to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Make America Great Again slogan. 51% said they were not part of that movement.\par \par \uc2 * Trump led Haley and DeSantis by double digits among men and women alike. But among college graduates Trump was preferred by about 36% of caucus-goers, compared to 30% for Haley and 27% for DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 * 37% percent of caucus-goers said the economy was the issue that mattered most in deciding who to vote for on Monday, compared to 34% who cited immigration, while the rest cited foreign policy or \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * 14% said the most important quality a Republican presidential nominee should have is the ability to beat Biden, compared to 41% who said shared values mattered most.\par \par \uc2 Edison Research conducted the poll on behalf of the National Election Pool, a consortium of news organizations including Reuters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  is dropping out of the race, per multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  recites the Pledge of Allegiance as he visits a caucus site at Horizon Event Center in Clive, Iowa. Photograph: Sergio Flores/Reuters\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear who he\u8217\'20\'19ll endorse once he\u8217\'20\'19s out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is still talking, and after he delivered a few likely planned lines on unity, he\u8217\'20\'19s started improvising, as he\u8217\'20\'19s wont to.\par \par \uc2 Calling for law and order, the former president referenced the defacement of the Capitol on January 6.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: "We're gonna scrub those marble columns and get the swastickers off them." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WbcGh7jAOV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WbcGh7jAOV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1747109945978298513?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 He also boasted about polling showing that the majority of caucusgoers questioned the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s caucus night watch party is taking place at a Sheraton hotel in West Des Moines.\par \par \uc2 A scene from \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 's Iowa caucus watch party, in West Des Moines. Photograph: Alyssa Pointer/Reuters\par \par \uc2 A ballroom packed with supporters, reporters and children is waiting for the Florida governor, but there\u8217\'20\'19s no sign of him yet. Perhaps he\u8217\'20\'19s waiting to find out for sure whether he finished in second or third.\par \par \uc2 If it\u8217\'20\'19s the latter, many believe it would be a crushing blow to his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s viability. But with a second place finish, he could make the case to supporters that he has a path forward in New Hampshire, the next state to vote in the GOP nomination process.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 An estimated 100,000 voters participated in the caucus today, according to the Iowa Republican Party chairman, Jeff Kaufmann.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s far short of the 187,000 Republicans who caucused in 2016.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe are on track to have nearly 100k Iowans participating in the 2024 Caucus despite freezing temperatures and our beautiful state being blanketed in snow just two days ago.\par \par \uc2 Iowans will brave the cold for the future of their families, communities, and country.\par \par \uc2 THANK YOU, IOWA!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeff Kaufmann (@kaufmannGOP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaufmannGOP/status/1747107045692629355?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump speaks in Des Moines\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is addressing a cheering crowd in Des Moines. \u8220\'20\'1CI really think this is time now for everybody, our country, to come together,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Trump speaks during his Iowa caucus night watch party in Des Moines. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Caucusgoers faced sub-zero temperatures and bitter winds, which may have affected turnout today. The National Weather Service warned of \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous weather\u8221\'20\'1D and warned people to \u8220\'20\'1Cavoid outside activities if possible.\u8221\'20\'1D Parts of the state were also under a wind chill advisory.\par \par \uc2 Signs in support of \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  are displayed at a caucus site at Horizon Event Center in Clive, Iowa. Photograph: Sergio Flores/Reuters\par \par \uc2 These caucuses were officially the coldest on record \u8211\'20\'13 even colder than 2004 when Des Moines had a low temperature of 2F. The high in Des Moines is 1F.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump won so quickly that not many people had yet gathered at his election watch party in Des Moines. There was no great cheer to celebrate the moment.\par \par \uc2 But now hundreds of Trump supporters are in a cavernous hall at the Iowa Events Center, many sporting \u8220\'20\'1CMaga\u8221\'20\'1D regalia. Among them are Florida congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , former Arizona gubernatorial candidate Kari Lake and notorious far-right extremist Laura Loomer.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wait for him to speak at the Iowa Events Center. Photograph: Jim Lo Scalzo/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Two giant screens proclaim: TRUMP WINS IOWA! in white letters on a black background, then switch to Fox News. Between them is a big US national flag and a row of more US national flags. Golden oldies by Elvis and others \u8211\'20\'13 and from the musical The Phantom of the Opera \u8211\'20\'13 are booming from loudspeakers.\par \par \uc2 A lectern has \u8220\'20\'1CTrump: Make America great again\u8221\'20\'1D written on it. He is expected to give a victory speech sooner or later.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 Economy, border, foreign policy: key issues for Iowans\par \par \uc2 David Erlacher hadn\u8217\'20\'19t made up his mind about who he was going to caucus for when he showed up to a Cedar Rapids brewery to hear {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2  speak on Sunday afternoon. But inside his jacket pocket was a handwritten list of issues that mattered most to him.\par \par \uc2 At the top was the economy, followed by the southern border. He then listed a series of foreign policy conflicts, including the Houthi attacks in Yemen, the war in Israel, and the war between Ukraine and Russia.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , right, speaks during a campaign event at Jerseys Pub and Grub in Cedar Rapids, Iowa. Photograph: Nick Rohlman/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe world\u8217\'20\'19s a dumpster fire right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Erlacher, a 76-year-old retiree who lives in Cedar Rapids, said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe got to try and find some water to throw on it. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure how that\u8217\'20\'19s gonna happen. I\u8217\'20\'19m just glad there\u8217\'20\'19s smarter people than myself out there to do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Those three priorities \u8211\'20\'13 the economy, the border and international instability \u8211\'20\'13 echoed what many Iowa voters said were their top issues as they prepared to caucus in the US\u8217\'20\'19s first nominating contest on Monday, with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and DeSantis at the top. A November Des Moines Register/NBC News/Mediacom Iowa Poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/iowa-poll/caucus/2023/11/01/iowa-poll-how-republican-caucusgoers-rank-issues-from-the-economy-to-abortion-israel-ukraine/71328389007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that 81% of likely caucusgoers listed the economy as a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery important issue\u8221\'20\'1D and 80% of caucusgoers listed \u8220\'20\'1Cimmigration and border security as \u8220\'20\'1Cvery important issues\u8221\'20\'1D in the same poll.\par \par \uc2 Concerns over the economy underscore a significant challenge for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as he seeks a second term. Traditional metrics have shown that the US economy is strong, but nearly two-thirds of Americans are unhappy with it, according to a September Harris survey {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/15/biden-economy-bidenomics-poll-republicans-democrats-independents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conducted}}}\uc2  by the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Kevin Hochstedler, 65, who works in home construction in Iowa City, was one of several voters who said his top issues were \u8220\'20\'1Cnumber one the economy, number two, southern border\u8221\'20\'1D. Hochstedler, who planned to caucus for Haley, said he had seen a huge slowdown in his industry. He blamed the federal reserve for raising interest rates too quickly.\par \par \uc2 A supporter in a wall-printed suit and a Maga hat awaited \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who plans to speak at a Des Moines caucus night party. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe economy is slowing, slowing, slowing, it\u8217\'20\'19s like a giant sucking sound,\u8221\'20\'1D Hochstedler said at a Saturday event for Haley, whom he planned to support on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Hochstedler was one of several voters who said they were outraged by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s handling of migrants at the US-Mexico border. He said he supported the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/texas-is-blocking-u-s-border-agents-from-patrolling-biden-administration-tells-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state of Texas }}}\uc2  in an ongoing dispute with the Biden administration over policing the border. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I were governor of Texas, I\u8217\'20\'19d call in the national guard, block it all off and keep the people in Mexico.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-key-issues-voters-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Economy, border, foreign policy: key issues as Iowans head to caucus}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Lincoln Project, the anti-Trump Republican group, said that the results today make clear that Trump will win the nomination.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been obvious for months that Trump would crush his rivals and will win the nomination. Dems and independents must wake up to the threat he poses. He will destroy individual rights and empower dictators overseas. Biden is the only one who can stop him and keep America safe,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gregory Minchak, the group\u8217\'20\'19s communications director.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Retired farmer Ron Osborn\u8217\'20\'19s reason for supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who won the most votes in Malcom, was simple.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he\u8217\'20\'19s the only one who can beat the cheating Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D the 73-year-old said.\par \par \uc2 Terry Stanek said he had voted the same way because he believed Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only one who wants to build the wall, wipe out the cartels and stop the fentanyl\u8221\'20\'1D as well as reduce inflation.\par \par \uc2 To the 67-year-old, who restores classic cars, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s four years in office were a far more placid period than the tumult he sees today, specifically the conflict between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s chaotic withdrawal of US forces from Afghanistan in 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, when Trump was in office, it was a calm planet,\u8221\'20\'1D Stanek said.\par \par \uc2 He believed the former president can best the current one in November \u8220\'20\'1Cif it\u8217\'20\'19s a fair election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf it\u8217\'20\'19s not a fair election, no one can beat him,\u8221\'20\'1D Stanek said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This live blog was amended on 16 January 2024 to reflect the correct spelling of a town in Iowa: it is Malcom, not Malcolm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Farmer Jane Axmear said she was one of four people at the Malcom caucus to vote for \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  because the former South Carolina governor is the best choice to protect \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen\u8217\'20\'19s rights\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 including access to abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s right for some people isn\u8217\'20\'19t right for everyone,\u8221\'20\'1D the 57-year-old said of efforts by Republican elected officials nationwide to ban the procedure, or at thresholds so early that they\u8217\'20\'19re before most women realize they are pregnant. \u8220\'20\'1CA 12-year-old shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be forced to have a kid because she made a mistake,\u8221\'20\'1D Axmear said.\par \par \uc2 The question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access has vexed Republicans ever since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022, and is also credited with giving momentum to Democratic candidates who have campaigned on restoring the former precedent. Haley {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/29/republicans-democrats-abortion-plans-election-2024-trump-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has suggested }}}\uc2  that, as president, she would support any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions that Congress approves, while saying such legislation was unlikely to be passed.\par \par \uc2 Asked why she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t considering voting for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democrats, Axmear said the party\u8217\'20\'19s philosophy on other issues did not appeal to her as a corn, soy and cattle farmer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe in a handout,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn farming, you take a risk every day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some images from caucuses across the state.\par \par \uc2 Voters walk into a caucus site at Interstate-35 high school in Truro, Iowa. Photograph: Lily Smith/AP A person collects votes at a caucus site to choose a Republican presidential candidate at Fellows elementary school, in Ames, Iowa. Photograph: Cheney Orr/Reuters Caucusgoers sign in before a Republican caucus at Stutsman\u8217\'20\'19s Agricultural Products and Services in Hills, Iowa. Photograph: Geoff Stellfox/AP Nancy Voigt speaks on behalf of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  during a caucus at the home of Silver City mayor, Sharon McNutt, and her husband, Gary. Photograph: Scott Morgan/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 DeSantis campaign complains about vote call for Trump\par \par \uc2 The DeSantis campaign isn\u8217\'20\'19t too happy with the AP\u8217\'20\'19s call in favor of Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is absolutely outrageous that the media would participate in election interference by calling the race before tens of thousands of Iowans even had a chance to vote,\u8221\'20\'1D said DeSantis communications director Andrew Romeo. \u8220\'20\'1CThe media is in the tank for Trump and this is the most egregious example yet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 (To be clear: the AP\u8217\'20\'19s projection in favor of Trump does not amount to interference, and was based on polls and early results.)\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Malcom, chemical company worker Brad Hamilton, 53, used to support \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , but was pulled into \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s camp after seeing him speak at the Iowa state fair. Hamilton voted for DeSantis at his caucus site, where he came in a close second to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , because he thought the Florida governor would be more effective at governing in Washington than Trump, who he had supported in the past.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just a friggin clown show right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Hamilton told me after the vote. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be nice to have smoother politics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Isaac Hammond of Grinnell braves the sub-zero weather for caucus night on Monday in Malcom, Iowa. Photograph: Geoff Stellfox/AP\par \par \uc2 Saying he was concerned about foreign militant groups like \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  and the Houthis, Hamilton, an army veteran, said America needed to look strong on the world stage, and he believed DeSantis could achieve that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor some reason, I think we\u8217\'20\'19ve come at the world with a look of weakness,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think we need to calm this whole world down. It\u8217\'20\'19s getting out of hand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign celebrating win\par \par \uc2 The Trump camp is celebrating a victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe people of Iowa sent a clear message tonight: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be the next Republican nominee for President. It\u8217\'20\'19s now time to make him the next president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alex Pfeiffer, communications director for Make America Great Again Inc, the Super Pac backing Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  to face reality and stop wasting time and resources.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 It took only a half an hour for the AP to declare \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the winner of the Iowa caucuses, but some precincts hadn\u8217\'20\'19t even started voting when the result was announced.\par \par \uc2 Here in West Des Moines, the precinct was just wrapping up speeches from candidate representatives when networks started calling the race for Trump.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs multiple networks declare \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the winner of the Iowa caucuses, voting is just getting underway at this precinct in West Des Moines. (Please note the repurposed HyVee grocery bag for ballots.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bANj57BDGl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bANj57BDGl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1747070149813735666?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Even with the outcome known, caucusgoers proceeded to cast their ballots, which were thrown into a repurposed grocery bag before being counted by officials.\par \par \uc2 In the end, Trump won both precincts here, although \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  came in a close second in one precinct. In the other precinct, DeSantis and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  tied for second place.\par \par \uc2 Haley is expected to soon deliver remarks at the hotel in West Des Moines where those two precincts just concluded voting.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 They just announced the results of the caucus here at Kingston steakhouse in Cedar Rapids:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  got 38 votes, followed by \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , who got 22. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  got 17 votes and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  got 7 votes.\par \par \uc2 Asa Hutchinson got 0 votes. One person voted \u8220\'20\'1Cother\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here in Cedar Rapids, where the caucus is still happening, a speaker for \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  also did away with prepared remarks in favor of a more improvisational speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s not beholden to big donors. He\u8217\'20\'19s so eloquent. If you get him onstage with anybody, he\u8217\'20\'19s gonna come out ahead,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Brett Mason, dressed in a red Make America Great Again (Maga) hat, gave the speech nominating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He said that when Trump ran in 2016 he thought was was \u8220\'20\'1Ccapricious\u8221\'20\'1D and that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cslow to get on that bandwagon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , right, listens as Republican presidential candidate former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speaks at a caucus site in Clive, Iowa. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 But now, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Che has a record\u8221\'20\'1D. He also said \u8220\'20\'1Cit was kind of crazy all the conspiracies turned out to be true\u8221\'20\'1D and went on to talk about the Hunter Biden laptop story.\par \par \uc2 He also said Trump was approachable and that he had the chance to meet him a month or so ago. Mason said he asked Trump why he was running and Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a landslide election in 2020 - America put me in there and I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to drop the ball for them.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump lost both the popular vote and the electoral college to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 The cacuses are still under way, and the fight for second place still continues.\par \par \uc2 Votes are counted during a caucus to choose a Republican presidential candidate, at Fellows Elementary School, in Ames, Iowa. Photograph: Cheney Orr/Reuters\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s entrance polls, which were taken as caucusgoers arrived at their sites, found that the majority identified with the \u8220\'20\'1CMaga movement\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to the \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D movement started by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . That gives you a bit of an idea of where voters were ahead of the voting tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins the Republican presidential caucuses in Iowa, AP projects\par \par \uc2 The caucuses kicked off just 30 minutes ago, but the Associated Press has already made its call for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A person votes for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a caucus site in Ames. Photograph: Cheney Orr/Reuters\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise \u8211\'20\'13 Trump has been by far the frontrunner. \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  are in a high-stakes fight for second place. How big Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory is, and how closely behind Haley and DeSantis trail could set the tone for how the rest of the primaries pan out.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 With the ballots counted, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  came out on top in Malcom, Iowa, with \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in a close second.\par \par \uc2 The final tally was 10 votes for Trump, eight for DeSantis, four for ex-South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and one for Ryan Binkley, a pastor and long-shot candidate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 A man who did not give his name just gave a speech on behalf of \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and decried fellow Republicans attacking each other.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we want to defeat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , good lord folks, we can\u8217\'20\'19t let that slip away by attacking one another. Whoever the Republicans nominee is I\u8217\'20\'19m voting for them,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. He also spoke about Haley\u8217\'20\'19s experience on the international stage and standing by America\u8217\'20\'19s allies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 Voting wrapped up quickly, and they\u8217\'20\'19re counting ballots now.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mR79GSQWAt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mR79GSQWAt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1747067951121887385?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is going to win,\u8221\'20\'1D a voter said, as they counted ballots. \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason why the news media is attacking him is because they and the Democrats are afraid of him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Malcom, precinct chair Rick Jacoby is now making his case for nominating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he\u8217\'20\'19s done a great job for us in the past. I think he will do a great job for us in the future,\u8221\'20\'1D Jacoby said.\par \par \uc2 Another caucusgoer spoke in favor of Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am afraid that as much as I supported \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the last two elections, I\u8217\'20\'19m afraid that he has gotten so much negative against him, between the press and the Democrat party, that he will be ineffective if he gets elected,\u8221\'20\'1D the voter said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, a voter piped up to say he did not think DeSantis should stand. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s got a job already, he\u8217\'20\'19s the governor of Florida. That\u8217\'20\'19s what he needs to focus on,\u8221\'20\'1D the voter said.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re now handing out ballots to determine who will win this precinct.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here at Kingston steakhouse in Cedar Rapids, speeches on behalf of candidates are getting under way. Barrett Hubbard, the caucus chair, is giving remarks on behalf of DeSantis. Many of the lines are similar or identical to what I\u8217\'20\'19ve heard DeSantis say on the campaign trail the last few days.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe precinct chair is explaining how the various conventions work - county, congressional district, state, national. Speeches on behalf of candidates are about to begin. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7OKlZS1j8I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7OKlZS1j8I}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1747064955805827145?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDC is swampier today than ever before,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is running on his own issues, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  is running for her donors\u8217\'20\'19 issues and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is running for the issues theater matter to the American people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re kicking things off here in Malcom with the pledge of allegiance and a prayer.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s also the matter of Rick Jacoby \u8217\'20\'19s role. He\u8217\'20\'19s the temporary caucus precinct chair, because the person who was originally supposed to do it got sick. He asked the attendees to elect him the permanent chair, and they granted it.\par \par \uc2 A major component of the caucuses is local Republican party business. Jacoby is passing around an envelope for donations to the party, and looking for people to serve on the county central committee and attend the county convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  asked if he would run in 2028\par \par \uc2 On a night when the 2024 race for the White House gets under way, some people are already talking about 2028.\par \par \uc2 At a Trump campaign event in Ankeny, Iowa, a voter asked \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  if he would consider a run next time. His girlfriend Kimberly Guilfoyle exclaimed: \u8220\'20\'1COh, god.\u8221\'20\'1D Don Jr, 46, looked over at her and shouted: \u8220\'20\'1CHey, princess, you ready for this?\u8221\'20\'1D She replied: \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s go, Iowa!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Don Jr then told the audience of 62 seated supporters: \u8220\'20\'1CYou never know. Listen, I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to say no because then if you decide to do it, like, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, my God, he\u8217\'20\'19s a major liar\u8217\'20\'19, you know... I guess the answer is I will continue to fight no matter what. The question is do you want the day job of actually doing it?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another voter asked Don Jr if he believes his father was anointed by God. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s eldest son replied: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not for me to decide. There\u8217\'20\'19s a higher power that decides that. But I\u8217\'20\'19ll say he\u8217\'20\'19s fought for this country where he\u8217\'20\'19s taking on forces that probably no one else has, certainly in modern history, and I think he\u8217\'20\'19s delivered accordingly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Arriving two and a half hours late because of a weather delayed flight, Don Jr endorsed \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat replacement theory\u8221\'20\'1D, arguing that Democrats are deliberately importing people more likely to vote for them. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s literally more illegal immigrants coming across our border now on an annualised basis than there are babies born in America,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not racist; it\u8217\'20\'19s just statistics and facts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also took swipes at his father\u8217\'20\'19s rivals in the Iowa caucuses. \u8220\'20\'1CWho here thinks it\u8217\'20\'19s acceptable for men to be wearing high heels while running for the Republican nomination for president of the United States?\u8221\'20\'1D he asked in a clear dig at Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who has faced claims that he wears heel lifts to make him look taller.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  has never met a war she didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to be in,\u8221\'20\'1D Don Jr added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe would be fighting, like, a 30-front war.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 In the Iowa caucuses, the task of persuading attendees to vote for a certain candidate falls to the precinct captains.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tCSez2XeC9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tCSez2XeC9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1747061307923190223?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Rick Jacoby is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s temporary precinct caucus chair at the site where I am \u8211\'20\'13 and also the only captain in attendance for any candidate.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he expects captains for any other contender to show up, Jacoby, who is also checking in voters as the precinct chair, replied, \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be nice, but we\u8217\'20\'19ll see what happens\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Much has been made about whether the chilly weather Iowans are enduring will keep them from caucusing. Jacoby isn\u8217\'20\'19t buying it. \u8220\'20\'1CIowans are used to cold weather,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 There are also five members of the press in attendance, indicating the interest in covering caucuses that happen in unusual settings.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Scott Duffy, a 46-year-old engineer, arrived early here to the caucus at the Kingston steakhouse in Cedar Rapids. He\u8217\'20\'19s supporting \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe seems to get it and he\u8217\'20\'19s not afraid to talk to you guys [the press], talk to anybody,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19ll get down to it, he\u8217\'20\'19ll get deep into the details on it. It\u8217\'20\'19s not the boilerplate standard politician lines from everyone else. He\u8217\'20\'19s a smart dude,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He acknowledged that Trump is the \u8220\'20\'1Codds on favorite,\u8221\'20\'1D but I\u8217\'20\'19m not particularly fond of how he ran the country, especially in 2020. And then he caused a lot of problems in this country that I\u8217\'20\'19m not real happy with.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added that he was interested to see how the weather affected turnout. He said he had seen rural roads nearby that were not yet plowed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve just arrived at the Heartland Co-op grain elevator, which is the caucus site for Malcom, Iowa, a town of a few hundred people located 62 miles east of Des Moines.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CrgiXQXZzQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CrgiXQXZzQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1747053021731623027?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 So far, about a dozen cacusgoers are in the chilly, spartan basement of the grain elevator\u8217\'20\'19s office, where the caucus is to be held.\par \par \uc2 Malcom is located in Poweshiek county, which is among the rural Iowa counties that trended Democratic through \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s term, but shifted Republican after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ran in 2016. The county, and Malcom itself, voted for him in both the 2016 and in 2020 general elections.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to find out tonight if the town\u8217\'20\'19s Republicans think he is the right candidate to take on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m at a caucus site inside the Kingston steakhouse in Cedar Rapids, and Brett Mason, who\u8217\'20\'19s manning the registration table here, just informed caucusgoers that they couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get the room unless they bought hors d\u8217\'20\'19oeuvres. So the county GOP party bought everyone free hors d\u8217\'20\'19oeuvres that are being served on a buffet. People are now flocking to it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bar is open but that\u8217\'20\'19s your own wallet,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 Caucuses in Iowa kick off\par \par \uc2 The caucuses are now under way, with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  widely expected to be declared the winner.\par \par \uc2 Voters are gathering at schools, steakhouses, churches, and even living rooms and grain elevators to decide the Republican presidential nominee. Today marks the first round of voting in the 2024 presidential primary.\par \par \uc2 Eligible voters, who have braved brutally cold conditions today to show up at their caucus location, will discuss candidates and issues with their neighbors. Representatives will speak up in behalf of their preferred candidates.\par \par \uc2 Within an hour or so, caucusgoers write their preferred candidate\u8217\'20\'19s name on a slip of paper and hand it to the caucus chair of the caucus, who tallies the votes and release results to the state party, which will tally all the results. Candidates are then assigned delegates to the Republican national convention proportional to their share of the statewide votes.\par \par \uc2 First results are expected before 9pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/12/what-are-iowa-caucuses-2024-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What are the Iowa caucuses and how will they shape the 2024 US election?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 With less than one hour left until the start of the Iowa caucuses, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18s campaign is setting up at a hotel in West Des Moines, where the former South Carolina governor and \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador will address supporters later tonight.\par \par \uc2 enltrGreetings from West Des Moines. \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  will address supporters in this ballroom later tonight. Less than one hour until the Iowa caucuses start. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5FRscCmki3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5FRscCmki3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1747049216000557106?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Haley is hoping for a strong second place finish tonight, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is widely expected to cruise to victory in Iowa. But Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is also hoping to secure second place and has devoted considerable resources to turning out voters across Iowa.\par \par \uc2 Regardless of Haley\u8217\'20\'19s performance tonight, once the caucuses end, she will quickly turn her attention to New Hampshire, where she has seen momentum in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/new-hampshire/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FiveThirtyEight average}}}\uc2  of New Hampshire polls, Haley is now roughly 11 points behind Trump, having cut his lead in half over the past month.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve just arrived at Kingston steakhouse, a caucus site here in Cedar Rapids. Dinner is being served in the front and voters are slowly checking in and are seated around round tables. The caucus will get started at 7pm CT.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m here at Kingston steakhouse in Cedar Rapids, which is a caucus site. The restaurant is open in the front and the caucus is being held in an event space in the back. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sCZ4WNOPYy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sCZ4WNOPYy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1747049303586000960?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/vivek-ramaswamy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy}}}\uc2 , the biotech entrepreneur who has gone all in on Iowa to jumpstart his presidential bid, urged supporters not to believe the polls.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  speaks during a "Commit to Caucus" rally at Lion Bridge Brewing in Cedar Rapids, Iowa. Photograph: Savannah Blake/AP\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy has visited all 99 counties {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/elections/presidential/caucus/2024/01/15/vivek-ramaswamy-makes-caucus-day-pitch-insists-will-win-iowa-contest/72226924007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Iowa twice}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/elections/presidential/caucus/2023/11/01/vivek-ramaswamy-rents-des-moines-apartment-as-he-hones-in-on-iowa/71412699007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even rented}}}\uc2  an apartment in Des Moines during the final stretch of the campaign. He said on Monday he had done nearly 400 events in the state.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/iowa-poll/caucus/2024/01/13/iowa-poll-nikki-haley-leads-ron-desantis-ahead-of-republican-caucus-night-big-lead-for-donald-trump/72216523007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A final Des Moines Register/NBC News/Mediacom Iowa poll}}}\uc2  on Saturday showed him with the support of 8% of likely Republican caucusgoers, trailing \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  for second place. DeSantis registered support with 16% of likely GOP caucusgoers while Haley had 20%. Trump held a commanding lead of 48% of likely caucusgoers in the poll.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen is bordering on a kind of election interference in our GOP primary,\u8221\'20\'1D he told about 100 supporters on Monday. He went on to claim that his name wasn\u8217\'20\'19t being included in polls when voters were asked who they support, causing him to register lower levels of support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the media has prebaked a narrative about this race that is disconnected from the reality of where people are on the ground, but does have an effect of shaping what some of those less engaged people who don\u8217\'20\'19t come to events think about the race.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy spoke for 30 minutes and then spent nearly 45 minutes taking questions from attendees on a range of topics, including immigration and gun rights. He also dismissed a last-minute attack from Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/trump-criticizes-ramaswamy-publicly-1st-time-ahead-iowa/story?id=106355596"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  who urged his supporters}}}\uc2  over the weekend not to vote for Ramaswamy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVery sly, but a vote for Vivek is a vote for the \u8216\'20\'18other side\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 don\u8217\'20\'19t get duped by this. Vote for \u8216\'20\'18TRUMP,\u8217\'20\'19 don\u8217\'20\'19t waste your vote! Vivek is not MAGA,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a post on Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy seemed to suggest the attacks came from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Chandlers\u8221\'20\'1D and continued to decline to attack Trump. He emphasized how he has staunchly defended the former president as he has come under attack \u8220\'20\'1CThis system has made clear that they will stop at nothing, I mean nothing, to keep this man away from the White House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/15/vivek-ramaswamy-iowa-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy urges supporters not to believe polls in final Iowa pitch}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 Amid the snowy plains of Iowa, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to pull off one of the most improbable of all political comebacks.\par \par \uc2 A Trump campaign sign sits in a snow mound outside a caucus site at the Horizon Events Center in Clive, Iowa. Photograph: Kevin Dietsch/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, he held a campaign rally more akin to a victory lap in a state where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/iowa-caucuses-who-will-win-trump-desantis-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican caucus-goers}}}\uc2  look certain to back him for a swift return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/trump-admits-concern-that-icy-weather-could-harm-his-support-in-iowa-caucuses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 freezing temperatures and icy roads}}}\uc2 , the event at a college campus in Indianola drew more than 500 supporters in heavy winter coats and hats, filling the room to capacity and forcing some to watch on a big screen in an overspill auditorium. Some had driven from more than a hundred miles away.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou didn\u8217\'20\'19t need a plug-in to get energised in there,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gary Leffler, 62, wearing a white cap with \u8220\'20\'1CTrump caucus captain\u8221\'20\'1D sewn in gold lettering. \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, it was electric. It was powerful. People were ramped up. We\u8217\'20\'19re ready to rumble.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone is asking, hey, are Iowans going to get out and caucus tomorrow night? Well, I\u8217\'20\'19m telling you what, it was -48 windchill factor and look at the crowd. The room was full. People couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get in. They had overflow. I\u8217\'20\'19m telling you, that is the energy, that is the magnetism that Trump has.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?532626-1/president-trump-holds-rally-indianola-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The rally}}}\uc2  dwarfed those of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Republican rivals. He looks set to win Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s first-in-nation vote in the Republican presidential nomination race by a record margin on Monday night. A final poll by renowned Iowa pollster Ann Selzer shows Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/final-iowa-poll-trump-maintains-dominant-lead-caucuses-rcna132669"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with the support of 48% of likely caucus-goers}}}\uc2 , followed by \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  at 20%, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  at 16% and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  at 8%.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/donald-trump-iowa-rally-republican-caucuses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Ready to rumble\u8217\'20\'19: Trump holds Iowa campaign rally more akin to victory lap}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people have counted us out and so if we can exceed those expectations that should be a storyline,\u8221\'20\'1D says Asa Hutchinson.\par \par \uc2 Asa Hutchinson greets people during the Republican Party of Iowa legislative breakfast at the Hilton Des Moines Downtown. Photograph: Alyssa Pointer/Reuters\par \par \uc2 America in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  years can feel like a wild horse trying to throw off its rider but Hutchinson, the former Arkansas governor, is still clinging on with one hand. He has made around 60 trips to a hundred cities in Iowa over the past year in a long shot bid for the White House. He has embarked on a solemn crusade against Trump in a state where the former president retains a cult-like following.\par \par \uc2 But he enjoys one advantage over his nemesis: whereas Trump has set impossibly high expectations for Monday\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa caucuses, Hutchinson\u8217\'20\'19s performance will disappoint no one: his support stands at 1% in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/24360638-final-iowa-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 final NBC News/Des Moines Register/Mediacom Iowa poll}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Jonathan Capehart\uc2 , a host on the MSNBC network, admitted on Saturday: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d forgotten that Asa Hutchinson, the former governor of Arkansas, is still in the race.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If life is tough at the top, it can also be hard at the bottom. Over a lunch of chicken and a waffle with syrup at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tupelohoneycafe.com/restaurant/des-moines/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restaurant in snowy dowtown Des Moines}}}\uc2 , Hutchinson recalls his struggle earlier that morning for votes in the Iowa caucuses, which require people to show up in person \u8211\'20\'13 no absentee voting is allowed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomebody said, this lady here is about ready to support you but she has a few questions. So I call her up, spend 25 minutes answering very detailed questions on how I\u8217\'20\'19m going to constrain the growth of federal government and on and on and on, even covering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues and so on. And at the end of it, she says she\u8217\'20\'19s about to get in the car to go to Florida. I said, you mean you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to be in the caucus next week? And she said, no, but I\u8217\'20\'19ll vote for you in November!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They don\u8217\'20\'19t make Republicans like Hutchinson any more. Last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2023/08/11/asa-hutchinson-post-trump-republican-candidate-00110698"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Politico website called him}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most normal Republican presidential candidate\u8221\'20\'1D . He calls himself a \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  conservative\u8221\'20\'1D, appointed by Reagan as the youngest US attorney in the country at the time at the age of 31. He served in Congress and was head of the \uc2 Drug Enforcement Administration\uc2  (DEA) in the \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  administration. Like \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 , he had two terms as governor of Arkansas.\par \par \uc2 Now 73, Hutchinson launched his White House bid in April in his hometown of Bentonville, pledging to reform federal law enforcement agencies and \u8220\'20\'1Cbring out the best of America\u8221\'20\'1D. He also called on Trump, who had just been indicted by a grand jury in New York over hush money payments, to drop out of the race, contending that the office is more important than any individual.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe in traditional conservative principles and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has tried to reshape our party into an ego-driven machine that I don\u8217\'20\'19t think reflects well in our country or our party,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/asa-hutchinson-presidential-race-republican-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Asa Hutchinson on staying in the race and the Republican party: \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re in trouble\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 As she made her final pitch to Iowa voters, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  directly called out \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , warning that his re-election would only bring more \u8220\'20\'1Cchaos\u8221\'20\'1D at an already chaotic time for the nation.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  speaks during a campaign event at PB\u8217\'20\'19s Pub in Newton, Iowa, Monday. Photograph: Carolyn Kaster/AP\par \par \uc2 One day before the Iowa caucuses, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley}}}\uc2  addressed an energized crowd at a barbecue restaurant in Ames, just a few miles from \uc2 Iowa State University\uc2 . Despite the freezing temperatures, the room was filled to capacity with campaign volunteers, journalists and a few undecided caucusgoers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is truly cold,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we\u8217\'20\'19re going to keep on going anywhere and everywhere. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to go all the way until the last hour because we know what situation we\u8217\'20\'19re in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haley\u8217\'20\'19s own situation has improved in recent days, as the former South Carolina governor and US ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  has gained momentum in the race for the Republican presidential nomination. After trailing Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  for months, the latest Des Moines Register/NBC News/\uc2 Mediacom{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/final-iowa-poll-trump-maintains-dominant-lead-caucuses-rcna132669"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  showed Haley in second place in Iowa, winning the support of 20% of likely Republican caucusgoers compared to DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s 16%.\par \par \uc2 But the poll also underscored the profound challenges that Haley \u8211\'20\'13 and any other Republican not named \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 faces in the quest for the nomination. Trump easily beat all of his opponents in the Iowa poll, capturing the support of 48% of likely caucus-goers. Even if Haley can squeak out a second-place finish in Iowa, the results are unlikely to answer the question that has shaped the entire Republican primary: how can any candidate defeat a former president who remains overwhelmingly popular with the party\u8217\'20\'19s base?\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/nikki-haley-iowa-caucuses-republican-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley rides Iowa momentum, but likely for second place}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , the governor of Iowa, is caucusing for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After initial insisting on remaining neutral, Reynolds eventually backed DeSantis because she said she didn\u8217\'20\'19t think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could win the general election against Biden. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to look towards the future and not the past,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the Des Moines Register.\par \par \uc2 Her choice predictably landed her in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s crosshairs. Reynolds had campaigned alongside Trump and initially aligned herself with him during her run for governor in 2018, and she campaigned for him in 2020.\par \par \uc2 At a rally yesterday, Trump called her \u8220\'20\'1Cdisloyal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s the thing I\u8217\'20\'19m most proud of: She went from the most popular governor in the United States in two weeks to the least popular governor. She\u8217\'20\'19s the least popular governor in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D he told supporters.\par \par \uc2 Still, on Fox News today Reynolds said she\u8217\'20\'19ll support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , if he wins the nomination.\par \par \uc2 enltrReynolds: I\u8217\'20\'19ll support Trump if he\u8217\'20\'19s the nominee\par \par \uc2 Cavuto: After all the stuff he\u8217\'20\'19s said about you?\par \par \uc2 Reynolds: Yeah because we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to win {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5drNhRa7v5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5drNhRa7v5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1747005245111071068?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , just wrapped up his final pitch to voters here in at a bar in Cedar Rapids, saying their vote for him on Monday could change the trajectory of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , right, greets supporters following a campaign event at Jerseys Pub and Grub in Cedar Rapids, Iowa. Photograph: Nick Rohlman/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re never gonna have an opportunity to have your vote pack as much of a punch as it will tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said in remarks that lasted about 15 minutes. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t know how many people are going to be able to turn out given the weather.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The comments were part of an effort by DeSantis to keep enthusiasm high after a Des Moines Register/NBC News/Mediacom Iowa Poll showed him with the support of 16% of likely GOP caucusgoers. That trails \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , who has the support of 20% of likely caucusgoers and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has the support of 48% of likely caucusgoers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe live in a country now where the media thinks they should just be able to pick candidates,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think the people should be able to pick the candidates.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A year ago, DeSantis was considered a serious contender in Iowa and a threat to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning the nomination. His poll numbers have faded, even as he\u8217\'20\'19s campaigned heavily in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m proud we\u8217\'20\'19ve done Iowa right in terms of how you\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to approach this caucus,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI visited all 99 counties. We did events in all 99 counties. We took questions from people all up and down this state.\u8221\'20\'1D While he didn\u8217\'20\'19t mention them by name, it was a dig at Haley, whom DeSantis has criticized for not being as open with Iowa voters and Trump, the latter of whom has not campaigned as extensively in the state.\par \par \uc2 Listening in the audience was Steve Kessler, a 65-year-old retired engineer from Coralville. He said he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t made up his mind about who he\u8217\'20\'19s caucusing for yet. He said DeSantis gave a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood talk here\u8221\'20\'1D and he likes what he\u8217\'20\'19s done in Florida.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVivek - I like the change he\u8217\'20\'19s talking about. Very specific, very forceful and very knowledgable,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CNikki\u8217\'20\'19s got quite a bit of horsepower behind her right now.\par \par \uc2 Kissler said he would not be caucusing for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s too flamboyant. And he distracts from the message,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/ron-desantis-iowa-caucuses-republican-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis makes his pitch before Iowa caucuses amid faltering campaign}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  meets campaign advisers in Des Moines\par \par \uc2 Trump is in Iowa, where he expects to see a sizable victory tonight. The former US president, who is running for a second term, was pictured leaving a meeting with advisers in Des Moines \u8211\'20\'13 hours before caucus votes were due to begin.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, when he arrived, he acknowledged he worried that the weather could affect turnout, though he noted that Trump supporters were passionate.\par \par \uc2 He rallied supporters on Sunday night in Indianola, Iowa, telling them they needed to show up Monday no matter what.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t sit home,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re sick as a dog, you say \u8216\'20\'18Darling, I gotta make it.\u8217\'20\'19 Even if you vote and then pass away, it\u8217\'20\'19s worth it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  leaves a meeting with campaign advisors on caucus day, Monday, in Des Moines, Iowa. Photograph: Chip Somodevilla/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary of Iowa caucuses before voting begins...\par \par \uc2 The caucuses are set to begin in two hours, kicking off the 2024 election season in the US. Trump is expected to win handily, though the weather will prove the ultimate wild card.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 It is very cold. The frigid, snow-filled state has seemed dormant the last few days, mostly because people are quickly running in and out of buildings to escape the cold. Candidates still hosted events around the state on Monday to snag last-minute votes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The caucus begins at precinct sites around the state at 7pm CT (8pm ET). Voters will stream into their local school gyms or community centers, where caucus captains volunteering for candidates will try to whip voters to their side. Results will be posted on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://results.iacaucus2024.com/?mc_cid=bc011e5ac4&mc_eid=384a13735e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this website}}}\uc2  as they come in.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who\u8217\'20\'19s going to show up? The extreme cold could affect whose voters turn out to caucus. Some parts of the state still have snow-covered or icy roads. Low turnout could boost candidates polling lower if Trump supporters think their votes won\u8217\'20\'19t be needed to ensure a victory.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 After former president and GOP frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attacked Republican candidates \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  on Monday, Haley called Trump\u8217\'20\'19s insults \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D while Ramaswamy refused to insult the former president in return.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 including Illinois governor \uc2 JB Pritzker\uc2  and Minnesota senator Tina Smith \u8211\'20\'13 held a press conference in Iowa with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  re-election campaign surrogates, who denounced the Republican candidates as extremists.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  spoke in South Carolina, Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 first primary state, at a \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2  day event, where she recalled King\u8217\'20\'19s words and said Republicans served as a threat to freedoms like reproductive rights and access to education.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 It is MLK day, a federal holiday honoring the civil rights leader. Republicans set their caucus date without regard for the holiday, though the Iowa GOP leader said he believes holding the caucus on the holiday honors King.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This is the true start of the 2024 election. Depending on tonight\u8217\'20\'19s results, some Republican candidates could decide to end their campaigns and throw their support toward someone else. Or they could all continue, discounting the role of one rural midwestern state in the country\u8217\'20\'19s politics.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  urges Iowa voters to show up for Trump despite cold\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  and Kimberly Guilfoyle are in Ankeny, Iowa, telling voters they need to show up tonight to support Trump Sr, despite the frigid weather.\par \par \uc2 Guilfoyle laid out the high stakes for the election, saying Trump is the only choice to get the country back on track and that the country will be unrecognizable if Trump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t take back the White House.\par \par \uc2 Trump Jr took jabs at \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s closest competitor, and said people needed to vote tonight despite Trump polling well ahead.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re trying desperately to suppress the vote by saying you have it in the bag,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Jr. does an interview after speaking at the Machine Shed in Urbandale, Iowa, Thursday, Jan. 11, 2024. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is set to make a closing pitch at Jersey\u8217\'20\'19s pub and Grub in Cedar Rapids as Iowans prepare to head to their caucus sites Monday evening.\par \par \uc2 Wyatt Landuyt-Kruger, 22, is plans to caucus for DeSantis and said he\u8217\'20\'19s going straight from this event to his caucus site. The caucuses are at 7pm and people aren\u8217\'20\'19t let in if they arrive late.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s principled, he\u8217\'20\'19s got good conservative values,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He added that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t believe the polls, which show DeSantis with the support of 16% of caucusgoers, trailing \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  (20%) and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  (48%).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t listen to the polls at all,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think the polls elevate Trump because they know Trump would get beaten by Trump in a general election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kevin Rigdon, another DeSantis supporter here, said he started following the Florida governor and was impressed with how he ran the state during the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 enltrFlorida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is set to speak here at a bar in Cedar Rapids in a closing pitch before tonight\u8217\'20\'19s 7pm caucuses. Some people are going straight from here to their caucus sites {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ySQByJgF4i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ySQByJgF4i}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1747019296734150788?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  and girlfriend Kimberly Guilfoyle are running very late for a campaign stop at a bar in Ankeny, Iowa. \u8220\'20\'1CDo you think we\u8217\'20\'19ll still make it to the caucus?\u8221\'20\'1D one anxious supporter asked the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Patiently hanging on is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blake_Marnell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blake Marnell}}}\uc2 , 59, who works in sales and lives in San Diego, California. He is one of the peculiar characters thrown up by the Trump era: he is wearing his trademark brick-patterned suit, a symbol of his support for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s border wall, along with a \u8220\'20\'1CMaga\u8221\'20\'1D cap signed by Trump.\par \par \uc2 He says the suit was marketed in Britain for stag parties and he bought it off the internet. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are suits made for bachelor parties in London where the lads all want to go out for a night drinking but the dress code at the club says you must wear suits, so there\u8217\'20\'19s this industry of semi-disposable suits with garish patterns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Marnell estimates he has been to between 35 and 40 Trump rallies and confidently predicts the former president will win the Iowa caucuses. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe President Trump will win. I think everybody knows that so the real question is by how much? If you go by polling, I think that he will be over 50%.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1CBrick Man\u8221\'20\'1D is also looking forward to seeing the president\u8217\'20\'19s eldest son in action soon. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s an excellent speaker for President Trump, for his father, because one thing that a lot of President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s surrogates don\u8217\'20\'19t have but \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  does have is they share the same sense of humour: at times irreverent, at times offensive to some people, at times perhaps people might think it\u8217\'20\'19s a little bit too much, but if you\u8217\'20\'19re a fan of President Trump and his humour, you\u8217\'20\'19re also going to be a fan of Don Jr.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe politician that supports President Trump won\u8217\'20\'19t have the freedom or the latitude to say things because they have to worry about their constituency back home and how that impacts their office. \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 ? No filters. He can say what he wants to say. He can say what he\u8217\'20\'19s feeling and people understand that and they gravitate towards him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump supporter and \u8216\'20\'18Brick \u8216\'20\'18Man\u8217\'20\'19 Blake Marnell: \u8220\'20\'1CI believe President Trump will win. I think everybody knows that so the real question is by how much? If you go by polling, I think that he will be over 50%.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/z7WYiezVnK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/z7WYiezVnK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1747011515947901088?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  warns of Republicans posing 'profound threat' to freedoms\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom is under profound threat\u8221\'20\'1D in a speech in South Carolina to commemorate Martin Luther King Jr Day.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president spoke as Republicans campaigned around Iowa in the final push to sway voters before the caucus began this evening. Democrats aren\u8217\'20\'19t holding an Iowa caucus this year, after shifting their calendar to make South Carolina the first official primary because Iowa and New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s voters don\u8217\'20\'19t represent the diversity of the party. Republicans set their Iowa caucus on MLK day to maintain its status as the first election contest, but the fact that it was a federal holiday didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to enter into the decision.\par \par \uc2 Harris cited MLK\u8217\'20\'19s iconic \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.csuchico.edu/iege/_assets/documents/susi-letter-from-birmingham-jail.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Letter from Birmingham Jail}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, where the civil rights leader wrote that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe goal of America is freedom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so, as we gather to honor his legacy, I pose a question I believe Dr. King would today ask: In 2024, where exactly is America in our fight for freedom?\u8230\'20\'26As Vice President of the United States, I\u8217\'20\'19d say: At this moment, in America, freedom is under profound threat,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an NAACP event, Harris sought to make the case that supporting Democrats in this year\u8217\'20\'19s elections would protect freedoms in the wake of attacks on reproductive rights, book bans and voting rights. She implored attendees to join the fight against these restrictions by voting blue in 2024.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis generation now has fewer rights than their mothers and grandmothers,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not hypothetical that from kindergarten to 12th grade, this generation has had to endure active shooter drills. Our children, who should be in a classroom fulfilling their God-given potential and exploring their wonder for the beauty of the world, instead have to worry that someone might burst through their classroom door with a gun. It is not hypothetical. When students go to vote, they often have to wait in line for hours because of laws that intentionally make it more difficult for them to cast a ballot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speaks to a crowd gathered at the South Carolina State House in Columbia, SC, earlier today. Photograph: Tracy Glantz/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Shortly after that, the Biden campaign\u8217\'20\'19s press conference wrapped up.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now four hours away from the start of the Republican caucuses in Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s 99 counties, and you can expect the Biden campaign will speak up again once their choice becomes clear.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 JB Pritzker\uc2  was asked about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s persistent unpopularity.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating has been underwater for more than two-and-a-half years, and has lately lurked in the low 40% range. The factors behind this trend are myriad and include Biden\u8217\'20\'19s advanced age as well as the hangover from the record inflation Americans experienced in 2022, but the trend has been enough to make many Democrats nervous about his bid to win another four years in the White House.\par \par \uc2 Pritzker argued that polls don\u8217\'20\'19t yet reflect the reality of the presidential race, since the Republican nominee hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet been decided.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUntil we see that we won\u8217\'20\'19t know really what the numbers are,\u8221\'20\'1D the governor said (though many pollsters have surveyed how the president would perform against various Republicans, including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/09/trump-biden-poll-election-presidential"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some polls have found}}}\uc2  voters prefer.)\par \par \uc2 But I can tell you this, that it\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that\u8217\'20\'19s delivered for the American public, it\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that\u8217\'20\'19s got an awful lot to brag about, and I think the dangers that are posed by this Republican field will be well known to people once... one of them is chosen.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Katzenberg\uc2 , a movie mogul who is co-chairing the national advisory board for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign, is talking up the mammoth fundraising haul the president received in the final quarter of last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast quarter, Team Biden Harris raised more than $97m and reported $117m of cash on hand,\u8221\'20\'1D Katzenberg said.\par \par \uc2 It means team Biden-Harris is entering the election year with more cash on hand than any democratic candidate in history.\par \par \uc2 He said the Biden campaign\u8217\'20\'19s financial firepower now dwarfs his Republican rivals, no matter who that may be, and allows them to focus their efforts on winning the November general election. Katzenberg said:\par \par \uc2 Republicans are spending money in a race for the Maga base without a single dime going towards the voters who will ultimately decide the general election. By the time they are finished with the primary and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or whichever extremists is finally in a position where they can start trying to compete with us, it\u8217\'20\'19s just going to be too late.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota senator Tina Smith laid into the Republican field, saying all the candidates had plans to cut off access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We know one thing for sure. Every one of these extremist candidates is attacking women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom to make their own decisions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These extreme Republican candidates want a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that is what they will try to do if given the chance.\par \par \uc2 The reality is that none of these candidates trust women to make their own decisions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because they believe that they know and that is why we cannot trust them to be president.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a6fUnl6FFi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/a6fUnl6FFi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1746997629660102745?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican candidates espousing extremist ideas, Illinois governor tells Iowa Democratic event\par \par \uc2 The Illinois governor, \uc2 JB Pritzker\uc2 , is up at the podium first, and saying that all Republican candidates competing in tonight\u8217\'20\'19s caucus are ignoring the country\u8217\'20\'19s needs and espousing extremist policies. Pritzker said:\par \par \uc2 Here we stand on Martin Luther King Jr Day, and this field of candidates is espousing Adolf Hitler\u8217\'20\'19s ideas, denying that... the civil war was about slavery, or demonizing and discounting the rights of large groups of Americans. All of these Republican candidates are singing the same, terrible song.\par \par \uc2 In an apparent reference to \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , the former South Carolina governor and sole woman in the Republican race, and the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who has been accused of wearing footwear that boosts his stature, Pritzker said:\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s contest is simply a question of whether you like your Maga Trump agenda wrapped in the original packaging with high heels, or with lifts in their boots.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZIPeJkUf5i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZIPeJkUf5i}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1746995753635963038?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While everyone will be watching who Iowa Republicans select as their nominee tonight, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign is in town to, in their words, \u8220\'20\'1Cremind voters what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake this November as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Maga Republicans launch an all-out assault on Americans\u8217\'20\'19 freedoms\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19ve got some Democratic heavy hitters speaking to the press this afternoon at the Iowa Events Center in Des Moines, including the Illinois governor \uc2 JB Pritzker\uc2 , the Minnesota senator Tina Smith and \uc2 Jeffrey Katzenberg\uc2 , co-chair of the Biden-Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s national advisory board.\par \par \uc2 I am in the room and will let you know what they have to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 What is a precinct captain - and what do they do?\par \par \uc2 Precinct captains in Iowa will try to persuade caucus voters tonight to pick their preferred candidate, a practice common to the Iowa caucuses but not typical of US elections otherwise.\par \par \uc2 Candidates work to have volunteer caucus captains at all precinct voting sites, usually local schools or community gathering places. Those captains whip votes at the precinct, speechifying and debating with voters who are unsure who to vote for or could be swayed from one candidate to another.\par \par \uc2 Outside the caucus process, it\u8217\'20\'19s usually illegal to actively campaign at a polling site.\par \par \uc2 This year, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s precinct captains are donning white hats with \u8220\'20\'1CTrump Caucus Captain\u8221\'20\'1D written in gold lettering. The hats were given to 2,000 caucus captains and have become \u8220\'20\'1Cthe hottest item in Maga world\u8221\'20\'1D, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/01/15/iowa-caucus/cold-state-hot-item-00135603"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Trump Caucus Captain\u8217\'20\'19 hats have become the \u8216\'20\'18hottest item in Maga world\u8217\'20\'19, according to Politico. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 The precinct captains, while their role is important on caucus day, are typically regular Iowa voters who volunteer to help their preferred candidate because they\u8217\'20\'19re passionate about that person winning. They\u8217\'20\'19re often seen as people who can influence their neighbors at the hyperlocal precinct sites.\par \par \uc2 Sometimes, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/15/us/politics/iowa-caucus-captains.html#:~:text=At%20every%20precinct%20from%20Sioux,sway%20voters%20to%20their%20side."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2  in its feature about caucus captains, the captains can be more high-profile. \u8220\'20\'1COne of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s captains is a former co-chairman of the Iowa Republican Party, and one of \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s is a state senator,\u8221\'20\'1D the paper notes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Climate activists from the Sunrise Movement protested outside a diner near \uc2 Drake University\uc2  in Des Moines, Iowa, where \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  was addressing supporters today.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  greets supporters as climate activists unfurl a banner following a campaign stop at the Drake Diner in Des Moines, Iowa. Photograph: Win McNamee/Getty Images \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  moves past climate protesters to greet supporters as she moves to a waiting vehicle after a campaign event at Drake Diner, in Des Moines, Iowa. Photograph: Carolyn Kaster/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party has announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://results.iacaucus2024.com/?mc_cid=bc011e5ac4&mc_eid=384a13735e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a website}}}\uc2  where it will publicly collate the results of this evening\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses.\par \par \uc2 The website will post results from precincts in all 99 counties, and include the following candidates: the former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ; the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  ; the former South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  ; the former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  ; the entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  ; and the pastor Ryan Binkley. The former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  will also appear in the results because, the state GOP said, they had planned for him to be there. Christie suspended his campaign last week.\par \par \uc2 Doors to caucus sites will open at 7pm ET, with the caucusing beginning at 8pm. All sites are open to reporters, except for those in Perry, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/iowa-principal-wounded-school-shooting-dies-dan-marburger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a school shooting occurred}}}\uc2  last week. The community has requested the press not be present, the Iowa GOP says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This year\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa caucuses coincide with \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2  Day in the US, a federal holiday that honors the civil rights leader on the third Monday in January.\par \par \uc2 The holiday didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to initially factor into Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 decision to set the date, reporting from the Associated Press last July {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/iowa-caucuses-2024-new-hampshire-primary-republican-election-ab362c03166a97c50a4db87c3bb494d9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 . Democrats aren\u8217\'20\'19t holding a caucus in Iowa this year.\par \par \uc2 Setting the Iowa caucus on 15 January ensured it would occur before New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s contest and maintain its first-in-the-nation status.\par \par \uc2 After the decision was made, Iowa Republican Party Chairman Jeff Kaufmann said:\par \par \uc2 As Republicans, we can, I, we see this as honoring the legacy of \uc2 Martin Luther King\uc2  in terms of having a caucus here.\par \par \uc2 The Monday night caucus interfered with scheduled events meant to commemorate MLK Day. The Sioux City NAACP shifted a celebration to Sunday, though organizers didn\u8217\'20\'19t mind, the Sioux City Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://siouxcityjournal.com/news/local/sioux-city-mlk-day-celebration/article_3e1b783a-aefa-11ee-95d4-1bff81a11c69.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe Iowa Caucuses are very important. If you want to participate, you should be able to participate,\u8221\'20\'1D Sandra Pearson told the paper.\par \par \uc2 In Ames, Iowa, an annual MLK day celebration is still set for Monday night, which has some local leaders frustrated and residents deciding whether to attend one or the other, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iowastatedaily.com/287875/news/iowa-caucuses-to-conflict-with-ames-and-story-countys-mlk-day-celebration/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa State Daily}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy do we even make people have to choose on something like this?\u8221\'20\'1D Ames council representative Tim Gartin said, according to Iowa State Daily.\par \par \uc2 So that\u8217\'20\'19s the part that\u8217\'20\'19s painful to me is that this is a choice that we should never have to make, you should be able to do both.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  has also responded to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s post on his Truth Social site this morning, where he said voting for the tech entrepreneur would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cwasted vote\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy refused to cricitize the former president, saying instead that he had \u8220\'20\'1Cdefended Trump and respect him immensely\u8221\'20\'1D. He added:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m asking for your vote tonight because I believe it\u8217\'20\'19s the right thing for our country. We cannot walk into the other side\u8217\'20\'19s trap & watch the puppet masters quietly trot Nikki into power.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19ve defended Trump at every step & respect him immensely. You won\u8217\'20\'19t hear me attacking him. I\u8217\'20\'19m asking for your vote tonight because I believe it\u8217\'20\'19s the right thing for our country. We cannot walk into the other side\u8217\'20\'19s trap & watch the puppet masters quietly trot Nikki into power. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/E1gM5ydrXW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/E1gM5ydrXW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  (@VivekGRamaswamy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VivekGRamaswamy/status/1746933646039175522?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'Don\u8217\'20\'19t believe the fake news': Haley hits back at Trump's attacks\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  has dismissed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comments earlier today that she is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-donald-trump-republicans-ron-desantis-nikki-haley-us-election-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-65a56c788f08e4f5a262ff4c#block-65a56c788f08e4f5a262ff4c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a \u8220\'20\'1CGlobalist Rino\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-donald-trump-republicans-ron-desantis-nikki-haley-us-election-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-65a565818f0867bef96c7237#block-65a565818f0867bef96c7237"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have Maga\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  knows \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  is a strong conservative who he praises repeatedly for her toughness at the United Nations,\u8221\'20\'1D said a national spokesperson for Haley, Olivia Perez-Cubas.\par \par \uc2 Now that Nikki is surging and Trump is dropping, his campaign is flinging phony, contradictory attacks. Don\u8217\'20\'19t believe the fake news from Trump world \u8211\'20\'13 they don\u8217\'20\'19t believe it themselves.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-donald-trump-republicans-ron-desantis-nikki-haley-us-election-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-65a584cf8f0867bef96c73a3#block-65a584cf8f0867bef96c73a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Before Vivek Ramaswamy\u8217\'20\'19s event}}}\uc2  started in Cedar Rapids, I spoke with Gaylen Vance, a 68-year-old retiree who said he\u8217\'20\'19s still undecided about who to caucus for.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  has the best chance of winning the general election, he said. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most like Trump without some of the extraneous crap\u8221\'20\'1D. And Ramaswamy is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe smartest guy in the room\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vance said his wife was a caucus captain for Trump in tonight\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses but he was hesitant to support the former president because of his lies about the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  is about to take the stage here at a brewery in Cedar Rapids just a few hours ahead of the Iowa caucuses.\par \par \uc2 The room here is crowded \u8211\'20\'13 I would guess around 100 people are here \u8211\'20\'13 though noticeably smaller than the crowd at events I\u8217\'20\'19ve been to for \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in recent days. Ramaswamy trails DeSantis by 8% and Haley by double digits in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 Before the program started, a speaker asked how many voters were undecided and a smattering of hands went up. She said this was a chance for those undecided voters to ask Ramaswamy anything.\par \par \uc2 enltrVivek Ramaswamy is about to speak here at a Brewery in Cedar Rapids. One of his supporters, Steven Mosnik said he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t believe the polls, which show Ramaswamy with the support of 8% of likely GOP caucus goers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RAxHBa5wGR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RAxHBa5wGR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1746971073860518219?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Steve King\uc2 , a far right former Republican congressman who has endorsed Ramaswamy, spoke before the candidate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I step in and endorse in and endorse a candidate I\u8217\'20\'19m all in,\u8221\'20\'1D King said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd today where am I? I\u8217\'20\'19m really really enthusiastically all in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to put into words just what the -1F (-18C) temperature in Des Moines feels like.\par \par \uc2 Suffice to say, few people are outside in downtown Des Moines, and those that must go out are typically darting from a car into a building.\par \par \uc2 Conditions remain treacherous, and the sub-freezing temperatures that have stretched on since Friday\u8217\'20\'19s snow dump mean roads remains slick with slush, sidewalks are piled high with drifts, and it\u8217\'20\'19s still typical to see cars stuck in piles of snow.\par \par \uc2 The one group of people spending more time outside than most is television reporters doing standups, who apparently have no option but to brave the frigid weather in exchange for a nice background of the state capital:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ips7H3ucho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ips7H3ucho}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1746966391528309002?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The caucuses are a big event for Des Moines, drawing reporters and politicians from all over the country. The city rolls out the welcome mat in a variety of ways, including with banners posted all over the downtown\u8217\'20\'19s very useful skywalk system:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QpMO7gTwsS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QpMO7gTwsS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1746966848082444308?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The longshot right winger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/vivek-ramaswamy-disqualified-debate-iowa-republican-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy}}}\uc2  is out and about on the frozen trail in Iowa today, too, earlier hanging with one of Britain\u8217\'20\'19s ultimate Brexiteers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/nigel-farage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nigel Farage}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  is interviewed by Nigel Farage as he makes a campaign visit to Machine Shed Restaurant before the Iowa caucus vote in Urbandale, Iowa, 15 January 2024. Photograph: Sergio Flores/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a very ordinary post on X/\uc2 Twitter\uc2  from Ramaswamy earlier.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m a businessman, not a politician. My parents came to this country 40 years ago with no money, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve gone on to found multibillion dollar companies. I did it while getting married to my wife Apoorva and raising our two sons. That\u8217\'20\'19s the American Dream. For a long time, we\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4es2ycLFNx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4es2ycLFNx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  (@VivekGRamaswamy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VivekGRamaswamy/status/1746915232545399107?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And the less ordinary, giving his provocative, ultra-conservative definition of \u8220\'20\'1Ctruth\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrTRUTH.\par \par \uc2 1. God is real.\par \par \uc2 2. There are two genders.\par \par \uc2 3. Human flourishing requires fossil fuels.\par \par \uc2 4. Reverse racism is racism.\par \par \uc2 5. An open border is no border.\par \par \uc2 6. Parents determine the education of their children.\par \par \uc2 7. The nuclear family is the greatest form of governance known to\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xZgqgBjC5v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xZgqgBjC5v}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  (@VivekGRamaswamy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VivekGRamaswamy/status/1746917538808648120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Iowa is a crucial state for every Republican candidate, but it\u8217\'20\'19s shaping up to be a uniquely important test for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor whose bid for president does not seem to be catching on with voters.\par \par \uc2 Recent state polls have shown him either tied with the former South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  or trailing her, and a third-place finish for DeSantis in Iowa, a state he has banked on winning, would do great damage to his campaign.\par \par \uc2 In downtown Des Moines, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s US politics live blog ran into Chuck Volpe, a political talkshow host from north-eastern Pennsylvania who is on DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s national finance committee, and will be speaking at a caucus site when the vote is held this evening.\par \par \uc2 Asked for his thoughts on the much-debated impact of the foul weather on the election, Volpe replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI think if you\u8217\'20\'19re projected as the underdog, the weather should be a benefit because you could depress turnout.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He noted that DeSantis had visited every county in the state, completing what\u8217\'20\'19s known as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfull Grassley\u8221\'20\'1D after the long-serving Iowa senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2 , and has the endorsement of the Republican governor, \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 . Volpe also recounted how candidates that seemed to be struggling in the past, such as the former Pennsylvania senator \uc2 Rick Santorum\uc2  in 2012, have won over the state\u8217\'20\'19s voters and seen their campaigns regain strength.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt literally breathed life into a campaign that was defunct... Iowans seem to do that. So, we\u8217\'20\'19re confident,\u8221\'20\'1D Volpe said.\par \par \uc2 Left unsaid was that despite Santorum\u8217\'20\'19s win in Iowa in 12 years ago, it was \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  who won the Republican nomination that year, only to lose the presidential race to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has Reynolds on side, per this post via his team.\par \par \uc2 enltrIowa Governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KimReynoldsIA?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KimReynoldsIA}}}\uc2  message to caucusgoers today: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonDeSantis?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RonDeSantis}}}\uc2  is the one true conservative in this race, and he's got a record to back it up. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lR0OEgEqpk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lR0OEgEqpk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Gloria Taylor (@Glo_Tay) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Glo_Tay/status/1746964108354744693?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary of Iowa caucuses day so far\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a bracing day in Iowa as the caucus gatherings approach later on Monday, and there are other items of US politics news occurring too, all brought to you as they happen. We are here, live, to bring you all the events.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Economy, border, foreign policy are key issues as Iowans head to caucus, with Republican voters in the Hawkeye state saying these themes are top of mind as they prepare to caucus tonight in the US\u8217\'20\'19s first nominating contest.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has stepped up his attacks on \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  on the morning of the day Iowans go to vote on their Republican candidate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Pentagonsaid the US defense secretary,Lloyd Austin, has been released from hospital today. Austin, 70, had been hospitalized since 1 January due to complications after prostate cancer treatment, but there was uproar because he didn\u8217\'20\'19t tell the White House (or many others) about it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Iowa Republicans will brave brutally cold temperatures on Monday evening to participate in the state\u8217\'20\'19s presidential caucuses, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  remains the clear frontrunner in the race for his party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination. The final results will depend on turnout, which could be acutely impacted by the weather.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Iowans have been told to \u8220\'20\'1Climit outdoor exposure\u8221\'20\'1D as much as possible with forecasters saying the wind chill temperature could go down to as low as -35F on Monday evening in the \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous cold\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The 2024 US presidential election begins in earnest in Iowa today. The final Des Moines Register/NBC News poll before Monday night\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses found former president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , maintaining a formidable lead over his opponents, supported by 48% of likely caucus-goers. After trailing the two-term Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  for months, the latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/final-iowa-poll-trump-maintains-dominant-lead-caucuses-rcna132669"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  showed \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , the former South Carolina governor, in second place in Iowa, winning the support of 20% of likely Republican caucus-goers, compared to DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s 16%, with \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  at 8%.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s caucus day. Get excited!\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  told a crowd of supporters as they packed into a diner near \uc2 Drake University\uc2  in Des Moines, Iowa.\par \par \uc2 Speaking directly to those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/15/us/politics/iowa-caucus-captains.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 serving as caucus captains}}}\uc2 , Haley asked them to \u8220\'20\'1Cspeak from the heart\u8221\'20\'1D in their Monday night speeches, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 The former South Carolina governor and US ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  plans to make several stops in central Iowa ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s votes, including making an appearance at a caucus location before heading to her campaign celebration.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  speaks during a campaign stop at the Drake Diner in Des Moines, Iowa. Photograph: Brian Snyder/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Economy, border, foreign policy: key issues as Iowans head to caucus\par \par \uc2 David Erlacher hadn\u8217\'20\'19t made up his mind about who he was going to caucus for when he showed up to a Cedar Rapids brewery to hear \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  speak on Sunday afternoon. But inside his jacket pocket was a handwritten list of issues that mattered most to him.\par \par \uc2 At the top was the economy, followed by the southern border. He then listed a series of foreign policy conflicts, including the Houthi attacks in Yemen, the war in Israel, and the war between Ukraine and Russia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe world\u8217\'20\'19s a dumpster fire right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Erlacher, a 76-year-old retiree who lives in Cedar Rapids, said.\par \par \uc2 We got to try and find some water to throw on it. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure how that\u8217\'20\'19s gonna happen. I\u8217\'20\'19m just glad there\u8217\'20\'19s smarter people than myself out there to do it.\par \par \uc2 Those three priorities \u8211\'20\'13 the economy, the border and international instability \u8211\'20\'13 echoed what many Iowa voters said were their top issues as they prepare to caucus in the US\u8217\'20\'19s first nominating contest on Monday, with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and DeSantis at the top. A November Des Moines Register/NBC News/Mediacom Iowa Poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/iowa-poll/caucus/2023/11/01/iowa-poll-how-republican-caucusgoers-rank-issues-from-the-economy-to-abortion-israel-ukraine/71328389007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that 81% of likely caucus-goers listed the economy as a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery important issue\u8221\'20\'1D and 80% of caucus-goers listed \u8220\'20\'1Cimmigration and border security as \u8220\'20\'1Cvery important issues\u8221\'20\'1D in the same poll.\par \par \uc2 Concerns over the economy underscore a significant challenge for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as he seeks a second term. Traditional metrics have shown that the US economy is strong, but nearly two-thirds of Americans are unhappy with it, according to a September Harris survey {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/15/biden-economy-bidenomics-poll-republicans-democrats-independents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conducted by the Guardian.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-key-issues-voters-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Economy, border, foreign policy: key issues as Iowans head to caucus}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump steps up attacks against Haley and DeSantis on morning of Iowa caucuses\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stepped up attacks against his rivals on Monday morning ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 On his Truth Social site, Trump knocked his former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , as \u8220\'20\'1CGlobalist Rino\u8221\'20\'1D (short for Republican In Name Only) who is \u8220\'20\'1Cweak on the Border, and will always be willing to obliterate Social Security and Medicare, while at the same time raising your taxes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump also described voting for \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cwasted vote\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that the tech entrepreneur conducted \u8220\'20\'1Cdeceitful campaign tricks\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cplayed it too \u8216\'20\'18cute\u8217\'20\'19 with us\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A convoy of black Chevrolet Suburbans and police cars idling in downtown Des Moines stood out this morning. Chances are, they were waiting for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to head out for the day.\par \par \uc2 The convoy was parked outside Hotel Fort Des Moines, where the former president is staying and which has become a hangout for journalists hoping to hear from his advisers and catch a glimpse of the Republican frontrunner.\par \par \uc2 The Washington Examiner caught video of him arriving on Saturday evening, where the bitter temperatures could not escape his notice (perhaps because he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t particularly bundled up):\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Trump walks into the Hotel Fort Des Moines where I happen to also be staying. Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of cold weather. We have a lot of meetings tonight, a lot of tremendous support, but it\u8217\'20\'19s nasty out there.\u8221\'20\'1D Cc: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dcexaminer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @dcexaminer}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/B3obeiVxhK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/B3obeiVxhK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Samantha-Jo Roth (@SamanthaJoRoth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SamanthaJoRoth/status/1746323529006477677?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Trump held a rally in the town of Indianola, just south of Des Moines. There, he announced the endorsement of North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , and delivered, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/donald-trump-iowa-rally-republican-caucuses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the words of}}}\uc2  the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s David Smith:\par \par \uc2 A typically meandering, disjointed and falsehood-laced speech for an hour and a half, ranging from the proximity of a third world war to lambasting Washington as \u8216\'20\'18a rat-infested, graffiti-infested shithole\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Fewer than half of likely Republican caucus -goers in Iowa identify with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s M aga, or \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D, base, according to a new poll.\par \par \uc2 The Des Moines Register/NBC News/Mediacom Iowa {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/iowa-poll/caucus/2024/01/15/iowa-poll-most-ia-republican-caucusgoers-do-not-identify-maga-movement-donald-trump-nikki-haley/72201589007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  shows 40% of registered voters who said they are likely to attend the Iowa caucuses identify themselves as either \u8220\'20\'1CUltra Maga\u8221\'20\'1D (18%) or \u8220\'20\'1CRegular Maga\u8221\'20\'1D (22%) when asked how they view the phrase.\par \par \uc2 Another 38% said they are neutral to the Maga movement, and 17% are anti-Maga.\par \par \uc2 Sixty percent of likely caucus goers who said Trump is their first choice described themselves as either \u8220\'20\'1CUltra Maga\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1CRegular Maga\u8221\'20\'1D. By contrast, only 11% of those who selected \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  as their first choice identified with the Maga brand.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wearing a Make America Great Again hat. Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-donald-trump-republicans-ron-desantis-nikki-haley-us-election-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-65a552c98f08150a06c5f216#block-65a552c98f08150a06c5f216"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  more}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interview with CNN this morning, in which he said he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t regret previously supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who endorsed him ahead of his first run for Florida governor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen he was president, I supported his policies. He was under assault from the left and the media,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said.\par \par \uc2 I was happy to do that, because he was our chance to get things done in a positive direction.\par \par \uc2 But this time is different, he added.\par \par \uc2 When you\u8217\'20\'19re in a primary situation, I want Republicans to do well. If someone\u8217\'20\'19s endorsed me, great. If they haven\u8217\'20\'19t, if they\u8217\'20\'19re doing a good job, I\u8217\'20\'19m happy for that. I want our party to do well. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is not that way. He wants to trash Governor [Kim] Reynolds who is gold here in Iowa, simply because she\u8217\'20\'19s on my team.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Good morning from Des Moines, where the temperature is -5F (-25C), but feels like -19F (-28C).\par \par \uc2 All of that raises the question \u8211\'20\'13 who will feel like showing up to the Republican caucus this evening?\par \par \uc2 While the snow stopped falling, the big winter storm that struck Friday is expected to dent turnout for this evening\u8217\'20\'19s vote, with unpredictable effects on contenders\u8217\'20\'19 fortunes. Perhaps the candidate most at risk is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-donald-trump-republicans-ron-desantis-nikki-haley-us-election-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65a5308e8f08edc701f75c91#block-65a5308e8f08edc701f75c91"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  polls indicate }}}\uc2  has a massive lead in the state.\par \par \uc2 His campaign wants not just to win, but to win big to cement his frontrunner status. Much of his voters come from rural areas where the storm has left the roads most treacherous, and one of the big questions of today is whether they will be able to make it to their caucus sites, and give Trump the margin of victory he is looking for.\par \par \uc2 Even Des Moines, the state capital and largest city, is still digging out from the eight inches-plus of snow that the storm brought. The city\u8217\'20\'19s downtown has felt deserted for days, not because no one is around, but because it\u8217\'20\'19s too cold to walk outside \u8211\'20\'13 everyone is driving from place to place. This morning, the few people on the streets were busy shoveling snow off sidewalks and away from storefronts. While winters are typically cold in Iowa, the awful weather has kept the candidates inside as well for the last few days, and discouraged the door-to-door campaigning that typically takes place in the run-up to the vote.\par \par \uc2 Temperatures won\u8217\'20\'19t improve much as the day goes; today\u8217\'20\'19s high is expected to be 0F (-17C).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Austin released from hospital, says Pentagon\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon said the US defense secretary, Lloyd Austin, has been released from hospital today.\par \par \uc2 Austin, 70, had been hospitalized since 1 January due to complications after prostate cancer treatment.\par \par \uc2 He had been admitted to Walter Reed national military medical center in Washington on 22 December and underwent surgery to treat the cancer. He was hospitalized again to treat a urinary tract infection related to that operation.\par \par \uc2 Doctors said he remained in the hospital due to ongoing leg pain resulting from the infection and so he could get physical therapy.\par \par \uc2 Austin is expected to perform his duties remotely before returning full-time to the Pentagon.\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Austin in Seoul in November last year. Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Fire engines and other emergency vehicles responded to a fake 911 call this morning that the White House was on fire, while \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his family were at Camp David.\par \par \uc2 Within minutes of the report, which came just after 7am, District of Columbia fire and emergency medical services and \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  personnel determined that it was a false report and called off the response, AP reported, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 Biden is set to return to the White House this afternoon after spending part of the weekend at the presidential retreat in Maryland and participating in a service event in Philadelphia to mark Martin Luther King Jr Day.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A passing weather system brought snowfall and temperatures dropped to about -20C (-4F) as voters prepared for the Republican party of Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s presidential caucuses on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The National Weather Service in Des Moines has warned voters to expect \u8220\'20\'1Cfrigid\u8221\'20\'1D conditions to continue today with temperatures to rise midweek.\par \par \uc2 enltrFrigid conditions are expected to continue, with coldest conditions today as highs remain below zero. By midweek, temperatures will improve into the teens before falling back into the single digits by Friday. Light snow chances remain late Wednesday and Thursday. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/iawx?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #iawx}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kPCzHncUpt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kPCzHncUpt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NWS Des Moines (@NWSDesMoines) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NWSDesMoines/status/1746910108079264129?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has dismissed Florida senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s backing of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as evidence that the former president is in line with the \u8220\'20\'1CDC establishment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-donald-trump-republicans-ron-desantis-nikki-haley-us-election-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-65a5341b8f086c5dbf627d5a#block-65a5341b8f086c5dbf627d5a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier,}}}\uc2  Rubio endorsed Trump on Sunday despite previously calling him a \u8220\'20\'1Ccon artist\u8221\'20\'1D who was not worthy of the presidency.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to CNN this morning, DeSantis pointed out that he had endorsements from more state lawmakers than Trump and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 . He said:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the party of Washington DC establishment. They have lined up behind him. I am the candidate that would be a change agent in Washington DC. And I like that contrast.\par \par \uc2 He said tonight\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses will create a clear, binary choice for voters, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI think people are going to say there\u8217\'20\'19s only two possible nominees: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or Governor DeSantis\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re the only ones that have strong support amongst bedrock Republican conservative voters, and to win a Republican nomination, you have got to be able to do that. I think Iowa will show that very clearly.\par \par \uc2 Florida governor and Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  during a campaign event at an event space in Ankeny, Iowa, USA, on Sunday. Photograph: Justin Lane/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  celebrated the Iowa caucuses by releasing its first youth-focused campaign ad of the 2024 election cycle.\par \par \uc2 The ad, which is running on campus kiosks at the \uc2 University of Iowa\uc2  and \uc2 Iowa State University\uc2 , criticizes the Republican presidential candidates for their positions on the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 In the video, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is seen describing climate change as a \u8220\'20\'1Choax\u8221\'20\'1D, while \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  brags about helping the US withdraw from the Paris climate agreement. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  similarly dismisses the climate crisis as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe politicization of the weather\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The DNC national press secretary, Sarafina Chitika, said of the ad:\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the first nominating contest for the most extreme Republican presidential field America has ever seen, where denying the threat of climate change has been the party line for the GOP, this campus campaign kicks off the DNC\u8217\'20\'19s early work to emphasize how the MAGA [\u8216\'20\'18Make America Great Again\u8217\'20\'19] agenda would be a disaster for generations to come.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 How will Iowa shape the 2024 US election?\par \par \uc2 Iowa winners don\u8217\'20\'19t always go on to be nominees \u8211\'20\'13 or presidents.\par \par \uc2 Among the Democrats, the last winner of a competitive Iowa caucus was \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , then the little-known mayor of South Bend, Indiana. He ended up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/mar/02/after-early-iowa-success-pete-buttigiegs-fiery-campaign-floundered-in-more-diverse-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsing Joe Biden}}}\uc2 , his reward a cabinet post. Before that, in 2008, Barack Obama beat \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  narrowly in Iowa and went on to the White House. In 2004, \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  beat \uc2 John Edwards\uc2  and won the nomination but lost the general election. In 2000, \uc2 Al Gore\uc2  won Iowa and the nomination but lost the White House to \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Of late, fewer Republicans have won Iowa and the nomination. In 2016, Ted Cruz lost the nomination to Trump. In 2012, \uc2 Rick Santorum{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/itsallpolitics/2012/01/21/145553419/iowa-gop-officially-declares-santorum-the-iowa-caucus-winner#:~:text=Music%20Of%202023-,Iowa%20GOP%20Officially%20Declares%20Santorum%20The%20Iowa%20Caucus%20Winner%20%3A%20It's,Romney%20an%20eight%2Dvote%20lead."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  won}}}\uc2  Iowa but lost the nomination to \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 . In 2008, \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2  beat Romney but \uc2 John McCain\uc2 , fourth in Iowa, became the nominee. In 2000, \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a rare candidate with appeal both to evangelicals and moderates \u8211\'20\'13 was a clear winner on his way to the White House.\par \par \uc2 So losers in Iowa can very much go on to win the race elsewhere. As Tom Beaumont of the Associated Press explains, for Iowa Republicans this year:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  remains the dominant frontrunner [and] the race is essentially for second place. \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  is in the race for second place in Iowa. Should Haley beat \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , that would almost certainly signal the end of the DeSantis campaign and provide a lift to Haley, who is stronger than any other [non-Trump] candidate in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Why does Iowa get to go first?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIowa got its spot by historical accident,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/article/iowa-caucus-explainer.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times puts it}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Responding to a previous political fiasco, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/mar/13/donald-trump-1968-election-violence-chicago-richard-nixon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protest-racked}}}\uc2  Chicago convention of 1968, Democrats wanted to give voters more of a say than party insiders in picking a nominee. In 1972, Iowa Democrats happened to schedule the first such contest. Four years later, Iowa Republicans did the same, while \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  came from nowhere to win the Democratic caucus, the nomination and the keys to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe power of going first thus clearly demonstrated,\u8221\'20\'1D the Times said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Iowa legislature passed a law requiring the state to continue scheduling its caucuses before any others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Is Iowa the right state to vote first?\par \par \uc2 Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s first-in-the-nation status has long been questioned, given that it \u8211\'20\'13 like New Hampshire \u8211\'20\'13 is predominantly rural and white in a country trending ever more urban and demographically mixed.\par \par \uc2 On the flip side, David Yepsen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2016/01/29/464804185/why-does-iowa-vote-first-anyway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offers}}}\uc2  a historical nugget that points to a place in the tapestry of US life \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CCaucus is thought to be a Native American term, Algonquin for meeting of tribal leaders\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and even Iowa is changing: white children, for example, are now in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dmschools.org/about/facts-figures/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a clear minority}}}\uc2  in Des Moines public schools.\par \par \uc2 If they were running a traditional caucus, the lack of diversity would be an issue for Democrats. But they aren\u8217\'20\'19t, because of the mess last time and because of concerns about diversity. They now kick off with South Carolina, where Black voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/feb/29/south-carolina-primary-voters-joe-biden-bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saved Joe Biden}}}\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 For the Republicans, the question of whiteness is less of an (internal) problem. Heavily influenced by evangelical Christians, the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa caucuses offer a reasonable indicator of the temperature inside the party. Eight years ago, the last time the GOP caucuses were competitive, the Texas senator Ted Cruz courted evangelicals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/feb/01/ted-cruz-wins-iowa-caucus-donald-trump-marco-rubio-2016-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and won}}}\uc2 . This year, a key {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/nov/23/trump-iowa-evangelicals-pieces-of-shit-book-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsement}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  notwithstanding, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  seems to have the evangelical vote sewn up.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Explainer: What are the Iowa caucuses?\par \par \uc2 The 2024 US presidential election begins in earnest in Iowa on Monday, as Republicans in the midwestern state stage their caucuses, events through which their preferred nominee is selected. The process is hallowed but arcane. Here\u8217\'20\'19s an attempt to explain.\par \par \uc2 What is a caucus?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/caucus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Merriam-Webster}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s Most Trusted Dictionary\u8221\'20\'1D, defines a caucus thus:\par \par \uc2 A closed meeting of a group of persons belonging to the same political party or faction usually to select candidates or to decide on policy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2016/01/29/464804185/why-does-iowa-vote-first-anyway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Yepsen}}}\uc2 , a doyen of Iowa political journalism, boils it down:\par \par \uc2 A caucus \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s a neighbourhood meeting.\par \par \uc2 And as Tom Beaumont of the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/video/new-hampshire-des-moines-florida-joe-biden-tom-beaumont-d84b3c489fa948b3bed83a76d84eb7f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explains}}}\uc2 , more than 1,600 such meetings will take place on Monday, \u8220\'20\'1Cone for every precinct in the state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Either which way, it\u8217\'20\'19s not a primary, the straight-vote contest held by most states, starting in New Hampshire next week.\par \par \uc2 How does a caucus work?\par \par \uc2 In Iowa, Republican and Democratic caucuses work differently. Now, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/02/04/us/politics/what-happened-iowa-caucuses.html#:~:text=Unexplained%20%E2%80%9Cinconsistencies%E2%80%9D%20in%20results%2C,state%20of%20almost%20suspended%20animation."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chaos and confusion}}}\uc2  in 2020, Democrats have made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/iowa-democrats-move-caucus-results-super-tuesday-rcna119222"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changes}}}\uc2  : they will meet on caucus day and conduct political business, but their choice for president will be made by mail and announced later.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are going ahead as usual. That means participants will gather in each precinct \u8211\'20\'13 usually a school, community center or similar venue \u8211\'20\'13 at 7pm local time (8pm ET) on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Eligible voters, who must be registered Republicans, check in to the caucus and then start discussing candidates and issues with their neighbors. As Beaumont said, some also \u8220\'20\'1Cstand up and speak on behalf of the candidates\u8221\'20\'1D. Within an hour or so, the caucusgoers write their choice of candidate on a slip of paper and hand it to the chair of the caucus, who then tallies the votes and submits them to the state party. The state party counts and releases the results, usually within a few hours.\par \par \uc2 Each precinct is then assigned a number of delegates based on the results. Ultimately, 40 delegates from Iowa will go to the Republican national convention, where the presidential nominee for the party is chosen.\par \par \uc2 In terms of the presidential race, the person with the most votes \u8220\'20\'1Cwins\u8221\'20\'1D Iowa. In practice, delegates to a state convention are awarded on a proportionate basis, so everyone \u8220\'20\'1Cwins\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 in a way.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A cold coming we had of it. Icy winds blow across the plains, numbing the face and cutting to the bone. Stranded cars and tractor trailers lie abandoned at the side of highways. Snow is piled high on the side of every road in the state capital, where giant icicles hang off buildings. Candidates\u8217\'20\'19 yard signs and children\u8217\'20\'19s playgrounds have been enveloped by a white blanket.\par \par \uc2 Welcome to Iowa, often described as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/feb/01/iowa-caucuses-temporary-center-america-political-universe-us-election-2020-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 centre of the political universe}}}\uc2  at this stage of the US electoral cycle, but currently feeling more like the outer reaches of our solar system.\par \par \uc2 It is here, amid wind chills of around -40F (-40C), that Monday will witness the dawn of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/27/politics-2024-trump-biden-election-democracy-authoritarian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 2024 presidential election}}}\uc2 , the first since the insurrection of 6 January 2021, when US democracy itself hung by a thread.\par \par \uc2 The brutal weather has proved timely for reporters in need of something to talk about ahead of some particularly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/iowa-caucuses-who-will-win-trump-desantis-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-climactic Iowa caucuses}}}\uc2 . Democrats are not actively engaged this time, while the Republican race has never been such a foregone conclusion: Donald Trump in an avalanche.\par \par \uc2 The only suspenseful questions on what is expected to be the coldest caucus night ever are: will Trump exceed 50% of the vote and will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/nikki-haley-iowa-caucuses-republican-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley}}}\uc2 , a former US ambassador to the UN, eclipse the one-time rising star {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/ron-desantis-iowa-caucuses-republican-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , the governor of Florida?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-2024-donald-trump-weather"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read our Washington DC bureau chief David Smith\u8217\'20\'19s full report from Des Moines, Iowa: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-2024-donald-trump-weather"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In deep Iowa snow, Trump expected to win caucuses in an avalanche}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/15/iowa-caucuses-2024-donald-trump-weather"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In deep Iowa snow, Trump expected to win caucuses in an avalanche}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re still hours away from the 7pm CT start of the caucuses here in Des Moines, but Nikki Haley\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign has started their day off by releasing a new television ad dinging Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 The spot makes light of his predictions that he will win the first state to vote in the Republican primary process by 60% \u8211\'20\'13 which would be the biggest-ever win for a non-incumbent Republican. Haley\u8217\'20\'19s campaign wrote:\par \par \uc2 Sixty points? The latest Des Moines Register/NBC News poll shows Trump with a lead of less than half his prediction and the kick-off to a two-person race between Nikki Haley and Trump.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the ad:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley expressed confidence that Iowans would not be deterred from the cold weather and turn out and caucus for her today.\par \par \uc2 Haley, in an interview with on Fox and Friends this morning, said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermined to be out there in the snow until the very last second, trying to earn every vote\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Citing a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/WSJ_Poll_Dec_2023.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  that found her beating Joe Biden in a head-to-head match by 17 points, Haley said she would have a \u8220\'20\'1Cdouble digit mandate going into DC\u8221\'20\'1D to make sure \u8220\'20\'1Cwe get our economy back under control, reduce inflation, get our kids reading again, securing our borders once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Former South Carolina Governor and Republican presidential candidate Nikki Haley campaigns in Ames, Iowa, on Sunday. Photograph: Alex Wroblewski/UPI/REX/Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 On the eve of the caucuses, Donald Trump predicted he would set a modern-day record for an Iowa Republican caucus with a margin-of-victory exceeding the nearly 13 percentage points that Bob Dole earned in 1988.\par \par \uc2 He also sought to downplay expectations that he would earn as much as 50% of the total vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump, Haley, DeSantis in big test in freezing Iowa\par \par \uc2 Iowa Republicans will brave brutally cold temperatures on Monday evening to participate in the state\u8217\'20\'19s presidential caucuses, as Donald Trump remains the clear frontrunner in the race for his party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination.\par \par \uc2 The final results will depend on turnout, which could be acutely impacted by the weather. After a blizzard swept through Iowa on Friday, many roads remained covered in snow as temperatures dropped well below freezing.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/trump-admits-concern-that-icy-weather-could-harm-his-support-in-iowa-caucuses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 acknowledged}}}\uc2  on Saturday that he was concerned about the weather affecting caucus turnout but expressed confidence in his supporters\u8217\'20\'19 dedication.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to be cold. It\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be pleasant,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said at a campaign event in West Des Moines on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re willing to brave the elements and be there for the couple hours that you have to be there, if you\u8217\'20\'19re willing to do that and you\u8217\'20\'19re willing to fight for me on Monday night, then as president I\u8217\'20\'19ll be fighting for you for the next eight years.\par \par \uc2 Even as the National Weather Service {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NWSDesMoines/status/1746321478650323228"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Clife-threatening\u8221\'20\'1D cold, Iowa voters largely shrugged off questions about how they would reach their caucus sites.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in the country live like this all the time,\u8221\'20\'1D said Abbey Sindt, a caucus-goer who attended Haley\u8217\'20\'19s town hall in Ames on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CSo it\u8217\'20\'19s really not that big of a deal, in my opinion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Max Richardson, who also attended the town hall, agreed with Sindt, saying,\par \par \uc2 Everyone\u8217\'20\'19s shoveled out. Everyone\u8217\'20\'19s getting the ice melt down. It\u8217\'20\'19s just a question of, can you get the car there?\par \par \uc2 A supporter of former Donald Trump places a placard in a pile of snow as he braves the below zero temperatures to attend a rally in Indianola, Iowa. Photograph: Jim Watson/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Florida senator Marco Rubio formally endorsed Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential campaign on Sunday, effectively snubbing his state\u8217\'20\'19s own governor Ron DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 In a social media post, Rubio cited his work with Trump to expand child tax credit as well as sanctions placed on Cuba and Venezuela as reasons for throwing his support behind the former president. Rubio added:\par \par \uc2 I support Trump because that kind of leadership is the ONLY way we will get the extraordinary actions needed to fix the disaster Biden has created.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhen Trump was in WH I achieved major policies I had worked on for years (like expanded Child Tax Credit & tough sanctions on regime in Cuba & Venezuela) because we had a President who didn\u8217\'20\'19t cave to special interests or let bureaucrats block us.\par \par \uc2 I support Trump because that\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Marco Rubio (@marcorubio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marcorubio/status/1746629924432310551?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Rubio previously ran against Trump in 2016, during which he called him a \u8220\'20\'1Ccon artist\u8221\'20\'1D who had \u8220\'20\'1Cno ideas of any substance\u8221\'20\'1D before dropping out after losing the Florida primary. Trump, meanwhile, repeatedly taunted Rubio with the nickname \u8220\'20\'1CLittle Marco\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Rubio\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement means that both of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senators have opted not to back their own governor. Rick Scott endorsed Trump in November.\par \par \uc2 Republican US senator for Florida Marco Rubio at his midterm election night 8 November, 2022. Photograph: Joe Skipper/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump holds dominant lead ahead of Iowa caucuses, poll finds\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump looks set to win Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s first-in-nation vote in the Republican presidential nomination race by a record margin tonight.\par \par \uc2 A final poll by renowned Iowa pollster Ann Selzer published on Saturday night shows the former president holding a nearly 30-point lead over his rivals.\par \par \uc2 The final NBC News/Des Moines Register/Mediacom Iowa {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/24360638-final-iowa-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  poll}}}\uc2  before today\u8217\'20\'19s GOP caucuses shows Trump with the support of 48% of likely caucus-goers, followed by Nikki Haley at 20%, Ron DeSantis at 16% and Vivek Ramaswamy at 8%.\par \par \uc2 If Trump\u8217\'20\'19s current lead holds, it would be the largest margin of victory for a non-incumbent competing in Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s Republican presidential caucuses. The current record margin, 13 points, was set by Bob Dole in 1988.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Iowans are set to brave subzero temperatures on Monday when they arrive at their caucus sites at 7pm to formally kick off the process to choose their nominee.\par \par \uc2 In terms of pure numbers, the Iowa caucuses won\u8217\'20\'19t have much of a role in determining who the Republican nominee is. The state allocates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.270towin.com/2024-republican-nomination/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  40 delegates}}}\uc2  in the Republican nominating contest, roughly just 1.6% of the more than 2,400 that are up for grabs. But that small total belies the outsized influence the state can have on US presidential politics.\par \par \uc2 For more than half a century, Iowa has come to occupy a near-mythological place in American politics \u8211\'20\'13 becoming known as the place where underdogs can become serious contenders and where dreams of the White House can die. The rural state\u8217\'20\'19s voters often reward retail politicking, giving hope to candidates who visit its 99 counties to shake hands and give stump speeches.\par \par \uc2 Since the 1970s, its caucuses have been the first nominating contest in each presidential cycle. Candidates crisscross the state in hopes of exceeding expectations and gaining momentum. And while it does not always pick the eventual nominee \u8211\'20\'13 Ted Cruz, Rick Santorum and Mike Huckabee have all won there \u8211\'20\'13 victories there have been rocket fuel to candidates like Jimmy Carter and Barack Obama.\par \par \uc2 Iowa is not first because it\u8217\'20\'19s important. It\u8217\'20\'19s important because it\u8217\'20\'19s first\par \par \uc2 said Dennis Goldford, a professor at Drake University in Des Moines and the co-author of The Iowa Precinct Caucuses: The Making of a Media Event. \u8220\'20\'1CThe morning after the caucuses, Iowa falls off the face of the earth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/13/why-is-iowa-caucus-first-important-democratic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read our full explainer here: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/13/why-is-iowa-caucus-first-important-democratic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa caucuses are \u8216\'20\'18important because they\u8217\'20\'19re first\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 but are they democratic?}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/13/why-is-iowa-caucus-first-important-democratic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa caucuses are \u8216\'20\'18important because they\u8217\'20\'19re first\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 but are they democratic?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As well as the extreme cold weather possibly affecting turnout later, Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses are also playing out on Martin Luther King Day, which is a federal holiday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Iowans told to 'limit outdoor exposure' as the 'dangerous cold' sweeps the state\par \par \uc2 Iowans have been told to \u8220\'20\'1Climit outdoor exposure\u8221\'20\'1D as much as possible with forecasters saying the wind chill temperature could go down to as low as -35F on Monday evening in the \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous cold\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The life-threatening cold blanketing the midwest, which already forced the campaigns to cancel several events over the weekend, could lead to a lower turnout later today.\par \par \uc2 Unlike a regular election, Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses require voters to gather in person.\par \par \uc2 enltrDangerous cold is expected to continue today and into Tuesday morning, with wind chills down to 30 to 35 below zero expected. If possible, limit outdoor exposure as much as possible and dress warmly. Stay warm out there! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/iawx?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #iawx}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/weyZ2iJsFJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/weyZ2iJsFJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NWS Des Moines (@NWSDesMoines) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NWSDesMoines/status/1746868467029144052?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Monday has been forecast to potentially be a record cold caucus night with temperatures as low as -20F (-29C). Biting winds could make it feel as cold as -45F in some places.\par \par \uc2 Data from the National Weather Service indicates that the coldest caucus before this year was in 2004, when temperatures did not rise above 16 degrees.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The MyPillow chief, Mike Lindell, a close ally and cheerleader for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his bogus stolen election claims, is expanding his own conspiratorial TV network, while aggressively stumping for Trump again and fighting defamation lawsuits from two electronic voting firms, one of which wants over $1bn in damages.\par \par \uc2 The moves by Lindell show the continuing presence of powerful parts of the pro-Trump movement, undeterred by the extensive legal peril their false claims of election fraud due to electronic voting machines have caused them.\par \par \uc2 His expansion of his television network also shows the growing power of rightwing media as the 2024 race for the White House gets under way, and its ability to elevate conspiracy theories.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story by my colleague, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/peter-stone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Stone}}}\uc2 , here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/15/mypillow-ceo-expand-lindell-tv-network-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Election-denying MyPillow chief plots TV expansion in bid to help Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden and the Democrats raise $97m to close out 2023\par \par \uc2 US president, Joe Biden, and the Democratic National Committee have said they raised more than $97m (\u163\'00\'A376m) in the final three months of last year.\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign said it took in $235m (\u163\'00\'A3185m) from its launch last April until the end of 2023 and finished the year with $117m (\u163\'00\'A392m) in cash on hand \u8211\'20\'13 which it said was the highest total amassed by any Democratic candidate at this point in the cycle.\par \par \uc2 It added that over 520,000 donors made 926,000-plus contributions in the last quarter of 2023.\par \par \uc2 Julie Chavez Rodriguez, the Biden-Harris 2024 campaign manager, said:\par \par \uc2 This historic haul- proudly powered by strong and growing grassroots enthusiasm \u8211\'20\'13 sends a clear message: the team Biden-Harris coalition knows the stakes of this election and is ready to win this November.\par \par \uc2 Across our coalition, we are seeing early, sustained support that is helping us scale our growing operation across the country and take our message to the communities that will determine this election.\par \par \uc2 Our democracy and hard-fought basic rights and freedoms are on the line in 2024, and these numbers prove that the American people know the stakes and are taking action early to help defeat the extreme Maga Republican agenda again.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis and Nikki Haley have both expressed confidence that they would exceed expectations on Monday.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis \u8211\'20\'13 whose pitch to voters has been that he would replicate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/florida-man"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his conservative remaking of Florida}}}\uc2  on the national stage \u8211\'20\'13 told Fox News on Sunday: \u8220\'20\'1CI have a record of doing well as the underdog \u8230\'20\'26 we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna do well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only numbers that matter are the ones that we\u8217\'20\'19re going up and everybody else went down,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley told the network. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that shows that we\u8217\'20\'19re doing the right thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis at a campaign event in Ankeny, Iowa. Photograph: Justin Lane/EPA Nikki Haley holds final rally in Adel before Iowa caucus day. Photograph: Gage Skidmore/ZUMA Press Wire/REX/Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Iowa caucuses begin at 8pm ET on Monday evening (1am GMT on Tuesday). Caucus participants will gather inside more than 1,500 schools, churches and community centers to debate their options, in some cases for hours, before casting secret ballots.\par \par \uc2 To find out more about the mechanics of the Iowa caucuses and the influence they will have on the 2024 US election, you can read this useful explainer by my colleague, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2 , here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/12/what-are-iowa-caucuses-2024-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What are the Iowa caucuses and how will they shape the 2024 US election?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump forecast to get nearly 50% of vote in final Iowa poll as brutal cold grips state\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The 2024 US presidential election begins in earnest in Iowa on Monday, when voters across the midwestern state will battle freezing temperatures to gather in the unique caucus format to select their Republican candidate of choice.\par \par \uc2 The final Des Moines Register/NBC News poll before Monday night\u8217\'20\'19s caucuses found former president, Donald Trump, maintaining a formidable lead over his opponents, supported by 48% of likely caucus-goers.\par \par \uc2 After trailing the two-term Florida governor, Ron DeSantis for months, the latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/final-iowa-poll-trump-maintains-dominant-lead-caucuses-rcna132669"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  showed Nikki Haley, the former South Carolina governor, in second place in Iowa, winning the support of 20% of likely Republican caucus-goers, compared to DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s 16%, with Vivek Ramaswamy at 8%.\par \par \uc2 Should DeSantis finish lower than second place, it could prove fatal to his ability to continue competing in New Hampshire, the next state to vote, and later in the primaries.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Trump campaign hopes that a victory in Iowa would give him enough momentum to win the next contests in New Hampshire, South Carolina and Michigan, putting him ahead of the field for Super Tuesday on 5 March.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump supports carry placards as they brave the below zero temperatures to attend a rally in Indianola, Iowa, on 14 January 2024. Photograph: Jim Watson/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 If he exceeds 50% of the vote in Iowa, Trump will earn what he predicted would be \u8220\'20\'1Ca historic landslide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Monday is forecast to be a record cold caucus night with temperatures potentially reaching around as low as -20F (-29C).\par \par \uc2 The Florida senator, Marco Rubio, on Sunday become the 24th Republican senator to endorse Trump for president, meaning he is now one Republican senator short of securing the majority support of the GOP senators.\par \par \uc2 Former Republican presidential candidate and North Dakota governor, Doug Burgum, also endorsed Trump for president on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240115ek1f001ms\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
