\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump accuses judge and Letitia James of bias in surprise court address during fraud trial closing arguments - as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now); Chris Stein, Erum Salam and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 6,958 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 January 2024\par 22:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The live blog is now closed, but please read about the Trump civil fraud trial here:Trump says he is \u8216\'20\'18innocent\u8217\'20\'19 of fraud as bomb threat upends last day of trial\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today's recap\par \par \uc2 The last day of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial set off a frenzy in New York on Thursday morning, with a bomb squad called to the home of the judge overseeing the case and crowds of reporters and spectators packing the courtroom to see the trial\u8217\'20\'19s end.\par \par \uc2 Thursday was the last chance for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team to make an appeal to Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , who will decide whether Trump will be fined as much as $370m for falsifying financial statements to inflate his net worth.\par \par \uc2 Before the hearing, police in Nassau county on Long Island said they responded to a security incident at Engoron\u8217\'20\'19s residence at 5.30am. Engoron and his staff have been frequent targets of vitriolic criticism from Trump throughout the case, and his office has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/22/new-york-trump-trial-judge-arthur-engoron-clerk-death-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bombarded with death threats}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 After sitting quietly during his attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 closing arguments, the former president launched into a rant. Trump insisted that he was persecuted by \u8220\'20\'1Csomeone running for office\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to Letitia James, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  attorney general who brought the case against him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A small group of anti-Trump protesters briefly blocked traffic in front of the courthouse holding a banner and chanting \u8220\'20\'1CNo dictators in the USA!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Christopher Kise called the case \u8220\'20\'1Cinsane\u8221\'20\'1D and said James was prosecuting a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictimless\u8221\'20\'1D offense.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  says he intends to release his decision by the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dominic-rushe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic Rushe}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2  in New York\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/11/trump-judge-bomb-threat-new-york-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump says he is \u8216\'20\'18innocent\u8217\'20\'19 of fraud as bomb threat upends last day of trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will do my best and I hope to issue a final decision in this case by January 31,\u8221\'20\'1D said Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CNot a promise. Not a guarantee. But I\u8217\'20\'19m reasonably confident I\u8217\'20\'19ll be able to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a review of how the day unfolded:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/11/trump-judge-bomb-threat-new-york-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump says he is \u8216\'20\'18innocent\u8217\'20\'19 of fraud as bomb threat upends last day of trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Per reporters in the courtroom, closing arguments in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil trial have now concluded.\par \par \uc2 Attorneys for both parties are leaving the room, and Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  says he intends to release his decision by the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge says he will decide Trump civil penalties by 31 January - report\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  just said he will aim to release his decision in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial by the end of the month, MSNBC reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrEngoron: I will do my best to issue my opinion by Jan. 31 and am \u8220\'20\'1Creasonably confident that I will be able to do so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745565237095415814?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The New York attorney general, Letitia James, wants the former president to pay $370m and be banned from the real estate industry for life, among other penalties, for fraudulently inflating the value of his assets to secure better financial terms.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a different courtroom on the other side of the country, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  just entered a plea of not guilty to federal tax charges that were recently leveled against him.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/hunter-biden-criminal-case-joe-biden-2024-015cba20dfba90930706fc8a7d4ae38d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the Associated Press}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s son pleaded not guilty Thursday to federal tax charges filed after the collapse of a plea deal that could have spared him the spectacle of a criminal trial during the 2024 campaign.\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  has been accused of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/hunter-biden-tax-charges-special-counsel-75b2aa05f247535677454ff2dfa7c71f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nine felony and misdemeanor tax offenses}}}\uc2 . The charges stem from what federal prosecutors say was a four-year scheme to skip out on paying the $1.4 million he owed to the \uc2 IRS\uc2  and instead use the money to fund an extravagant lifestyle that by his own admission included drugs and alcohol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here today because you\u8217\'20\'19ve been accused by the United States of a criminal offense,\u8221\'20\'1D Judge Mark Scarsi said to Biden, who entered the not guilty plea himself.\par \par \uc2 The judge set a tentative trial date of June 20 during the half-hour-long hearing.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/hunter-biden-court-gun-charges-indictment-investigation-68b186294bb36071c02428834ec5f470"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meanwhile, Hunter Biden has also been charged in Delaware}}}\uc2  with lying in October 2018 on a federal form for gun purchasers when he swore he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t using or addicted to illegal drugs. He was addicted to crack cocaine at the time. He\u8217\'20\'19s also accused of possessing the gun illegally and has pleaded not guilty in that case.\par \par \uc2 The accusations all come from a yearslong federal investigation into \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tax and business dealings that had been expected to wind down over the summer with a plea deal in which he would have gotten two years\u8217\'20\'19 probation after pleading guilty to misdemeanor tax charges. He also would have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/hunter-biden-gun-charges-e9b902d7cd7061101d616bdececfc078"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 avoided prosecution on the gun charge}}}\uc2  if he stayed out of trouble.\par \par \uc2 From July, here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  with an explainer on how a deal with prosecutors for Biden to avoid going to trial on the allegations suddenly collapsed:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/26/why-hunter-biden-plea-deal-fell-apart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden: what happened with his plea deal and why?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York prosecutors again demand $370m penalty against Trump for real estate fraud - report\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors for the New York attorney general, Letitia James, have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/05/trump-civil-fraud-new-york-letitia-james"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reiterated}}}\uc2  that they would like to see a $370m penalty and lifetime ban from the real estate business for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in his civil fraud trial, the Messenger reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrSummations return to AG's counsel Kevin Wallace one more time to describe the relief the state is requesting, e.g. the ~$370M disgorgement, lifetime NY real estate industry ban, and other injunctions.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745559325995667748?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 They said the weighty penalty was necessary because Trump kept breaking the law even after authorities began investigating his business practices:\par \par \uc2 enltrWallace notes that the severity of the punishment depends in part on whether it was an isolated incident.\par \par \uc2 It wasn't; it was pervasive, he answers.\par \par \uc2 "The conduct continued even while the defendants were under investigation by the Manhattan DA and by our office," he adds.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745560430804631928?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors with the New York attorney general \u8217\'20\'19s office are delivering their closing arguments at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s New York fraud trial.\par \par \uc2 Trump left the building after delivering a bizarre impromptu rant, which was cut off by the judge, who called for a lunch break.\par \par \uc2 State attorney Kevin Wallace said that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers relied on expert testimony, rather than witness testimony or documented evidence, to bolster their arguments. At one point, Wallace put up a presentation slide that showed the 11 expert witnesses the defense had called during the trial. He noted that many of the expert witnesses were purposely shown limited evidence, and a handful of them were close allies of Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey cannot argue that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s triplex was in fact 30,000 sq ft,\u8221\'20\'1D Wallace said. \u8220\'20\'1COr that unsold units at Trump Park Avenue weren\u8217\'20\'19t rent stabilized.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wallace also argued that the loans the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  received with the inflated financial statements were \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical to the business\u8221\'20\'1D and the business was strapped for cash in the mid-2010s as the company pursued renovation of properties and Trump was running for president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey could have cut costs or sell assets, but these interest rates were vital to the operation of the company,\u8221\'20\'1D Wallace said, adding that Trump was also able to run for president with the loans bolstering his company. \u8220\'20\'1CThey didn\u8217\'20\'19t have to choose between their priorities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Arguments in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial have now resumed, MSNBC reports, and will probably conclude soon:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: In the final stretch of their closing argument, the New York AG\u8217\'20\'19s office focuses on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own intent. He testified he reviewed and approved the final versions of the statements of financial condition and occasionally had comments.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745551031625228642?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is being arraigned in Los Angeles today on federal tax charges recently filed against him. Expect to hear plenty about this from Republicans as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign continues:\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is expected to be arraigned on Thursday on federal tax charges in a Los Angeles courthouse.\par \par \uc2 Biden, who has a home in Malibu, is expected to plead not guilty to nine tax-related charges that were filed in December. Three of the charges faced by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s son are felony counts, and he could face up to 17 years in prison if found guilty.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe defendant engaged in a four-year scheme to not pay at least $1.4m in self-assessed federal taxes he owed for tax years 2016 through 2019,\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/07/us/politics/hunter-biden-indictment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 56-page}}}\uc2  indictment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/doj-files-new-criminal-charges-against-hunter-biden-cnn-2023-12-08/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , adding that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cspent millions of dollars on an extravagant lifestyle rather than paying his tax bills\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is expected to plead not guilty.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/11/hunter-biden-arraignment-federal-tax-charges-los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden expected to be arraigned on federal tax charges in Los Angeles}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing arguments in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s New York civil fraud trial are now paused while the court takes a brief recess, the Messenger reports.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dominic-rushe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic Rushe}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2  with a recap of what has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/11/trump-judge-bomb-threat-new-york-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bomb squad called to Trump judge\u8217\'20\'19s house hours before end of fraud trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Back at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial, his attorney Chris Kise has repeatedly interrupted Kevin Wallace, who is delivering closing arguments on behalf of the New York attorney general, Letitia James.\par \par \uc2 It appears to be a tactic on Kise\u8217\'20\'19s part. From MSNBC:\par \par \uc2 enltrChris Kise just interrupted Wallace, who described the 11 experts as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmurderer\u8217\'20\'19s row,\u8221\'20\'1D which Kise screamed was \u8220\'20\'1Coutrageous.\u8221\'20\'1D Engoron is unmoved; Wallace notes Lawrence Moens\u8217\'20\'19s valuation of Mar-a-Lago is only possible if one ignores the legal restrictions on the use of\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745532959199735970?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrKise is back on his feet, objecting that there is no evidence to support another of Wallace\u8217\'20\'19s arguments: that the Trump Org. was bleeding cash. \u8220\'20\'1CChris, just stop!\u8221\'20\'1D Wallace blurts. Engoron diffuses what could have devolved quickly.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745533526982705214?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr(What Kise is doing is tactical. He is purposefully trying to break Wallace\u8217\'20\'19s flow\u8212\'20\'14and is doing so with some success.)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745533871079211098?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he 'will go to all of my trials'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been spending quite a bit of time in court lately, and plans to continue doing so, even though he is also campaigning for president.\par \par \uc2 In remarks this afternoon, after going on a tirade against the New York attorney general, Letitia James, and Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  during the closing arguments of his civil fraud trial and then leaving the courtroom, Trump said he would attend all of his trials in person:\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer President Trump: "I want to go to all of my trials. These are all set up by Biden and the Democrats. This is their new form of cheating." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mV7mLJt6qt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mV7mLJt6qt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1745533998267269122?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 That is potentially {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quite a lot of court proceedings}}}\uc2 . Trump has been indicted four times at the state and federal level, and is also embroiled in multiple civil suits. He will have to balance these legal matters with his quest to win the Republican presidential nomination \u8211\'20\'13 which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/?ex_cid=abcpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls show he is the favorite}}}\uc2  to do \u8211\'20\'13 and beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the November general election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House condemns threats against judges after New York bomb scare\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  has condemned a recent wave of threats targeting elected officials and judges.\par \par \uc2 Her comments at the daily White House press briefing came after a bomb squad was dispatched to the home of judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  this morning, ahead of the start of the closing arguments in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe condemn any violence or threats against any judges \u8230\'20\'26 or anyone. \u8230\'20\'26 We are going to continue to be steadfast about that,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 Lawyer for the former president have spent today making Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case before Engoron, who will decide whether Trump will be fined as much as $370m for falsifying financial statements to inflate his net worth.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the hearing, police in Nassau county on Long Island said they responded to a security incident at Engoron\u8217\'20\'19s residence at 5.30am. Engoron and his staff have been frequent targets of vitriolic criticism from Trump throughout the case, and his office has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/22/new-york-trump-trial-judge-arthur-engoron-clerk-death-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bombarded with death threats}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More on that here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/11/trump-judge-bomb-threat-new-york-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bomb squad called to Trump judge\u8217\'20\'19s house hours before end of fraud trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors begin closing arguments in Trump fraud trial - report\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general Letitia James \u8217\'20\'19s prosecutors have now started delivering their closing arguments in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial, the Messenger reports:\par \par \uc2 Lawyer Kevin Wallace is telling the court that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s arguments in his defense were based on facts already known to be invalid. Trump is not in the room, the Messenger says, having left after his unexpected tirade at the conclusion of his side\u8217\'20\'19s closing arguments:\par \par \uc2 enltrAssistant AG Kevin Wallace kicks off his closing arguments with a Watergate reference:\par \par \uc2 "What did the defendants know, and when did they know it?"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745526886468366719?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWallace:\par \par \uc2 "You certainly did not hear that the numbers the defendants used were accurate."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745527117129937096?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWallace describes Trump's efforts to shift the blame to accounting firm \uc2 Mazars\uc2  as one of the defense's "undead arguments."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745527977662681490?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 John Kirby was also questioned on the hospitalization of the US secretary of defense, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , and why the White House was not informed in a timely manner that the Pentagon chief transferred his authority to his deputy.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s internal watchdog said a review will be conducted surrounding the secrecy of Austin\u8217\'20\'19s health condition and why the defense department waited days to inform the White House about the transfer of authority.\par \par \uc2 Austin is still hospitalized. He is being treated for complications from prostate cancer surgery.\par \par \uc2 Kirby said the lack of communication was a learning opportunity and that it shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have happened.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, as South Africa formally accuses Israel of committing genocide against Palestinians in the United Nations\u8217\'20\'19 top court, John Kirby, spokesperson for the US national security council, answered questions about the war in Gaza in a White House press briefing.\par \par \uc2 When asked if the US will accept any penalties or punishments handed down by the international court, Kirby said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to get into hypotheticals here. We\u8217\'20\'19ve made our position clear.\u8221\'20\'1D He said the Biden administration sees \u8220\'20\'1Cno indication Israel is violating laws surrounding armed conflict\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He was also asked about the timeline of the US\u8217\'20\'19s pleas to Israel to de-escalate the violence in Gaza, to which he responded: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ll have to talk to the \uc2 IDF\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is also running a global live blog on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza and the wider situation in the Middle East, which you can follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jan/11/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-israel-gaza-war-hamas-palestine-south-africa-genocide-case-icj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/11/trump-trial-civil-fraud-case-latest-biden-republicans-updates?page=with:block-65a0069c8f08438ab216c4c8#block-65a0069c8f08438ab216c4c8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hours}}}\uc2  of closing arguments by his attorneys, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  went on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/11/trump-trial-civil-fraud-case-latest-biden-republicans-updates?page=with:block-65a02bfc8f08319df2049187#block-65a02bfc8f08319df2049187"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a surprise tirade}}}\uc2  in the Manhattan courtroom where his civil fraud trial is being held, accusing Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  and the New York attorney general, Letitia James, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/11/trump-trial-civil-fraud-case-latest-biden-republicans-updates?page=with:block-65a02e6a8f0880950d17eb36#block-65a02e6a8f0880950d17eb36"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of bias}}}\uc2  against him. He then left the courtroom, and prosecutors now are expected to deliver their final statements in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/11/trump-trial-civil-fraud-case-latest-biden-republicans-updates?page=with:block-659ed5f98f08b223cc64c856#block-659ed5f98f08b223cc64c856"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the case}}}\uc2  that could see Engoron impose severe penalties on the former president and his co-defendants.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at the day so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Police investigated{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/11/trump-trial-civil-fraud-case-latest-biden-republicans-updates?page=with:block-659ff4cb8f086f8ed62f2b5d#block-659ff4cb8f086f8ed62f2b5d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bomb threat at Engoron\u8217\'20\'19s home}}}\uc2  just before closing arguments began this morning.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail in Iowa, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/11/trump-trial-civil-fraud-case-latest-biden-republicans-updates?page=with:block-65a001f08f08438ab216c486#block-65a001f08f08438ab216c486"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump took credit}}}\uc2  for the downfall of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Anti-Trump protesters{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jan/11/trump-trial-civil-fraud-case-latest-biden-republicans-updates?page=with:block-65a003fe8f086f8ed62f2c18#block-65a003fe8f086f8ed62f2c18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gathered}}}\uc2  outside the courthouse briefly blocked traffic this morning.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump leaves courtroom after accusing judge, attorney general of bias - report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  walked out of the courtroom after excoriating both New York attorney general Letitia James and Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  for the civil fraud accusations against him, MSNBC reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump goes on \u8212\'20\'14 without any interruption from Engoron or her team \u8212\'20\'14 and attacks James, accusing her of election interference. \u8220\'20\'1CYou have your own agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump angrily says to Engoron. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t listen for more than one minute!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745505818022154403?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrEngoron pleads with Kise, \u8220\'20\'1CMr. Kise, please control your client.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump nonetheless accuses James of going after him for her political gain, including an allegedly \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed\u8221\'20\'1D run for Governor, at which point Engoron shuts it down.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745506174198329698?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBut it\u8217\'20\'19s too late. Everything Trump wanted to say was said. And now, having said it, he has left the courtroom after insisting James should pay him for the havoc she\u8217\'20\'19s wreaked on his company.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745506304821453216?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he's being 'politically persecuted', in surprise address at civil fraud trial - report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has started addressing the court in the closing arguments of his civil fraud trial, MSNBC reports.\par \par \uc2 The former president had asked to deliver the closing arguments himself, rather than his attorneys, but Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  rejected that request yesterday. It was unclear if he was going to speak in the courtroom today, but MSNBC reports that Trump began talking shortly after his lawyer Chris Kise asked Engoron for permission:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Chris Kise asks for permission to have Trump speak. Engoron, \u8220\'20\'1CDo you promise to just comment on the facts and the law?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump starts talking immediately without agreeing.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745504676513014081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThis was a political witch hunt; we should receive damages for what they have taken our company through. They have no documents\u8212\'20\'14they have nothing!\u8221\'20\'1D The only thing they have, Trump concedes, is the triplex, which was a mistake.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745505089802965132?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI am not sure the dollar amount would have been that far off, if you want to know!\u8221\'20\'1D But Trump continues, \u8220\'20\'1CI am an innocent man. I have been politically persecuted.... This statute is vicious.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745505236653924779?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney Alina Habba is relying heavily on sarcasm in her closing arguments, the Messenger reports.\par \par \uc2 While the New York attorney general, Letitia James, successfully argued that Trump and his co-defendants knowingly inflated the value of his organization\u8217\'20\'19s assets to get better financial terms, Habba argued that the former president was guilty only of committing \u8220\'20\'1Chuman error\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrHabba's summations have been laced with heavy sarcasm and grand, dismissive gestures.\par \par \uc2 A representative quote: "Some fraud! What a fraudster!"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745498450366451989?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIn the same sarcastic tone, Habba disputes that Trump intentionally inflated the size of his New York triplex.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CExplain to me, if you\u8217\'20\'19re trying to commit fraud, why you would put in writing to a real estate agent, 'Excuse me, can you tell me how big this apartment is?'\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745499575194918966?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHabba:\par \par \uc2 "We\u8217\'20\'19re human beings. He did his best."\par \par \uc2 She calls it "human error."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745499900261937450?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorneys are continuing their closing arguments after a short break, with Alina Habba now up for the former president, MSNBC reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrAlina Habba, prowling the well of the courtroom, said this case started before Tish James was elected, pointing at the Attorney General. Engoron reminds her to stick to the facts, which she says she is trying to do, but that James\u8217\'20\'19s conduct is part of the factual record. 1/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745495531797848119?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrShe has not proven her case in the 44 days of this trial, Habba argues. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re right, Your Honor, you\u8217\'20\'19re not a pushover,\u8221\'20\'1D she agrees. But \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  thinks you are, and that\u8217\'20\'19s why he lied on the stand, Habba says.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745495935348507085?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  is, of course, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former attorney and fixer, who has since turned against him. He testified {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/michael-cohen-testify-trump-fraud-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in October}}}\uc2  that he inflated the value of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s assets to \u8220\'20\'1Cwhatever number Mr Trump told us to\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Congress and elsewhere who are allied with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have accused the Biden administration of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/donald-trump-fbi-durham-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weaponizing}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D the federal government against their enemies.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney Chris Kise is making a similar argument as his civil fraud trial draws to a close, MSNBC reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Trump civil fraud case is not just victimless, but is bigger than Trump and \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely dangerous.\u8221\'20\'1D It\u8217\'20\'19s the weaponization of Executive Law 63(12), Chris Kise insists, and it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cpreposterous\u8221\'20\'1D for the AG to \u8220\'20\'1Cattack demonstrably successful real estate\u8221\'20\'1D businesses.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745490292046786681?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a license for the AG to strip individuals of all their property\u8221\'20\'1D just because she says so based on her interpretation of a \u8220\'20\'1Cconsumer fraud statute.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t do it, Your Honor.\u8221\'20\'1D And with that, Kise sits down.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745490650647421243?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney Chris Kise called \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud \u8216\'20\'18victimless\u8217\'20\'19, the Messenger reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrKise argues that the AG is going after Trump in a "victimless" offense.\par \par \uc2 "It's insane," he says.\par \par \uc2 The AG's counsel Kevin Wallace argued it wasn't "victimless" in opening statements, and the state almost certainly will dispute this assertion this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745486658659635604?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Per MSNBC, it looks like Kise will soon finish his closing arguments. He is currently arguing the charges against Trump are unconstitutional:\par \par \uc2 enltrKise claims he\u8217\'20\'19ll be done in roughly 5 minutes, but before he concludes, he asserts that the remedies the AG seeks are not only unsupported by the evidence but are also unconstitutional. How so? 1/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745488766591021269?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHe says the relief would violate the Excessive Fines Clause, the Due Process Clause, the Takings Clause (as the relief sought would prevent Trump from disposing of his own property), and the Commerce Clause in that it would prohibit non-party New York businesses from transacting\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745488986859057552?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some images from the Manhattan courtroom, just before closing arguments got under way in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , with his attorneys Chris Kise (left) and Alina Habba (right). Photograph: Getty Images The New York attorney general, Letitia James, seated behind the former president. Photograph: Seth Wenig/AFP/Getty Images \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , the New York supreme court judge hearing the case. Photograph: Shannon Stapleton/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Christopher Kise accused the New York attorney general, Letitia James, of \u8220\'20\'1Cdragging Trump through the door\u8221\'20\'1D in the case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is an industry expert. He\u8217\'20\'19s been dealing with banks for 50 years,\u8221\'20\'1D Kise said. He repeated arguments made by the defense team over the course of the trial: that the lenders Trump worked with weren\u8217\'20\'19t defrauded and that the financial statements at the center of the case were prepared by the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmultimillion-dollar\u8221\'20\'1D accounting company, \uc2 Mazars USA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kise cited the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s brand value as evidence that the company had accurately valued, or even undervalued, its assets. He also argued that a disclaimer on the financial statement made clear to lenders to use the information at their discretion.\par \par \uc2 Engoron, in his pre-trial judgment, had struck down much of these arguments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese non-party disclaimers do not insulate defendants from liability,\u8221\'20\'1D Engoron had written.\par \par \uc2 There have been moments in Kise\u8217\'20\'19s arguments when Engoron appeared to be growing impatient. At one point, the judge told him that he does not have to accept testimony if he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t find it credible.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Central to New York attorney general Letitia James\u8217\'20\'19s case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been her claim that he deliberately inflated the value of Mar-a-Lago (among other properties) to secure better loan terms.\par \par \uc2 Chris Kise is arguing that the sprawling Florida resort is, in fact, a \u8220\'20\'1Csingle-family home\u8221\'20\'1D under the laws of Palm Beach, MSNBC reports, noting that James\u8217\'20\'19s prosecutors will probably hit back strongly at this:\par \par \uc2 enltrKise is now arguing that Trump is entitled to value Mar-a-Lago as a single family residence because nothing in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agreement with the Town of Palm Beach prohibits it. Suffice it to say that I expect a robust answer to this by the AG\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745473395725103213?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporters in the courtroom say \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney Chris Kise is arguing that that the New York attorney general, Letitia James, failed to prove the former president and his co-defendants committed fraud in his business dealings.\par \par \uc2 From MSNBC:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump lawyer Chris Kise argues they should win because according to two expert witnesses, Eli Bartov and Jason Flemmons, there were no indicia of fraud in the statements of financial condition.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745469201685319976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrUnsaid: The fact that Bartov never looked at the underlying supporting data that would have revealed the valuation methods and assumptions used therein and what made them allegedly fraudulent.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745469359110119583?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Per the Messenger, he\u8217\'20\'19s also saying Trump is important to New York\u8217\'20\'19s real estate market:\par \par \uc2 enltrKise says the AG is trying to "put someone who's been part of the fabric" of the New York State real estate industry out of business.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745464446502478211?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m in the courthouse for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fraud trial, and the courtroom is packed to the brim with reporters and spectators.\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  allowed photographers to take photos of the former president sitting with his attorneys at the defense table. Trump is wearing a navy suit and a red tie and is sitting next to attorneys Christopher Kise and Alina Habba.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI see the usual mixture of anticipation and dread out there,\u8221\'20\'1D Engoron joked as the room waited for the photographers. \u8220\'20\'1CTrust me, this will be painless.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t look any different than a month ago,\u8221\'20\'1D Engoron remarked.\par \par \uc2 The judge started with brief remarks marking the end of the trial.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here on the last today of a trial that commenced October 2,\u8221\'20\'1D Engoron said, thanking the attorneys for \u8220\'20\'1Chow hard you all worked\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney Kise is kicking things off today with closing arguments for the defense. He has about two hours to lay things out for Engoron. In the afternoon, prosecutors for the New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office will deliver their closing arguments.\par \par \uc2 Kise started the speech off by emphasizing there is no jury in the civil trial. \u8220\'20\'1CIf there was a jury in that box, I\u8217\'20\'19d be looking at them right now,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing arguments begin in Trump's New York civil fraud trial\par \par \uc2 Closing arguments have officially started in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial.\par \par \uc2 His defense attorneys are up first, and MSNBC reports Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  has given them about two and a half hours to make their case. Arguing for Trump is former Florida solicitor general Chris Kise :\par \par \uc2 enltrEngoron, after setting out the time limits for today\u8217\'20\'19s closing, congratulates and thanks the lawyers for their diligence and timely filings. Chris Kise is up, and with his co-counsel, he has until 12:45 to sum up (with one 15 min. break allowed).\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1745463617536033190?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  briefly allowed photographers and videographers into the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 Per their images, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was seated with his attorneys at the defense table. The New York attorney general, Letitia James, was in the audience behind him and to his right. Her prosecutors were at the table across from him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A large crowd of reporters were gathered outside the courthouse this morning in anticipation of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s arrival at his New York fraud trial for closing arguments.\par \par \uc2 The scene was reminiscent of other key days in the trial, such as when former Trump fixer \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  testified in October, and when Trump took the stand in November. Of the 44 days in the trial, which began in early October, only a few have drawn such a crowd.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s closing arguments will be the formal ending of the trial. Attorneys for both sides had issued written closing briefs, summarizing their view of how the trial went. Today is the last chance for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team to make an in-person appeal to Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to show up to court today, though he will likely not speak. Engoron struck down his request to make his own closing statement, saying there should be no campaign speeches in the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 Trump stands accused of falsifying business records to boost his net worth. He is being sued for $370m.\par \par \uc2 A small group of anti-Trump protestors briefly blocked traffic in front of the courthouse holding a banner and chanting \u8220\'20\'1CNo dictators in the USA!\u8221\'20\'1D The group had shown up on the first day of the trial and had then chanted \u8220\'20\'1CTrump lies all the time!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Letitia James, ascended the courthouse steps, the small crowd, now standing in the park across the street, chanted \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, Tish!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump arrives for closing arguments in New York civil fraud trial - report\par \par \uc2 The Messenger reports that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has entered the courtroom for the closing arguments in the civil fraud case brought against him by the New York attorney general, Letitia James :\par \par \uc2 enltrNow:\par \par \uc2 Trump enters the courtroom, followed by his son \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2 , and his lawyers.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1745460386567241839?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected in the Manhattan courtroom today for closing arguments in his civil fraud trial (which he wanted to make himself). Yesterday, he was in Iowa, where the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  reports he took credit for the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 2022 decision overturning Roe v Wade and allowing states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the former US president, boasted about the \u8220\'20\'1Cmiracle\u8221\'20\'1D of ending the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but warned that Republicans who tout extreme bans are being \u8220\'20\'1Cdecimated\u8221\'20\'1D in elections.\par \par \uc2 Trump was put on the spot on Wednesday during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/how-where-watch-fox-news-town-hall-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Fox News town hall}}}\uc2  in Des Moines, Iowa, his latest attempt at counter-programming a Republican debate that was being shown on CNN at the same time.\par \par \uc2 A female voter, undecided between Trump and rival \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , raised concerns over the Republican frontrunner\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/03/donald-trump-abortion-republicans-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent attempts to back away}}}\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions unpopular in elections and opinion polls.\par \par \uc2 She said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been vocal in celebrating with you all of your pro-life victories from the past but then in this campaign you\u8217\'20\'19ve also blamed pro-lifers for some of the GOP losses around the country and you\u8217\'20\'19ve called heartbeat laws like Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s terrible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The voter added: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d just like some clarity on this because it\u8217\'20\'19s such an important question to me. I\u8217\'20\'19d like for you to reassure me that you can protect all life, every person\u8217\'20\'19s right to life without compromise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/donald-trump-abortion-election-republicans-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump claims credit for \u8216\'20\'18miracle\u8217\'20\'19 of overturning right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ahead of presenting the closing arguments in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil business fraud trial, the New York attorney general, Letitia James, offered a summary of the case against the former president on X:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump and his team intentionally misrepresented the value of his assets.\par \par \uc2 Mar-a-Lago:\par \par \uc2 ??Trump\u8217\'20\'19s value: $739 million\par \par \uc2 ?Appraised value: $25 million\par \par \uc2 And knowingly lied about the size of his apartment in NYC to inflate its value:\par \par \uc2 ??Trump\u8217\'20\'19s size: 30,000 sqft\par \par \uc2 ?True size: 10,966 sqft\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NY AG James (@NewYorkStateAG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewYorkStateAG/status/1745448813324800012?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThey regularly and intentionally pretended that legal restrictions on properties didn\u8217\'20\'19t exist to inflate these values.\par \par \uc2 Take the 12 apartments on Park Avenue that they pretended were not rent-stabilized.\par \par \uc2 Park Avenue:\par \par \uc2 ??Trump\u8217\'20\'19s value: ~$50 million\par \par \uc2 ?True value: $739,000\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NY AG James (@NewYorkStateAG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewYorkStateAG/status/1745448816856428772?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump used his falsely inflated net worth to obtain a host of benefits.\par \par \uc2 More favorable loans and insurance coverage that saved him hundreds of millions of dollars.\par \par \uc2 Obtaining these loans at discounted rates was absolutely critical to the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  staying afloat.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NY AG James (@NewYorkStateAG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewYorkStateAG/status/1745448821768036616?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 According {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/arthur-engoron-bomb-threat-made-at-home-of-judge-in-trumps-bank-fraud-trial?via=twitter_page&utm_campaign=owned_social&utm_source=twitter_owned_tdb&utm_medium=socialflow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the Daily Beast}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than half a dozen police cars and a bomb squad rushed\u8221\'20\'1D to Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Long Island home after a bomb threat was phoned in.\par \par \uc2 The message was \u8220\'20\'1Cperceived as a blatant attempt to delay the trial\u8217\'20\'19s closing arguments\u8221\'20\'1D, and a spokesman for the Nassau county police said they have opened an \u8220\'20\'1Cactive investigation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Police investigate bomb threat at judge's home - reports\par \par \uc2 Police are investigating a bomb threat made against the judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , who is presiding over the fraud trial of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his family business empire in New York, NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/bomb-threat-targeted-home-judge-trumps-civil-fraud-trial-rcna133416"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A law enforcement bomb squad went to the judge\u8217\'20\'19s home in Nassau county, on the outskirts of New York City, yesterday, sources told the TV station. It is not known if Engoron or anyone else was home at the time.\par \par \uc2 Engoron is expected at court in Manhattan today to sit as closing arguments are presented in the New York attorney general Letitia James \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud case against Trump, his sons Don Jr and Eric and other senior figures in the New York-based \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , the family real estate empire.\par \par \uc2 Letitia James leaves the courtroom during the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  trial, 13 November 2023. Photograph: Brendan McDermid/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump to attend closing arguments in New York fraud trial\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers will make their closing arguments in a New York court room today as they attempt to see off a legal judgment that could impose a $370m fraud fine on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s family firm and ban it from doing business in the state, where the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  real estate empire is based.\par \par \uc2 The former US president reportedly planned to deliver his own closing statement at the trial \u8211\'20\'13 a last chance to defend himself against charges he inflated the value of his assets on financial statements for profit. But the judge overseeing the civil case blocked that move on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  fraud trial had been on a nearly month-long break for the holidays since December after 11 weeks of witness testimony. It is unclear when Engoron will issue a verdict, though he has indicated he will make a decision by the end of the month. Because the trial is a bench trial, there is no jury, and Engoron is the sole decider of the case.\par \par \uc2 In a pre-trial ruling, Engoron already found Trump, his adult sons and the former \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  executives \uc2 Allen Weisselberg\uc2  and Jeff McConney guilty of fraud, saying they botched the value of various Trump properties on government forms.\par \par \uc2 More details {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/11/donald-trump-fraud-trial-closing-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  and more background {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/06/donald-trump-new-york-fraud-trial-business-impact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is questioned, next to Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , during the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  civil fraud trial in New York state supreme court in Manhattan, 6 November 2023, in this courtroom sketch. Photograph: Jane Rosenberg/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump expected in New York for closing arguments in civil fraud trial\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Today, in New York City, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will take yet another break from the campaign trail to appear for the closing arguments in the civil fraud trial the New York attorney general, Letitia James, brought against his business empire. The former president, who is no lawyer, intended to deliver the arguments himself in court, but that was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/trump-closing-arguments-civil-fraud-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 knocked down}}}\uc2  yesterday by \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , the judge hearing the case. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/06/donald-trump-new-york-fraud-trial-business-impact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stakes are high}}}\uc2  for Trump, since Engoron has already found he and his co-defendants engaged in fraud for years, and is now considering what penalties to levy against them.\par \par \uc2 The trial\u8217\'20\'19s conclusion takes place four days before Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s first-in-the-nation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/08/trump-campaign-iowa-rule-changes-republican-presidential-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican caucuses}}}\uc2  on Monday, which the former president is expected to win. That would put him on course to once again claim the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, despite Trump facing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 91 criminal charges}}}\uc2  in four cases, in addition to ongoing civil cases. We\u8217\'20\'19ll cover today\u8217\'20\'19s proceedings \u8211\'20\'13 Trump included \u8211\'20\'13 live.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively last 12 hours and the next 12 are set to be just as fascinating. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/11/donald-trump-fraud-trial-closing-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will make}}}\uc2  their closing arguments as they attempt to see off a civil case judgment that could impose a $370m fraud fine on his family firm and ban it from doing business in New York state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Before heading to the court house in New York today, the former US president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/donald-trump-abortion-election-republicans-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said at a Fox News town hall}}}\uc2  in Des Moines last night that the overturning of Roe v Wade, ending the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by a \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  he helped to tip rightwards was a \u8220\'20\'1Cmiracle\u8221\'20\'1D, and also that he knows who his running mate will be if he wins the Republican nomination for president, though he\u8217\'20\'19s not telling. The town hall was his alternative to taking part in \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 The last GOP debate before Monday\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa caucuses, last night, where just two of the three rivals who qualified for the event were in a hostile {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/nikki-haley-ron-desantis-iowa-republican-debate-candidates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 head-to-head clash}}}\uc2 . Nikki Haley and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  traded insults and accusations, shortly after their trailing rival Chris Christie{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/republican-chris-christie-suspends-presidential-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended}}}\uc2  his 2024 campaign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been hosting top donors and others for private lunches at the White House in an effort to bolster support for his re-election campaign, the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/01/10/biden-holding-private-meetings-white-house-reassure-supporters/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , while Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/01/10/biden-donors-oval-office-tours-warning-legal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  that the White House counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office has advised the president to stop giving big donors tours of the Oval Office, to avoid an ethics problem.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , hot from his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/hunter-biden-contempt-congress-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unexpected visit}}}\uc2  to Capitol Hill to attend a House committee hearing where the Republican majority wants to hold him in contempt of Congress, will have to show up in a Los Angeles court room today. The president\u8217\'20\'19s son is expected to deny tax offenses.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is also running global live blogs on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza and the wider situation in the Middle East, which you can follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jan/11/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-israel-gaza-war-hamas-palestine-south-africa-genocide-case-icj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine, which you can follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jan/11/russia-ukraine-war-live-latest-updates-volodymyr-zelenskiy-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240111ek1b0020d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
