\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republican debate: Haley and DeSantis clash on immigration and Ukraine but absent Trump is the winner \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh \par \uc2 2,920 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 January 2024\par 04:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 With less than a week to go before the first-in-the-country Iowa caucuses two challengers to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  make their case\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Tonight's recap\par \par \uc2 Just days away from the Iowa caucuses, when the first voters will make their picks for a Republican presidential nominee, Nikki Haley and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  exchanged bitter barbs and often circuitous criticisms in a debate that yielded few memorable points.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  carried on as usual in a televised Fox News town hall, comfortable in his spot as the top candidate.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for following along. And stay tuned for more updates and analysis across the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing thoughts from each candidate are \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t run under a banner of pale pastels of warmed-over corporatism, the likes of which is practice by Nikki Haley,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , trying once again to make \u8220\'20\'1Cpale pastels\u8221\'20\'1D stick as an insult.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t go through four more years of chaos,\u8221\'20\'1D said Haley. Though her real catch-phrase tonight was \u8220\'20\'1CDesantislies.com\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 A question about climate change, and what each candidate is willing to do about it, has \u8211\'20\'13 as expected \u8211\'20\'13 yielded little useful information.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis promised to tear up the \u8220\'20\'1CBiden\u8217\'20\'19s green new deal\u8221\'20\'1D while Haley said she opposed \u8220\'20\'1Cextremes\u8221\'20\'1D in policy and transitioned the conversation over to the topic of crime.\par \par \uc2 Last summer, during the first Republican presidential debate, a pointed question from a young activist elicited slightly more interesting results. Alexander Diaz, a young conservative who is part of the American Conservation Coalition (ACC), a youth conservative group that pushes for action on the climate crisis, asked candidates what they would do to improve the party\u8217\'20\'19s standing on climate policy. None of the candidates at that time raised their hands to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/republicans-climate-crisis-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 affirm}}}\uc2  that climate change was real.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Demonstrating a careful balancing act, DeSantis both defends and critiques Trump, saying that the former president is being wrongly prosecuted but also, \u8220\'20\'1Cif Trump is the nominee, it is going to be about Jan 6\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Haley, meanwhile, said that no president should be immune from all prosecution, but as she tends to do, cast her self as a leader who could restore civility after too much \u8220\'20\'1Cchaos\u8221\'20\'1D surrounding Trump.\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  out of the running, there\u8217\'20\'19s no one where willing to overtly or forcefully take down Trump. The resulting debate has been an odd, largely disengaging slog for for a silver medal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, on the debate stage, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has just come up.\par \par \uc2 And DeSantis has started by questioning whether Trump and Haley are adequately pro-life. But he also mentioned that Republicans need to do a better job of highlighting support for mothers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans need to do a better job of lifting up folks who are having children,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very difficult to raise kids in this environment. You need to help with medical care, you need to help with affordability and we need to help with education choice. You got to be pro life for the whole life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In an implicit acknowledgment about how extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions are alienating voters, he claimed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents do not support criminalizing women. That\u8217\'20\'19s not quite right, as the \uc2 Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/30/self-managed-abortions-arrest-investiagtion-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has reported}}}\uc2 . Bills in state legislatures have proposed prosecuting women for seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Haley, meanwhile, said of Trump and DeSantis: \u8220\'20\'1CThese fellas don\u8217\'20\'19t know how to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going to play politics with this issue any more. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to treat it like the respectful issue that it is and the tropes that you want,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Over at the Trump town hall, the former president is taking credit for ending the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump takes credit for "terminating" the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : "I did it. And I'm proud to have done it." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9hnjBD0e5z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9hnjBD0e5z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1745276417011536117?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s a notable stance for the GOP frontrunner, at a time when it\u8217\'20\'19s become increasingly clear that extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies are alienating voters. More than a dozen states could ultimately vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2024. And voters have already enshrined rights to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in state constitutions in Ohio, Arizona and Florida.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Lauren Gambino reported recently:\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  delivered Republicans one of their most significant policy victories in a generation. But in the year and a half since the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, the ruling has also become one of their biggest political vulnerabilities.\par \par \uc2 Over the last 18 months, voters have favored \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in seven consecutive ballot measures, including in conservative states. Republicans underperformed in the 2022 midterm elections while Democrats scored off-year election wins in Wisconsin, Kentucky and Virginia \u8211\'20\'13 results that again emphasized the enduring power of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there\u8217\'20\'19s really a kind of catch-22 for Republicans,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2  and a leading expert on the history of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US. \u8220\'20\'1COn the one hand, you have a lot of base Republican voters who really care about opposing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on the other you have a huge group of something like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/506759/broader-support-abortion-rights-continues-post-dobbs.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 70%}}}\uc2  of Americans who don\u8217\'20\'19t like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/29/republicans-democrats-abortion-plans-election-2024-trump-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans seek winning strategy on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  for 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 with Democrats also in a tricky spot}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 The crossfire has gotten away from the moderators, Jake Tapper and Dana Bash, struggling to rein in DeSantis shouting over Haley.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think I hit a nerve,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and Nikki Haley during the fifth Republican presidential primary debate at \uc2 Drake University\uc2  in Des Moines, Iowa. Photograph: Jim Watson/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Over on Fox News, which is airing the Trump town hall, the former president was pressed on his recent warning that \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19ll be bedlam in the country\u8221\'20\'1D if he loses the election.\par \par \uc2 Co-host Bret Baier asked: \u8220\'20\'1CCan you say tonight that political violence is never acceptable?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump replied: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, of course that\u8217\'20\'19s right. And of course, I\u8217\'20\'19m the one that had very little of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Later Trump offered some idle speculation on the origins of the coronavirus in Wuhan, China. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it was done out of incompetence,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that a scientist went out, said hello to his girlfriend, and that was the end of that. She died and then people started dying all over the place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 After a short break, we\u8217\'20\'19re on to the issue of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s battle with \uc2 Disney\uc2 , following the company\u8217\'20\'19s condemnation of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis was asked whether it aligns with conservative values to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/may/09/disney-v-desantis-florida-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 antagonize businesses. }}}\uc2  The Florida governor doubled down on his choice to go after the company for \u8220\'20\'1Ctrans-ing\u8221\'20\'1D kids, repeating a slew of baseless talking points about what education, parental and medical support for transgender children entails. \u8220\'20\'1CMost corporate Republicans would have caved. I stood and I fought,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Haley accused DeSantis of supporting \uc2 Disney\uc2  until they came out against his policies. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen they went and criticized him he got thin-skinned and suddenly started to fight back,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more context on DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s beef with \uc2 Disney\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/may/09/disney-v-desantis-florida-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Disney v DeSantis: what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake for Florida as legal tug-of-war ramps up?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 The candidates are divided on Ukraine, and tonight reiterated views they\u8217\'20\'19ve expressed before.\par \par \uc2 Haley is for the US supporting Ukraine which she said is is \u8220\'20\'1Ca pro-American, freedom-loving country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is against sending more money to Ukraine, preferring to \u8220\'20\'1C focus on our issues here at home\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates are for sending aid to Israel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Fact checks: Immigration\par \par \uc2 Haley said that millions of people who cross the border should be deported \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause they are jumping the line\u8221\'20\'1D. This is a mischaracterization of how immigration policy works. Migrants at the border are allowed to just show up and ask for asylum, per US law.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis said that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Clet in\u8221\'20\'1D 8 million people coming through the southern border. A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dhs.gov/ohss/topics/immigration/enforcement-and-legal-processes-monthly-tables"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  notes that the administration has expelled about 4 million migrants taken into custody, and released 2.3 million.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 The debate has turned to the topic of immigration, an issue that\u8217\'20\'19s loomed large for both Democrats and Republicans.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis said that Trump did not deport enough people, noting that more people were deported under the Obama administration. Haley, whose governorship was defined by her signing into law some of the country\u8217\'20\'19s harshest immigration policies, exchanged barbs about her record versus that of DeSantis. But the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 rapid exchange of criticisms on specific policies, and efforts to one-up each other on who has been harsher toward immigrants will be hard to follow for most voters.\par \par \uc2 Neither candidate has thus far delivered a memorable line, or a clear idea of what their vision for the presidency is beyond generic endorsements of the right\u8217\'20\'19s tenets (lower taxes, more energy independence and fewer undocumented immigrants).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has decided the identity of his running mate in the presidential election but is not yet ready to announce it, he told a Fox News town hall in Iowa on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Asked who he would pick as vice-president, Trump replied: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I can\u8217\'20\'19t tell you that, really. I mean, I know who it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be but \u8211\'20\'13\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Co-host Bret Baier entreated: \u8220\'20\'1CGive us a hint.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump joked in response: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll do another show some time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 At competing town hall, Trump attacks Haley and DeSantis\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  began his Iowa town hall on Fox News by highlighting an incident in which \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  was caught on a hot mic. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s going to get smoked, and you and I both know it,\u8221\'20\'1D the former New Jersey governor was heard saying on his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s live stream. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s not up to this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is widely assumed that Christie, who dropped out of the Republican primary race today, was referring to Nikki Haley, perceived as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s principal rival in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  was in and he got a hot mic I heard about. I thought the bigger story wasn\u8217\'20\'19t actually the fact that he dropped out \u8211\'20\'13 nobody cared too much about that \u8211\'20\'13 but he had a hot mic where he was talking to somebody about the weather and he happened to say she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have what it takes, she\u8217\'20\'19ll be creamed in the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The former president added: \u8220\'20\'1CI know her very well and I happen to believe that \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s right. That\u8217\'20\'19s one of the few things he\u8217\'20\'19s been right about actually.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump admitted he didn\u8217\'20\'19t known whether Christie\u8217\'20\'19s departure would change the dynamic of the race and complained that independents and Democrats can vote in the Republican primary. \u8220\'20\'1CEven with that, I think we\u8217\'20\'19ll win substantially,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve barely started, but the gloves are off.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis called Haley \u8220\'20\'1Canother mealy-mouthed politician who just tells you what she thinks you want to hear\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Haley mentioned her new campaign website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://desantislies.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 desantislies.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Neither was especially strong in their critiques of Trump. DeSantis mentioned debt increasing under Trump, and his failure to prosecute \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . Haley demurred in response to a question about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s character, saying his way \u8220\'20\'1Cis not my way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Haley and DeSantis take the stage\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s buckle up for a two-hour debate!\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re starting with a question about why voters looking for an alternative to Trump should vote for them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 As Nikki Haley\u8217\'20\'19s poll numbers inch up, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has dredged up his nativist birther conspiracies.\par \par \uc2 This week, the former president shared on his Truth Social platform a post from Gateway Pundit, a far-right site, falsely claiming that Haley was disqualified for the presidency because her Indian immigrant parents weren\u8217\'20\'19t citizens when she was born. Haley was born in South Carolina and therefore meets the \u8220\'20\'1Cnatural born citizen\u8221\'20\'1D requirement to become president.\par \par \uc2 Trump previously pushed the baseless and racist claim that \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  was born in Kenya and therefore disqualified from the presidency. He also pushed misinformation that Ted Cruz, his 2016 rival, was intelligible because he was born in Canada to American parents.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/trump-nikki-haley-birther-conspiracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Totally baseless\u8217\'20\'19: Trump denounced for Nikki Haley \u8216\'20\'18birther\u8217\'20\'19 lie}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Haley and DeSantis fight for second place\par \par \uc2 If DeSantis and Haley are fighting neck and neck, it is probably for second place. Polls show Trump holding an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4385556-donald-trump-iowa-caucuses-ron-desantis-nikki-haley/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly}}}\uc2  commanding lead in Iowa in the weeks before the caucuses \u8211\'20\'13 despite putting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/08/trump-campaign-iowa-rule-changes-republican-presidential-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fewer campaign resources}}}\uc2  into the early primary than his opponents.\par \par \uc2 If DeSantis fails to eat into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s share of Iowa voters, his campaign \u8211\'20\'13 which has faltered repeatedly among gaffes and staffing shake-ups \u8211\'20\'13 could shutter before he sees another primary.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/chris-christie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris Christie}}}\uc2  suspended his campaign for the Republican presidential nomination, he announced on Wednesday evening.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is clear to me tonight that there is not a path to win the nomination,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at a town hall in Windham, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Hampshire}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former New Jersey governor, who also ran unsuccessfully for the presidency in 2016, when he lost out to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , has been struggling in the polls for weeks and had failed to qualify for the last GOP debate before Monday\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa caucuses kick off the nominating contest of the 2024 race for the White House.\par \par \uc2 He had always stood out as the Republican candidate with the most overtly critical viewpoint of the policies and character of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He has yet to endorse a rival and was heard publicly on an apparent inadvertent \u8220\'20\'1Chot mic\u8221\'20\'1D before he took the stage in New Hampshire predicting that one, almost certainly Nikki Haley, will \u8220\'20\'1Cget smoked\u8221\'20\'1D in the race for the nomination and that a \u8220\'20\'1Cpetrified\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor, had called him, while a person he was talking to was heard predicting that the struggling DeSantis would not last beyond next week\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa caucuses. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/nikki-haley-ron-desantis-iowa-republican-debate-candidates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Haley and DeSantis}}}\uc2  are the closest contenders behind the solid frontrunner, Trump.\par \par \uc2 The hot-mic comments were widely heard on a \uc2 YouTube\uc2  audio livestream before Christie\u8217\'20\'19s event began, with the audio being cut abruptly after a few seconds.\par \par \uc2 Appearing before a subdued crowd at the town hall event a few moments later, Christie said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis race has always been bigger than me.\u8221\'20\'1D And he warned the US against re-electing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to a second term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we put him back behind the desk at the Oval Office, and a choice is needed to be made about whether to put himself first or you [the public] first, how much more evidence do you need? He will put himself first,\u8221\'20\'1D Christie said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/republican-chris-christie-suspends-presidential-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Chris Christie suspends presidential bid}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Haley and DeSantis are set for fifth Republican debate\par \par \uc2 As Nikki Haley and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  face off for a fifth Republican presidential debate on CNN, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 by far the frontrunner for the 2024 GOP nomination \u8211\'20\'13 will be on Fox News for a live town hall event.\par \par \uc2 All three candidates are in Iowa today, just five days out from the caucuses, when the first voters will begin to picking their preferred nominee. Unlike the last four debates, this one isn\u8217\'20\'19t coordinated by the Republican National Convention. CNN\u8217\'20\'19s requirement that candidates poll at 10% in at least three surveys left only Haley, DeSantis and Trump qualifying. The former president has declined to participate in any debates this far.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the former New Jersey governor and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s biggest critic among the Republican candidates \u8211\'20\'13 announced he was dropping out of the race. \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , the rightwing tech entrepreneur, remains in the running but trails far behind the competition in polls. He\u8217\'20\'19s in Iowa as well, at a live taping of a podast hosted by right-wing commentator Tim Pool.\par \par \uc2 Follow along for live debate coverage.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/nikki-haley-ron-desantis-iowa-republican-debate-candidates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley and Ron DeSantis to face off in Iowa Republican debate}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240111ek1b0002u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
