\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Florida  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights amendment proposal looks likely to appear on ballot\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 462 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 January 2024\par 17:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in constitution seems to have enough signatures to head to vote in state that has a 15-week ban\par \par \uc2 A Florida ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution seems to have enough signatures to head to voters come November \u8211\'20\'13 if advocates can defeat Republican efforts to stop it.\par \par \uc2 As of Friday, totals from the Florida division of elections show that the campaign behind the measure, Floridians Protecting Freedom, had collected more than 910,00 verified signatures in support of the measure \u8211\'20\'13 roughly 20,000 more than the threshold needed to get it on the ballot in Florida. Those totals are unofficial and not finalized.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSignatures came from everyone and everywhere, proving once again this is not a Republican or Democratic issue \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s about freedom, healthcare, and safety,\u8221\'20\'1D the Florida state senate minority leader, Lauren Book, a Democrat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderBookFL/status/1743277844325687411"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted on X}}}\uc2  on Friday in celebration. \u8220\'20\'1CNo woman and no doctor should fear imprisonment over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. No woman or mother should face death because she can\u8217\'20\'19t get proper care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Currently, Florida bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks of pregnancy, although the state supreme court is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/08/florida-abortion-ban-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now deliberating}}}\uc2  over a case that could ultimately lead to a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The proposed amendment would amend the state constitution to declare that \u8220\'20\'1Cno law shall prohibit, penalize, delay, or restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before viability or when necessary to protect the patient\u8217\'20\'19s health, as determined by the patient\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare provider\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the ballot proposal\u8217\'20\'19s summary.\par \par \uc2 Viability, or the point at which a fetus can survive outside the womb, is typically pegged at around 24 weeks of pregnancy. Under Roe v Wade, which the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned in 2022, states were broadly banned from prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before viability.\par \par \uc2 Florida is one of roughly a dozen states that may give voters a chance to decide on an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measure in November. Several states have already voted on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights referendums since the overturning of Roe; so far, in every state, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters have triumphed.\par \par \uc2 However, the Florida ballot measure\u8217\'20\'19s path to voters is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/15/florida-abortion-right-constitution-amendment-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far from assured}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Ashley Moody\uc2 , the Republican attorney general, has filed a legal brief asking the Florida supreme court to block the amendment, arguing, in part, that the term \u8220\'20\'1Cviability\u8221\'20\'1D can have too many meanings.\par \par \uc2 The ballot summary, \uc2 Moody\uc2  argued in court documents, is part of a \u8220\'20\'1Csimilar overall design to lay ticking time bombs that will enable \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  proponents later to argue that the amendment has a much broader meaning than voters would ever have thought\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Florida supreme court is set to hear arguments in the case in early February.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240105ek150028q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
