\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The year in patriarchy:  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans, circumboob and deepfake porn\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,312 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 December 2023\par 18:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 To help you look back, here are 10 memorable moments from the year in patriarchy, from Spain\u8217\'20\'19s reckoning with sexism to Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s takeover\par \par \uc2 2023 was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/12/28/1221827923/2023-hottest-year-record-climate-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hottest year on record}}}\uc2 . And it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just a year of extreme weather \u8211\'20\'13 the political climate also became more heated, with the far-right {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inthesetimes.com/article/global-far-right-meloni-milei-putin-bannon-orban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gaining traction}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/30/far-right-on-the-march-europe-growing-taste-for-control-and-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 around the world}}}\uc2 . In the US, Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/sep/22/democracy-book-bans-us-public-schools-rise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned books}}}\uc2 , censored {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/florida-education-board-approves-expansion-dont-say-gay-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discussions of gender identity}}}\uc2 , and tried their best to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/10/republican-wave-state-bills-homicide-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prosecute}}}\uc2  any woman who dared to so much think of having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In Italy, \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s far-right government went on a crusade to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/italian-far-right-government-limits-parental-rights-of-same-sex-couples"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 erode}}}\uc2  LGBTQ+ rights. In Afghanistan, two years of oppressive \uc2 Taliban\uc2  rule have resulted in what some activists are terming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://giwps.georgetown.edu/the-talibans-oppression-of-women-is-gender-apartheid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18gender apartheid.\u8217\'20\'19}}}\uc2  From Kabul to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/13/kentucky-abortion-ban-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky}}}\uc2 , it feels like we went backwards in 2023 when it comes to the rights of women and minorities.\par \par \uc2 While it\u8217\'20\'19s been a bad year politically for women, things have been a little brighter in popular culture. 2023 was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/dec/25/tipping-point-2023-was-the-year-money-finally-talked-in-womens-sport"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banner year for female sports}}}\uc2  with events such as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/apr/29/england-france-womens-six-nations-rugby-union-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s Six Nations}}}\uc2 , the Women\u8217\'20\'19s World Cup and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/jun/21/womens-ashes-not-afterthought-fans-ecb-tickets-cricket"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women\u8217\'20\'19s Ashes}}}\uc2  notching up record viewing figures. It was also a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/11/14/1213008545/with-barbie-leading-the-way-2023-was-a-big-year-for-women-in-film"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 big year for women in film}}}\uc2 , with Barbie leading the charge: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/jul/24/barbie-movie-spoilers-themes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greta Gerwig\u8217\'20\'19s feminist take}}}\uc2  on the plastic, anatomically incorrect doll, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/aug/07/barbie-movie-tops-1bn-in-global-box-office-ticket-sales-breaking-record-for-female-directors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 topped $1bn in global box office ticket sales}}}\uc2  and spawned approximately 9 million thinkpieces. As one viral tweet noted, we\u8217\'20\'19ve all got a little Barbie in us (the microplastics).\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been quite the year, eh? To help you look back, here are 10 memorable moments from the year in patriarchy.\par \par \uc2 1 A jury found Trump sexually abused E Jean Carroll\par \par \uc2 After decades of boasting about being a sexual predator (\u8220\'20\'1C When you\u8217\'20\'19re a star, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2016/oct/08/donald-trumps-sex-boasts-when-you-are-a-star-they-let-you-do-anything-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they let you do it}}}\uc2 , you can do anything \u8230\'20\'26 grab \u8216\'20\'18em by the pussy\u8221\'20\'1D ) and facing zero consequences for it, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s past finally caught up with him. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/09/e-jean-carroll-wins-trump-trial-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In May, a New York jury found}}}\uc2  that the former president sexually abused the advice columnist E Jean Carroll in a New York department store changing room in 1996. Will the fact that he has been legally branded a sexual predator stop Trump from having a second go at the presidency? No, of course it won\u8217\'20\'19t. There\u8217\'20\'19s a very real chance that Trump is going to get a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/11/donald-trump-president-2024-biden-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Crevenge term\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\uc2  God (who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/02/10/1155792333/god-gender-pronouns-church-of-england"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may or may not be a woman}}}\uc2  ) help us all.\par \par \uc2 2 \uc2 Jacinda Ardern\uc2  unexpectedly resigned as prime minister of New Zealand\par \par \uc2 Ardern, who was the world\u8217\'20\'19s youngest female leader when she was elected, said very honestly that she \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jan/19/jacinda-ardern-resigns-as-prime-minister-of-new-zealand"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no longer had enough in the tank}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to do the job. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abc.net.au/news/2023-09-30/jacinda-ardern-chris-hipkins-labour-trailing-christopher-luxon/102901556"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two men called Chris}}}\uc2  then battled it out to replace her.\par \par \uc2 3 Spain won the Women\u8217\'20\'19s World Cup \u8230\'20\'26 and had a reckoning with sexism\par \par \uc2 Spain beat England and won a historic victory in the World Cup. It should have been a moment of pure joy, but the players immediately had their success marred by the misogyny of Luis Rubiales, then head of the \uc2 Spanish football federation\uc2 , who grabbed his crotch in celebration then planted an unsolicited kiss on Jenni Hermoso\u8217\'20\'19s lips. He could have just said sorry and everyone would have moved on, but instead he threw a fit and acted like a victim, drawing the story out for weeks. (His mother \u8211\'20\'13 from whom he may get his taste for drama \u8211\'20\'13 also locked herself in a church and went on a short-lived {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/66664374"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hunger strike}}}\uc2  in support of her son.) Eventually, following a Fifa disciplinary committee investigation into his conduct, Rubiales was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/oct/30/luis-rubiales-banned-from-football-for-three-years-over-jenni-hermoso-kiss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned from all football-related activities}}}\uc2  for three years.\par \par \uc2 4 Artificial intelligence boomed \u8211\'20\'13 and so too did non-consensual deepfake porn\par \par \uc2 Thanks to the success of ChatGPT, 2023 was the year that artificial intelligence went mainstream \u8211\'20\'13 indeed, AI was crowned \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-67271252"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 word of the year}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D by the Collins dictionary. And as AI technology proliferated, so too did AI-generated deepfake porn: apps which let people create lewd imagery to order {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/01/ai-deepfake-porn-fake-images"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were suddenly everywhere}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 even in high schools. In October, a New Jersey high school {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.technologyreview.com/2023/12/01/1084164/deepfake-porn-scandal-pushing-us-lawmakers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found itself in the middle of a deepfake scandal}}}\uc2  after it transpired boys in the school had used AI to create pornographic photos of their female classmates, some of whom were just 14. The scandal helped move US lawmakers into action, and there is now a growing push to provide legal recourse for people who find themselves victims of deepfake porn.\par \par \uc2 5 The war on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights continued in the US\par \par \uc2 Since Roe v Wade was overturned in 2022, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/us/abortion-access-restrictions-bans-us-dg/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost two dozen US states}}}\uc2  have banned or limited access to abortions. 2023 was filled with harrowing stories of women who have been forced to carry {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/20/texas-women-pregnancy-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 life-threatening pregnancies}}}\uc2 , or to flee to other states because of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/12/kate-cox-texas-abortion-case-explained#:~:text=Explainer-,Kate%20Cox%20case%3A%20what%20led%20to%20the%20Texan,the%20state%20for%20an%20abortion%3F&text=A%20Texas%20woman%20fled%20her,her%20life%20and%20future%20fertility."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrictive \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws}}}\uc2 . But there were also moments of hope: activists won a number of ballot measures to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/26/us-abortion-rights-2024-election-pill-doctor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even in conservative states such as Ohio}}}\uc2 . Going into 2024, access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills will be front and center. In December, the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/13/abortion-pill-us-supreme-court-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed to consider arguments}}}\uc2  that could determine the future of mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 the pill used in most abortions in the US. A decision in the case will probably arrive next summer.\par \par \uc2 6 Three people were stabbed during a gender studies class in Canada\par \par \uc2 The incident was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/29/canada-stabbing-attack-university-waterloo-gender-issues-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believed to be hate-motivated}}}\uc2  and stoked by rightwing fear-mongering in North America over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/commentisfree/2021/oct/23/judith-butler-gender-ideology-backlash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gender}}}\uc2  and gender studies. \u8220\'20\'1CA rightwing culture war and transphobic propaganda is never just about discourse, debate, or the \u8216\'20\'18potential for violence\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D said one gender studies professor in response to the attack. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about actual violence.\u8221\'20\'1D And it seems depressingly inevitable that that violence will only escalate.\par \par \uc2 7 It was the year of Taylor Swift\par \par \uc2 Swift, who was named {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2023/dec/06/taylor-swift-lambasts-music-industry-and-says-kim-kardashian-feud-took-me-down-psychologically"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Time magazine\u8217\'20\'19s person of the year}}}\uc2 , has always been ridiculously successful but 2023 was the year she went stratospheric. As she\u8217\'20\'19s pointed out herself, however, she\u8217\'20\'19s not the only female artist in the spotlight \u8211\'20\'13 women dominate the 2024 Grammy dominations. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we\u8217\'20\'19re going to look at this in the most cynical way possible, feminine ideas becoming lucrative means that more female art will get made,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2023/dec/06/taylor-swift-lambasts-music-industry-and-says-kim-kardashian-feud-took-me-down-psychologically"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Swift said in her Time interview}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s extremely heartening.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 8 A humanitarian crisis unfolded in Gaza, with women and children bearing the brunt of the conflict\par \par \uc2 According to figures {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unwomen.org/en/news-stories/feature-story/2023/10/facts-and-figures-women-and-girls-during-the-war-in-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from UN Women}}}\uc2  from 22 December, almost 13,000 women and children have been killed due to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s indiscriminate bombing of Gaza. Almost one million women and girls have been displaced from their homes, two mothers are killed every hour, and 50,000 women in Gaza are currently pregnant. They are now facing cesareans without anaesthetic or painkillers and facing an increased risk of premature births. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abc.net.au/news/2023-12-29/being-pregnant-in-gaza-unsafe-women-paying-heaviest-price-in-war/103241724"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Giving birth safely in a hospital has become impossible}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 9 Iranian women continued to fight for their rights\par \par \uc2 Last September a 22-year-old woman, Mahsa Amini, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/18/mahsa-amini-dozens-injured-in-iran-protests-after-death-in-custody"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 died in custody}}}\uc2  after being detained by the \u8220\'20\'1Cmorality police\u8221\'20\'1D for allegedly not wearing a headscarf properly. Her death set off nationwide protests which, in turn, were met with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/01/12/iran-brute-force-used-crackdown-dissent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brutal government violence}}}\uc2 . While the fight for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in Iran may no longer command the headlines it once did, it\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2023/10/iranian-women-and-girls-face-further-violations-of-their-rights-under-compulsory-veiling-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still very much ongoing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 10 Fashion saw some very silly moments\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just a year of extreme weather and extreme politics \u8211\'20\'13 the dial on pretty much everything this year seems to have been turned as far as it could possibly go. Including fashion. Standout moments in the world of couture include cleavage going all out with the rise of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/feb/28/welcome-to-the-circumboob-the-cleavage-trend-for-a-chaotic-era"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 circumboob}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vogue.com/article/the-pantless-trend-really-is-happening"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the no-pants trend}}}\uc2 , and the rise of the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecut.com/2022/08/we-explained-the-weird-girl-aesthetic.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weird-girl aesthetic}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. The world is growing increasingly berserk, and it seems everyone is dressing accordingly.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231230ejcu001e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
