\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans seek winning strategy on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  for 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 with Democrats also in a tricky spot\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 2,127 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 December 2023\par 12:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Issue animated conservatives for 50 years but has tormented Republicans since the fall of Roe \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear also whether it will continue to fuel Democratic victories\par \par \uc2 As the 2024 election season ramps up, Republicans continue to struggle to find a winning national strategy on the flashpoint issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 where restricting the procedure has animated the conservative movement for half a century but tormented the party since the fall of Roe.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade delivered Republicans one of their most significant policy victories in a generation. But in the year and a half since the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, the ruling has also become one of their biggest political vulnerabilities.\par \par \uc2 Over the last 18 months, voters have favored \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in seven consecutive ballot measures, including in conservative states. Republicans underperformed in the 2022 midterm elections while Democrats scored off-year election wins in Wisconsin, Kentucky and Virginia \u8211\'20\'13 results that again emphasized the enduring power of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Now the presidential election year brings a further huge test.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there\u8217\'20\'19s really a kind of catch-22 for Republicans,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2  and a leading expert on the history of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US. \u8220\'20\'1COn the one hand, you have a lot of base Republican voters who really care about opposing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on the other you have a huge group of something like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/506759/broader-support-abortion-rights-continues-post-dobbs.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 70%}}}\uc2  of Americans who don\u8217\'20\'19t like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  meanwhile set the stage for another major showdown over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, this time just months before the 2024 presidential election. The court has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/13/abortion-pill-us-supreme-court-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed to decide a case}}}\uc2  that could determine the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/17/what-abortion-pill-supreme-court-case-access-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accessibility of a widely used \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill}}}\uc2 , including in states where the procedure remains legal.\par \par \uc2 But whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to fuel Democratic victories in a presidential election year is also unclear.\par \par \uc2 Despite delivering a long list of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  victories, voters tend to view the Republican frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a thrice-married former Democrat from New York, as less socially conservative than his rivals, says Gunner Ramer, political director for the anti-Trump Republican Accountability Pac.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  likes to stoke culture wars and own the libs but on social issues he\u8217\'20\'19s seen as more moderate,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramer said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CIf Trump is the nominee, Democrats are in a much trickier position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 For decades, the Republican party championed the mission of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement \u8211\'20\'13 to overturn Roe \u8211\'20\'13 without clearly articulating what would follow. Now they are contending with the real-world consequences: pregnancy resulting from rape and incest, life-threatening complications, fatal fetal conditions and miscarriages that require the procedure.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sixteen states now ban}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at conception or after six weeks, before many women know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant. Among them is Texas, where Kate Cox, a pregnant woman whose fetus was diagnosed with a fatal condition, was forced to leave the state this month to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/texas-abortion-ken-paxton-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened legal action}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cincluding first-degree felony prosecutions\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 against doctors or anyone else who assisted in performing the procedure. The Texas supreme court ultimately ruled against \uc2 Cox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s request to have an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 Seizing on the turn of events, top officials on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign assailed the \u8220\'20\'1Cunspeakable reality\u8221\'20\'1D now facing women in states with limited or no access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They drew a direct line to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the former president and likely Republican presidential nominee, blaming his appointment of three supreme court justices who cast decisive votes to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKate had to leave her home state to seek the healthcare she urgently needs,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodriguez, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is happening right here in the United States of America and it\u8217\'20\'19s happening because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the increasingly noncompetitive race for the Republican presidential nomination, disagreements among the White House hopefuls over how to approach or even talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflect a wide lack of unity within the GOP on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Trump, in conspicuous fashion, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/03/donald-trump-abortion-republicans-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trying to have it both ways}}}\uc2 . He has blamed conservative activists\u8217\'20\'19 uncompromising positions on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue\u8221\'20\'1D for costing Republicans at the ballot box while touting his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legacy to the party\u8217\'20\'19s socially conservative base.\par \par \uc2 In Iowa, which launches the Republican presidential primary contest next month, Trump is running ads declaring himself \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most pro-life president ever\u8221\'20\'1D. But on the major litmus test for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists \u8211\'20\'13 support for a national ban \u8211\'20\'13 he has been noncommittal.\par \par \uc2 At a CNN town hall this month, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor who is challenging Trump for the nomination, accused the former president of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/desantis-cnn-town-hall-12-12-23/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flip-flopping on the pro-life issue}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. Trump has said DeSantis made a \u8220\'20\'1Cterrible mistake\u8221\'20\'1D when the governor signed into law earlier this year a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Pressed to commit to a national standard, DeSantis has said he would support a federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-republicans-desantis-trump-bdccde60987da99018bf3abcbafedea0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after 15 weeks of pregnancy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nikky Haley, the former United Nations ambassador and the only woman in the race, has sought a different tack, calling for \u8220\'20\'1Cconsensus\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccompassion\u8221\'20\'1D. Haley, who as governor of South Carolina in 2016 signed a 20-week ban, has suggested that as president she would enact any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions that reached her desk, but said such measures were unlikely in the narrowly divided and deeply polarized Congress.\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , the former New Jersey governor who is running for president, is incredulous that Republicans are calling for federal action on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after waging a 50-year legal battle to return the issue to the states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI trust the people of this country, state by state, to make the call for themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D he said during a recent debate.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a view shared by the entrepreneur and author \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who opposes a federal ban but says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/meetthepressblog/vivek-ramaswamy-issues-rcna119091"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he supports state}}}\uc2  laws outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Among the Republican presidential candidates, the two most avowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the former vice-president, and Tim Scott, the South Carolina senator, have already exited the race.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Furthering the divide, leading anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are pressuring Republican candidates to back a national ban starting at least at 15 weeks of pregnancy if not earlier, while some party strategists are advising them to clearly state their opposition to any such federal limit.\par \par \uc2 In a post-election memo Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of the powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America, said the losses were \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor disappointments for the pro-life movement\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cwarning signs for the GOP\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is long past due for the GOP to define where it stands on the issue nationally,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CHaving a clear position and contrasting it isn\u8217\'20\'19t enough \u8211\'20\'13 campaigns and the party must put real advertising dollars behind it, going toe-to-toe with the Democrats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her group has urged candidates to support a federal ban on abortions after 15 weeks of gestation at a minimum or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/news/campaigns/sba-vows-withhold-endorsement-gop-15-week-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 risk losing its endorsement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 , chair of the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 , has criticized Republicans for not confronting the issue more aggressively. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t hide in a corner and think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s not going to be an issue,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/rncs-ronna-mcdaniel-says-gop-must-talk-abortion-election-losses-rcna124808?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiossneakpeek&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she said on NBC News}}}\uc2  in November, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t just say it\u8217\'20\'19s a state\u8217\'20\'19s issue and be done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Others have urged candidates to emphasize its support for exceptions, while expressing more compassion and empathy when discussing what can be a deeply personal \u8211\'20\'13 and in some cases medically advisable \u8211\'20\'13 decision. Still, some say its a matter of semantics, suggesting Republicans avoid terms like \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cban\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to Politico, a group of prominent Republican pollsters suggested candidates change the subject, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/12/13/kellyanne-conway-contraception-republicans-2024-00131410"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presenting polling to members of Congress}}}\uc2  that showed they could sharpen their appeal with women and independent voters by focusing on protecting contraception rather than banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is, as the courts decided, an issue for states to decide, not the federal government,\u8221\'20\'1D states the campaign website for Kari Lake, who is expected to be the Republican Senate nominee in the race for \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s seat. It\u8217\'20\'19s a retreat from her position as a candidate for governor in 2022, when the far-right Republican cast herself as an outspoken ally of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement and embraced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/12/arizona-abortion-ban-supreme-court#:~:text=In%20addition%20to%20host%20of,signed%20into%20law%20in%202022."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s territorial-era law}}}\uc2  that would ban nearly all abortions in the state.\par \par \uc2 Lake is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/14/us/politics/kari-lake-senate-republicans-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  one of several Republican candidates}}}\uc2  running in battleground Senate races who have adjusted their stance \u8211\'20\'13 and their rhetoric \u8211\'20\'13 on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in the House, now led by Mike Johnson, the Louisiana congressman, one of the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s staunchest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  crusaders, vulnerable Republicans have sought to distance themselves from absolutists in the party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court needs to stand down,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mike Lawler, a New York Republican who represents a district Biden won in 2020, in response to the high court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to take up the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill case. In a statement, he emphasized his opposition to a national ban.\par \par \uc2 **\par \par \uc2 As Republicans struggle, Democrats say the problem is taking positions that are deeply unpopular with the American public.\par \par \uc2 When Democrats won full control of the Virginia state legislature in November, the Republican governor, \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2 , declared support for what he called a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/virginia-elections-reasonable-15-week-abortion-ban-exceptions/story?id=104635775"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reasonable}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 That same night \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , the Democratic Kentucky governor, won re-election after his campaign ran {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/04/kentucky-abortion-ad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a powerful ad}}}\uc2  featuring a woman who was raped by her stepfather as a child. In the video, she criticized \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 , Beshear\u8217\'20\'19s Republican opponent, for supporting Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which does not include exceptions in cases involving rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 And in beet-red Ohio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/11/07/us/elections/results-ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 56.6% of voters}}}\uc2  chose to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn every election since the overturning of Roe, voters have sent a resounding message: they want more freedom, not less \u8211\'20\'13 and come 2024, Republicans will once again face the repercussions of their unrelenting crusade to strip away our rights,\u8221\'20\'1D Sarafina Chitika, a spokesperson for the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 At the state-level, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot initiatives could help Democrats mobilize Republican women and independent voters who have helped make up their winning coalition in the years since Trump was elected.\par \par \uc2 Building on the success of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot initiatives, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates are working to put the issue before voters in battleground states, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/12/arizona-abortion-ban-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/10/democrats-ballot-measures-protect-abortion-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2 . An effort is also underway in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/12/08/montana-abortion-law-rights-state-constitution-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Montana}}}\uc2 , where Democrats hope a constitutional amendment enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections could boost turnout and help one of the party\u8217\'20\'19s most vulnerable incumbent senators, \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 , win re-election.\par \par \uc2 As long as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is severely restricted in large swaths of the country where Republicans hold power, candidates at the national level will likely struggle to convince voters that they have moderated on the issue, even if they now champion later-stage \u8220\'20\'1Cconsensus\u8221\'20\'1D limits and exceptions, Ziegler said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the pro-life movement has a different agenda that they continue to pursue in a large swath of the country, national Republicans either have to say, \u8216\'20\'18that\u8217\'20\'19s not what we\u8217\'20\'19re doing. We\u8217\'20\'19re not for that\u8217\'20\'19; or they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be associated with that,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Even so, the road ahead for Democrats is not straightforward.\par \par \uc2 A string of recent surveys found a mixed picture: Biden is trailing Trump nationally and in several swing states. In a Wall Street Journal poll, voters said Trump was better equipped to handle most major policy issues with the exception of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which Biden led by a double-digit margin.\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign has vowed to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  front and center this election cycle. They have argued that Trump \u8211\'20\'13 or any of his Republican rivals \u8211\'20\'13 would seek to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as president, possibly through policy changes that would not require congressional approval {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/conservatism/commentary/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as some conservatives have proposed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There are risks to the strategy, especially if Trump is the nominee, says Ramer, from the anti-Trump Republican Accountability Pac.\par \par \uc2 Ramer says there was a key dynamic in play in 2022. While Democrats harnessed voter fury over the loss of constitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, he said they were helped by Republicans, who nominated candidates with \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme\u8221\'20\'1D absolutist positions on the issue, such as \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  in Pennsylvania and Tudor Dixon in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 That may not continue in 2024.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a very nuanced issue for voters,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the economy, at the end of the day, is more top of mind for Republicans and swing-state voters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231229ejct001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
