\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas city is latest to debate ban on road travel for those seeking  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 699 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2023\par 14:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Amarillo considers ordinance that has become part of new anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactic to undermine people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to flee states\par \par \uc2 A string of Texas localities have passed controversial ordinances banning so-called \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and another city may soon join their number.\par \par \uc2 Over the last several weeks, the city of Amarillo, Texas, has become embroiled in a debate over whether to pass an ordinance to block people from using the city\u8217\'20\'19s roads to transport pregnant people seeking abortions in other states. The city council met on Tuesday to debate the issue. As expected, it did not vote.\par \par \uc2 This type of ordinance has sprung up as part of a new anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactic to undermine people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to flee states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Since the fall of Roe v Wade, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes have scrambled to find a way to cut off what they see as \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D, even though many experts argue that the US constitution protects the right to interstate travel.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the meeting, the city council did not specify what the exact language of the ordinance under discussion would look like. After an opening prayer and an hour-long presentation by an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctor from Florida, the council discussed multiple possible anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordinances, including an ordinance that would seemingly deal with \u8220\'20\'1Ctrafficking\u8221\'20\'1D as well as one that tackled \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 However, from the discussion, it was not always clear what, exactly, each draft ordinance would do. A city government staffer declined to provide copies of the drafts to the Guardian without a public records request.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhatever we come back with, it needs to protect life. So if it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t, then maybe we\u8217\'20\'19ve done enough,\u8221\'20\'1D Cole Stanley, the Amarillo mayor, said in the meeting. \u8220\'20\'1CBut the right measure of enough is what we\u8217\'20\'19re trying to get to. Nobody\u8217\'20\'19s in here saying how they\u8217\'20\'19ll vote, but I would greatly appreciate and much more entertain something that\u8217\'20\'19s limited.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In October, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/texas-abortion-travel-ban-lubbock-county"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lubbock county became the largest Texas locality}}}\uc2  yet to enact an ordinance restricting people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to transport others for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related travel. Idaho has also passed a separate law banning \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D, which would block people from taking minors across state lines for abortions without parental permission. A judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/idaho-abortion-trafficking-travel-ban-270a403d7b4a5e99e566433556614728"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 froze that law}}}\uc2  earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTexas has the most restrictive and harmful \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation in place, period. So we feel that municipalities taking an additional stand on it is redundant,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lindsay London, a local activist who works with the Amarillo Reproductive Freedom Alliance , ahead of the Tuesday meeting. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19s really scary. Our options are so limited.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Texas law currently bans almost all abortions. Amarillo lies at the north-western corner of Texas, so Texans fleeing the state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in nearby New Mexico, Colorado or Kansas may travel along its roads.\par \par \uc2 Texas has been at the center of the national debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe \u8211\'20\'13 a case that originated in Texas \u8211\'20\'13 in summer 2022. Twenty Texas women have filed a lawsuit, aided by two doctors, alleging that they were denied abortions in medical emergencies because the medical exceptions in Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are too vague. Earlier this month, yet another Texan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/16/abortion-ban-lawsuits-pregnancy-complication-emergency-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became the first woman}}}\uc2  since the fall of Roe v Wade to file a lawsuit seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  while still pregnant.\par \par \uc2 She ultimately fled the state for the procedure, hours before the Texas state supreme court overturned an order that would have let her undergo it in her home state.\par \par \uc2 Amarillo is also the original home of the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related case to hit the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 . Just last week, the justices announced that they would take a case about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/17/what-abortion-pill-supreme-court-case-access-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the availability of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills}}}\uc2  that began in Amarillo federal court.\par \par \uc2 London stressed that she was grateful that Amarillo\u8217\'20\'19s leadership had met with members of the Amarillo Reproductive Freedom Alliance about their concerns over the proposed ordinance.\par \par \uc2 But, she added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s five white men who are staunchly anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in our leadership. It\u8217\'20\'19s kind of grim.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231219ejcj002js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
