\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Senate eyes vote on Ukraine aid and border security as House adjourns \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve \par \uc2 4,127 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 December 2023\par 21:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read all our latest US politics coverage here:See all our US politics coverage\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today in US politics\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in US politics on this relatively sleepy Friday:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate is continuing to negotiate over a supplemental funding package to provide aid to Ukraine and money for border security. The secretary of homeland security, Alejandro Mayorkas, met with senators on Capitol Hill today as the talks continue. However, the House has already adjourned for its holiday recess, so it is unclear how a spending package could pass both chambers of Congress before the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Negotiators are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/dec/15/senate-vote-ukraine-aid-house-border-trump-trials-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-657c9bf98f08a7f5b9267280#block-657c9bf98f08a7f5b9267280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  hoping to reach a deal on the package as early as Sunday, but it will likely take more time to draft text of a bill. That text will then be closely scrutinized by lawmakers of both parties as well as immigrant rights groups.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The jury in \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s defamation trial resumed its deliberations today, but jurors have not yet reached a decision on what damages the former Trump lawyer should pay to the former Georgia election workers Ruby Freeman and her daughter Shaye Moss. Freeman and Moss\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer argued that Giuliani substantially damaged their reputations by spreading lies about them related to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/15/us/supreme-court-dobbs-roe-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that the supreme court justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  took just 10 minutes to sign off on Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s opinion overturning Roe v Wade in 2022. The Times reports: \u8220\'20\'1CJustice Alito appeared to have pregamed it among some of the conservative justices, out of view from other colleagues, to safeguard a coalition more fragile than it looked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will be back on Monday for more updates from Washington.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Following a 90-minute meeting with the secretary of homeland security, Alejandro Mayorkas, this morning, one of the Democratic negotiators in the immigration talks, Senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  of Connecticut, expressed optimism about the direction of the negotiations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a very aggressive goal to get this on the floor next week, but there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of good faith in that room,\u8221\'20\'1D Murphy said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/article/dhs-mayorkas-meets-senate-negotiators-biden-officials/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per Punchbowl News}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThere are still disagreements. We continue to work at it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meetings are expected to continue this afternoon and into the weekend, as the Senate hopes to hold a vote next week on a supplemental funding package.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congress has taken steps to restrict public access to records related to UFOs, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Richard Liscombe reports:\par \par \uc2 If the truth about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ufos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UFOs}}}\uc2  is out there, the American government doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want you to see it yet.\par \par \uc2 Just months after \uc2 US space agency\uc2 Nasa\uc2  appointed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/14/ufo-nasa-research-chief-announcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research director of unidentified anomalous phenomena}}}\uc2 , and promised {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/01/pentagon-ufos-online-reports-aaro"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more transparency}}}\uc2  about what it knows, the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  has acted to throttle the flow of information that ultimately reaches the public.\par \par \uc2 Measures to create a presidential commission to review UFO records, and to order the Department of Defense to declassify certain \u8220\'20\'1Crecords relating to publicly known sightings of unidentified aerial phenomena (UAP)\u8221\'20\'1D, were stripped from the sweeping defense policy bill that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/14/congress-defense-bill-pay-raise-military"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed Congress on Thursday}}}\uc2  with bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 What was left were provisions ordering the National Archives to collect reports of \u8220\'20\'1Cunidentified anomalous phenomena, technologies of unknown origin and nonhuman intelligence\u8221\'20\'1D, but giving various government departments broad authority to keep the records secret.\par \par \uc2 Read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/15/ufo-records-release-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Congress passes stripped-down measure to release UFO records}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While many hard-right Republicans remain staunchly opposed to sending more money to Ukraine, one prominent Democrat warned that their rhetoric risked empowering dictators.\par \par \uc2 In response to \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Washington earlier this week, congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , a hard-right Republican of Georgia, accused the Ukrainian president of \u8220\'20\'1Cbegging for your money\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrNo sweeter Christmas gift to \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  than statements like this.\par \par \uc2 Our inaction warms the heart of dictators and despots across the globe. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ILXgPJI9To"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ILXgPJI9To}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  (@RepStenyHoyer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepStenyHoyer/status/1735730459726753899?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow much money will Washington spend to slaughter an entire generation of young Ukrainian men as Washington fights it\u8217\'20\'19s proxy war with Russia?\u8221\'20\'1D Greene said Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CShame!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , a Democrat of Maryland and the former House majority leader, responded to the comment today, attacking Greene for promoting the interests of Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo sweeter Christmas gift to \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  than statements like this,\u8221\'20\'1D Hoyer said. \u8220\'20\'1COur inaction warms the heart of dictators and despots across the globe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will \u8220\'20\'1Chave an LBJ moment\u8221\'20\'1D and decide not to run for re-election next year, the leftwing academic and independent presidential candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/cornel-west"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cornel West}}}\uc2  has predicted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not even sure whether I\u8217\'20\'19ll be running against Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/12/15/cornel-west-biden-election-00131944"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West told Politico}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBiden \u8211\'20\'13 I think he\u8217\'20\'19s going to have an LBJ moment [and] pull back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 West was referring to the moment on 31 March 1968 when Lyndon B Johnson, in office since the assassination of \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2  in November 1963, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://voicesofdemocracy.umd.edu/lyndon-baines-johnson-withdrawal-speech-31-march-1968/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that he would not seek re-election.\par \par \uc2 Already the oldest president ever sworn in, Biden is 81 and would be 86 at the end of a second term. In polling, clear majorities {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-age-poll-trump-2024-620e0a5cfa0039a6448f607c17c7f23e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 say he is too old}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/15/biden-lbj-moment-cornel-west"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden will have \u8216\'20\'18LBJ moment\u8217\'20\'19 and not run for re-election, Cornel West says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a moment of levity before the holidays, comedian Conan O\u8217\'20\'19Brien visited the White House press briefing room and chatted with reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey won\u8217\'20\'19t let me take questions,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien joked. \u8220\'20\'1CBut, boy, I have the answers to everything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Brien explained that he was visiting the White House because he is a \u8220\'20\'1Chuge history buff slash nerd\u8221\'20\'1D who has toured the building a number of times.\par \par \uc2 Watch the full clip:\par \par \uc2 enltr"They won't let me take questions, but boy I have the answers to everything."\par \par \uc2 WATCH: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ConanOBrien?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ConanOBrien}}}\uc2  visits the White House Press Briefing Room. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QZq4vt2j7s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QZq4vt2j7s}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1735717815988961756?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Border deal could be announced this weekend, report says\par \par \uc2 A Senate deal to overhaul border policies could be unveiled as early as Sunday, sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/josephzeballos/status/1735722038382186598"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Semafor}}}\uc2 . But it remains unclear how quickly senators can compile the text of a bill, which will be closely scrutinized by immigration groups.\par \par \uc2 One of the chief negotiators, Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  of Arizona , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1735716140880412873"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2  that they were \u8220\'20\'1Cmaking progress\u8221\'20\'1D in their talks and would hold more meetings this afternoon and over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , has already indicated he wants to hold a vote on a supplemental funding package next week, and he has delayed the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s holiday recess to accommodate a potential vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , a Democrat of Maryland and the former House majority leader, is imploring the House speaker, Republican Mike Johnson, to call the chamber back to session if the Senate passes a supplemental funding package.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hoyer.house.gov//sites/evo-subsites/hoyer.house.gov/files/evo-media-document/letter-to-speaker-johnson-on-ukraine-funding.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  sent to Johnson today, Hoyer argued the House must act swiftly if the Senate reaches a deal on Ukraine aid and border policy changes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Members return to their districts for the holidays and the people of Ukraine and Israel continue to wait anxiously for supplemental aid, I write to urge you to call the House back within 72 hours of the Senate passing legislation to provide additional assistance to our allies,\u8221\'20\'1D Hoyer wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe ought to have secured these vital resources for our allies months ago. There is no cause that demands the attention of this Congress more than the preservation of democracy, freedom, and our national defense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So far, Johnson has shown little interest in calling members back from their holiday recess, saying yesterday: \u8220\'20\'1CThe House will not wait around to receive and debate a rushed product.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has refused to overturn an Illinois ban on assault weapons and high-capacity ammunition, Michael Sainato reports:\par \par \uc2 The court rejected the request, made by a gun shop and a national gun rights group in an appeal of a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to allow a preliminary injunction to block the law.\par \par \uc2 A previous injunction request was also denied by the supreme court in May 2023. As is customary, the justices did not comment on their denial of the injunction.\par \par \uc2 The latest request came from a firearms retailer owned by Robert Bevis in Naperville and the National Association for Gun Rights.\par \par \uc2 In November 2023, a US appeals court upheld the Illinois assault weapons ban, rejecting appeals that challenged the law by claiming it violated the second amendment of the US constitution.\par \par \uc2 Read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/15/supreme-court-assault-weapons-ban-illinois"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court refuses to overturn Illinois assault weapons ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate is continuing to negotiate over a supplemental funding package to provide aid to Ukraine and money for border security. The secretary of homeland security, Alejandro Mayorkas, was spotted on Capitol Hill today as the talks continue. However, the House has already adjourned for its holiday recess, so it is unclear how a spending package could pass both chambers of Congress before the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The jury in \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s defamation trial resumed its deliberations today, as jurors weigh what damages the former Trump lawyer should pay to Georgia election workers Ruby Freeman and her daughter Shaye Moss. Freeman and Moss\u8217\'20\'19 lawyer argued that Giuliani substantially damaged their reputations by spreading lies about them related to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/15/us/supreme-court-dobbs-roe-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that supreme court Justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  took just 10 minutes to sign off on Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s opinion overturning Roe v Wade in 2022. The Times reports: \u8220\'20\'1CJustice Alito appeared to have pregamed it among some of the conservative justices, out of view from other colleagues, to safeguard a coalition more fragile than it looked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The secretary of homeland security, Alejandro Mayorkas, was seen leaving Capitol Hill after meeting with senators to continue talks over a potential deal on border policy changes.\par \par \uc2 The cabinet secretary did not answer reporters\u8217\'20\'19 questions as he left the Capitol, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1735708393422074200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per Punchbowl News}}}\uc2 , so it is unclear what (if any) progress was made in the negotiations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch took 10 minutes to approve Dobbs \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opinion \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 The conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  took just 10 minutes to approve without changes a 98-page draft of the opinion that would remove the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had been guaranteed for nearly 50 years, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/15/us/supreme-court-dobbs-roe-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to the paper, \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , the author of the opinion in Dobbs v Jackson, the case that struck down {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , from 1973, circulated his draft at 11.16am on 10 February 2022.\par \par \uc2 Citing two people who saw communications between the justices, the Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/15/us/supreme-court-dobbs-roe-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CAfter a justice shares an opinion inside the court, other members scrutinise it. Those in the majority can request revisions, sometimes as the price of their votes, sweating sentences or even words.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut this time, despite the document\u8217\'20\'19s length, Justice \uc2 Neil M Gorsuch\uc2  wrote back just 10 minutes later to say that he would sign on to the opinion and had no changes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Three other conservatives \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  and \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 signed on in the following days.\par \par \uc2 Read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/dec/15/neil-gorsuch-us-supreme-court-dobbs-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice Neil Gorsuch took 10 minutes to approve Dobbs \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  opinion \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As the Senate continues to negotiate over a potential deal on Ukraine aid and border policy changes, Congress did manage to pass one substantial bill this week.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the House passed an $886bn defense policy bill in a vote of 310-118, sending the legislation to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s desk. The Senate had easily passed the bill a day earlier, in a vote of 87-13.\par \par \uc2 The legislation includes the largest pay raise for troops in more than two decades and represents a funding increase of about 3% compared to the prior year.\par \par \uc2 The bill\u8217\'20\'19s passage caps off months of conflict between the House and the Senate, after the two chambers passed very different versions of the bill. The proposal initially passed by the House included controversial provisions aimed at restricting transgender troops\u8217\'20\'19 access to gender-affirming healthcare and blocking the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s reimbursement policy for service members who travel to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those policies were stripped out of the bill to get it passed through both chambers of Congress, angering the hard-right Republicans who had pushed for their inclusion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou almost feel like a parent who\u8217\'20\'19s sent a child off to summer camp and they came back a monster,\u8221\'20\'1D congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , a hard-right Republican of Florida, said of the final bill. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19ve done. This bill came back in far worse shape.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jury continues to deliberate in Giuliani defamation case\par \par \uc2 The jury is still deliberating in a federal case to determine how much \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  should have to pay two Georgia election workers he spread lies about after the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The jury started deliberating around 1:30 pm yesterday and went home at five. They returned this morning at 9 a.m. In total, they\u8217\'20\'19ve now deliberated for around 5.5 hours.\par \par \uc2 The press room here is still packed. While she\u8217\'20\'19s waiting for the jury, U.S. District Judge \uc2 Beryl Howell\uc2  is moving through her docket. Several of the cases are scheduling matters in January 6 cases.\par \par \uc2 During one case, Howell was confused, and slightly incredulous, to learn about the term \u8220\'20\'1Cghost bus,\u8221\'20\'1D a right-wing conspiracy theory about January 6.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , a Democrat of Pennsylvania who has been celebrated on the left for his anti-establishment persona, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/news/philadelphia/john-fetterman-israel-gaza-philadelphia-protest-20231026.html#loaded"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attracted criticism}}}\uc2  from progressives over his staunch support of Israel amid the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to NBC News about his views, Fetterman reiterated that he does not identify as a progressive and stood by his position on Israel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not a progressive,\u8221\'20\'1D Fetterman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/-not-progressive-fetterman-breaks-left-israel-immigration-rcna129747"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI just think I\u8217\'20\'19m a Democrat that is very committed to choice and other things. But with Israel, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be on the right side of that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fetterman also emphasized the urgent need to pass an aid package for Ukraine and Israel, even if it means making significant concessions to Republicans on immigration policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProgressives better do that because we can\u8217\'20\'19t leave Israel \u8212\'20\'14 we can\u8217\'20\'19t sell them out, and we can\u8217\'20\'19t sell Ukraine out, and we have to deliver on this,\u8221\'20\'1D Fetterman said. \u8220\'20\'1CI just would very much like to get a deal to deliver this critical aid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A Punchbowl News reporter spotted the secretary of homeland security, Alejandro Mayorkas, and some White House staffers arriving on Capitol Hill this morning. Their presence in the Capitol indicates the Senate negotiations over border policies are continuing in earnest today:\par \par \uc2 enltrDHS Secretary Mayorkas & WH staff arrive at Senate for border talks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JxawFl7UPA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JxawFl7UPA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Desiderio (@AndrewDesiderio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1735684974563532862?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 After Senate Republicans blocked one version of the supplemental funding package last week, members called on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to become more actively engaged in the talks over immigration reform.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe commander in chief \u8212\'20\'14 if there\u8217\'20\'19s a deal to be made \u8212\'20\'14 is going to have to get involved in the negotiations,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , a Republican of South Carolina, said on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s his job above all others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Republicans voted on Wednesday to formally authorize the impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , even though they have uncovered no proof that the president financially benefited from his family\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings. Some right-wing media figures appear to have grown weary of the investigation, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Richard Luscombe reports:\par \par \uc2 Several figures at Fox News, a usually reliable mouthpiece for most Republican party initiatives in Washington DC, have shown signs of \u8220\'20\'1Cimpeachment fatigue\u8221\'20\'1D, appearing to question the motivation of the vote to authorize an impeachment inquiry that Biden himself has condemned as \u8220\'20\'1Ca baseless political stunt that even Republicans in Congress admit is not supported by facts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Peter Doocy, Fox\u8217\'20\'19s White House correspondent, was among the most vocal, telling viewers that \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans are still trying to connect\u8221\'20\'1D money that the president\u8217\'20\'19s son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , earned overseas to accounts controlled by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe House oversight committee has been at this for years, and they have so far not been able to provide any concrete evidence that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  personally profited from his son Hunter\u8217\'20\'19s overseas business,\u8221\'20\'1D Doocy said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut they are going to try again with this impeachment inquiry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/dec/15/us-rightwing-media-biden-impeachment-fatigue-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US rightwing media begins to show signs of \u8216\'20\'18impeachment fatigue\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans are skeptical supplemental funding package can be passed quickly\par \par \uc2 Despite signs of progress in the Senate negotiations over a supplemental funding package, some Republicans are skeptical that a bill can be passed quickly.\par \par \uc2 For one thing, the House has already adjourned for its holiday recess, and the speaker, Republican Mike Johnson, has shown little interest in calling members back.\par \par \uc2 In addition to those logistical concerns, at least one Republican senator has indicated he wants to see some assurance that the House will pass the bill as well before the Senate votes on it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen recently, just because the speaker supports something doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean the House will go along with it,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 , a Republican of Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/why-you-should-be-skeptical-of-an-immigration-deal-this-month/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Punchbowl News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no reason for us to rush to pass something that\u8217\'20\'19s dead on arrival in the House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But House passage of a funding bill is far from guaranteed, even if Republicans win some concessions on immigration policies. Dozens of hard-right House Republicans remain adamantly opposed to additional Ukraine aid, which could jeopardize the bill\u8217\'20\'19s passage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters in Florida hope to enshrine the right to terminate a pregnancy in the state constitution by approving a ballot measure next year. Republican voters may be key to realizing that goal, Joseph Contreras reports for the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 More than 150,000 registered Republican voters in Florida have now signed a petition calling for a constitutional amendment that would guarantee a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the point of a fetus\u8217\'20\'19s viability, which is generally considered to be around the 24th week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The effort is a no-brainer, according to Miami-born Republican Carlos Lacasa.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow can my party be so vigorous in its defense of the right to bear arms yet not defend a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to make decisions about her own healthcare?\u8221\'20\'1D says the son and grandson of Cuban immigrants who fled communism under \uc2 Fidel Castro\uc2  in the early 1960s.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe in small government, and morality cannot be legislated without an overwhelming consensus of the governed \u8211\'20\'13 and there is no such consensus on this issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In supporting this effort, Lacasa will break ranks with the state\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and his allies in the Florida legislature who have sharply limited access to abortions in the state in the last two years, encouraged in part by the supreme court overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/15/florida-abortion-right-constitution-amendment-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida Republican voters could be key to push for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights referendum}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The jury in \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s defamation trial will continue its deliberations today, as they weigh what damages the former Trump lawyer should pay to Ruby Freeman and her daughter Shaye Moss.\par \par \uc2 Freeman and Moss\u8217\'20\'19 lawyer argued that Giuliani substantially damaged their reputations by spreading lies about them related to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The lawyer, Michael Gottlieb, has asked the jury to award Freeman and Moss at least $24m each to \u8220\'20\'1Csend a message\u8221\'20\'1D to others who might consider similar election schemes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey say when someone shows you who they are, believe them. Mr Giuliani has shown us over and over and over again that he will not take our clients names out of his mouth,\u8221\'20\'1D Gottlieb said yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFacts do not and will not stop him. He\u8217\'20\'19s telegraphing that he will do this again. Believe him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full report from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/14/rudy-giuliani-testimony-federal-defamation-case-atlanta-election-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jury in Rudy Giuliani defamation trial urged to send message: \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t do it\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court is expected to consider Friday whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former White House chief of staff, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mark-meadows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Meadows}}}\uc2  , charged by Fulton county prosecutors over his role in efforts to overturn the 2020 election in Georgia, should see his criminal case transferred from state to federal court.\par \par \uc2 Meadows has so far been unsuccessful in his removal efforts. The US district judge Steve Jones denied the motion in September and Meadows challenged the decision to the US court of appeals for the eleventh circuit, which scheduled oral arguments for 9am.\par \par \uc2 The appeal before judges William Pryor, Robin Rosenbaum and Nancy Abudu \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , Obama and Biden appointees \u8211\'20\'13 marks possibly the final chance for Meadows to have his case transferred, a move that would give him key advantages at trial as well as affect the case against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read more of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/15/mark-meadows-trump-georgia-election-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Second chance for Mark Meadows to move racketeering case to federal court}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate eyes Ukraine vote as House adjourns\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , said yesterday that negotiators had made \u8220\'20\'1Cgood progress\u8221\'20\'1D in their talks regarding a supplemental funding package aimed at providing aid to Ukraine and reforming immigration policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe plan is for the Senate to act as soon as we are ready to move forward on the supplemental,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hope to come to an agreement. But no matter what, members should be aware that we will vote on a supplemental proposal next week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The timeline will force senators to delay their planned holiday recess, although Schumer did not provide a specific schedule for next week.\par \par \uc2 Even if the Senate can get a funding bill passed, it would still need to pass the House, which adjourned yesterday for its own holiday recess and is not expected to return to session until the new year.\par \par \uc2 Despite the apparent progress in the Senate, the House speaker, Republican Mike Johnson, has indicated he will not call members back from their recess even if a supplemental funding bill passes the upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 Johnson said yesterday, \u8220\'20\'1CWhile that work should continue, the House will not wait around to receive and debate a rushed product.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSince I became Speaker in late October, I have clearly and consistently told the White House and Leader Schumer that we must secure our own border before we secure another country\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 For some reason, the Biden Administration waited until this week to even begin negotiations\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Speaker Mike Johnson (@SpeakerJohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerJohnson/status/1735436867980398865?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hungary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/15/hungary-blocks-50bn-in-eu-aid-for-ukraine-hours-after-membership-talks-were-approved"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2  the \uc2 EU\uc2  from approving a \u8364\'20\'AC50bn aid package to Ukraine. The move came hours after \uc2 EU\uc2  leaders agreed to open membership talks with Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans named Nassau County legislator Mazi Melesa Pilip as their nominee to replace George Santos in the House. The special election has been scheduled for 13 February.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court will consider a request from \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff, to move his case from state to federal court. Meadows has been charged by Fulton county prosecutors over his role in efforts to overturn the 2020 election results in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231215ejcf00268\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
