\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Florida Republican voters could be key to push for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights referendum\b0\par\par\uc2 Joseph Contreras \par \uc2 1,047 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 December 2023\par 13:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 46\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 150,000 Republicans among 1.3m signatures collected for plan to put constitutional amendment to voters next year\par \par \uc2 Pro-choice activists in Florida, where nearly all abortions are banned after the 15th week of pregnancy, want voters to enshrine the right to a termination in the state constitution via a referendum on next year\u8217\'20\'19s election ballot.\par \par \uc2 More than 150,000 registered Republican voters in Florida have now signed a petition calling for a constitutional amendment that would guarantee a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the point of a fetus\u8217\'20\'19s viability, which is generally considered to be around the 24th week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The effort is a no-brainer, according to Miami-born Republican Carlos Lacasa.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow can my party be so vigorous in its defense of the right to bear arms yet not defend a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to make decisions about her own healthcare?\u8221\'20\'1D says the son and grandson of Cuban immigrants who fled communism under \uc2 Fidel Castro\uc2  in the early 1960s. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe in small government, and morality cannot be legislated without an overwhelming consensus of the governed \u8211\'20\'13 and there is no such consensus on this issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lacasa says he has always opposed excessive government interference in the private lives of his fellow citizens. A self-described \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  Republican who served four terms in the lower house of the Florida state legislature, the 60-year-old attorney took strong exception to the vaccine mandates and mandatory lockdowns that some authorities imposed at the height of the Covid-19 epidemic \u8211\'20\'13 an attitude now also extending to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In supporting this effort, Lacasa will break ranks with the state\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and his allies in the Florida legislature who have sharply limited access to abortions in the state in the last two years, encouraged in part by the supreme court overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 To enshrine the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida, it requires the collection of verified signatures from nearly 900,000 registered voters statewide by the end of this month. The six groups that have joined forces on behalf of the proposed constitutional amendment say they have already garnered support from more than 1.3 million voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vast majority of Floridians don\u8217\'20\'19t support an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D says Anna Hochkammer, executive director of the bipartisan Florida Women\u8217\'20\'19s Freedom Coalition. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the past, we\u8217\'20\'19ve been protected by the explicit right to privacy contained in the state constitution, but we want specific language in the constitution that prohibits government interference with access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The issue has become a political minefield for many Republican leaders nationwide.\par \par \uc2 When Roe was overturned last year, outraged women\u8217\'20\'19s rights groups responded with protests and galvanized support for pro-choice candidates and ballot measures across party lines.\par \par \uc2 Since then, seven states have taken steps to protect reproductive rights, from deep-blue Vermont and California to longtime Republican strongholds like Kansas and Kentucky. Democrats regained control of the Virginia general assembly in legislative elections last month by campaigning on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights issue.\par \par \uc2 Florida has bucked that trend thus far.\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU)\uc2  and a group of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers filed a lawsuit in 2022 challenging the constitutionality of the recently instituted 15-week ban, DeSantis and the Republican-dominated state legislature doubled down on the issue by approving a six-week prohibition last spring. The lawsuit is currently before the Florida supreme court. If the justices, all of whom were appointed by Republican governors, throw out the litigation, a more draconian six-week ban would instantly take effect.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general, \uc2 Ashley Moody\uc2 , has vowed to block the proposed ballot measure by asking the Florida supreme court to invalidate it on the grounds that its two-sentence text is vaguely worded and designed to \u8220\'20\'1Choodwink\u8221\'20\'1D voters about the scope of the reproductive freedoms it would grant. Multiple requests from the Guardian for an interview with \uc2 Moody\uc2  went unanswered.\par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates maintain that Republican leaders are out of step with most Floridians.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 University of North Florida\uc2  poll of 716 registered voters in November found that 62% of respondents would support the proposed constitutional amendment while only 29% would reject the measure. Slightly over half of the registered Republican voters surveyed in the poll also signaled their backing of the initiative.\par \par \uc2 For their part, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups say they will defeat the amendment in the new year if it comes to a vote.\par \par \uc2 Aaron DiPietro, legislative affairs director of the Florida Family Policy Council (FFPC), lambasted the amendment as \u8220\'20\'1Cvery extreme and deceptive as it would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand and allow abortions for virtually any reason up to nine months of pregnancy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would legally trump almost every commonsense safety law in Florida regulating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , [and] we are organized in a way no other state has been to [stop] this amendment,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 If the referendum does qualify for the 2024 ballot, its ratification will not be a slam dunk. Florida law requires a supermajority of 60% approval among voters to enact a ballot measure. Some seasoned political analysts expect the outcome would be a closely run affair.\par \par \uc2 Kevin Wagner\uc2 , a political science professor at \uc2 Florida Atlantic University\uc2 , notes that voter turnout will be a huge factor as the proposed amendment \u8220\'20\'1Cis likely to draw out some people on either side of the issue who otherwise would not vote\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democrats think it will bring out more of their supporters, especially among young people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that he believed it would pass.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may have acknowledged that message to some degree. During an interview on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press program last September, the former US president condemned the six-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  championed by DeSantis as \u8220\'20\'1Ca terrible mistake\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 much to the dismay of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby in America\u8217\'20\'19s third most populous state.\par \par \uc2 Hochkammer warns that any Republican politician who denounces the ballot measure next year would do so at their own peril.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is a third-rail issue,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans who insist on going down that road would be smart to rethink that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231215ejcf001me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
