\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 An \u8216\'20\'18 \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  abolitionist\u8217\'20\'19 became an Oklahoma senator. The fringe is celebrating its big victory\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,175 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 December 2023\par 15:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The hardline fragment of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is gaining traction in the wake of Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19s fall\par \par \uc2 When Dusty Deevers won his race to become an Oklahoma state senator on Tuesday night, he wasted no time in making sure his new constituents knew what he stood for.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere in Oklahoma, it\u8217\'20\'19s time to abolish \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , abolish pornography, abolish the state income tax and give power and equal representation back to the people!\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican posted on X, the platform formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Deevers\u8217\'20\'19 use of the term \u8220\'20\'1Cabolish \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D is no mere rhetorical flourish. On his campaign website, Deevers has identified himself as an \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  abolitionist\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 an adherent of a hardline, fringe segment of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement that, in Oklahoma and elsewhere, is growing in the wake of the fall of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is rooted in the belief that fetuses are people, worthy of rights and protections. But the mainstream \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D movement posits that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients should not be punished, since they are seen as the bamboozled victims of nefarious doctors and the \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry\u8221\'20\'1D. Typically, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans target \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, not patients.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionists,\u8221\'20\'1D on the other hand, hold what they believe to be a more ideologically consistent stance: if a fetus is a person, then \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is tantamount to murder. And patients should be punished accordingly.\par \par \uc2 Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturning has made a broader range of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ideas look acceptable, as well as cast a spotlight on the contradictions and limits in current anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, said Mary Ziegler, a University of California, Davis School of Law professor who studies the legal history of reproduction. In turn, that\u8217\'20\'19s emboldened the abolitionists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not an easy question about how you can be consistent and exempt women from punishment,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler said. The abolitionists, she says, are essentially saying: \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re the pragmatists, because if a lot of abortions are self-managed, or involve medical practitioners from out of state or even out of the US altogether, how do you propose meaningfully enforcing [bans] if you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to punish women or other pregnant folks?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve also been hated because people who are not opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn\u8217\'20\'19t know that they existed,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler added. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd people who are opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not happy that people discovered that they existed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Over the last several years, \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  abolitionists\u8221\'20\'1D and their ideology have quietly amassed popularity in churches, state legislatures and online. Several abolitionist organizations filed an amicus brief in the decision that overturned Roe. Abolitionists Rising \u8211\'20\'13 which features a video of Deevers on its website \u8211\'20\'13 has almost 200,000 subscribers on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , with at least one video with more than half a million views. (Deevers did not immediately reply to an interview request.) The \uc2 YouTube\uc2  account of Apologia Studios, which is run by prominent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionist\u8221\'20\'1D and pastor Jeff Durbin, has more than 500,000 subscribers.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, legislators in at least nine states introduced bills that would advance the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  abolition cause, such as by erasing provisions in laws that explicitly protect pregnant people from being prosecuted for having abortions. At least two of those bills explicitly cite the 14th amendment, which was originally passed to ensure that formerly enslaved people had equal rights, to extend rights and protections to fetuses.\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has a long history of drawing comparisons between their cause and that of pre-civil war abolitionists trying to end US slavery, as well as civil rights crusaders. For decades, they have tried to use the 14th amendment to establish fetuses\u8217\'20\'19 right to personhood, a push that is seeing renewed interest post-Roe.\par \par \uc2 However, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionists\u8221\'20\'1D often draw a line between their work and that of the mainstream pro-life movement. Not only do they frequently disdain the pro-life label, but while the pro-life movement has increasingly sought to portray its mission as secular, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionists\u8221\'20\'1D are staunchly and openly Christian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that the abolitionist movement is a litmus test for how much the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement needs to win or wants to win in democratic politics versus other means,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you need to win with voters, abolitionists are not going to get anywhere, ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There is little support for severe punishments for people who get illegal abortions. Although 47% of US adults believe that women who have illegal abortions should face some form of penalty, just 14% think they should serve jail time, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2022/05/06/americans-views-on-whether-and-in-what-circumstances-abortion-should-be-legal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 2022 poll by the Pew Research Center}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAbolitionists\u8221\'20\'1D don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily believe that people should face the death penalty for abortions. \u8220\'20\'1CI do believe that the unjustified taking of human life, if provable, ultimately, justly, ought to be capital punishment,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/01/us/abortion-abolitionists.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Durbin told the New York Times last year}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, I don\u8217\'20\'19t trust our system today to deal that out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 None of the \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionist\u8221\'20\'1D-style bills ultimately advanced very far in state legislatures this year. Still, they can be something of a PR nightmare for Republicans and the mainstream pro-life movement. After a host of news articles about South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Prenatal Equal Protection Act, which would allow people who have abortions to face the death penalty, 10 Republican state legislators asked to remove their names as sponsors of the bill.\par \par \uc2 That bill died in committee.\par \par \uc2 While these bills technically focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers, in reality they would probably also be used to penalize people of color or poor people who have unintended pregnancy losses, according to Farah Diaz-Tello, senior counsel and legal director of If/When/How, a legal advocacy group for reproductive justice.\par \par \uc2 Things that for people of wealth and privilege would be considered a tragedy end up being charged as a crime against people of color\par \par \uc2 Farah Diaz-Tello\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know who the targets of these laws would be, because they\u8217\'20\'19re the people who are already criminalized for pregnancy outcomes. So we would see an escalation of that status quo,\u8221\'20\'1D Diaz-Tello said. \u8220\'20\'1CThings that for people of wealth and privilege would be considered a tragedy end up being charged as a crime against people of color, in particular Black women, and people who are in poverty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Deevers won his seat in the Oklahoma state legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsfromthestates.com/article/republican-dusty-deevers-wins-lawton-senate-seat-special-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after its former occupant resigned}}}\uc2  for another job. On his campaign website, Deevers says that he supports Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s version of the Prenatal Equal Protection Act, which was introduced in 2023. That bill eliminates language that would block Oklahoma prosecutors from targeting pregnant people for \u8220\'20\'1Ccausing the death of the unborn child\u8221\'20\'1D. Its sponsor, whose 2020 election was supported by the abolitionist group Free the States, did not immediately reply to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill would abolish \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by making preborn children equal under law and closing the loopholes which allow for self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Deevers\u8217\'20\'19 campaign website reads, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CI am 100% against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and for its abolition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231214ejce001p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
