\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Woman suing Kentucky over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  laws learns her embryo no longer viable\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 579 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 December 2023\par 18:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Woman, referred to as Jane Doe in court documents, was about eight weeks pregnant when she filed lawsuit against state\par \par \uc2 A pregnant woman in Kentucky who is suing the Republican state over its restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws has learned that her embryo is no longer viable, her lawyers said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The woman, who is referred to as Jane Doe in court documents, was about eight weeks pregnant when she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/08/kentucky-woman-abortion-ban-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed the lawsuit}}}\uc2  against Kentucky in a state court in Louisville.\par \par \uc2 Brigitte Amiri, the deputy director of \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Freedom Project and lawyer for Jane Doe, released a statement with the update and encouraged other Kentuckians to join the case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJane Doe sought an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Kentucky, and when she could not get one, she bravely came forward to challenge the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu.org/press-releases/update-on-kentucky-abortion-ban-class-action"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Amiri said}}}\uc2  in the statement, shared with the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCountless Kentuckians face the same harm every day as the result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A representative from \uc2 ACLU\uc2  was not able to confirm how the loss of the embryo will affect the case.\par \par \uc2 In a press release on Friday, Doe said she was suing the state as she wants to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Kentucky, but is legally not able to do so. Doe is seeking class-action status for the suit in order to include other Kentuckians who are pregnant and want to access an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , either currently or in the future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is my decision \u8211\'20\'13 not the government\u8217\'20\'19s or any other person\u8217\'20\'19s,\u8221\'20\'1D Doe said in the Friday news release issued by the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI am bringing this lawsuit because I firmly believe that everyone should have the ability to make their own decisions about their pregnancies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the overturning of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  last June, Kentucky has had in effect two laws severely restricting abortions. One law bans nearly all abortions, and another six-week ban bars abortions after an embryo\u8217\'20\'19s cardiac activity is detected.\par \par \uc2 In February, the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court refused to halt either law, essentially leaving abortions banned in the Bluegrass state.\par \par \uc2 The latest update comes after a woman in Texas fled the state to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Texas supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/09/texas-supreme-court-temporarily-blocks-woman-from-abortion-for-non-viable-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paused}}}\uc2  a previous court ruling that allowed the woman to obtain the emergency procedure.\par \par \uc2 Kate Cox, a mother of two from Texas, filed a lawsuit to obtain an immediate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after her fetus had been diagnosed with a terminal condition. \uc2 Cox\uc2  learned that carrying her pregnancy to term could impact \uc2 Cox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s health and future pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not a matter of if I will have to say goodbye to my baby, but when,\u8221\'20\'1D Cox said in a statement when the suit was filed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do not want to continue the pain and suffering that has plagued this pregnancy. I do not want to put my body through the risks of continuing this pregnancy. I do not want my baby to arrive in this world only to watch her suffer. I need to end my pregnancy now so that I have the best chance for my health and a future pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 While a Texas court had initially granted Cox\u8217\'20\'19s request, the state attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/texas-abortion-ken-paxton-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened to prosecute}}}\uc2  anyone who helped with the procedure. The higher court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/11/texas-supreme-court-overturns-ruling-kate-cox-emergency-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultimately overturned}}}\uc2  the lower court decision which would have allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231213ejcd002h1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
