\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  agrees to consider  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill access\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 983 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 December 2023\par 17:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 25\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Case will determine future of mifepristone in first major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue to reach country\u8217\'20\'19s highest court since it overturned Roe\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  on Wednesday agreed to hear oral arguments in a case that could determine the future of a pill used in most abortions in the US, in the first major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case to land at the country\u8217\'20\'19s highest court since the justices overturned Roe v Wade and abolished the national right to the procedure in 2022.\par \par \uc2 A decision in the case will probably arrive in summer 2024, just months before the presidential election. The outcome of the case could affect not just access to the pill, which has been repeatedly deemed safe and effective, but the Federal Drug Administration\u8217\'20\'19s authority to regulate all manner of medications.\par \par \uc2 The drug at the heart of the case is mifepristone, one of the two drugs typically used in medication abortions, which make up the majority of US abortions. Last year, an association of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organizations and doctors, the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, filed a federal lawsuit arguing that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  had overstepped its authority when it approved mifepristone in 2000.\par \par \uc2 In April, a Texas federal judge appointed by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  issued a preliminary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/07/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-trump-judge-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling to suspend}}}\uc2  the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone and pull the medication off the market. The US court of appeals for the fifth circuit \u8211\'20\'13 one of the most conservative federal appeals courts in the US \u8211\'20\'13 ruled in August that, while it was too late to suspend the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval, the agency should {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/16/restriction-abortion-pill-mifepristone-access-fda-court-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significantly restrict}}}\uc2  access to mifepristone. The Biden administration and Danco Laboratories, which manufactures mifepristone, then asked the supreme court to weigh in on the case.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court paused lower-court rulings while the case plays out, so mifepristone remains widely available in states that permit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If the court allows the fifth circuit ruling to stand, it would roll back recent \uc2 FDA\uc2  efforts that refined the drug\u8217\'20\'19s dosage and expanded access by allowing it to be prescribed later on in pregnancy and through telehealth.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the supreme court agreed to hear the consolidated petitions from the Biden administration and Danco Laboratories, which asked the justices to focus on the legal attempts to roll back those later \uc2 FDA\uc2  efforts. Those petitions also asked the justices to consider whether the challengers have the legal right, or standing, to bring the case in the first place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t just bring random lawsuits in court. You actually have to have been harmed by something,\u8221\'20\'1D said Greer Donley, an associate law professor at the University of Pittsburgh Law School. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s really what standing analysis is all about, to try to figure out if if the people who bring the lawsuit actually have a stake in the case.\u8221\'20\'1D Numerous legal experts have questioned whether the challengers in this case have properly demonstrated that they have been harmed by mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s continued legality.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court also denied a petition from the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine that asked the justices to explicitly consider the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2000 approval of mifepristone. That move suggests that the supreme court is unlikely to pull mifepristone off the market entirely.\par \par \uc2 In Donley\u8217\'20\'19s view, the outcome of this case will probably signal whether the supreme court, which is controlled 6-3 by conservatives, wants to be involved in the post-Roe war over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. If the justices decide to focus on the standing issues in the case, they could sidestep having to rule on the substance of the case entirely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI could see the more moderates on the supreme court thinking: \u8216\'20\'18we don\u8217\'20\'19t want to touch this,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Donley said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt might make the supreme court look like less of an activist court if it were to dismiss this case on the basis of really legitimate standing problems.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Any ruling by the court would affect all 50 states, including those that have protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. (In recent months, officials in states such as Washington and California {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/22/democratic-states-stockpile-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have announced}}}\uc2  that they have begun to stockpile mifepristone.)\par \par \uc2 A ruling could also imperil the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s regulatory power writ large and pose an existential threat to pharmaceutical companies. If courts can rewrite the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, any kind of drug \u8211\'20\'13 including, for example, drugs used to protect against HIV or to provide gender-affirming care \u8211\'20\'13 could end up in conservative jurists\u8217\'20\'19 crosshairs.\par \par \uc2 The ruling from the federal appeals court, Danco Laboratories warned in its briefs to the supreme court, \u8220\'20\'1Cdestabilizes the pharmaceutical and biotechnology industries by questioning when scientific studies \u8211\'20\'13 accepted by \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 are sufficient\u8221\'20\'1D. More than 100 studies, conducted across 26 countries, have concluded that mifepristone is safe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a New York Times review found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If deprived of access to mifepristone, several \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics have said that they would keep providing medication abortions using only misoprostol, the other drug typically used in medication abortions. Although misoprostol-only abortions are still overwhelmingly safe, they can have more side-effects and are slightly less effective than the two-drug protocol.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, regardless of how the supreme court rules, its decision will not curtail the thriving underground networks that routinely supply mifepristone to women looking to end their pregnancies, including in the 16 states with near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. In fact, a move to ban mifepristone is likely to cause a sharp rise in demand for the drug through those networks.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s fall, a vast web of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters and opportunistic merchants have sprung up to ship \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to Americans. Inducing your own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not illegal in most US states, even in states that have banned in-clinic abortions, and medical experts widely agree that it can be safe to use pills to \u8220\'20\'1Cself-manage\u8221\'20\'1D an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231213ejcd00238\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
