\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Giuliani defamation trial: election worker testifies ex-Trump lawyer\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 lies ruined her life \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino (now), Rachel Leingang (earlier) \par \uc2 4,335 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2023\par 21:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For our latest reporting on Giuliani trial, you can read our latest report:Judge asks if Giuliani is mentally fit as ex-mayor defends poll worker lies\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 It was a day of emotional testimony in a Washington courtroom, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/rudy-giuliani-election-workers-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/rudy-giuliani-election-workers-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shaye Moss }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/rudy-giuliani-election-workers-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took the stand in the defamation trial against }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/rudy-giuliani-election-workers-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}\uc2 . She recounted in devastating detail the ways the former New York City mayor\u8217\'20\'19s lies and the ensuing harassment upended her life, destroyed her sense of security and self-worth and hurt her family.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Under cross-examination, Moss pointedly noted that the harm caused by Giuliani continues to this day as the former mayor repeated his lies about her to reporters as recently as Monday. Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s comments to reporters drew a sharp rebuke from the judge.\par \par \uc2 Beyond the trial, other big stories today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s top court said the state must redraw its congressional maps, in a decision widely seen as a victory for Democrats in the battle to win control of the narrowly divided House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Texas supreme court overturned a lower court order that would have allowed Kate Cox to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a fetus with a fatal condition. Cox went out of state for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Claudine Gay will remain the president of \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  despite calls for her removal following testimony before a congressional hearing about antisemitism on campus last week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/dec/12/us-inflation-rate-report-november"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US inflation ticked down again last month}}}\uc2 , with cheaper gas helping further lighten the weight of consumer price increases in the US.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  failed to persuade congressional Republicans to rush aid to Ukraine as Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war nears its third year. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/dec/12/russia-ukraine-war-live-zelenskiy-to-meet-biden-in-push-for-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 During a visit to Washington}}}\uc2 , Zelenskiy met with members of Congress and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Still to come: CNN will host a presidential town hall in Iowa with Republican White House hopeful Ron DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/rudy-giuliani-election-workers-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s lies turned my life \u8216\'20\'18upside down\u8217\'20\'19, election worker testifies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Moss concludes her testimony\par \par \uc2 Sam reports that Shaye Moss has completed her testimony after taking the witness stand to answer questions from \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer and her own.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Joseph Sibley, sought to undercut the idea millions of dollars in damages were required to repair her reputation. He also sought to distance Giuliani from any harm Moss suffered.\par \par \uc2 John Langford, one of Moss\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys, asked her to further explain why she was not looking for work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI definitely would have to start off again at the bottom and work my way up. I am wanting to do that but I am not mentally able to do that with things are the way are now,\u8221\'20\'1D Moss said. \u8220\'20\'1CMost days I pray that God does not wake me up and I just disappear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also explained that she does not go out alone, except for one instance in which she did it as homework for her therapist.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI did it so terrified. I felt extremely nauseous. But thankfully there was this guy at the bar,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was a Jewish guy. He literally talked the entire time about this movie about this family that is in the pharmaceuticals. The guy was just talking. And I did it. I was very proud of myself. But unfortunately I have not been able to do that again. But I did do it once.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Plaintiffs are now playing a videotaped deposition from Bernard Kerik.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some background on the situation in New York written by our in-house expert on redistricting, Sam Levine (yes, the same one in court covering the election case).\par \par \uc2 Despite outperforming expectations on election night last year, Republicans made stunning gains across New York, one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most liberal states. They won four toss-up races and picked off congressman \uc2 Sean Patrick Maloney\uc2 , the House Democratic campaign chairman charged with protecting his party\u8217\'20\'19s hold on Congress.\par \par \uc2 That was possible under the map that will now be redrawn.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/feb/03/new-york-democrats-plan-gain-three-seats-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 After decrying Republican election rigging, Democrats embrace it in New York }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Breaking from the Giuliani trial to mark a new legal development out of New York, where a court has agreed to allow the state to redraw its congressional map in a decision widely seen as a victory for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 In an opinion issued on Tuesday afternoon, the liberal-leaning New York State Court of Appeals ordered the state\u8217\'20\'19s redistricting commission to draw new maps by February 28, 2024. The court is effectively tossing out the highly competitive electoral map that gave Republicans an edge in several key House races last cycle \u8211\'20\'13 just enough to win the majority.\par \par \uc2 The commission is split evenly between Republicans and Democrats, but the Democratic-controlled state legislature has final say over the redrawn map. Given the narrow divide in the US House, New York Democrats will be under pressure to reject any proposal that does not improve their electoral odds, particularly after Republicans aggressive gerrymanders in states like North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 enltrRight now, Dems have a meager 15D-11R majority in NY's House seats. This ruling could put up to six GOP seats in deeper danger, including: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NY01?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NY01}}}\uc2  Nick LaLota (R) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NY03?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NY03}}}\uc2  VACANT (R) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NY04?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NY04}}}\uc2  Anthony D'Esposito (R) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NY17?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NY17}}}\uc2  Mike Lawler (R) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NY19?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NY19}}}\uc2  Marc Molinaro (R) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NY22?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NY22}}}\uc2  Brandon Williams (R)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1734682145040584778?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer is pressing Moss to disclose additional details about her medical health as a result of the former mayor\u8217\'20\'19s lies.\par \par \uc2 enltrShaye Moss is on the stand with her head in her hands during a brief sidebar as Giuliani's lawyer is pressing her to disclose what additional medical issues she's had as a result of Giuliani's conduct. She just said she only just told her mom she's on medication.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1734667733755707652?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMOSS, who has not mentione Trump much, does so when pressed by Sibley about whether her doctors tied her anxiety/depression to Giuliani.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt started with Trump and his allies \u8212\'20\'14 meaning \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and his crew were the start of it all. They lit the torch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1734668997608575473?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some more back-and-forth in what appears to be a somewhat combative round of questioning.\par \par \uc2 enltrSIBLEY: Why don\u8217\'20\'19t you have enough money to repair your reputation?\par \par \uc2 MOSS: Because your client is still lying on me and ruining my reputation further... How could you work in law if everyone is saying you\u8217\'20\'19re a horrible lawyer?\par \par \uc2 SIBLEY: You\u8217\'20\'19d be surprised actually.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1734658914539442284?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More from our man on the ground:\par \par \uc2 enltrGiuliani's lawyer is pursuing a line of questioning that Moss is seeking much more money than is necessary to repair her reputation\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1734658938904150299?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 I personally cannot repair my reputation at the moment because your client is still lying on me and ruining my reputation further. How could I do that? How could you work in law everyone was saying you\u8217\'20\'19re a horrible lawyer? Moss said under questioning.\par \par \uc2 She added, per Sam: \u8220\'20\'1C We need to make a statement. We need to ensure that the election workers that are still there don\u8217\'20\'19t have to go through this. Hopefully by hitting someone in their pockets, for someone whose whole career has been about their pockets, we will send a message.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Sam is back in the courtroom in the defamation trial in Washington DC, where Moss is being cross-examined.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear where exactly Sibley is going with his questions, Sam reports.\par \par \uc2 A lot of his questions seem to be trying to get Moss to concede that there was confusion or uncertainty about what happened immediately after the 2020 election. The US district judge \uc2 Beryl Howell\uc2  has already found Giuliani liable for defamation, so whether or not Giuliani had grounds to make his outlandish claims is not really at issue in the trial.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It cannot be easy to be the lawyer for the voluble former New York mayor. Moss is back on the stand for cross-examination from Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, Joseph Sibley.\par \par \uc2 enltr"My client likes to talk a lot, unfortunately," said \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 's lawyer, Joseph Sibley.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1734650408440619011?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While we await the return of the Giuliani trial in DC, we\u8217\'20\'19re linking to our Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war blog, where Biden has said Israel is \u8220\'20\'1Cstarting to lose support\u8221\'20\'1D of international community over its bombardment of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Biden also said that Netanyahu needs to change his hardline government.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments come as Netanyahu thanked the US for its support on Tuesday, but noted that the US and Israel have had disagreements about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe day after \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/IsraeliPM/status/1734596112588095939?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister on X}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/dec/12/israel-gaza-war-live-updates-news-gaza-attack-palestine-un-ceasefire-vote-hostages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Gaza war live: Israel \u8216\'20\'18starting to lose support\u8217\'20\'19 of international community over Gaza bombing, says Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 It is 1.20pm in Washington DC. Here is a round-up of what\u8217\'20\'19s happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia election worker Shaye Moss took the stand in the defamation trial against \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , giving a haunting testimony of the ways the former New York City mayor\u8217\'20\'19s lies and the ensuing harassment ruined her life and affected her family.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moss told the court she was a \u8220\'20\'1Cbubbly, outgoing, happy Shaye\u8221\'20\'1D before she first became aware of lies Giuliani was spreading about her \u8211\'20\'13 and that threats left her feeling scared for her life. She recalled how she started receiving racist text messages and threats. \u8220\'20\'1CI was afraid for my life. I literally felt like someone was going to come and attempt to hang me and there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing anyone can do about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moss also told the court how her life has been ruined and she often still feels like she is being followed. She doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go out alone and has panic attacks. She had to leave her job because she says she became a \u8220\'20\'1Cpariah\u8221\'20\'1D in the office. Moss told the court her ordeal has left her feeling \u8220\'20\'1Cin a dark place\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s mental fitness was questioned by the judge after he again told lies about Moss and Ruby Freeman in response to media questions after court last night. His comments entered into the court case Tuesday when Moss brought up how he had never apologized and continued to lie about her.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moss will be back on the stand at 2pm in Washington for cross-examination from Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s attorney.\par \par \uc2 Beyond the trial, other big stories today \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Texas supreme court overturned a lower court order that would have allowed Kate Cox to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a fetus with a fatal condition. Cox went out of state for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Claudine Gay will remain the president of \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  despite calls for her removal following testimony before a congressional hearing about antisemitism on campus last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Election worker testifies Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 lies ruined her life\par \par \uc2 Shaye Moss just ended approximately two hours of haunting testimony detailing how her life has been ruined ever since \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  spread lies about her after the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Her worst fear, she said, is that her teenage son will come home to find her and her mother hanging from a tree in front of their home. She still pulls over in her neighborhood because she feels like someone is following them. She doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go out alone. She has panic attacks. She left the job that she worked hard to get because she had become a \u8220\'20\'1Cpariah\u8221\'20\'1D in the office. When her son started getting harassing messages and failed all of his classes in the 9th grade, she felt responsible and like \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst mom in the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like I\u8217\'20\'19m in a dark place and the only thing that surrounds me are the conspiracy and the lies,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She ended her direct testimony by talking about how she\u8217\'20\'19s trapped in a cycle of eating, sleeping, and crying. \u8220\'20\'1CSadly that\u8217\'20\'19s my life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer will cross-examine her when court resumes this afternoon at 2pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Though Giuliani has already been found liable for defaming Moss and Freeman, his comments last night to the media where he claimed his lies about them were true will likely factor into the trial.\par \par \uc2 Already, the US district judge \uc2 Beryl Howell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/rudy-giuliani-election-workers-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked about Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s mental fitness}}}\uc2 , given his comments: \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything I said about them is true.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And on the stand this afternoon, Moss brought up his remarks, saying he was still \u8220\'20\'1Cspreading lies about us last night\u8221\'20\'1D. Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Kyle Cheney wrote on X that the judge is permitting Moss to talk about these comments, despite an objection from Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer.\par \par \uc2 enltrLooks like Moss' side won the argument. Howell permits her to discuss Rudy's comments from yesterday: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JoRXz8XNdS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JoRXz8XNdS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1734629236051235146?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Giuliani defamation trial is one of the first tests of the many prongs pro-democracy groups are using in the courts to try to hold purveyors of election lies accountable.\par \par \uc2 Several lawsuits {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/18/election-2020-defamation-lawsuit-giuliani-lindell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 use anti-defamation laws}}}\uc2  in civil lawsuits against big names who joined with Trump to deny the results of the 2020 election, including Giuliani, Mike Lindell and Dinesh D\u8217\'20\'19Souza.\par \par \uc2 Separately, other groups are working to keep Trump off the ballot for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/04/can-trump-be-removed-ballot-insurrection-clause-colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violating the 14th amendment}}}\uc2  by engaging in insurrection. Attempts in several states have so far failed to remove the former president from the running, though the lawsuits are still ongoing. The 14th amendment is one of several Reconstruction-era laws to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/nov/26/us-election-trump-reconstructiopn-era-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 come back into the courtroom}}}\uc2  in recent years to confront Trump and his allies.\par \par \uc2 In another avenue for accountability, the parties defending against frivolous election lawsuits are increasingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/10/attorneys-fees-sanctions-lawsuits-election-fraud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking monetary sanctions}}}\uc2  from plaintiffs who make broad claims without the facts to back them up. The courts are now granting these sanctions at times as a clear message that lawsuits need a factual basis.\par \par \uc2 At the state level, multiple states have charged or are investigating the fake electors scheme, resulting in criminal charges now in Georgia, Nevada and Michigan. Fake electors in Wisconsin settled a civil lawsuit recently.\par \par \uc2 And most prominent of the legal routes to hold election deniers accountable: the criminal charges Trump faces for his role in election subversion.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Moss tells court: 'I was afraid for my life'\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine has just left the courtroom where Shaye Moss, a former Atlanta election worker, laid out strikingly emotional testimony about how \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lies upended her life after the 2020 election. He sends this dispatch.\par \par \uc2 Moss, dressed in a black blazer, green blouse and long sparkling white acrylic nails, came to tears on several occasions as she testified and at times her voice was barely audible. Her hand shook as she was sworn on the witness stand.\par \par \uc2 She recalled 4 December 2020, the day that she first became aware of the lies Giuliani was spreading about her. When her boss in Fulton county\u8217\'20\'19s election office first asked to speak with her, she thought she was being promoted. But when she went into his office, she realized she was the only one smiling. It was then that she saw the lies Giuliani was spreading about her for the first time.\par \par \uc2 4 December was the \u8220\'20\'1Clast day I was this bubbly, outgoing, happy Shaye. The day everything in life changed. The day I changed. The day everything I turned upside down,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She recalled how she started receiving racist text messages and threats. \u8220\'20\'1CI was afraid for my life. I literally felt like someone was going to come and attempt to hang me and there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing anyone can do about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And she detailed the shame she felt as she got moved off handling absentee ballots. \u8220\'20\'1CI felt like a pariah in the office,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some background on Shaye Moss, who testified before the January 6 committee last year, offering wrenching details about how Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s lies upended their lives.\par \par \uc2 In powerful and emotional testimony about the sinister results of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn the 2020 election, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-election-threats-georgia-exclusiv-idCAKBN2IP0VZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mother and daughter}}}\uc2  who were Georgia elections workers described how Trump and his allies upended their lives, fueling harassment and racist threats by claiming they were involved in voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 Read more: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/21/giuliani-no-evidence-voter-fraud-arizona-jan-6-commitee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Giuliani told Arizona official \u8216\'20\'18We just don\u8217\'20\'19t have the evidence\u8217\'20\'19 of voter fraud}}}\par \par \uc2 Testifying to the January 6 committee in Washington, Shaye Moss said she received \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot of threats. Wishing death upon me. Telling me that I\u8217\'20\'19ll be in jail with my mother and saying things like, \u8216\'20\'18Be glad it\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 and not 1920.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That was a reference to lynching, the violent extra-judicial fate of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/15/lynchings-report-reconstruction-era-black-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thousands of Black men}}}\uc2  in the American south.\par \par \uc2 Moss also said her grandmother\u8217\'20\'19s home had been threatened by Trump supporters seeking to make \u8220\'20\'1Ccitizen\u8217\'20\'19s arrests\u8221\'20\'1D of the two poll workers.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/21/january-6-hearings-georgia-elections-workers-mother-daughter-testify"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18There\u8217\'20\'19s nowhere I feel safe\u8217\'20\'19: Georgia election workers on how Trump upended their lives}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Per Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Kyle Cheney who has helpfully transcribed some of Moss\u8217\'20\'19s testimony to the court, Moss recalls being brought into her boss\u8217\'20\'19s office on 4 December.\par \par \uc2 Moss recalled thinking wistfully that she might be given a recognition award for her work that cycle \u8211\'20\'13 or that she would finally get that new position she was seeking. Instead, she recalls, her hopes faded when the team opened a laptop and showed her all of the videos that were at the center of the fraud conspiracy Giuliani promoted.\par \par \uc2 enltrHere's how MOSS described the moment on Dec. 4, 2020 that she realized that she was the subject of a smear campaign about her work on the election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/faMQI9W6qG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/faMQI9W6qG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1734605268527522239?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 For the next little stretch, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be relying on reactions from court reporters who are in the court\u8217\'20\'19s media room and are able to tweet while watching a live stream of the proceedings. Our Sam Levine is inside the courtroom, where he cannot use his phone.\par \par \uc2 enltrQ: What does the date Dec. 4, 2020 mean to you\par \par \uc2 MOSS: "That was the day that everything changed, everything in my life changed. The day that I changed. Everything just flipped upside down."\par \par \uc2 "Crazy lies were spread about me and my mom."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1734604043446796688?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Shaye Moss takes the stand\par \par \uc2 Shaye Moss is now testifying about the onslaught of threats and harassment she faced as a result of Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s lies about her and her mother.\par \par \uc2 enltrMOSS Is on the stand. She appears nervous but smiles to the jury and introduces herself as a 39 year old mom and former election worker.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1734600827568804187?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMOSS now describing her joy when -- after 5 years as a temp -- she was hired as a permanent election worker in Fulton County.\par \par \uc2 "It was like winning a golden ticket in Willie Wonka," she said.\par \par \uc2 "I loved my job so much," she said, choking up.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1734601622016159792?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While we wait for news out of the federal court in Washington, here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest out of Texas:\par \par \uc2 Last night the Texas supreme court overturned a lower court order allowing a pregnant mother whose fetus was diagnosed with a fatal condition to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The decision was handed down hours after lawyers for the woman, Kate Cox, announced that she had left Texas to get the procedure as a result of the state\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Cox, the mother of two who is around 20 weeks pregnant, learned that her developing fetus has trisomy 18, a fatal diagnosis. She sought to terminate her pregnancy to protect her health and her ability to get pregnant again in the future.\par \par \uc2 The court said in its unsigned opinion that a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood faith belief\u8221\'20\'1D by Damla Karsan, a doctor who sought to perform the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sued alongside Cox, that the procedure was medically necessary was not enough to qualify for the state\u8217\'20\'19s exception.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/11/texas-supreme-court-overturns-ruling-kate-cox-emergency-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas court overturns ruling that would have let woman get emergency \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Moss set to testify against Giuliani\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a quick update from inside the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 Shaye Moss, one of the two election workers \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  defamed after the 2020, is set to testify shortly in the defamation trial against \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  about the horrific consequences she suffered after the former mayor told lies about her.\par \par \uc2 Her testimony is at the heart of the case for why plaintiffs believe Giuliani should pay up to $43m in damages. She will likely testify about the humiliation she faced as she sought a new job after the 2020 election and the anxiety and harassment she and her son suffered.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Our Sam Levine is in federal court covering Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s trial in Washington\par \par \uc2 The second day of a federal defamation trial in Washington is not off to a good start for \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 . The US district judge \uc2 Beryl Howell\uc2  needled him and his attorney after Giuliani told reporters outside the courthouse on Monday evening that he intended to prove statements he made about Ruby Freeman and Shaye Moss, two Atlanta election workers, were true.\par \par \uc2 Howell has already found Giuliani liable for defamation. The only issue in the trial is how much he should pay in damages. She asked whether he was just \u8220\'20\'1Cplaying for the cameras\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not sure. He\u8217\'20\'19s 80 years old. It\u8217\'20\'19s taken a toll on him. He\u8217\'20\'19s 80 years old, \u8221\'20\'1D Joseph Sibley, his attorney, said. Sibley told Howell he could not control what Giuliani does outside of court.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for Freeman and Moss are now playing a video deposition from Frank Paul Braun III, an investigator for the secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office, who investigated Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s allegations and proved they were untrue.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harvard board backs president amid calls for removal\par \par \uc2 Claudine Gay will remain the president of \uc2 Harvard University\uc2 , the school\u8217\'20\'19s governing board announced on Tuesday, amid calls for her removal following testimony before a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/harvard-mit-penn-campus-antisemitism-backlash-2c89312cdd0d2652a9b57ce71f1533fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 congressional hearing about antisemitism on campus}}}\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Harvard Corporation: \u8220\'20\'1CIn this tumultuous and difficult time, we unanimously stand in support of President Gay.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/stSvH4t1BP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/stSvH4t1BP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  (@Harvard) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Harvard/status/1734563802509676713?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Gay and the presidents of University of Pennsylvania and Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) faced an uproar for their academic responses to sharp questions about what could trigger disciplinary action under their universities\u8217\'20\'19 codes of conduct as part of a hearing earlier this month to address the rise of antisemitism on campus since the start of the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war.\par \par \uc2 The backlash was swift. Liz Magill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/09/university-of-pennsylvania-president-free-speech-antisemitism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  stepped down as president of the University of Pennsylvania}}}\uc2  over the weekend in response to calls for her removal. Upon news of Magill\u8217\'20\'19s resignation, Congresswoman \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , a far-right New York Republican who led the questioning, tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1COne down. Two to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , is in Washington DC to make a last-ditch appeal to congressional Republicans to approve additional aid to Ukraine as the Russian invasion grinds into a third year. During his visit he will meet with members of Congress and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prospects of passing the aforementioned aid, part of a package that includes assistance to Israel as well as other national security asks, are dim \u8211\'20\'13 at least this week. Republicans are demanding steep concessions on border security and US immigration policy in exchange for sending more funds to Ukraine, which parts of their base has soured on. On Monday night, Senator \uc2 James Lankford\uc2 , a Republican from Oklahoma, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/senate-immigration-negotiations-unlikely-this-week-ukraine-israel-aid-rcna129122"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s no way to get it done this week\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  is back in federal court in Washington DC on Tuesday to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/rudy-giuliani-election-workers-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defend himself against a defamation lawsuit}}}\uc2  filed against him for false comments he made about two Georgia election workers after the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2023/dec/12/harvard-board-backs-president-antisemitism-row"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Harvard board backs president amid calls for removal over antisemitism testimony}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231212ejcc00232\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
