\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Stunning\u8217\'20\'19 threat in Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  case steps up Paxton criminalization crusade\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 956 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2023\par 17:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 State attorney general threatened to prosecute doctors if they provided \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care to a woman with a nonviable pregnancy\par \par \uc2 When a Texas court ruled that a 31-year-old woman with a non-viable pregnancy could have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the state\u8217\'20\'19s strict bans, the Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , responded with a brazen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/08/ken-paxton-texas-abortion-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threat to prosecute}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chospitals, doctors, or anyone else\u8221\'20\'1D who would assist in providing the procedure. The letter he sent Texas hospitals hours after the ruling, threatening {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/news/releases/attorney-general-ken-paxton-responds-travis-county-tro"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first-degree felonies}}}\uc2  that could result in life in prison, was a \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning\u8221\'20\'1D move indicative of his longstanding crusade to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, say legal experts and advocates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is extraordinary that Paxton would threaten hospitals and doctors with this letter before even winning an appeal,\u8221\'20\'1D Mary Ziegler, a \uc2 UC-Davis\uc2  law professor who focuses on reproductive rights, told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a very unusual maneuver, but does certainly reflect his ultimate goal of wanting to go after \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and supporters at all costs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After Paxton sent his menacing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TXAG/status/1732849903154450622"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter to Texas hospitals}}}\uc2 , the state petitioned the all-Republican Texas supreme court to block the ruling allowing Kate Cox to access an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas. On Friday, the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/09/texas-supreme-court-temporarily-blocks-woman-from-abortion-for-non-viable-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily halted}}}\uc2  the lower court order that had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/07/texas-judge-abortion-ruling-non-viable-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed}}}\uc2  Cox to receive emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, before ruling on Monday to vacate the order that would have permitted her to get care in her home state.\par \par \uc2 With a risky pregnancy that threatened her health, Cox waited nearly three days for the Court to issue a final order. On Monday, hours before the final order from the court, she finally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/11/texas-abortion-kate-cox-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fled out-of-state}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care at 20 weeks pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Cox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorneys called Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s strategy a \u8220\'20\'1Cfearmongering\u8221\'20\'1D tactic and an effort to \u8220\'20\'1Cbulldoze the legal system\u8221\'20\'1D to ensure Cox continued to suffer.\par \par \uc2 Her case underscores the aggressive nature of the state\u8217\'20\'19s top attorney when it comes to not only enforcing a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even in dire circumstances, but creating a climate of fear around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that targets providers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  was trying to say who the judge\u8217\'20\'19s emergency order protected or didn\u8217\'20\'19t protect \u8211\'20\'13 but he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t actually have the authority to do that,\u8221\'20\'1D said Joanna Grossman, professor at the Southern Methodist University Dedman School of Law in Dallas. \u8220\'20\'1CHis behavior here is a continuation of what he\u8217\'20\'19s been doing for the past three years and beyond \u8211\'20\'13 and that is enforcement through fear. His MO is to make threats, be a bully, and scare people and providers out of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The actual legal rules aren\u8217\'20\'19t as important to him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Backed by the state\u8217\'20\'19s major anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, Paxton has cemented himself as a staunch anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocate since his tenure as a Texas house and senate representative, and even more so as attorney general starting in 2015, from which position he has zealously litigated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.austinchronicle.com/news/2020-01-10/ken-paxton-urges-u-s-supreme-court-to-overturn-historic-whole-womans-ruling/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/news/releases/ag-paxton-celebrates-end-roe-v-wade-announces-abortion-now-illegal-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 openly celebrated}}}\uc2  the fall of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/news/releases/paxton-defends-sb8-saving-thousands-lives-process"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support and defense}}}\uc2  of 2021\u8217\'20\'19s Senate Bill 8 \u8211\'20\'13 a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that empowers private citizens to sue those who \u8220\'20\'1Caid or abet\u8221\'20\'1D care \u8211\'20\'13 helped create a chilling effect among \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, who stopped providing care months before the Dobbs decision that overturned Roe, out of fear of threats to their livelihoods. The attorney general has also successfully {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/sites/default/files/images/executive-management/20220714_1-0_Original%20Complaint%20Biden%20Admin.pdf?utm_content=&utm_medium=email&utm_name=&utm_source=govdelivery&utm_term="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  sued the Biden administration}}}\uc2  to fight against protections for Texas physicians who perform abortions in emergency circumstances.\par \par \uc2 And his office is currently battling a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/28/texas-supreme-court-hears-extreme-abortion-ban-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal challenge}}}\uc2  that seeks to clarify the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/13/texas-abortion-ban-maternal-health-risk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medical exceptions}}}\uc2  in Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law for doctors who say that the law is so vague that their hands are tied even in major emergencies. Filed by 20 women who have faced often severe pregnancy complications \u8211\'20\'13 including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/20/texas-women-pregnancy-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near-death circumstances}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as a result of being denied emergency abortions, the case is now before the Texas supreme court, which granted Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s recent appeal.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, shortly after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reversal of Roe v Wade and a month before a law banning abortions in almost all circumstances was slated to take effect in Texas, Paxton began to sharpen his aim at providers by issuing an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/sites/default/files/images/executive-management/Post-Roe%20Advisory%20(updated%20draft%2006.21.2022)%20(1).pdf?utm_content=&utm_medium=email&utm_name=&utm_source=govdelivery&utm_term="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advisory}}}\uc2  encouraging \u8211\'20\'13 and vowing assistance to \u8211\'20\'13 local prosecutors who pursue criminal charges against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors with a potential prison sentence of up to five years, writing that providers could be immediately held \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminally liable\u8221\'20\'1D, under an antiquated Texas statute.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a shot across the bow to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors and supporters,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Blake Rocap\uc2 , director of the Sissy Farenthold Reproductive Justice Defense Project at the Rapoport Center for Human Rights and Justice at the UT-School of Law. \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s been a foot soldier in the march to criminalizing care. That\u8217\'20\'19s been the aim all along for him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr Ghazaleh Moayedi can speak directly to experiencing fear of prosecution by Paxton. Along with a number of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/texas-abortion-funds-resume-service-legal-reprieve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed suit}}}\uc2  against Paxton last year to obtain legal protections after the attorney general indicated he could prosecute people who help Texans access abortions out of state. At the time, Moayedi, who had been traveling to states like Kansas to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care after Texas\u8217\'20\'19s law took effect, stopped seeing patients from Texas, because she was frightened by the threat of possible jail time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe state has been coordinating these efforts against us for a long time,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in reference to \uc2 Cox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s case. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is exhausting to be constantly vigilant, especially when I know I\u8217\'20\'19m a good doctor. The case reminds us that we could still be put in the crosshairs. It continues to worry me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231212ejcc002bj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
