\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Woman who sued Texas for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  left state to have procedure after \u8216\'20\'18hellish\u8217\'20\'19 week\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 809 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2023\par 14:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Center for the Reproductive Rights, which is representing Kate Cox, says she left after being \u8216\'20\'18in and out of the emergency room\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Texas woman who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/05/texas-woman-emergency-abortion-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued the state}}}\uc2  for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after receiving a lethal fetal diagnosis has now fled Texas in order to obtain the procedure, the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/reprorights/status/1734286514937381314?s=46&t=HbWdTXkVm84FFtl6RuE-cA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  in a statement Monday.\par \par \uc2 The woman, Kate Cox, a 31-year-old mother of two from Dallas, sued Texas last week. While a lower-court judge ruled to allow Cox to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Texas state supreme court on Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/09/texas-supreme-court-temporarily-blocks-woman-from-abortion-for-non-viable-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paused that ruling}}}\uc2 . In her lawsuit, Cox said that continuing the pregnancy could threaten her life and future fertility.\par \par \uc2 Texas bans almost all abortions. Although the ban technically includes exceptions for cases of medical emergencies, doctors have said that the exceptions are too vague and force them to wait until their patients get sick enough to intervene.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis past week of legal limbo has been hellish for Kate. Her health is on the line,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , president of the Center for the Reproductive Rights, which is representing Cox. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s been in and out of the emergency room and she couldn\u8217\'20\'19t wait any longer. This is why judges and politicians should not be making healthcare decisions for pregnant people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cox\uc2  is believed to be the first adult woman to sue for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  while still pregnant since Roe v Wade was overturned last year.\par \par \uc2 Her case is separate from an ongoing lawsuit, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/28/texas-supreme-court-hears-extreme-abortion-ban-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brought by 20 Texan women and two doctors}}}\uc2 , who have accused the state of denying abortions while they were in medical emergencies. That case, which is also before the Republican-stacked Texas state supreme court, is seeking to clarify the medical exceptions in the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKate desperately wanted to be able to get care where she lives and recover at home surrounded by family,\u8221\'20\'1D Northup continued in a statement, which was posted to X. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile Kate had the ability to leave the state, most people do not, and a situation like this could be a death sentence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When Cox first learned she was pregnant in August 2023, she was thrilled, since she and her husband had been hoping for a third child, according to \uc2 Cox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit. But in October, she learned that her pregnancy was at high risk for trisomy 18, a condition that would likely lead Cox to miscarry or give birth to a baby who may only live for a few days at most.\par \par \uc2 Over several weeks of testing, the prognosis for \uc2 Cox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pregnancy grew worse. Cox also went to the emergency room on at least three separate occasions, dealing with severe cramping and what the lawsuit called \u8220\'20\'1Cunidentifiable fluid leaks\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Cox\uc2  is also at high risk of gestational diabetes, post-operative infections and anesthesia complications, among other health conditions, the lawsuit said.\par \par \uc2 On 28 November, the same day that the Texas supreme court heard arguments in the broader case over the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Cox\u8217\'20\'19s doctors confirmed that her fetus had trisomy 18, according to the lawsuit. After talking to her husband and family, Cox decided to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the time of her lawsuit, Cox was 20 weeks into her pregnancy. Dr Damla Karsan, an OB-GYN in Houston and one of the doctors involved in the broader lawsuit over the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, said in court records that she might be able to perform Cox\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if permitted by the court.\par \par \uc2 However, after the lower-court order in Cox\u8217\'20\'19s favor, the Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/08/ken-paxton-texas-abortion-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened legal action against doctors}}}\uc2  who performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Cox.\par \par \uc2 That order, Paxton wrote in a letter to three Houston-area hospitals, \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not insulate you, or anyone else, from civil and criminal liability for violating Texas\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws\u8221\'20\'1D. Texas has a law on the books that permits private individuals to sue over suspected illegal abortions. Regardless of the court order, doctors could be held liable under that law, Paxton warned.\par \par \uc2 When she filed her lawsuit, Cox said in a statement that she was \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying to do what is best for my baby and myself, but the state of Texas is making us both suffer\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not a matter of if I will have to say goodbye to my baby, but when,\u8221\'20\'1D Cox said. \u8220\'20\'1CI do not want to continue the pain and suffering that has plagued this pregnancy. I do not want to put my body through the risks of continuing this pregnancy. I do not want my baby to arrive in this world only to watch her suffer. I need to end my pregnancy now so that I have the best chance for my health and a future pregnancy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231211ejcb00336\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
