\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Arizona supreme court to hear case on state\u8217\'20\'19s 1864  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,551 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2023\par 11:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 After months of disarray over the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the state supreme court will decide whether to reinstate \u8216\'20\'18zombie\u8217\'20\'19 ban. Plus, seven ways to make your holidays a little greener\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The Arizona state supreme court will today hear arguments in a case over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/12/arizona-abortion-ban-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whether to reinstate an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban that originated in 1864}}}\uc2 , before Arizona even became a state. The ban blocks people from helping to \u8220\'20\'1Cprocure the miscarriage\u8221\'20\'1D of a pregnant woman and allows abortions only to save her life. There are no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Other states, such as Texas and Wisconsin, have tried to revive pre-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, often referred to as \u8220\'20\'1Czombie bans\u8221\'20\'1D. But Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s ban has been mired in more legal uncertainty than those in most other states. In addition to a host of other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations, Arizona had on the books the 1864 ban \u8211\'20\'13 which was initiated under Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s pre-state territorial government, then updated and codified in 1901 \u8211\'20\'13 as well as a ban on the procedure past 15 weeks, which was signed into law in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Barbara Atwood, the director of the Family and Juvenile Law Certificate Program at the University of Arizona James E Rogers College of Law, said Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s revival of a law that has gone unenforced for half a century would be \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a huge regulatory structure that\u8217\'20\'19s been enacted in the last 50 years post-Roe v Wade, where the Arizona legislature has very deliberately created lots of restrictions on the availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Atwood said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the old ban is brought back into effect, how it meshes with this other regulatory structure is very, very confusing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Texas? The Texas supreme court yesterday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/11/texas-supreme-court-overturns-ruling-kate-cox-emergency-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling}}}\uc2  that would have allowed a pregnant woman to get an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the medical exception for the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, granting a petition by the Republican attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 . The ruling came hours after lawyers for the woman, Kate Cox, said in a court filing that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/11/texas-abortion-kate-cox-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she had left the state}}}\uc2  to obtain the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but nonetheless wanted to pursue the case.\par \par \uc2 Israel says operation against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  could last months as heavy fighting reported across Gaza\par \par \uc2 Heavy fighting was reported across Gaza late into the evening last night, as Israel\u8217\'20\'19s defence minister pushed back against international calls to wrap up the country\u8217\'20\'19s military offensive in the territory, saying the current phase of the operation against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  would \u8220\'20\'1Ctake time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Yoav Gallant told the Associated Press the current phase of the conflict, characterised by heavy ground fighting backed up by air power, could stretch on for weeks and that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/dec/12/israel-gaza-war-live-updates-news-gaza-attack-palestine-un-ceasefire-vote-hostages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 further military activity could continue for months}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gallant said the next phase would be lower-intensity fighting against \u8220\'20\'1Cpockets of resistance\u8221\'20\'1D and would require Israeli troops to maintain their freedom of operation.\par \par \uc2 Gallant spoke as Israeli forces battled militants in and around the southern city of Khan Younis, where the military opened a new line of attack last week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? The \uc2 UN\uc2  general assembly is due to vote today on a non-binding resolution demanding \u8220\'20\'1Can immediate humanitarian ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 a call that the paralysed security council has so far failed to make.\par \par \uc2 Talks extend beyond official end of climate summit after draft text proves \u8216\'20\'18grossly insufficient\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A draft deal to cut global fossil fuel production is \u8220\'20\'1Cgrossly insufficient\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cincoherent\u8221\'20\'1D and will not stop the world from facing dangerous climate breakdown, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/live/2023/dec/12/cop-28-live-latest-updates-climate-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to delegates at the UN\u8217\'20\'19s Cop28 summit}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The heads of delegation met until the early hours, mostly expressing their deep unhappiness with the draft text produced by the summit presidency late yesterday afternoon. The scheduled end of the two-week conference has come and gone and as yet there is no new text to replace the document.\par \par \uc2 Many countries speaking at a session overnight argued the section lacked the urgency and ambition needed to deliver on what the Cop president, Sultan Al Jaber, called his \u8220\'20\'1Cnorth star\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 keeping 1.5C of heating within reach. For example, the mention of the consumption and production of fossil fuels says they could be reduced \u8220\'20\'1Cin a just, orderly and equitable manner so as to achieve net zero by, before, or around 2050 in keeping with the science\u8221\'20\'1D. This suggests that fossil fuels could still be used after 2050, justified by an unlimited amount of problematic offsets \u8211\'20\'13 which definitely isn\u8217\'20\'19t what the science demands.\par \par \uc2 With little sign of agreement on the final scheduled day of Cop28, the pressure is intense on Al Jaber to bring the 198 countries to an ambitious final deal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What does the text say about fossil fuels? The draft text calls for \u8220\'20\'1Creducing both consumption and production of fossil fuels, in a just, orderly and equitable manner, so as to achieve net zero by, before or around 2050, in keeping with the science\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Special counsel prosecutors indicated yesterday they will call three expert witnesses at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trial over his efforts to overturn the 2020 election who could show how January 6 rioters moved on the Capitol {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/11/donald-trump-2020-election-trial-tweets-phone-data"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in response to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s tweets}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moscow will \u8220\'20\'1Cvery attentively\u8221\'20\'1D watch a meeting between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Volodymyr Zelenskiy planned for today, the Kremlin said. Meanwhile, the whereabouts of \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 , the jailed Russian opposition leader, inside the prison system {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/dec/12/russia-ukraine-war-live-zelenskiy-to-meet-biden-in-push-for-aid#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remains unknown}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Myanmar became the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest producer of opium in 2023, overtaking Afghanistan after the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  government\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on the trade, according to a United Nations report. Myanmar produced an estimated 1,080 metric tonnes of opium \u8211\'20\'13 essential for producing heroin \u8211\'20\'13 this year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The branded coffee chain craze may trace its roots to a single \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in Seattle\u8217\'20\'19s Pike Place market in 1971, but\par \par \uc2 China has toppled the US as the country with the most branded coffee shops. The number of branded coffee shops in China {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/dec/12/china-us-branded-coffee-shop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased by 58% over the past 12 months}}}\uc2  to a record 49,691 outlets.\par \par \uc2 Help us raise $1.5m to fund independent journalism in 2024\par \par \uc2 As we head into 2024, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s journalists are already hard at work preparing for one of the most consequential news cycles of our lifetimes. We need your support to raise $1.5m to fund our reporting on areas such as the 2024 election and the potential for another Trump presidency; war in the Middle East; the sweeping implications of artificial intelligence; the climate crisis; and investigations into high-stakes abuses of power. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.theguardian.com/us/contribute?utm_source=eml&CMP_BUNIT=edtrl&INTCMP=USEOY23_newsletters_firstthingusincopy_acq_email_phase1_US&acquisitionData=%7B%22source%22%3A%22EMAIL%22%2C%22componentType%22%3A%22ACQUISITIONS_EMAIL%22%2C%22componentId%22%3A%22USEOY23_newsletters_firstthingusincopy_acq_email_phase1_US%22%2C%22campaignCode%22%3A%22USEOY23_newsletters_firstthingusincopy_acq_email_phase1_US%22%7D&utm_content=Editorial_CNUSEOY23FirstThingUSInCopyAcq&utm_campaign=%7B%7Bcampaign_id%7D%7D&utm_medium=emedt&utm_term=%7B%7Bcampaign.%24%7Bdispatch_id%7D%7D%7D&CMP_TU=mawns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If you value our reporting, please make a year-end gift today}}}\uc2 . We\u8217\'20\'19re depending on you.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: More than 160 representatives with climate-denying track records got Cop28 access\par \par \uc2 Influential industry trade groups, thinktanks and public relations agencies with a track record in climate denialism and misleading the public have been given access to the \uc2 UN\uc2  climate talks in Dubai, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  can reveal. Corporate Accountability, a transparency watchdog, has found that \uc2 UN\uc2  organizers gave these groups the same or greater access to the international negotiations as Indigenous communities, human rights groups and climate justice organizations. The new data, derived from official \uc2 UN\uc2  delegate lists, found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/dec/11/climate-deniers-attend-cop28-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 166 climate deniers and fossil fuel public relations professionals are at Cop28}}}\uc2 . The true number is probably significantly higher.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: \u8216\'20\'18I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t believe this act of kindness\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 how Black women trying to get pregnant create their own healthcare networks\par \par \uc2 For many Black women in the US, infertility has a complicated duality. The inability to conceive is often invisible, pushed out of view by shame, the racist notion that Black women are hyper-fertile, or the idea that such struggles should remain private. Yet for people aspiring to parenthood amid fertility problems, getting the family they want often requires complete transparency about their condition.\par \par \uc2 Faced with so many barriers, Black women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/11/black-women-infertility-mutual-aid-healthcare-networks-medication-sharing-egg-sperm-donations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 often turn to mutual aid}}}\uc2  to navigate the medical system and infertility\u8217\'20\'19s emotional, financial and bodily tolls. The sharing of resources: information, medications, money and even donated biological material such as sperm, eggs and embryos is a key component of these groups.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: seven ways to make your holidays a little greener\par \par \uc2 During the holidays, it can be challenging to reconcile indulgence and tradition with environmental responsibility. Seven eco-experts explain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/wellness/2023/dec/11/eco-friendly-holiday-gifting-guide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 how they are planning to celebrate their holidays sustainably}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThinking about how much plastic packaging piles up around the holidays stresses me out \u8211\'20\'13 ditto how many toys are bought, only to go unused,\u8221\'20\'1D writes Jeff Wint, plastics reduction program manager at the Ocean Wise Conservation Institute. \u8220\'20\'1CPlastic toys aren\u8217\'20\'19t recyclable, so buying them second hand also saves them from landfill and extends their life. There\u8217\'20\'19s this idea that everything has to be brand new to be the best, but honestly, I find that if another kid already loved a toy, chances are good that mine will love it, too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231212ejcc001jo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
