\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Arizona court weighs 1864  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban that risks \u8216\'20\'18conditions of misery\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,212 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2023\par 10:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 After months of disarray over the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the state supreme court will decide whether to reinstate \u8216\'20\'18zombie\u8217\'20\'19 ban\par \par \uc2 Dr Gabrielle Goodrick can barely bring herself to talk about the weeks when Arizona banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the months after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  flickered in and out of legality in Arizona as state courts attempted to interpret a long-dormant 19th-century \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that was suddenly relevant again. Goodrick, a longtime \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in Phoenix, was forced to cancel patients\u8217\'20\'19 appointments, then desperately try to reschedule them during the brief period of time when the procedure became legal again. Patients sometimes showed up at the clinic for their appointment, were turned away, and sobbed outside the clinic. Stressed-out staffers quit, but given all the uncertainty, Goodrick couldn\u8217\'20\'19t hire new ones. She had to keep going with too few employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt destroyed clinics. It\u8217\'20\'19s very hard to function when you don\u8217\'20\'19t know what\u8217\'20\'19s gonna happen,\u8221\'20\'1D Goodrick said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea of that happening and losing the staff I have and not being able to see the patients that need us \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s just \u8211\'20\'13 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know, really. I really can\u8217\'20\'19t go there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Arizona state supreme court will hear arguments in a case over whether to reinstate an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that originated in 1864, before Arizona even became a state. The ban blocks people from helping to \u8220\'20\'1Cprocure the miscarriage\u8221\'20\'1D of a pregnant woman and only allows abortions to save her life. There are no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Other states, like Texas and Wisconsin, have recently tried to revive pre-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, often referred to as \u8220\'20\'1Czombie bans\u8221\'20\'1D. But Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s ban has been mired in more legal uncertainty than most other states\u8217\'20\'19. In addition to host of other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations, Arizona had on the books both the 1864 ban \u8211\'20\'13 which was initiated under Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s pre-state territorial government, then updated and codified in 1901 \u8211\'20\'13 as well as a ban on the procedure past 15 weeks, which was signed into law in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Barbara Atwood, the director of the Family and Juvenile Law Certificate Program at the University of Arizona James E Rogers College of Law, said that Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s revival of a law that has gone unenforced for half a century would be \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a huge regulatory structure that\u8217\'20\'19s been enacted in the last 50 years post-Roe v Wade, where the Arizona legislature has very deliberately created lots of restrictions on the availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Atwood said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the old ban is brought back into effect, how it meshes with this other regulatory structure is very, very confusing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After Roe was overturned, no one seemed to know for sure if the 1864 ban was in effect \u8211\'20\'13 not even Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s then governor, who said that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azmirror.com/2022/11/30/judges-mull-whether-arizonas-1864-abortion-ban-can-co-exist-with-50-years-of-laws-regulating-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15-week ban superseded}}}\uc2  the 1864 ban, or its former attorney general, who threw his weight behind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azmirror.com/2023/08/23/the-arizona-supreme-court-will-consider-reviving-a-civil-war-era-abortion-ban/#:~:text=The%201864%20law%20that%20former,to%205%2Dyear%20prison%20sentence."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 1864 ban}}}\uc2 . Those officials, both Republican men, have since been replaced by Democratic women.\par \par \uc2 Dr DeShawn Taylor, who runs an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Phoenix, Arizona, said her staffers were terrified and confused. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a Black woman,\u8221\'20\'1D she told them. \u8220\'20\'1CDo you think I want to go to jail? I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t put myself at risk. I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to put you at risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Out of an abundance of caution, most of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers stopped performing the procedure right after Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturning. Taylor was so unsure of what \u8220\'20\'1Cprocure\u8221\'20\'1D meant that she started giving patients their medical records outright, rather than referring them herself to another \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider out of state, because she feared that doing so could accidentally violate the ban.\par \par \uc2 To have people be forced to continue pregnancies and bear children without the resources to help \u8211\'20\'13 I just think we\u8217\'20\'19re creating conditions of misery\par \par \uc2 Dr DeShawn Taylor\par \par \uc2 Amid the confusion, some Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers resumed work in July 2022. But in September, a court reinstated the 1864 ban. For about two weeks, until a state appeals court order halted the ban, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers were once again unable to offer the procedure.\par \par \uc2 What is clear is that abortions are currently outlawed past 15 weeks in Arizona. A near-total ban, Taylor said, would push pregnant people in the state to a breaking point.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have an exploding homeless and drug-using population here,\u8221\'20\'1D Taylor said. She added that she was starting to see people terminate pregnancies they would otherwise keep out of fear of something going wrong later in pregnancy when an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be legal. \u8220\'20\'1CTo have people be forced to continue pregnancies and bear children without the resources to help \u8211\'20\'13 I just think we\u8217\'20\'19re creating conditions of misery.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The consequences of a near-total ban in Arizona could also reverberate across the south-west. While most of Goodrick\u8217\'20\'19s patients are from Arizona, she estimates that about 10 to 20 Texans come to her clinic each month for abortions.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , a party in the lawsuit over the 1864 ban, has argued that the pre-statehood ban clashes with Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations and that the courts need to \u8220\'20\'1Charmonize\u8221\'20\'1D the state\u8217\'20\'19s laws around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider already scored a surprising win in the case in late November.\par \par \uc2 One of the justices who was originally set to rule on the 1864 ban, Bill Montgomery, said in a 2017 \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post that \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cis responsible for the greatest genocide known to man\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.phoenixnewtimes.com/news/supreme-court-justice-montgomery-planned-parenthood-abortion-arizona-11360365"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Phoenix New Times reported in 2019}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eastvalleytribune.com/arizona/politics/article_a713abda-d682-11e1-acb1-0019bb2963f4.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Montgomery has also said}}}\uc2  that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should only be allowed when a pregnancy threatens someone\u8217\'20\'19s health or life and that the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.catholicsun.org/2015/08/26/planned-parenthood-protests-draw-4700-throughout-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unborn are entitled}}}\uc2  to the same degree of protection as anyone else\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Montgomery initially declined to recuse himself from the case. The statements were made before he became a member of the state supreme court, he said in court papers. However, days later, he changed his mind.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAdditional information related to the parties and respective counsel has come to my attention warranting that I recuse myself from any further deliberations in this matter,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote in court papers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a significant victory for our friends at \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , and for anyone in the state who is providing care in the state and all the patients that need to access care, to not have a biased judge on the court hearing them on 12 December,\u8221\'20\'1D said Caroline Mello Roberson, director of state campaigns for \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2  is part of a coalition that is now at work amassing signatures for a 2024 ballot measure that would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s state constitution. It will need to turn in more than 400,000 signatures to the state government by summer 2024, and the outcome of the court case could turbocharge that fight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would definitely push us over the edge. My motto would be just burn it all down,\u8221\'20\'1D Goodrick said. \u8220\'20\'1CI really, truly believe that the people of Arizona do not want a total ban. We\u8217\'20\'19re not going to go back to 1864, where women were property.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231212ejcc001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
