\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas attorney general says he will sue doctor who gives  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  to Kate Cox\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 718 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par 04:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  issues threat after judge ruled this week that Cox, a pregnant woman with a lethal fetal diagnosis, can get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , has threatened to prosecute any doctor who provides an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Kate Cox, a woman with a non-viable pregnancy, advising hospitals to ignore a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/07/texas-judge-abortion-ruling-non-viable-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court order issued on Thursday}}}\uc2  allowing her to get the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The rightwing Paxton issued the warning to three Houston-area hospitals after a Texas judge ruled this week that Cox, a pregnant woman with a lethal fetal diagnosis, may obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the narrow medical exceptions offered by the state bans.\par \par \uc2 In a brazen dismissal of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, Paxton {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TXAG/status/1732849903154450622/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  that the judge\u8217\'20\'19s order \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not insulate hospitals, doctors or anyone else from civil and criminal liability\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Paxton also wrote that the hospital where \uc2 Cox\uc2  obtains an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmay be liable for negligent credentialing the physician\u8221\'20\'1D who performs the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/07/texas-judge-abortion-ruling-non-viable-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  on behalf of Cox after she learned last week that her fetus has trisomy 18, a fatal chromosomal condition, as well as other health issues, including a spinal abnormality. Continuing the pregnancy could threaten \uc2 Cox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s life and future fertility. The 31-year-old mother of two has already rushed to the emergency room four times with severe cramping and fluid loss, but doctors have told her that their hands are tied by the state laws.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Travis county judge, Maya Guerra Gamble, issued a temporary restraining order to permit Cox\u8217\'20\'19s doctor to perform the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that Ms Cox wants desperately to be a parent and this law might actually cause her to lose that ability is shocking and would be a genuine miscarriage of justice,\u8221\'20\'1D the judge said, following an emergency hearing on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday night, the state appealed the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, in a motion asking the Texas supreme court to immediately block Gamble\u8217\'20\'19s order.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court on Friday night put Gamble\u8217\'20\'19s order on hold, saying it was temporarily staying Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout regard to the merits\u8221\'20\'1D. The case is still pending.\par \par \uc2 Molly Duane\uc2 , an attorney at the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , which is representing Cox, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we still hope that the court ultimately rejects the state\u8217\'20\'19s request and does so quickly, in this case we fear that justice delayed will be justice denied.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s letter to the hospitals involved in Cox\u8217\'20\'19s case, the attorney general wrote that Gamble was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot medically qualified to make this determination\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is trying to bulldoze the legal system to make sure Kate and pregnant women like her continue to suffer,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marc Hearron, the senior counsel at the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CFearmongering has been \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s main tactic in enforcing these \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Rather than respect the judiciary, he is misrepresenting the court\u8217\'20\'19s order.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s case marks the first time a pregnant person has asked a court for an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Roe v Wade was decided in 1973.\par \par \uc2 Paxton, a seasoned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent, faced off against the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2  just last month, in a case involving {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/28/texas-supreme-court-hears-extreme-abortion-ban-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 20 women}}}\uc2  who had been denied emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care despite suffering severe complications with their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement generally enjoyed broad {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/08/abortion-winning-issue-rights-victories-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 electoral}}}\uc2  victories in the aftermath of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade. Paxton, a particularly active champion of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, was re-elected to a third term as Texas\u8217\'20\'19s top prosecutor in November 2022.\par \par \uc2 Last month, the Department of Justice asked a US appeals court to allow the federal government to enforce a rule that instructs doctors to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when required in medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 Paxton has called the effort to re-establish federal rules on emergency medicine \u8220\'20\'1Cunconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the Biden administration continues to make up rules that are unconstitutional, I will keep holding them accountable,\u8221\'20\'1D Paxton said in a statement released earlier this year. \u8220\'20\'1CI will not allow the Biden administration to threaten doctors and hospitals with this unlawful mandate and put millions of Texans\u8217\'20\'19 access to healthcare on the line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231208ejc8002uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
