\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 His debate with \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  showed \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  will never be president\b0\par\par\uc2 Lloyd Green \par \uc2 997 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 December 2023\par 10:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The fight between two of America\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful governors, billed by Fox as \u8216\'20\'18The Great Red v Blue State Debate\u8217\'20\'19, mostly hurt DeSantis\par \par \uc2 On Thursday night, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the governor of Florida, reminded the US why he will never be president. His voice grates, his visage a cross between a squinted grimace and scowl. He looks like Manuel Noriega, the ex-Panamanian dictator, without the scarring. On a personal level, he lacks humor, warmth, wit or uplift. He is ham-handed, an awkward social warrior.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis comes across as too hot. This is the guy who picked a fight with Mickey Mouse, his state\u8217\'20\'19s largest employer. He holds degrees from Yale and Harvard, but repeatedly flashes clouded judgment. In other words, there are plenty of reasons why he is getting walloped among Republicans by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re down 41 points in your own home state,\u8221\'20\'1D California\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  happily reminded DeSantis during their televised debate, which Fox moderated.\par \par \uc2 And if you can\u8217\'20\'19t win your own state, you are going nowhere. Recall: Senator Elizabeth Warren lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020\u8217\'20\'19s Massachusetts primary and never regained her former stature.\par \par \uc2 The dust-up was organized and moderated by \uc2 Fox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , with \uc2 Fox\uc2  advertising the gubernatorial cage match \u8211\'20\'13 between the governors of two of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest states \u8211\'20\'13 as \u8220\'20\'1CDeSantis vs Newsom: The Great Red v Blue State Debate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Over 90-plus minutes, DeSantis attacked Newsom \u8211\'20\'13 whose Republican ex-wife Kimberly Guilfoyle is engaged to Don Jr \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/30/ron-desantis-gavin-newsom-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 without lasting impact}}}\uc2 . He ran through a litany of California\u8217\'20\'19s woes but couldn\u8217\'20\'19t make them stick. Then again, he carries a ton of baggage, from crime and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to January 6 and needless Covid-related deaths. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/15/ron-desantis-republican-presidential-campaign-covid-data-florida-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent court settlement}}}\uc2  over Florida\u8217\'20\'19s improper withholding of Covid records highlights the fact that DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s boasts were empty.\par \par \uc2 Florida is plagued by high murder and gun mortality \u8211\'20\'13 as Trump, DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s bitter rival, is fond of reminding Republican primary voters. DeSantis has dangled the prospect of pardoning January 6 defendants but claims to love the police.\par \par \uc2 By {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/pressroom/sosmap/homicide_mortality/homicide.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the numbers}}}\uc2 , Florida\u8217\'20\'19s homicide rate tops California\u8217\'20\'19s (and New York\u8217\'20\'19s, for that matter). Beyond that, Christian Ziegler, the chair of the Florida Republican party, is under investigation for rape and sexual assault. Law and order; traditional family values; whatever.\par \par \uc2 On the debate stage, DeSantis failed to land the blows he needed to rejuvenate his formerly promising campaign. His one-on-one confrontation did nothing to dent Nikki Haley\u8217\'20\'19s rise or bring him any closer to Trump. Air continues to exit DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s low-flying balloon.\par \par \uc2 He recently received the endorsement of Bob Vander Plaats, an evangelical leader in Iowa, but that gain has yet to move the dial. On the other hand, Haley just this week scored the endorsement of the Kochs\u8217\'20\'19 political network, which translates into money and campaign foot-soldiers, as DeSantis knows from personal experience.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDeSantis wins formal Koch backing as momentum continues to shift,\u8221\'20\'1D a Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/states/florida/story/2018/07/11/desantis-wins-formal-koch-backing-as-momentum-continues-to-shift-504166"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 headline}}}\uc2  from 2018 blared. Those days are so gone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen are you going to drop out and give Nikki Haley a shot to win?\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom zinged. Great question, one that DeSantis failed to answer in front of the Trump fan boy \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 . DeSantis \u8211\'20\'13 a \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  personal favorite \u8211\'20\'13 fell flat on Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s own network. Meanwhile, the \uc2 Fox\uc2  board member and ex-House speaker Paul Ryan was touting Haley to whoever would listen.\par \par \uc2 Much like \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the former vice-president and former presidential wannabe, DeSantis is bogged down in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Dobbs, the gift the right wing prayed for but is now living to regret. For Pence, it was a matter of conviction; for DeSantis it looks like a case of expedience that quickly headed south.\par \par \uc2 In July last year, Florida enacted a 15-week cut-off for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For DeSantis that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t enough. He doubled down on the issue and lost. To burnish his rightwing credentials, he then pressed the Florida legislature to adopt a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and it backfired. Tremendously.\par \par \uc2 He got what he demanded and is now living with its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/12/opinion/ohio-abortion-republicans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consequences}}}\uc2 . A majority of Floridians are pro-choice, by a 56-39 margin. Florida isn\u8217\'20\'19t Mississippi, to DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s chagrin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou want to roll back hard-earned national rights on voting rights and civil rights, human rights and women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, not just access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but also access to contraception,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom fired. The US is still waiting for DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s retort.\par \par \uc2 A majority of Floridians are pro-choice, by a 56-39 margin. Florida isn\u8217\'20\'19t Mississippi, to DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s chagrin\par \par \uc2 Here, Trump smells blood. He has privately derided anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaders as lacking \u8220\'20\'1Cleverage\u8221\'20\'1D to force his hand while tweaking them for having nowhere else to go once the supreme court struck down Roe v Wade. He has also reportedly mocked as \u8220\'20\'1Cdisloyal\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cout of touch\u8221\'20\'1D those evangelicals who cast their lot with DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 Simply put, Vander Plaats won\u8217\'20\'19t be receiving a Christmas card from the Trumps later this month. In that same vein, the evangelical rank and file has parted ways with its leadership. These days, Nascar and Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Daytona are their spiritual homes; church pews on Sunday, not so much.\par \par \uc2 In a sense, DeSantis is stuck in the past, rerunning yesteryear\u8217\'20\'19s campaigns. Right now, Trump demonstrates traction with younger voters and is making inroads with minority communities. By contrast, DeSantis is picking losing fights.\par \par \uc2 Gasping for attention, he unfurled a \u8220\'20\'1Cpoop map\u8221\'20\'1D of San Francisco to highlight the magnitude of the city\u8217\'20\'19s homeless problem. The stunt backfired. Right now, it\u8217\'20\'19s DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s campaign that seems to be the raging dung heap. The words \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida man\u8221\'20\'1D usually precede a punchline or something gruesome.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Green is an attorney in New York and served in the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  from 1990 to 1992\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231201ejc10028n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
