\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Kimmel on House Republicans: \u8216\'20\'18These guys are so desperate to smear Biden\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 634 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 November 2023\par 15:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Late-night hosts discuss efforts to impeach Biden and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s strategic pivot to moderate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel\par \par \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel took in the state of Washington DC on Tuesday evening, as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe swamp has somehow begun to drain itself\u8221\'20\'1D, with nearly 40 members of Congress announcing plans to retire at the end of their terms. \u8220\'20\'1CWhich is very unusual,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kimmel. \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, some members are retiring because the House and the Senate have become gridlocked by partisanship, but most of them just want to get away from \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  and Ted Cruz.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That, and avoiding the grind of fundraising for re-election every two years. \u8220\'20\'1CThe unfortunate secret about being a congressman that people don\u8217\'20\'19t know is that you spend most of your time calling and begging for money,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimmel explained. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re basically a telemarketer who gets to decide if we occasionally send money to Ukraine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other congressional news, lawyers for Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s son Hunter told a Republican-led committee that he is prepared to be questioned at their impeachment inquiry next month \u8211\'20\'13 but only if the hearings are held in public.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans don\u8217\'20\'19t want that,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimmel noted. \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t want it on TV. They\u8217\'20\'19re like \u8216\'20\'18if we don\u8217\'20\'19t do this behind closed doors, how are we supposed to make stuff up?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The chair of the oversight committee, James Comer, tried to publicly slam \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  for demanding special treatment: \u8220\'20\'1CHunter Biden is trying to play by his own rules instead of following the rules required of everyone else. That won\u8217\'20\'19t stand with House Republicans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhich is, of course, hilarious for about 10,000 different reasons,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kimmel. \u8220\'20\'1CEven though we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen no evidence, and they\u8217\'20\'19ve seen no evidence, that Joe Biden had anything to do with this, Hunter and the laptop \u8211\'20\'13 this will not go away. Joe Biden could become the first president ever to get impeached because his son didn\u8217\'20\'19t have Apple Care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese guys are so desperate to smear Joe Biden, they are literally now grasping at straws,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, pointing to a recent Fox News clip in which the host Jesse Watters criticized Biden for drinking a milkshake through a straw. Using a straw is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a good look\u8221\'20\'1D, he said, because \u8220\'20\'1Cmen should never suck anything through a straw\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReally? Is that a thing now?\u8221\'20\'1D Kimmel wondered. \u8220\'20\'1CAnyone feel like Jesse Watters might be going through some sort of an identity crisis?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Daily Show\par \par \uc2 Trump acting like he cares about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is like the Kool-Aid man suddenly caring about walls. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/michelleisawolf?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @michelleisawolf}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pTIm0phvBd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pTIm0phvBd}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 The Daily Show (@TheDailyShow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheDailyShow/status/1729677583191876042?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 And on the Daily Show, the guest host Michelle Wolf laughed at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pivot on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights after gutting access as president. \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys remember how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  killed Roe v Wade right after he killed \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 , I presume,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWell now, Trump is making the strategic decision to run as a moderate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump going moderate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after stacking the supreme court with the conservative majority that overturned Roe is \u8220\'20\'1Clike the Kool-Aid man suddenly caring about walls\u8221\'20\'1D, she continued. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s too late, dude! The damage is done, you big red bitch.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t let anyone tell you that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not popular in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CEven the man who killed them [sic] is acting like he supports them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 11/29/2023 15:50:20\par \par \uc2 2023-11-29T16:11:42Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/c5bf375d13cf1e9c8cde1fe94f66657c7df2ec9f/161_120_2579_1547/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/c5bf375d13cf1e9c8cde1fe94f66657c7df2ec9f/161_120_2579_1547/500.jpg}}}\uc2  Jimmy Kimmel on Republicans: \u8216\'20\'18These guys are so desperate to smear Joe Biden, they are literally now grasping at straws.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231129ejbt002bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
