\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 The choice: a rural mother and  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  care on the Washington-Idaho border\b0\par\par\uc2 Katia Riddle in Clarkston, Washington \par \uc2 2,225 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 November 2023\par 15:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Even in places where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal, the inaccessibility of the procedure elsewhere can seep over state lines\par \par \uc2 As she walks in the door on a recent afternoon to relieve her parents of caring for her five-month-old daughter, Jasmine feels a familiar pang of guilt.\par \par \uc2 Jasmine*, 28, is a single mother raising four kids in a small town in far eastern Washington, near the border of Idaho. Her partner of more than a decade \u8211\'20\'13 and father of her children \u8211\'20\'13 is incarcerated for an assault charge that she brought against him.\par \par \uc2 Without her parents stepping in to help, she\u8217\'20\'19d struggle to hold down her job at a factory. But she knows it\u8217\'20\'19s hard on them.\par \par \uc2 Most nights, her dad, Andrew, 52, finishes his swing shift as a janitor at the hospital around 1am, sleeps a few hours, and then rises again at 4am so he and his wife can watch their grandchild all day. Many weeks he gets by on 11 hours of sleep \u8211\'20\'13 total.\par \par \uc2 Her mother tries to reassure her. \u8220\'20\'1CYou know I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna take care of my kids,\u8221\'20\'1D says Kelli, 52, as she bustles around collecting her things to leave after watching the baby for nine hours.\par \par \uc2 Jasmine fantasizes aloud about what she would buy her parents if she had the money. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m thinking, like, a really nice recliner,\u8221\'20\'1D she says to them. Her dad smiles. \u8220\'20\'1CThen grandpa would never get up,\u8221\'20\'1D he teases.\par \par \uc2 Despite the sacrifice the situation demands of her family and how deeply tired and often lonely Jasmine is at the end of the day, she sees this last baby as a positive force that helped her stop using drugs and focus on her priorities.\par \par \uc2 But had \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed a more accessible and supported choice in this small American town during a few critical days early in her pregnancy, her life might have taken a different course.\par \par \uc2 For women like Jasmine across the country who are making this same choice in a quickly shifting cultural and legal landscape, the decision can be complicated by factors beyond simply what the laws permit.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re having a baby\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Jasmine found out she was pregnant in the summer of 2022, just weeks after the supreme court overturned the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The timing couldn\u8217\'20\'19t have been worse. Weeks before, she\u8217\'20\'19d been assaulted by her partner. They have both struggled with substance abuse. That weekend, they were on an especially bad meth bender. He became violent \u8211\'20\'13 according to a police incident report, he threw Jasmine on the floor and strangled her to the point of almost losing consciousness while saying he was \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to kill her\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The children were feet away, in the hallway. From the bedroom, she could hear them crying. This is what other parents do to their kids, she thought. Not me.\par \par \uc2 Jasmine fled with her children to her parents\u8217\'20\'19 place. Her call to the police set the legal system in motion: a no contact order, charges of assault, stalking. It had been 11 years of this kind of abuse. Jasmine was done.\par \par \uc2 Then came the pregnancy test. She took it standing in the bathroom with her best friend, who looked first. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re having a baby,\u8221\'20\'1D she said to Jasmine. \u8220\'20\'1CNo, we\u8217\'20\'19re fucking not. No. We\u8217\'20\'19re not,\u8221\'20\'1D Jasmine replied.\par \par \uc2 She doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have much time for politics, but Jasmine believes there\u8217\'20\'19s a place for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Had she been aware of a clinic close by where she could have accessed services in that first 24 hours, she says, she would have done it without question.\par \par \uc2 Choices about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region can be influenced by practical constraints where urban centers straddle state borders. The small town of Clarkston where Jasmine lives is located in Washington, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal. The state has taken an offensive stance to protect reproductive choice, passing a law that shields patients and providers from legal prosecution and makes Washington a safe harbor for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers. By some measures this effort has been successful; in the year since Dobbs, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  in Washington state has seen a 56% increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients from Idaho.\par \par \uc2 Despite being a Washington resident, Jasmine\u8217\'20\'19s closest healthcare facilities are a 10-minute drive over the Snake River in Lewiston, Idaho. On that side of the border, women live under some of the most austere anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the country \u8211\'20\'13 laws with tentacles that reach into Washington, despite its protections. A trigger law made the procedure illegal after the Dobbs decision in 2022 and the state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking law\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 currently on hold as its legality is challenged \u8211\'20\'13 would make it a felony to transport minors out of state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Debate around the law has left many people confused about what is legal, and intimidated by the severity of potential punishments. Many are afraid to leave the state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under any conditions.\par \par \uc2 This confusion of geography, laws and messaging means that for women like Jasmine in this region, the decision whether or not to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes down to a confluence of factors including readily available resources, pressure and influence from family and friends, and information that may or may not be accurate.\par \par \uc2 Jasmine is clear about the fact that had she been determined enough, she could have had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She doesn\u8217\'20\'19t see the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe as having much influence on her life.\par \par \uc2 But what she does acknowledge is that accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  involved many difficult steps.\par \par \uc2 Jasmine figured that her best bet for getting care would be in Spokane, Washington. She knew of a \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  clinic there, but it was a two-hour drive and in addition to the gas money and childcare that trip would demand, the procedure, she thought, would not be free. \u8220\'20\'1CI was like, you know, how am I going to come up with the money?\u8221\'20\'1D Skipping a car payment was a potential solution.\par \par \uc2 I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know what was more scary, the situation I was in or \u8211\'20\'13 you know, having to fork out the money and then do it by myself\par \par \uc2 Jasmine\par \par \uc2 In fact, the closest \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  clinic to Clarkston was not hours away in Spokane but just a 30-minute drive away in Pullman, Washington. The possibility that a closer facility exists might not occur to someone managing the daily chaos of a job, three kids and a domestic violence charge.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the travel and the expense, she grappled with the procedure itself. It would be emotional. She had a painful miscarriage in the second trimester of a pregnancy years before, and the loss still haunted her. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill could induce painful cramping and bleeding. She imagined enduring that at home while also caring for her kids, not telling anyone else.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t know what was more scary, the situation I was in or \u8211\'20\'13 you know, having to fork out the money and then do it by myself,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Sarah DeVleming is the health center manager at the Pullman clinic. Lately, she says, people are coming in scared and intimidated.\par \par \uc2 The experience of getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she says, is often an emotional one. Now people are dealing with the extra stress of navigating conflicting laws, particularly if they\u8217\'20\'19re coming from across the border in Idaho. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one should have to worry about getting in trouble with the law on top of that,\u8221\'20\'1D DeVleming says.\par \par \uc2 In response to their sense that patients aren\u8217\'20\'19t equipped with accurate information, the team at the clinic has launched a billboard campaign in Idaho, letting women know they can cross the border for care. \u8220\'20\'1C Extreme politicians in Idaho don\u8217\'20\'19t want you to know this,\u8221\'20\'1D reads one sign. \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in Oregon and Washington.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jasmine did not see any of these billboards the day she found out she was pregnant. Instead, she turned to the place she knew would be free and convenient: Reliance Center in Lewiston, Idaho. The clinic doesn\u8217\'20\'19t advertise as a crisis pregnancy center \u8211\'20\'13 the website uses the words \u8220\'20\'1Cfree sexual health clinic\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but it is affiliated with a ministry by the same name.\par \par \uc2 The Reliance waiting room features a soft couch and signs on the wall with affirming messages like \u8220\'20\'1Clove lives here\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1Cbe still\u8221\'20\'1D. Free beverages and snacks sit out against a wall. Signs advertise parenting classes. The promise of free ultrasounds often brings people in the door.\par \par \uc2 Crisis pregnancy centers \u8211\'20\'13 facilities in which non-medical staff, often using religious messaging, try to dissuade people from having abortions \u8211\'20\'13 have been the subject of much criticism in the wake of the Dobbs decision. Reliance Center blurs this distinction by employing some medical staff, but with an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  approach. The founder, Heather Lawless, says while they don\u8217\'20\'19t offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and birth control, their mission is not to talk people out of these things. \u8220\'20\'1CWe only speak medical truth,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 They also don\u8217\'20\'19t encourage these choices. Part of this truth includes describing to women possible dangers of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIs there a danger of perforating the uterus?\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1COf course there is.\u8221\'20\'1D (The risk of uterine perforation during \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is considered low. At least one study puts it at less than 1%.)\par \par \uc2 Often women come to her center emotional and irrational, their lives in chaos on top of grappling with an unplanned pregnancy. \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels very important when you\u8217\'20\'19re sitting down with a woman having that conversation,\u8221\'20\'1D says Jaclyn Zipse, who works there and remembers talking to Jasmine the day she came in. \u8220\'20\'1CThe choice is going to be lifelong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the Dobbs decision, the center has seen a 65% increase in patients it calls \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  minded\u8221\'20\'1D. After Jasmine visited \uc2 Reliance\uc2 , the staff sent her home with a box of baby items including a onesie that said \u8220\'20\'1Cbest gift ever\u8221\'20\'1D, and a sign that read \u8220\'20\'1Cbrave mama\u8221\'20\'1D. Looking at that onesie, she started crying. \u8220\'20\'1CI just needed someone to tell me I could do it,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 A new plan emerged. She would stop using drugs. She would have this baby.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after that, though her partner was still under a no contact order and legally forbidden to talk with her, the couple reconciled. Had she not been pregnant, she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t imagine it would have happened. Finding out about the baby reminded her of good times. \u8220\'20\'1CAnytime I\u8217\'20\'19m pregnant, he\u8217\'20\'19s his best self,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe just started treating each other the way we should.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This won\u8217\'20\'19t last forever\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Standing in her kitchen, Jasmine makes sandwiches for the trip to the prison. It\u8217\'20\'19s a two-hour drive. Due to the protective order, she\u8217\'20\'19s not allowed in to see her children\u8217\'20\'19s father, but the kids can go into the visiting room with a friend of hers. It\u8217\'20\'19s their second trip and his second time meeting his youngest child.\par \par \uc2 Taped to her cupboard is a flyer that reads \u8220\'20\'1CTen tips for stressless parenting\u8221\'20\'1D, alongside another that says \u8220\'20\'1CTen ways to help your child with homework\u8221\'20\'1D. The phone rings. A recording informs her that it\u8217\'20\'19s a free call from an individual at the correction center. \u8220\'20\'1CThis call is not private,\u8221\'20\'1D says the recording. \u8220\'20\'1CIt will be recorded and may be monitored.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo you want to say hi to your daddy?\u8221\'20\'1D she asks the baby. They\u8217\'20\'19re leaving in an hour. \u8220\'20\'1CI am going to stand by that gate, so hopefully you can look out the window and see me,\u8221\'20\'1D she tells him. \u8220\'20\'1CAll right, I love you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love you,\u8221\'20\'1D he replies.\par \par \uc2 Things will be different when he gets out of jail, thinks Jasmine. This time-out was the break they needed. They\u8217\'20\'19ll both stay sober. He\u8217\'20\'19s a good person, she repeats. A good dad who deserves a second chance.\par \par \uc2 Still, the doubt creeps in. There\u8217\'20\'19s a familiar tone in his voice sometimes on the phone that scares her.\par \par \uc2 If things go bad, she has a contingency plan: always keep $500 hidden away. Never be without a vehicle.\par \par \uc2 On her mirror, she\u8217\'20\'19s written a nightly checklist to make the morning routine easier the next day: \u8220\'20\'1CSet clothes out for everyone; tidy up house,\u8221\'20\'1D she instructs herself.\par \par \uc2 The last one: \u8220\'20\'1CRemember this won\u8217\'20\'19t last forever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *Jasmine\u8217\'20\'19s last name was wi\par \par \uc2 thjeld from this story at her request.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 In the US, the domestic violence hotline is 1-800-799-SAFE (7233). In the UK, call the national domestic abuse helpline on 0808 2000 247, or visit Women\u8217\'20\'19s Aid. In Australia, the national family violence counselling service is on 1800 737 732. Other international helplines may be found via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.befrienders.org"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.befrienders.org}}}\uc2 . Use the following endnote if a story is about a murder/suicide: In the US, the suicide prevention lifeline is 988 and the domestic violence hotline is 1-800-799-SAFE (7233). In the UK, Samaritans can be contacted on freephone 116 123 and the domestic abuse helpline is 0808 2000 247. In Australia, the crisis support service Lifeline is on 13 11 14 and the national family violence counselling service is on 1800 737 732. Other international helplines can be found via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.befrienders.org"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.befrienders.org}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231124ejbo00233\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
