\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson likened  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  to \u8216\'20\'18American holocaust\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 527 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 November 2023\par 16:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 CNN airs clip from May last year in which then Louisiana congressman \u8211\'20\'13 a leading anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  voice \u8211\'20\'13 made comparison\par \par \uc2 Before he became speaker of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 , the Louisiana Republican congressman Mike Johnson likened \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Can American holocaust\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reality is that \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and all these \u8230\'20\'26 big \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 they set up their clinics in inner cities,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson told a radio show in May 2022, in comments {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/videos/politics/2023/11/22/mike-johnson-trump-audio-kfile-ebof-vpx.cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aired by CNN on Tuesday}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey regard these people as easy prey.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But while these remarks may sound stunning, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists often refer to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the United States as a \u8220\'20\'1Cholocaust\u8221\'20\'1D. This isn\u8217\'20\'19t even the only time that Johnson has made the comparison.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDuring business hours today, 4,500 innocent American children will be killed,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson wrote in a 2005 op-ed for the Shreveport Times, which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/house-speaker-mike-johnson-abortion-holocaust/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently resurfaced by CBS News}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a holocaust that has been repeated every day for 32 years, since 1973\u8217\'20\'19s Roe v Wade.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In that op-ed, Johnson also said the judicial philosophy that undergirded Roe \u8211\'20\'13 and allowed for the removal of the feeding tube of Terri Schiavo, a womanwith severe brain damage who became a cause c\u233\'00\'E9l\u232\'00\'E8bre among anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists \u8211\'20\'13 to be \u8220\'20\'1Cno different than Hitler\u8217\'20\'19s\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Johnson went on to add that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had led to a dearth of \u8220\'20\'1Cable workers\u8221\'20\'1D and a crisis for social security, a claim he would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/26/republican-speaker-mike-johnson-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeat at a House hearing years later}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Comparisons between US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Holocaust date back decades, with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates writing books in the 1980s with titles such as The \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Holocaust: Today\u8217\'20\'19s Final Solution. Although the mainstream United States may have grown less tolerant of the comparison, it has never disappeared from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  circles, which are predominantly Christian.\par \par \uc2 In fact, it\u8217\'20\'19s sometimes used as a recruitment tool. One prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group even claims anyone born after the supreme court decided Roe in 1973 is a \u8220\'20\'1Csurvivor of the American \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  holocaust\u8221\'20\'1D and invites young people to become \u8220\'20\'1Cboots on the ground\u8221\'20\'1D in recognition of their aborted peers. In 2019, Texas Right to Life \u8211\'20\'13 a powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group in Texas \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/ne8j9m/7-days-inside-an-anti-abortion-summer-camp-training-the-next-generation-of-activists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held a training for young anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  activists}}}\uc2  where leaders screened documentaries about the Nazi Holocaust and urged the activists to \u8220\'20\'1Cwrite down three similarities between the Holocaust and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 These kinds of comparisons have even made their way into law. In a 2019 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case, the supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/18pdf/18-483_3d9g.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote an opinion}}}\uc2  claiming that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on the verge of becoming \u8220\'20\'1Ca tool of modern-day eugenics\u8221\'20\'1D. Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which was first passed in 2019 and took effect after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade last year, suggested \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was worse than famous 20th-century atrocities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMore than 50 million babies have been aborted in the United States since the Roe decision in 1973,\u8221\'20\'1D the ban reads, \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than three times the number who were killed in German death camps, Chinese purges, Stalin\u8217\'20\'19s gulags, Cambodian killing fields, and the Rwandan genocide combined.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231122ejbm002ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
