\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump return to White House would be perilous for democracy, conservative lawyers say \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 4,922 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 November 2023\par 21:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read the latest on the Wisconsin supreme court and Trump appealing Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s ruling here:Wisconsin supreme court appears poised to strike down legislative maps and end Republican dominanceTrump appeals Colorado ruling that said he engaged in January 6 insurrection\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the US politics blog now, thanks for joining us today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we covered:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Wisconsin supreme court appeared poised to strike down gerrymandered Republican-drawn state legislative maps that have maintained the party\u8217\'20\'19s domination for decades. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/21/wisconsin-supreme-court-redistricting-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a hearing Tuesday}}}\uc2 , the panel\u8217\'20\'19s new liberal majority appeared sympathetic to arguments from lawyers for Democratic governor \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  and others that the majority of districts breached strict rules.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two senior aides to \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s cratering campaign for the Republican presidential nomination almost got into a fist fight during a heated argument, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/21/trump-2024-election-republicans-biden-politics-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-655d11d98f0876a02a031d04#block-655d11d98f0876a02a031d04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it was reported}}}\uc2 . The altercation came last week as the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s Never Back Down political action committee discussed how to counter a rise in popularity of rival Nikki Haley, the former South Carolina governor.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/21/trump-appeals-january-6-ruling-colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appealed a ruling}}}\uc2  in which a Colorado judge said he could not be disqualified from the presidential ballot under the 14th amendment to the US constitution, even though he engaged in insurrection by inciting the deadly January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called on Congress to pass his $106bn supplementary budget request that he said includes funding to \u8220\'20\'1Cstep up\u8221\'20\'1D the fight against a flow of deadly fentanyl entering the US. The president, speaking at the White House before leaving for a Thanksgiving break in Massachusetts, said the fentanyl crisis was hurting families in every state and curbing it was \u8220\'20\'1Csomething every American needs to get behind\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A trio of prominent conservative lawyers said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/21/opinion/trump-lawyers-constitution-democracy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scathing New York Times oped}}}\uc2  that a second term in office for former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would imperil democracy.George Conway, \uc2 J Michael Luttig\uc2  and \uc2 Barbara Comstock\uc2 , who have formed a new group to \u8220\'20\'1Cspeak out against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s falsehoods\u8221\'20\'1D, say Trump has surrounded himself with \u8220\'20\'1Cgrifters, frauds and con men willing to subvert the Constitution\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cour country is in a constitutional emergency, if not a constitutional crisis\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A reminder that you can follow the latest developments in the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war, including the reported imminent deal for the release of some of the hostages held in Gaza, in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/21/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-hamas-leader-haniyeh-truce-ceasefire-talks-gaza-qatar-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s liveblog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Report: DeSantis aides in 'heated argument' over campaign direction\par \par \uc2 Two senior team members of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s flailing presidential campaign almost came to blows during a meeting last week to discuss how to counter Nikki Haley \u8217\'20\'19s rise in the polls, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/ron-desantis-nikki-haley-fight-right-never-back-down-rcna126102"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News is reporting}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Sophie Park/Reuters\par \par \uc2 According to the network, \uc2 Jeff Roe\uc2 , chief consultant for DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s Never Back Down political action committee, got into \u8220\'20\'1Ca heated argument\u8221\'20\'1D with longtime DeSantis associate and PAC board member \uc2 Scott Wagner\uc2 , the two being stopped just short of a physical altercation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have a stick up your ass, Scott,\u8221\'20\'1D Roe allegedly fumed at Wagner during the meeting in Tallahassee last Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy don\u8217\'20\'19t you come over here and get it?\u8221\'20\'1D Wagner responded, rising from his chair, according to NBC. Wagner was \u8220\'20\'1Cquickly restrained by two fellow board members\u8221\'20\'1D, the network\u8217\'20\'19s report said, adding its information came from sources in the room.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe've reached the terminal stage of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonDeSantis?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RonDeSantis}}}\uc2  campaign where you have senior staff having to be restrained from fighting one another. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tCxc6v0fvN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tCxc6v0fvN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wCfNstTnKI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wCfNstTnKI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Max Steele (@maxasteele) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maxasteele/status/1727058859964104914?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Florida governor DeSantis, once seen as a viable rival to runaway leader \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the race for the 2024 Republican presidential nomination, has been tanking in numerous opinion polls, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ron-desantis-trump-florida-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even in his own state}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He appears to be an an opposite trajectory to former South Carolina governor Haley, whose \u8220\'20\'1Csurging poll numbers and newfound affection from megadonors pose an existential threat to the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D NBC said.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis campaign insiders have indicated that the candidate and his wife \uc2 Casey DeSantis\uc2 , a former television news presenter who has assumed an increasingly prominent role in his political career, are growing unhappy at the performance of the Never Back Down PAC leadership.\par \par \uc2 Both DeSantis and Haley, however, still trail Trump by a substantial margin.\par \par \uc2 The unseemly scenes in DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s campaign meeting mirror those of last week\u8217\'20\'19s Senate labor committee meeting when Oklahoma senator \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2  rose from his seat and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/14/bernie-sanders-markwayne-mullin-teamsters-sean-obrien"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenged a Teamsters union official to a fight}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve been bringing you updates for much of the day from Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court, where arguments have tilted back and forth over the state\u8217\'20\'19s gerrymandered legislative maps.\par \par \uc2 According to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine, and Alice Herman in the courtroom in Madison, the panel\u8217\'20\'19s liberal majority appears poised to strike down the existing Republican-drawn maps and end the party\u8217\'20\'19s stranglehold on both legislative chambers of government.\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what that would mean for a redraw of the maps, or if special elections would be needed to fill legislative seats next year.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our latest report on today\u8217\'20\'19s developments, and a look at what might come next:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/21/wisconsin-supreme-court-redistricting-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin supreme court appears poised to strike down legislative maps and end Republican dominance}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A newly-elected Florida Republican state congressman has filed legislation that would effectively ban any LGBTQ group in the state from receiving taxpayer funding.\par \par \uc2 A House bill by Ryan Chamberlin would bar any non-profit from using \u8220\'20\'1Csexual orientation or gender identity\u8221\'20\'1D as a factor in any application for state contracts or grants, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://floridapolitics.com/archives/645632-dont-say-gay-for-nonprofits-ryan-chamberlin-files-bill-that-would-restrict-lgbtq-nonprofits-receiving-state-funding/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida Politics reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The proposal was immediately criticized by Democrats, who see the bill as an extension of the Republican-dominated legislature\u8217\'20\'19s well-documented assault on LGBTQ+ rights, including the infamous \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/florida-education-board-approves-expansion-dont-say-gay-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t Say Gay}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D bill and other restrictions championed by hard right governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bill is \u8220\'20\'1Cbigoted, unnecessary and highly unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D, Democratic state representative \uc2 Anna Eskamani\uc2  said on X, adding that groups such as Equality Florida would essentially be banned from existing.\par \par \uc2 enltrFlorida Republicans just filed legislation that would essentially ban gender pronouns in PRIVATE businesses and prohibit trainings about pronouns in nonprofits too. Would basically ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/equalityfl?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @equalityfl}}}\uc2  from existing.\par \par \uc2 Bigoted, unnecessary and highly unconstitutional. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/o4hzvN3yDY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/o4hzvN3yDY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Anna V. Eskamani ?? (@AnnaForFlorida) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnnaForFlorida/status/1726974337985683786?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Chamberlin captured his central Florida seat in May with 79% of a special election vote, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://floridapolitics.com/archives/612515-full-house-ryan-chamberlin-wins-hd-24-special-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promising at the time}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s work to be done. I\u8217\'20\'19m excited to help with that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Missouri supreme court won't hear \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  question appeal\par \par \uc2 Missouri \u8217\'20\'19s supreme court won\u8217\'20\'19t hear an appeal by Republican secretary of state \uc2 Jay Ashcroft\uc2  over the wording of ballot question on access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a win for advocates attempting to enshrine protections for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 A state appeals court ruled last month that wording asking voters if they were in favor of \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous and unregulated abortions until live birth\u8221\'20\'1D was politically partisan.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the state supreme court declined to hear Ashcroft\u8217\'20\'19s appeal of that ruling. Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s Republican controlled legislature banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except in cases of medical emergency after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  last year overturned the Roe v Wade ruling and ended 50 years of federal protections.\par \par \uc2 In all seven states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been on the ballot since, voters have either supported protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights or rejected attempts to erode them.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our state-by-state guide to where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws stand:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights across the US: we track where laws stand in every state}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge to rule on Trump co-defendant's bond\par \par \uc2 A judge in Atlanta is hearing arguments on a request to revoke the bond of Harrison Floyd, one of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s co-defendants in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/15/trump-georgia-trial-election-fani-willis-timeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia case}}}\uc2  related to efforts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  filed a motion last week telling superior court judge Scott McAfee that Floyd attempted to intimidate and contact likely witnesses and his co-defendants in violation of the terms of his release, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Harrison Floyd. Photograph: samiyah/AP\par \par \uc2 Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys wrote in a court filing that Willis\u8217\'20\'19 allegations are without merit and that the motion is a \u8220\'20\'1Cretaliatory measure\u8221\'20\'1D against their client. Floyd \u8220\'20\'1Cneither threatened or intimidated anyone and certainly did not communicate with a witness or co-defendant directly or indirectly,\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote.\par \par \uc2 Willis was in court Tuesday to present the prosecution\u8217\'20\'19s case. She planned to call three witnesses, including \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2 , a top election official in Georgia who strenuously defended the legitimacy of the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 vote count against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims that the election was fraudulent.\par \par \uc2 The charges against Floyd relate to allegations of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/capitol-siege-2022-midterm-elections-georgia-election-recounts-5cffe294a372eb32dc68588784202314"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 harassment toward Ruby Freeman}}}\uc2 , a Fulton county election worker who had been falsely accused of election fraud by Trump and his supporters. Floyd took part in a 4 January 2021 conversation in which Freeman was told she \u8220\'20\'1Cneeded protection\u8221\'20\'1D and was pressured to lie and say she had participated in election fraud, the indictment says.\par \par \uc2 Four of the original 19 defendants agreed plea deals that include a promise to testify in any trials in the case. Trump and the others have pleaded not guilty.\par \par \uc2 No trial date has been set, but Willis last week asked McAfee to set it for August next year, and warned the case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/15/trump-georgia-trial-election-fani-willis-timeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could stretch into 2025}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump appeals Colorado 'insurrection' ruling\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appealed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/18/colorado-judge-says-trump-engaged-in-insurrection-but-keeps-him-on-ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  in which a Colorado judge said he could not be disqualified from the presidential ballot under the 14th amendment to the US constitution, even though he engaged in insurrection by inciting the deadly January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 The former president took issue with the finding that he participated in insurrection in connection with the attack on the Capitol staged by his supporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe district court ruled that section three [of the 14th amendment] did not apply to the presidency, because that position is not an \u8216\'20\'18officer of the United States\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D lawyers for Trump said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/24173137-trump-colorado-14th-amendment-appeal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a court filing}}}\uc2 , responding to the ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/18/colorado-judge-says-trump-engaged-in-insurrection-but-keeps-him-on-ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe district court nonetheless applied section three to President Trump, finding that he \u8216\'20\'18engaged\u8217\'20\'19 in an \u8216\'20\'18insurrection\u8217\'20\'19. Should these findings be vacated because the district court self-admittedly lacked jurisdiction to apply section three to President Trump?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The group that filed the suit on behalf of six state petitioners, Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington (Crew), also lodged an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.citizensforethics.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/20231120-Petitioners-App-for-Review_Redacted.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It argued: \u8220\'20\'1CSection three of the 14th amendment, passed after the civil war, excludes from federal or state office those who engaged in insurrection against the constitution after previously taking an oath to support it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause the district court found that Trump engaged in insurrection after taking the presidential oath of office, it should have concluded that he is disqualified from office and ordered the secretary of state to exclude him from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colorado}}}\uc2  presidential primary ballot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read Martin Pengelly \u8217\'20\'19s full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/21/trump-appeals-january-6-ruling-colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump appeals Colorado ruling that said he engaged in January 6 insurrection}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 John Dean, former White House counsel to \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2 , is scathing about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/20/trump-lawyers-appeal-gag-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 persuade an appeals court}}}\uc2  that he should not have a gag order in his federal election interference case because he is running for president.\par \par \uc2 Dean has weighed in on what appears to be a court l {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/20/trump-lawyers-appeal-gag-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eaning towards}}}\uc2 , narrowing the gag order that bans Trump from making inflammatory statements and social media posts attacking prosecutors, potential witnesses and court staff.\par \par \uc2 Dean posted on X/\uc2 Twitter\uc2 , saying: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has turned the rule of law in the United States upside down, and it is stunning that federal circuit court judges are buying into his remarkable con!\u8221\'20\'1D He said the hearing yesterday in Washington, DC, \u8220\'20\'1Cbordered on pure farce.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dean, who ultimately helped bring down Nixon despite being involved in the-then president\u8217\'20\'19s cover-up of corrupt and illegal presidential conduct known as Watergate, must be experiencing deja vu right now. He told the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/05/watergate-50th-anniversary-john-dean-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 2022}}}\uc2 , of now-GOP frontrunner Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CI was never worried about the country and the government during Watergate but from the day Trump was nominated, I had a knot in my stomach\u8230\'20\'26he just discovered late in his presidency the enormous powers he does have as president\u8230\'20\'26he knows he can hurt his enemies and help his friends.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On X last night his new post on Trump concluded: \u8220\'20\'1CFor heaven sakes, hold this man responsible for his aberrant and bullying behavior before he further destroys our country. Enough is enough is enough!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI do not understand why an election campaign for the presidency is receiving special consideration for a person being held responsible for criminal behavior? (For example: Why are others who have been indicted not simply joining the race for president since they too should be\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John W. Dean (@JohnWDean) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnWDean/status/1726785535279239374?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hostage deal between Israel, \uc2 Hamas\uc2  'very close' - White House\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says negotiators are \u8220\'20\'1C very close\u8221\'20\'1D to securing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/21/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-hamas-leader-haniyeh-truce-ceasefire-talks-gaza-qatar-latest-news?page=with:block-655cd9578f0876a02a031a62#block-655cd9578f0876a02a031a62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the release}}}\uc2  of potentially dozens of hostages held by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hamas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hamas}}}\uc2  in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The US president was speaking at the White House and said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re now very close, very close \u8211\'20\'13 we can bring some of these hostages home very soon, but don\u8217\'20\'19t want to get into the details of things.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CNothing is done until it\u8217\'20\'19s done and when we have more to say we will, but things are looking good at the moment. \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We are closely covering all the news in the Israel-Gaza crisis via our global live blog and you can find the details {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/21/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-hamas-leader-haniyeh-truce-ceasefire-talks-gaza-qatar-latest-news?page=with:block-655cd9578f0876a02a031a62#block-655cd9578f0876a02a031a62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks during a meeting on combating fentanyl, in the Roosevelt Room of the White House, Tuesday. Sitting on his right is US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 . Other cabinet members also present. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s lunchtime on a quiet day so far in US politics, and time for a recap of what we\u8217\'20\'19ve looked at so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has called on Congress to pass his $106bn supplementary budget request that he said includes funding to \u8220\'20\'1Cstep up\u8221\'20\'1D the fight against a flow of deadly fentanyl entering the US. The president, speaking at the White House before leaving for a Thanksgiving break in Massachusetts, said the fentanyl crisis was hurting families in every state and curbing it was \u8220\'20\'1Csomething every American needs to get behind\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court justices have been grilling attorneys for both the respondents and plaintiffs in a much-watched gerrymandering case that could end in a complete redraw of the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislative districts. Lawyers for Democratic governor \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  say the current maps favoring Republicans breach a law that says they must be \u8220\'20\'1Ccontiguous\u8221\'20\'1D; a conservative justice says the plaintiffs want to upend 50 years of precedent.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A trio of prominent conservative lawyers said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/21/opinion/trump-lawyers-constitution-democracy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scathing New York Times oped}}}\uc2  that a second term in office for former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would imperil democracy.George Conway, \uc2 J Michael Luttig\uc2  and \uc2 Barbara Comstock\uc2  say Trump has surrounded himself with \u8220\'20\'1Cgrifters, frauds and con men willing to subvert the Constitution\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cour country is in a constitutional emergency, if not a constitutional crisis\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Back in Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court, lawyers for Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/21/wisconsin-supreme-court-redistricting-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defending gerrymandered state legislative maps}}}\uc2  are getting a grilling from the judges, as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Alice Herman reports from the courtroom:\par \par \uc2 An attorney representing the Republican-controlled state legislature, the respondent in the redistricting case, argued that petitioners asking for legislative districts to be redrawn before the 2024 elections have not allotted sufficient time to redraw the maps, and disputed their definition of \u8220\'20\'1Ccontiguous districts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Taylor Meehan argued that the existence of districts with literal water-bound islands invalidate the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 argument that the legislative maps should avoid non-contiguous districts and said that the court should adopt a looser definition of \u8220\'20\'1Ccontiguous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re telling us to use one definition because it will help your argument and I\u8217\'20\'19m pretty sure the rule is we\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to look at the definition to figure out what the law is,\u8221\'20\'1D said justice Jill Karofsky, who, along with bench colleague Ann Bradley, repeatedly questioned Dallet\u8217\'20\'19s definition of \u8220\'20\'1Ccontiguity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meehan questioned the right of plaintiffs in non-contiguous districts across the state to bring forward the case, comparing their complaint to an Illinois voter challenging Wisconsin maps.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see how a petitioner who lives in Beloit\u8221\'20\'1D can ask for a statewide redraw, Meehan said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden calls on Congress to 'step up' fentanyl fight\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has called on Congress to join him to \u8220\'20\'1Cstep up the fight\u8221\'20\'1D against the flow of fentanyl coming into the US.\par \par \uc2 The president was speaking at the White House in his final official engagement before he and first lady Jill Biden head to Nantucket later for their Thanksgiving break.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , with secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  (left) and attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , outlines efforts to counter the flow of fentanyl into the US at the White House on Tuesday. Photograph: ABACA/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Before a cabinet meeting that\u8217\'20\'19s now gone into private session, Biden said he was heartbroken for families who will have an empty seat at their Thanksgiving table because they had lost a loved one to the drug:\par \par \uc2 Fentanyl is likely the number one killer of Americans at this point. It\u8217\'20\'19s an issue that\u8217\'20\'19s hurting families in every state across the nation. Curbing this crisis is something that every American needs to get behind, Democrat and Republican.\par \par \uc2 How can we accelerate our efforts and make sure that we\u8217\'20\'19re delivering real results? Congress also has to step up in this fight. It can start by passing my {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/20/biden-israel-ukraine-gaza-aid-request-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supplemental budget request}}}\uc2  for national security, including significant resources to help stop the flow of fentanyl in our country, as well as funds to strengthen and support services for people struggling with fentanyl impacts.\par \par \uc2 I also urge Congress to permanently make fentanyl and related substances Schedule One drugs. Too many people are dying.\par \par \uc2 Biden prefaced his remarks with an update on progress towards a deal to free hostages held in Gaza by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  since the 7 October attacks on Israel. He said an agreement was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery close\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 You can follow that and other developments in the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war in our dedicated blog here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/21/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-hamas-leader-haniyeh-truce-ceasefire-talks-gaza-qatar-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Hamas war live: Netanyahu announces government meetings tonight \u8216\'20\'18in light of developments\u8217\'20\'19 on hostage releases}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Alice Herman covering the gerrymandering case in Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court:\par \par \uc2 Anthony Russomanno, an attorney representing Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , argued that the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislative maps, and the process for drawing them, violates the separation of powers \u8211\'20\'13 privileging the legislature, which is responsible for drafting the maps, over the executive branch.\par \par \uc2 Tamara Packard, representing five Democratic lawmakers, also argued the mapmaking process violated the separation of powers.\par \par \uc2 Conservative justices hammered Russomanno and Packard with questions of propriety regarding the timing of the litigation, and justice Rebecca Bradley accused attorneys of attempting to illegally overhaul the makeup of the state legislature.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou are ultimately asking that this court unseat every assemblyman that was elected last year,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bradley, comparing the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 request to implement a new map before the 2024 elections, and hold early special elections for representatives not up for election in 2024, to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Packard said her clients, Democratic lawmakers who would face special elections if the court were to side with the plaintiffs, were \u8220\'20\'1Cready, willing, and able\u8221\'20\'1D to face re-election and that other legislators should be willing as well\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A conservative judge on Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court questioned the timing of a lawsuit challenging the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislative districts as oral arguments got under way Tuesday in a much-watched case over gerrymandering.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Alice Herman, who is in the courtroom, reports that Mark Gaber, an attorney representing \uc2 Campaign Legal Center\uc2 , laid out one of the plaintiff\u8217\'20\'19s central arguments: that non-contiguous districts in the state are unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 Almost immediately, conservative judge Rebecca Bradley interrupted Gaber to question the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 timing in bringing the case forward.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhere were your clients two years ago?\u8221\'20\'1D she asked, pointing to the fact that the ideological sway of the court flipped when Janet Protasiewicz, a liberal judge, was elected this year. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re seeking to overturn 50 years of precedent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gaber disputedthe case was brought in a partisan manner, arguing that the state constitution requires contiguous districts \u8211\'20\'13 a non-partisan requirement. The argument that 75 of the state\u8217\'20\'19s 132 districts are non-contiguous is at the heart of the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 case against the gerrymandered maps.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson took a trip to visit \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida on Monday night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/11/20/politics/johnson-trump-mar-a-lago/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN is reporting}}}\uc2 , a pilgrimage similar to the one that exposed predecessor Kevin McCarthy to criticism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMaga Mike\u8221\'20\'1D, as some have branded the Louisiana Republican for his unswerving loyalty to the former president, has endorsed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign for the party\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential nomination, so a \u8220\'20\'1Ckiss the ring\u8221\'20\'1D visit to Mar-a-Lago was not entirely unexpected.\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson. Photograph: Shawn Thew/\uc2 EPA\uc2 -EFE/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 It is not known what the pair discussed, CNN says. But the trip has echoes of former speaker and then minority leader McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/04/mcarthy-democracy-congress-politics-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cgroveling\u8221\'20\'1D visit to see Trump}}}\uc2  in January 2021, days after condemning him for sparking the deadly 6 January Capitol riot.\par \par \uc2 With his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mike-johnson-donald-trump-2024-c0d8304f44bd7158415ac80673eb8c7f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsement of Trump}}}\uc2 , Johnson, who voted against certifying the 2020 election results, has gone even further than McCarthy did in backing the twice-impeached ex-president, who is currently facing dozens of charges in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple cases against him}}}\uc2  around the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m all in for President Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson told CNBC, adding he was \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the closest allies that President Trump had in Congress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine and Alice Herman are following oral arguments this morning at the Wisconsin supreme court, where the seven justices will adjudicate one of the most closely-watched gerrymandering cases this year.\par \par \uc2 The case is a challenge to the maps for Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s state legislature, which are so heavily distorted in favor of Republicans that it is all but impossible for Democrats to win a majority.\par \par \uc2 Republicans took over the legislature in 2010, and drew maps that have cemented their majority ever since. Democrats won statewide elections in the state in 2018, 2020, and 2022, but Republicans have never had fewer than 60 seats in the state assembly. State senate districts must be comprised of three assembly districts in Wisconsin, so any gerrymandering in the assembly carries over to the senate.\par \par \uc2 enltrWisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Supreme Court hears oral argument on Tuesday in a case that could bring an end to what may be the most gerrymandered maps in the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fRx9J2KnRd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/fRx9J2KnRd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1726617156450746786?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The challengers want the court to strike down the maps and order new elections in all 132 of the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislative districts in 2024.\par \par \uc2 They note that 75 of Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s 132 legislative districts are non-contiguous, a clear violation of a state constitutional requirement that says all districts need to be contiguous. The districts, Republicans argue, are contiguous because even with \u8220\'20\'1Cislands\u8221\'20\'1D they still keep municipalities whole.\par \par \uc2 The challengers also argue that the process by which the supreme court picked the current maps violated the separation of powers because the panel chose one the Democratic governor had vetoed.\par \par \uc2 Oral arguments have just begun. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you updates as we get them.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/21/wisconsin-supreme-court-redistricting-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin supreme court to hear high-stakes case challenging legislative maps}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Grifters, frauds and con men willing to subvert the Constitution and long-established constitutional principles for the whims of political expediency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s how a group of prominent conservative lawyers sees the legal team \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has surrounded himself with as the former president plots a return to the White House next year.\par \par \uc2 Warning of an unprecedented threat to democracy from a Trump second term, and the worsening of a \u8220\'20\'1Clegal emergency\u8221\'20\'1D set in motion by his unprecedented efforts to overturn his 2020 defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , they have founded a group called the Society for the Rule of Law Institute, which they say is needed \u8220\'20\'1Cto bring sanity back to conservative lawyering and jurisprudence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Barbara Comstock\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 A trio of lawyers form the new group\u8217\'20\'19s board. They are George Conway, ex-husband to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former senior adviser Kellyanne Conway; \uc2 J Michael Luttig\uc2 , formerly a US appeals court judge; and Republican former Virginia congresswoman \uc2 Barbara Comstock\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They set out their case Tuesday in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/21/opinion/trump-lawyers-constitution-democracy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hard-hitting editorial}}}\uc2  in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 American democracy, the Constitution and the rule of law are the righteous causes of our times, and the nation\u8217\'20\'19s legal profession is obligated to support them. But with the acquiescence of the larger conservative legal movement, these pillars of our system of governance are increasingly in peril. The dangers will only grow should \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  be returned to the White House next November.\par \par \uc2 Recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/11/13/trump-loyalists-2024-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporting}}}\uc2  about plans for a second Trump presidency are frightening. He would stock his administration with partisan loyalists committed to fast-tracking his agenda and sidestepping - if not circumventing altogether - existing laws and long-established legal norms.\par \par \uc2 They cite Trump\u8217\'20\'19s already publicized plans to appoint public officials investigate and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/11/donald-trump-president-2024-biden-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exact retribution}}}\uc2  against his political opponents; remove federal public servants at will; and invoke special powers to seize control of First Amendment-protected activities, criminal justice, elections, immigration and more.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1Cguest essay\u8221\'20\'1D continues with praise for the few lawyers in the first Trump administration who stood up to his excesses, and a warning that legal checks and balances would be largely absent from his second:\par \par \uc2 Alarming is the growing crowd of grifters, frauds and con men willing to subvert the Constitution and long-established constitutional principles for the whims of political expediency.\par \par \uc2 The actions of these conservative Republican lawyers are increasingly becoming the new normal. Any legal movement that could foment such a constitutional abdication and attract a sufficient number of lawyers willing to advocate its unlawful causes is ripe for a major reckoning.\par \par \uc2 Our country is in a constitutional emergency, if not a constitutional crisis.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Conservative lawyers: another Trump presidency would be perilous for democracy\par \par \uc2 Good morning US politics blog readers! A group of prominent conservative lawyers is warning that democracy would be placed in unprecedented peril if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returns to the White House next year, and that legal checks and balances on his conduct would be largely absent if he wins a second term.\par \par \uc2 The dire predictions come in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/21/opinion/trump-lawyers-constitution-democracy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hard-hitting opinion piece}}}\uc2  Tuesday in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump, the former president and runaway leader for the Republican 2024 nomination, has surrounded himself with \u8220\'20\'1Cgrowing crowd of grifters, frauds and con men willing to subvert the Constitution and long-established constitutional principles for the whims of political expediency,\u8221\'20\'1D they say, creating an unprecedented \u8220\'20\'1Clegal emergency\u8221\'20\'1D worsened by their support of his unsuccessful efforts to overturn his 2020 election defeat.\par \par \uc2 The authors, who include George Conway, ex-husband to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former senior adviser Kellyanne Conway, have formed an attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 group called the Society for the Rule of Law Institute, which they say is needed \u8220\'20\'1Cto bring sanity back to conservative lawyering and jurisprudence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have a closer look at that coming up.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today on a quiet pre-Thanksgiving Tuesday in Washington DC:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will host a White House meeting over efforts to stop the flow of fentanyl into the US this morning, before he and first lady Jill Biden head for their Thanksgiving break in Nantucket.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no action in Congress, but an election in Utah\u8217\'20\'19s 2nd congressional district Tuesday will restore the House to its full complement of 435 members since Democrat David Cicilline of Rhode Island resigned in May. Republican Celeste Maloy is expected to handily beat Democratic state senator Kathleen Riebe.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin \u8217\'20\'19s supreme court will hear oral argument in a high-stakes lawsuit seeking to strike down the maps for the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislature. The result could bring an end to what may be the most gerrymandered districts in the US. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/21/wisconsin-supreme-court-redistricting-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read more}}}\uc2  about that here.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231121ejbl002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
