\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ohio considers tax credits for anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  centers after historic vote\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 515 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 November 2023\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bill is being considered a week after Ohioans voted to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in state constitution\par \par \uc2 A week after Ohioans voted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enshrine \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights in the state constitution}}}\uc2 , members of the state legislature are considering a bill that would give tax credits for donations to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facilities.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Ohio senate finance committee discussed a bill from the state senator Sandra O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, a Republican, who proposed that individuals who give to \u8220\'20\'1Cqualifying pregnancy resource centers\u8221\'20\'1D may be eligible for tax credits, at a cost of up to $10m to Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  counseling centers \u8211\'20\'13 which are also known as crisis pregnancy centers \u8211\'20\'13 offer free services to pregnant women, are frequently faith-based and aim to convince people to continue their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 They have also been accused of attempting to mislead the people who walk through their doors. Because these centers are often located next to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and have names like \u8220\'20\'1CBirth Choice\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1CWoman\u8217\'20\'19s Choice\u8221\'20\'1D, critics say they purposely lead people seeking abortions to enter them by accident and then give them inaccurate information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://counterhate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/Profiting-from-Deceit-CCDH-FINAL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report for the Center for Countering Digital Hate}}}\uc2 , which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and analyzed 188 centers, found that more than 70% used some kind of misleading technique in their digital advertising. Almost 40% did not say on their homepage that they do not provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while 10% exaggerated the mental health risks of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and 7% exaggerated the possibility of complications in future pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 In the committee meeting, O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said that there are more than 175 \u8220\'20\'1Cpregnancy resource centers\u8221\'20\'1D in Ohio. (Her bill would specifically apply to donations to nonprofit centers.) More than 2,500 centers now dot the US; they outnumber \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics three to one.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir work and care day in and day out shows their commitment to serving women and families around them, and serving the lives of the unborn,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said. \u8220\'20\'1CA tax credit is the least we can do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many states have long funded these centers. After the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade last year, that funding increased in multiple states; Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbc4i.com/news/local-news/ohio-lawmakers-double-available-funds-for-crisis-pregnancy-centers/#:~:text=Signed%20by%20Gov.,with%20an%20anti%2Dabortion%20lens."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike DeWine, recently increased}}}\uc2  the two-year budget for a program that awards grant money to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  centers from $6m to $14m.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights amendment in Ohio, some Republicans in the Ohio state legislature have said that they will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/11/ohio-republicans-move-to-exclude-judges-interpreting-abortion-rights-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduce legislation}}}\uc2  to remove judges\u8217\'20\'19 ability to interpret the new amendment. Instead, they aim to hand that power back to the state legislature \u8211\'20\'13 which is controlled by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 The state senator Jerry Cirino, a Republican, seemed to reference the vote during the Tuesday hearing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need more of these centers because women are in crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D Cirino said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn light of recent initiatives at the polls, I should say, I think we need to make sure that we are reaching out to women that are in these situations and figuring out how we can help them more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231116ejbg001h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
