\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Pussy Riot founder protests Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s ban on nearly all abortions\b0\par\par\uc2 Audra Heinrichs \par \uc2 939 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 November 2023\par 20:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nadya Tolokonnikova performed in front of the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court and debuted the group\u8217\'20\'19s new single, God Save \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Pussy Riot\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2022/mar/08/pussy-riot-nadya-tolokonnikova-interview-putin-nfts-russian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nadya Tolokonnikova}}}\uc2  staged a performance art protest for reproductive rights on the steps of the Indiana supreme court building on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Joined by students and faculty from \uc2 Indiana University\uc2 , the longtime activist and artist said that the demonstration was prompted by both Tolokonnikova\u8217\'20\'19s frustration with the current state of reproductive rights in the state and the university\u8217\'20\'19s invitation for her to participate in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://do317.com/events/2023/11/13/pussy-riot-light-and-truth-tickets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ticketed Q&A }}}\uc2  with students about authoritarianism and activism\u8217\'20\'19s intersection with art.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am a great believer that you should combine theory and practice,\u8221\'20\'1D Tolokonnikova said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s fine to talk, but I called for the students and participants of the conversation to join me for a live performance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Featuring a 10ft-tall inflatable vagina, plumes of hot pink smoke, and the Russian feminist protest and performance art collective\u8217\'20\'19 signature balaclavas, Tolokonnikova said Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s action was an homage to Pussy Riot\u8217\'20\'19s previous actions and her mentor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2023/nov/06/women-ruled-world-judy-chicago-herstory-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feminist artist Judy Chicago}}}\uc2 , who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2013/oct/17/judy-chicago-best-photograph-woman-smoke"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 often deployed smoke}}}\uc2  to demonstrate taking up a space. God Save \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a new Pussy Riot song performed by Tolokonnikova, was also debuted at the demonstration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very important to go to places where people like me are a minority and they need help,\u8221\'20\'1D Tolokonnikova said of the importance of the protest\u8217\'20\'19s location \u8211\'20\'13 a state where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now banned. \u8220\'20\'1CI could come to New York, but it\u8217\'20\'19s like preaching to the choir, whereas, if you go to Texas, Alabama or Indiana, I feel like we can make a bigger difference. I\u8217\'20\'19m making a contribution in the way that I know how.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Maria Bucur-Deckard, a gender studies professor at the University of Indiana who moderated Tolokonnikova\u8217\'20\'19s conversation with students on Monday evening, said she has noted a swell in student-led protests and a marked interest in the country\u8217\'20\'19s complicated history with reproductive justice since \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/30/indiana-abortion-ban-court-clears-way"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlawed}}}\uc2  in Indiana in which a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 total ban after conception}}}\uc2  took effect in August.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI see students being more and more mobilized around this,\u8221\'20\'1D Bucur-Deckard said. \u8220\'20\'1CA course I\u8217\'20\'19m teaching on international feminist debate has a section on reproductive rights, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve made that a big feature because students have asked for it. They want to understand what\u8217\'20\'19s going on, where this is coming from and why it\u8217\'20\'19s happening now. I\u8217\'20\'19ve offered them some very sobering examples of the cost of what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Indiana now in terms of what the state will look like 10 years from now, for instance. The students have been listening and they\u8217\'20\'19re concerned. They want to see change happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tolokonnikova\u8217\'20\'19s protest took place just days after the Indiana supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s reprimand of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/18/indiana-attorney-general-rokita-rape-abortion-lawsuit-iu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican attorney general, Todd Rokita}}}\uc2 , for statements he made about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/indiana-abortion-ruling-caitlin-bernard-medical-license"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dr Caitlin Bernard}}}\uc2 , the Indiana obstetrician-gynecologist who performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a 10-year-old rape victim who traveled to the state from Ohio after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade. In July 2022, Rokita referred to Bernard as an \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indystar.com/story/news/politics/2023/11/02/todd-rokita-indiana-attorney-general-reprimand-supreme-court-abortion-caitlin-bernard/71421463007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  activist acting as a doctor}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D on Fox News. Rokita\u8217\'20\'19s comments were part of a national media firestorm during which Bernard was also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/5/26/us-doctor-reprimanded-fined-for-talking-about-childs-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicly reprimanded}}}\uc2  for speaking about the case and vilified by conservatives. Rokita has since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/18/indiana-attorney-general-rokita-rape-abortion-lawsuit-iu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2 Indiana University Health\uc2 , the largest hospital system in the state, alleging that it mishandled the 10-year-old rape victim\u8217\'20\'19s case.\par \par \uc2 At the same time last week, the University of Indiana {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/11/09/1211949718/the-kinsey-institute-faces-possible-separation-from-indiana-university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made headlines}}}\uc2  as the board of trustees said it could soon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://subscribe.indystar.com/restricted?return=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.indystar.com%2Fstory%2Fnews%2Feducation%2F2023%2F11%2F10%2Fkinsey-institute-indiana-university-board-of-trustees-human-sexuality-research%2F71516694007%2F&reg=true&sltsgmt=TBP_2meter_then_2_post_reg_B&gps-source=CPROADBLOCKDH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vote to sever ties}}}\uc2  with the Kinsey Institute, a longtime partner of the school. Storied for its study of human sexuality since 1947, the Kinsey Institute recently suffered a blow after the Republican representative Lorissa Sweet claimed it was conducting sexual experiments on children. State lawmakers \u8211\'20\'13 led by Sweet \u8211\'20\'13 soon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indystar.com/story/news/politics/2023/02/23/indiana-house-strips-state-dollars-from-indiana-university-kinsey-institute/69933555007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed an amendment}}}\uc2  that effectively blocked the institute\u8217\'20\'19s public funding. This news, too, is now weighing heavily on some students.\par \par \uc2 Zoe Bardon, a gender studies student who participated in the protest, said that she hopes Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s action draws attention to the difficulties of being a woman and \u8220\'20\'1Cjust a person in general\u8221\'20\'1D in the state of Indiana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do a lot of political organizing in voter registration, and trying to convince young people to vote in the first place is so difficult when you have people in power like \uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Bardon said, citing that in 2022 the state had the nation\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://policyinstitute.iu.edu/doc/maternal-mortality-brief.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third highest maternal mortality}}}\uc2  rate. \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels like you can\u8217\'20\'19t make a difference at some point. This is my last year and my plan beyond graduation is to move out of Indiana. I know that\u8217\'20\'19s the case for a lot of students. We cannot see ourselves living, starting our careers and raising families in Indiana when we know that we won\u8217\'20\'19t have access to healthcare if nothing changes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s discouraging.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to see, as a state, a brain drain of a lot of talented individuals who feel like Indiana is a hostile environment for a lot of people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bucur-Deckard said she hopes students realize in the continued fight for reproductive rights in the state that \u8220\'20\'1Cnot speaking out means that you\u8217\'20\'19re letting somebody else define your interests.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not what I\u8217\'20\'19m hoping young people in Indiana want to do,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231114ejbe002e8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
