\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Judge blocks Idaho law stopping adults from helping minors seeking  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 667 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 November 2023\par 21:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The law was first major push since fall of Roe to explicitly block people from crossing state lines to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has temporarily blocked an Idaho law that prohibits adults from helping minors get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still prohibited in Idaho with very narrow exceptions, this week\u8217\'20\'19s court order marks a victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates in the state who say the now-blocked law is unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/12/idaho-abortion-lawsuit-minors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This lawsuit}}}\uc2  is not about the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is about much more,\u8221\'20\'1D said US district magistrate Debora K Grasham in her order this week. \u8220\'20\'1CNamely, long-standing and well-recognized fundamental rights of freedom of speech, expression, due process, and parental rights. These are not competing rights, nor are they at odds.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under the statute, anyone who helps a minor get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be sentenced to two or five years in prison. Adults are also prohibited from \u8220\'20\'1Crecruiting\u8221\'20\'1D a pregnant minor, a term that reproductive justice advocates said is confusing and vague.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe judge seemed to agree that this is a confusing Idaho law that does not draw clear lines between what is legal and what will land you in prison,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kelly O\u8217\'20\'19Neill, a lawyer at Legal Voice, an advocacy group representing the plaintiffs challenging the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Idaho}}}\uc2  statute.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe could not get a clear answer on what \u8216\'20\'18recruiting\u8217\'20\'19 actually means,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Neill added.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/idaho-abortion-trafficking-law-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Signed by the governor, Brad Little, in April}}}\uc2 , the controversial law marked the first major push since the fall of Roe v Wade to explicitly block people from traveling across state lines to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. Idaho borders Oregon and Washington, two states where the procedure is legal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe big win here is being able to give out information, to tell people their full range of options, then give them the resources to make the decision about a pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lourdes Matsumoto, the only individual plaintiff in the case.\par \par \uc2 Matsumoto is an Idaho attorney who works with survivors of domestic and sexual violence, many of whom are minors.\par \par \uc2 Before the law\u8217\'20\'19s passage in April, she encountered cases where a child would be impregnated through rape \u8220\'20\'1Croughly once per month\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since the law\u8217\'20\'19s passage, pregnant victims have been more hesitant about reaching out for help and information, according to Matsumoto. The Idaho law created a culture of fear and confusion, restricting Matsumoto\u8217\'20\'19s ability to tell vulnerable young people about reproductive health resources.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDomestic violence shelters, doctors who work with these young pregnant patients, advocates, everyone is more protected thanks to this order,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can look at the 17-year-old girl standing in front of you and say, \u8216\'20\'18Here are all the options available to you as a person in Idaho, here\u8217\'20\'19s all the ways I can support you.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many Idaho doctors vocalized concerns about the statute earlier this year, before the law\u8217\'20\'19s passage. Bonner General Health, a hospital in northern Idaho, said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bonnergeneral.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Bonner-General-Health-Press-Release-Closure-of-LD-3.17.2023.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement released last March}}}\uc2  that it could no longer offer labor and delivery services, citing a shortage of doctors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Idaho Legislature continues to introduce and pass bills that criminalize physicians for medical care nationally recognized as the standard of care,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said. \u8220\'20\'1CHighly respected, talented physicians are leaving. Recruiting replacements will be extraordinarily difficult.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Matsumoto and the other plaintiffs hope this week\u8217\'20\'19s court order will offer doctors some peace of mind. Still, she worried about what might happen in January, when the Idaho legislature will reconvene.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI worry that the legislature might go ahead and amend the statute, addressing some of the concerns that the judge talked about, adding \u8216\'20\'18clarity\u8217\'20\'19 but making the law even more draconian,\u8221\'20\'1D Matsumoto said, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates in Idaho will keep a close eye on the statehouse come January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am so relieved and thrilled about the injunction, but this was one battle, not the war,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231111ejbb0013h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
