\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 West Virginia Democratic senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  will not seek re-election in 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 6,409 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 November 2023\par 15:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read the full report on Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s announcement here:Manchin will not seek re-election in 2024\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 already difficult road to keeping their Senate majority in next year\u8217\'20\'19s elections just got even more difficult after West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Joe Manchin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d357c8f08c3ba45a4ffed#block-654d357c8f08c3ba45a4ffed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  he would not run again. He would have faced a tough re-election contest in the deeply red state and the GOP is almost certain to claim the seat. Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d3d928f08c3ba45a50038#block-654d3d928f08c3ba45a50038"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 must now focus}}}\uc2  on winning key elections in Ohio, Montana, Arizona and a handful of swing states, along with the White House, if they want to control Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber. Meanwhile, the \uc2 US government\uc2  is once again {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d19888f08f02e9fec98b3#block-654d19888f08f02e9fec98b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 days away}}}\uc2  from shutting down, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no sign of an agreement in Congress to prevent it. House Speaker Mike Johnson reportedly wants a short-term measure that funds the government for varying periods of time, though many lawmakers view that as excessively complex, and the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d21418f08f02e9fec9952#block-654d21418f08f02e9fec9952"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  Democrats will not support it.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d25c08f08a95ef07eb61f#block-654d25c08f08a95ef07eb61f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there should be}}}\uc2  consequences for \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , the Republican lawmaker who led the charge to remove him as speaker of the House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d07d78f08a95ef07eb465#block-654d07d78f08a95ef07eb465"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 squabbled}}}\uc2  with a Fox News reporter over his age, polling and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654cfd8f8f08c3ba45a4fca7#block-654cfd8f8f08c3ba45a4fca7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended}}}\uc2  his attacks on fellow Republican presidential candidate Nikki Haley in last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Progressive congresswoman Cori Bush{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d322b8f08f02e9fec99ef#block-654d322b8f08f02e9fec99ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  Israel\u8217\'20\'19s decision to pause its bombing campaign in Gaza for brief periods every day \u8220\'20\'1Cheartless\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ohio \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d4a678f08c3ba45a5008a#block-654d4a678f08c3ba45a5008a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 imperiled}}}\uc2  Democratic senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  appealed for donations in the wake of Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s decision to step down.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In the statement announcing he would end his Senate career, \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1CI will not be running for re-election to the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 , but what I will be doing is traveling the country and speaking out to see if there is an interest in creating a movement to mobilize the middle and bring Americans together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That line stoked speculation he could launch a third-party presidential run next year, perhaps with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/04/no-labels-group-democrats-2024-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the help of centrist group No Labels}}}\uc2 . Democrats have been fretting over that possibility for months, as a Manchin candidacy could swing voters away from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , whose re-election campaign has been dogged by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-poll-democrats-swing-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worrying poll numbers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the Capitol, Politico says some of Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s counterparts don\u8217\'20\'19t believe he has presidential ambitions:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Tim Kaine, who is close to Manchin, says he doesn't think Manchin will run for POTUS.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo. I don\u8217\'20\'19t have any advice to give him\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another Dem source doubts he'll run, too.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Burgess Everett (@burgessev) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1722729839738617873?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There are two main Republicans vying for West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat, which Democrat \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  just said he would not stand for again.\par \par \uc2 The first is governor \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/aug/05/donald-trump-rallies-supporters-west-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 2017}}}\uc2  left the Democratic party and joined the GOP at a rally for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSenator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and I have not always agreed on policy and politics, but we\u8217\'20\'19re both lifelong West Virginians who love this state beyond belief, and I respect and thank him for his many years of public service,\u8221\'20\'1D Justice said in a statement after Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s announcement.\par \par \uc2 The second is Alex Mooney, a fifth term House lawmaker representing the northern half of the state. He is what he had to say about Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s departure:\par \par \uc2 enltrRead my campaign\u8217\'20\'19s reaction to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeManchinWV?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JoeManchinWV}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s latest announcement to not seek re-election: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IhcTEsdVId"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IhcTEsdVId}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alex Mooney (@MooneyforWV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MooneyforWV/status/1722712813456470131?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s primary elections are scheduled for 14 May of next year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Minutes after \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  announced he would not run for re-election, Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  made a veiled reference to the West Virginia senator\u8217\'20\'19s decision:\par \par \uc2 enltrIt's never been more clear that we need to win in Ohio. Chip in now: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BAY5gEUx9U"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/BAY5gEUx9U}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  (@SherrodBrown) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SherrodBrown/status/1722705605477953723?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Brown represents Ohio, which has supported Republican candidates in the past two presidential elections, albeit by a much smaller percentage than West Virginia. With Manchin gone and almost certain to be replaced by a Republican, Brown\u8217\'20\'19s victory next year is essential if the party has any chance of staying in the majority in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Following \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision not to seek re-election, the Cook Political Report has changed its rating of the race to \u8220\'20\'1Csolid Republican\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the same rating given to Senate races in other deep-red states like Nebraska, Tennessee and Wyoming:\par \par \uc2 enltrWith Manchin's retirement announcement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/WVSen?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WVSen}}}\uc2  will move to Solid Republican in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CookPolitical?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CookPolitical}}}\uc2  ratings. Best news GOP has gotten yet in Senate fight, as Dems now can only afford to lose one seat to keep majority (assuming they hold the WH)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jessica Taylor (@JessicaTaylor) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JessicaTaylor/status/1722706123034116441?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 In the 2020 election, West Virginia voted more than 68% for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his second biggest-margin of victory after Wyoming.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  first arrived in the Senate in 2010 after a stint as West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s governor, but the peak of his political power came in the first two years of the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 Democrats held a 50-seat majority in the Senate those two years, meaning the party had to vote unanimously on legislation that Republicans would not support. While Manchin backed most of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s agenda, he flexed his muscles in the negotiations over Build Back Better, an expansive plan to fight climate change and invest in a host of social programs that the president wanted approved.\par \par \uc2 Manchin opposed several of its measure, including continuing the expanded child tax credit that was credited with cutting child poverty in half in 2021. Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , then a member of the Democratic party, also rejected tax changes to offset some of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s costs. Negotiations over the legislation dragged all through 2021 and into 2022, and appeared to have stalled completely by that summer.\par \par \uc2 Then, suddenly, Manchin and the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  announced they had reached an agreement on a different bill called the Inflation Reduction Act, which included some measures to fight climate change and lower prescription drug costs, but lacked some of Build Back Better\u8217\'20\'19s most expansive proposals.\par \par \uc2 For climate activists who blamed the West Virginia senator and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/sep/30/joe-manchin-climate-coal-baron-stocks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coal businessman}}}\uc2  for defanging attempts to lower America\u8217\'20\'19s carbon emissions, it was a surprising change in course. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/oliver-milman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Milman}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s piece from last year analyzing Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s role in the agreement:\par \par \uc2 Climate advocates reacted with surprise and delight to \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/manchin-deal-democrats-schumer-reconciliation-bill-climate-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  to back a sweeping bill to combat the climate crisis, with analysts predicting the legislation will bring the US close to its target of slashing planet-heating emissions.\par \par \uc2 The West Virginia senator, who has made millions from his ownership of a coal-trading company, had seemingly thwarted \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hopes of passing meaningful climate legislation \u8211\'20\'13 only to reveal on Wednesday his support for a $369bn package to support renewable energy and electric vehicle rollout.\par \par \uc2 The move by the centrist Democrat shocked many of Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s colleagues, who despaired after more than 18 months of seemingly fruitless negotiations with the lawmaker, a crucial vote in an evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHoly shit,\u8221\'20\'1D tweeted \uc2 Tina Smith\uc2 , a Democrat from Minnesota. \u8220\'20\'1CStunned, but in a good way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Should the bill pass both chambers of Congress and be signed by Biden, it will be the biggest and arguably first piece of climate legislation ever enacted by the US. The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest historical carbon polluter has repeatedly failed to act on the climate crisis due to missed opportunities, staunch Republican opposition and the machinations of the fossil fuel lobby.\par \par \uc2 The climate spending, part of a broader bill called the Inflation Reduction Act, \u8220\'20\'1Chas the potential to be a historic turning point\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Al Gore\uc2 , the former vice-president.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/28/joe-manchin-climate-bill-fossil-fuels-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Activists surprised and relieved at Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s decision to back climate bill}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Manchin exit makes Democrats' quest to keep Senate majority even harder\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision not to seek re-election makes Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 quest to preserve their majority in the Senate even more difficult.\par \par \uc2 Manchin was one of three Democratic senators representing red states who are facing voters next year, and the party is not viewed as having a strong replacement candidate in West Virginia, a deeply Republican state.\par \par \uc2 The focus now shifts to Montana\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  and Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , both of whom have said they will stand again, but face difficult paths to victory. There is also the question of whether \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , an independent who caucuses with Democrats, will stand again in purple state Arizona, or if she will be replaced by a Democrat. The GOP may also launch offensives against incumbent Democratic senators in swing states Nevada, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, and try to win the open Senate seat in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Even if Democrats fail in West Virginia but win all the other races, they could still lose their Senate majority. That best-case scenario would give the party only 50 seats, one short of a majority, and control of the chamber would come down to whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wins re-election, or is replaced by a Republican.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow hours-long pauses to its bombing campaign in Gaza is \u8220\'20\'1Cheartless\u8221\'20\'1D and falls far short of what is necessary to protect civilian life in the territory, said Congresswoman \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2 , a Missouri Democrat who is the lead sponsor of a ceasefire resolution.\par \par \uc2 The White House said on Thursday that Israel has agreed to four-hour daily humanitarian pauses in its bombardment of northern Gaza, part of a negotiated deal to allow aid and assistance to flow to the enclave\u8217\'20\'19s increasingly desperate population of 2.3 million.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow dare we treat humans in that way,\u8221\'20\'1D Bush said, her voice rising with anger. \u8220\'20\'1CHow dare we be so careless and so inhumane and heartless to decide that four hours is enough time to get you some stuff so that you can live a little bit longer until the bombs hit. How dare we? How dare we treat humans as if we don\u8217\'20\'19t understand what it\u8217\'20\'19s like to be human.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not the way,\u8221\'20\'1D Bush added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want four hours. We don\u8217\'20\'19t want 16 hours. We don\u8217\'20\'19t want 22 hours. We want a ceasefire now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military has said it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/09/netanyahu-rejected-ceasefire-for-hostages-deal-in-gaza-sources-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not agreed to a ceasefire}}}\uc2  but that it will continue to allow \u8220\'20\'1Ctactical, local pauses\u8221\'20\'1D to let in humanitarian aid. It comes as Biden administration officials push Israel to agree for a longer stoppage in the fighting as part of an effort to free the hostages held by the militant group.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the prospect of a formal ceasefire on Thursday, Biden said that there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno possibility\u8221\'20\'1D at the moment.\par \par \uc2 His response angered a group of veterans gathered with Bush on Capitol Hill to call for an end to the hostilities. Drawing on their own recollections of war in Afghanistan and Iraq, they said peace and security could only be won through diplomacy.\par \par \uc2 Shaking with anger, Brittany Ramos DeBarros, a combat veteran and former army captain, addressed Biden directly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr President, you are the commander in chief of one of the most powerful militaries on the face of this planet in the history of the world,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHow can you be so powerful and so weak as to say that you are incapable of negotiating peace?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bush was also joined by congresswomen Summer Lee of Pennsylvania and Delia Ramirez of Illinois, who are among the 18 Democratic sponsors of the ceasefire legislation.\par \par \uc2 Bush vowed to keep up the pressure on the White House to advocate for a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf that is his position today, there is also a this afternoon and a tonight. There is a tomorrow. There is a Saturday and a Sunday,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI expect that there will be change. There will be change because \u8230\'20\'26 the people that elected this president are screaming out saying we want a ceasefire now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In response to the announcement from West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  that he will not seek Senate re-election in 2024, the National Republican Senatorial Committee said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe like our odds in West Virginia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 West Virginia's \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  will not seek Senate re-election\par \par \uc2 West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  has announced that he will not seek re-election in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released on Thursday, Manchin, who has held his Senate seat since 2010, said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter months of deliberation and long conversations with my family, I believe in my heart of hearts that I have accomplished what I set out to do for West Virginia. I have made one of the toughest decisions of my life and decided that I will not be running for re-election to the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 , but what I will be doing is traveling the country and speaking out to see if there is an interest in creating a movement to mobilize the middle and bring Americans together.\par \par \uc2 To the West Virginians who have put their trust in me and fought side by side to make our state better \u8211\'20\'13 it has been an honor of my life to serve you. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Every incentive in Washington is designed to make our politics extreme. The growing divide between Democrats and Republicans is paralyzing Congress and worsening our nation\u8217\'20\'19s problems. The majority of Americans are just plain worn out\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Public service has and continues to drive me every day. That is the vow that I made to my father 40 years ago, and I intend to keep that vow until my dying day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrTo the West Virginians who have put their trust in me and fought side by side to make our state better \u8211\'20\'13 it has been an honor of my life to serve you. Thank you. My statement on my political future: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dz8JuXAyTL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dz8JuXAyTL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  (@Sen_JoeManchin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Sen_JoeManchin/status/1722698734910210420?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  said that \u8220\'20\'1Cit feels good to get in the game\u8221\'20\'1D after endorsing Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 After seven months of hosting Republican presidential candidates in Iowa, Gov. \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  said it \u8220\'20\'1Cfeels good to get in the game\u8221\'20\'1D with her endorsement of of Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the popular Iowa governor declined to say whether other candidates should concede and throw their support behind him as well, even as she acknowledged that a wider field could advantage former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt some point, if we don\u8217\'20\'19t narrow the field, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be hard to... maybe, you know, that helps Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Reynolds said in an interview with \uc2 The Associated Press\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut I think that is for them to decide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In making the endorsement earlier this week, Reynolds broke with a longstanding tradition of Iowa governors staying neutral in their party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential contests, the first in the GOP nomination calendar\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Still, Reynolds said DeSantis is best poised for victory in the general election, a race she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t think Trump can win without attracting voters beyond his base. DeSantis \u8220\'20\'1Cwon in demographics that Republicans have never really won in Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic representative \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  has responded to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s agreement to implement a four-hour humanitarian pause in Gaza daily, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that we get a break for four hours. A break so that we can have food\u8230\'20\'26 And then we go back to bombing? So absolutely not four hours\u8230\'20\'26 What we need is to stop the bombing\u8230\'20\'26 We want a ceasefire now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  (D-MO) on Israel agreeing to implement a four-hour humanitarian pause in Gaza each day:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that we get a break for four hours \u8230\'20\'26 What we need is to stop the bombing \u8230\'20\'26 We don't want four hours \u8230\'20\'26 We want a ceasefire now.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FcgaVrBZbL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FcgaVrBZbL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722688530315362327?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government\uc2  is once again {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d19888f08f02e9fec98b3#block-654d19888f08f02e9fec98b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 days away}}}\uc2  from shutting down, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no sign of an agreement in Congress to prevent it. House Speaker Mike Johnson reportedly wants a short-term measure that funds the government for varying periods of time, though many lawmakers view that as excessively complex, and the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d21418f08f02e9fec9952#block-654d21418f08f02e9fec9952"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  Democrats will not support it. Outside of Washington DC, reproductive rights advocates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654cdcb08f0898cc3cb04466#block-654cdcb08f0898cc3cb04466"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are looking}}}\uc2  to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot in several states nationwide, after voters in red-leaning Ohio on Tuesday approved a constitutional amendment protecting the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d25c08f08a95ef07eb61f#block-654d25c08f08a95ef07eb61f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there should be}}}\uc2  consequences for \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , the Republican lawmaker who led the charge to remove him as speaker of the House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654d07d78f08a95ef07eb465#block-654d07d78f08a95ef07eb465"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 squabbled}}}\uc2  with a Fox News reporter over his age, polling and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/09/biden-trump-latest-updates-abortion-votes-swing-states-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-654cfd8f8f08c3ba45a4fca7#block-654cfd8f8f08c3ba45a4fca7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended}}}\uc2  his attacks on fellow Republican presidential candidate Nikki Haley in last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking of Kevin McCarthy, CNN sat down with the former House speaker, who called for \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , the ringleader of the successful effort to remove him from his job, to face consequences:\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mkraju}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , you've been mentioning a lot. How much would the Republican Party benefit if he were no longer a member of the House, in your opinion?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rep. Kevin McCarthy (R-CA): \u8220\'20\'1CTremendously.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UgagJJnkWe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UgagJJnkWe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722679917005930785?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Most House Republicans supported McCarthy staying on as speaker, but he was removed thanks to the votes of Gaetz and seven other Republicans, as well as the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Some House lawmakers have proposed changing the rules of the chamber to prevent such a vote from occurring again, or even expelling Gaetz from the House Republican Conference. No decision on that has yet been made.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A solution to the government shutdown threat that Republican House speaker Mike Johnson is reportedly thinking about is a so-called \u8220\'20\'1Claddered CR\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s code for a continuing resolution that would fund the government over the short term, but with the funding expiring at different times. House lawmakers on both sides of the aisle worry that would be far too complex a proposition, and at his press conference today, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the Democratic minority leader, said his party would not support it:\par \par \uc2 enltrMinority Leader Jeffries on House GOP\u8217\'20\'19s proposed laddered CR:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost members of the House Republican conference have no idea what a laddered CR means\u8230\'20\'26The notion of a laddered CR is another extreme right-wing policy joyride\u8230\'20\'26and would only crash and burn the federal government.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YvBYDRiOeT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YvBYDRiOeT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722640301305557354?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The GOP controls the House but by a slim five-vote majority. The short-term funding bill that Kevin McCarthy succeeded in getting approved in September (which resulted in him losing his job as speaker) passed with a mixture of both Democratic and Republican votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In comments to reporters earlier today, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  put the blame on the Republican-dominated House for again bringing the government to the brink of shutdown:\par \par \uc2 enltrReporter: \u8220\'20\'1CThe government shutdown \u8212\'20\'14 just 8 days \u8212\'20\'14 can you give us an update on what you\u8217\'20\'19re thinking on how to move past that?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 President Biden: \u8220\'20\'1CI wish the House would just get to work.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TWqGDOm3j7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TWqGDOm3j7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722654555358237170?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 He also mentioned his proposed $106bn security package, which would pay for assistance to Ukraine and Israel, as well as improved border security. House Republicans have shown a willingness to fund Israel, but are skeptical about Ukraine aid, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what will become of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s request.\par \par \uc2 The president is spending today in Illinois, where he\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  members and their president, Shawn Fain, and holding a campaign reception.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US government\uc2  days away from shutting down \u8211\'20\'13 again\par \par \uc2 Once again, the \uc2 US government\uc2  is a few days away from shutting down after its authorization to spend money expires, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no sign of an agreement in Congress to continue its operations.\par \par \uc2 The government is funded only through 17 November, and continuing its operations will require an agreement between both the Democratic-led Senate and the Republican-controlled House that is signed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . If this all sounds familiar, that\u8217\'20\'19s because it is \u8211\'20\'13 a shutdown was narrowly avoided at the end of September when the House\u8217\'20\'19s then-speaker Kevin McCarthy proposed a short-term funding measure that lacked the broad spending cuts conservative Republicans had demanded. Days later, he was voted out of the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s post by a small group of far-right lawmakers and Democrats, leading to Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s rise.\par \par \uc2 But Johnson faces much of the same obstacles in getting a funding measure passed that McCarthy did, even as many Republicans say they don\u8217\'20\'19t think there is anything to gain from government funding lapsing and a wide range of services being temporarily taken offline.\par \par \uc2 Fox News has a good primer on what may happen next. Take a look:\par \par \uc2 enltr1) There is a Looming Prospect Of a Possible Government Shutdown Next Week\par \par \uc2 House Speaker Mike Johnson (R-LA) did not put forth any plan to fund the government this week. Fox is told that was a mistake because the House basically lost a week of legislative time.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1722664520559063475?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr3) Now a senior House GOP leadership source says to expect legislative text for an interim spending spending bill sometime over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 Rank-and-file members are all over the map on what they want in an interim spending bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1722664523729866752?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr4) There are three things which can pass: A bipartisan Continuing Resolution. But that would inflame the right. This is why some members believe the honeymoon for Johnson has come to an end.\par \par \uc2 A \u8220\'20\'1Claddered\u8221\'20\'1D Continuing Resolution.\par \par \uc2 A straight CR with Israel aid attached.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1722664525487329648?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Israel was a major topic of discussion in last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate of Republican presidential candidates (excluding the frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who did not attend). The five candidates on stage all vowed to continue supporting the country, and backed varying degrees of hardline measures against \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war in Gaza and other foreign policy issues dominated Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s fiery third debate of Republican presidential hopefuls in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/miami"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miami}}}\uc2 . Candidates pledged wholehearted support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military response following last month\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks, and clashed over Ukraine, China and immigration.\par \par \uc2 The debate, minus {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , the runaway favorite for the party\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 nomination who was hosting his own private rally elsewhere in the area, was a more bitter affair than its predecessors in Wisconsin and California. Lively verbal sparring sometimes regressed into insults, with Nikki Haley at one point calling one of her rivals \u8220\'20\'1Cscum\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The candidates also grappled over immigration, the devastatingly bad night for Republicans in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s elections, and the party\u8217\'20\'19s staunchly anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/08/abortion-winning-issue-rights-victories-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysts say was the reason}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Discussion over Israel\u8217\'20\'19s actions in Gaza were, however, most prominent.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/08/republican-debate-miami-ron-desantis-nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Support for Israel and verbal sparring propel fiery third Republican debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Our live coverage of the invasion of Gaza continues, with today\u8217\'20\'19s main story being the White House\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that Israel will observe brief pauses in the fighting.\par \par \uc2 Read more about it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/09/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-who-disease-gaza-us-strikes-iran-site-syria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Hamas war live: Israel to begin daily four-hour pauses in fighting in northern Gaza, says White House}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 During Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic state representative Angie Nixon\u8217\'20\'19s tearful plea for a ceasefire in Gaza, she also asked how many dead Palestinians will be enough.\par \par \uc2 In response, an individual that has been reported to be Republican state representative Michelle Salzman, shouted, \u8220\'20\'1CAll of them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of my colleagues just said \u8216\'20\'18all of them.\u8217\'20\'19 Wow,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nixon in disbelief.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn tears, Florida State Rep {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AngieNixon?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AngieNixon}}}\uc2  begs for a ceasefire and asks how many dead Palestinians will be enough.\par \par \uc2 Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/michellesalzman?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @michellesalzman}}}\uc2  ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLHouseRep?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLHouseRep}}}\uc2  ) shouts out, "All of them." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0JfkIUH03b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0JfkIUH03b}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aamer Rahman (@aamer_rahman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aamer_rahman/status/1722641101528691193?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In response to a question from Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s Peter Doocy on why people should be more concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access than his age, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s a comparable comparsion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Doocy went on to ask Biden, \u8220\'20\'1CWhy do you think it is that you\u8217\'20\'19re trailing [Donald] Trump in all these swing states?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CBecause you don\u8217\'20\'19t read the polls\u8230\'20\'26 There are ten polls \u8211\'20\'13 eight of them I\u8217\'20\'19m beating him in those states. Eight of them. You guys only do two. CNN and \uc2 New York Times\uc2 . Check it out. We\u8217\'20\'19ll get you copies of all the [other] polls.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden and Peter Doocy have a moment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QUTQ1W9AmE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QUTQ1W9AmE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1722641938292109551?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hails \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  tentative deal: "Collective bargaining works"\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has hailed the tentative deal reached between \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  and television studios on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released by the White House on Thursday, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/11/09/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-the-tentative-agreement-between-the-alliance-of-motion-picture-and-television-producers-and-sag-aftra/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Collective bargaining works. I applaud \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  and \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  for working together in good faith towards an agreement that allows our entertainment industry to continue telling the stories of America.\par \par \uc2 When both sides come to the table to negotiate in earnest they can make businesses stronger and allow workers to secure pay and benefits that help them raise families and retire with dignity.\par \par \uc2 Over the last three years, workers have won historic victories that ensure record pay, record benefits, and an economy that grows from the middle out and bottom up. \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  members will have the final say on this contract, but the sacrifices they\u8217\'20\'19ve made will ensure a better future for them, their families, and all workers who deserve a fair share of the value they helped create.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  defends his heated exchange with Nikki Haley by mentioning \uc2 Hunter Biden\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  made an odd defense of his heated exchange last night with Nikki Haley by name-dropping \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaking on Fox News, Ramaswamy defended his actions during last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate in which he called Haley \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  in 3 inch heels\u8221\'20\'1D and mentioned her daughter on TikTok, while Haley called him \u8220\'20\'1Cscum.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe called me four-letter words in each of the last two debates\u8230\'20\'26 The reality is this \u8211\'20\'13 the Republican party has appropriately I think had scrutiny of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  for years. I mean, you know, not only the media but even Republican politicians, correctly,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ramaswamy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the last debate\u8230\'20\'26she said, \u8216\'20\'18I feel dumber every time I hear you speak\u8217\'20\'19\u8230\'20\'26 For using TikTok, the criticism wasn\u8217\'20\'19t of Nikki Haley\u8217\'20\'19s daughter. It was of Nikki Haley for having been completely oblivious to where the next generation of Americans is actually getting their information,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 enltrFox Business\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Stuart Varney\uc2  asks 2024 candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  about his tense exchanges with Nikki Haley at the GOP debate, including Haley calling him \u8220\'20\'1Cscum\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy did you go after her family? And her clothing? No woman\u8217\'20\'19s going to like that.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Gf592PHwZ2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Gf592PHwZ2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722639407201517628?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican presidential candidate and former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  got into a heated exchange with MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Mika Brzezinski\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In the Thursday interview, Brzezinski said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe can debate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but there isn\u8217\'20\'19t \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the ninth month.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Christie replied, \u8220\'20\'1CMika, you\u8217\'20\'19re the one who\u8217\'20\'19s not being honest. I did not say there was \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the ninth month. What I said was that the law in New Jersey and New York and Illinois and California permits it and you can\u8217\'20\'19t deny that that\u8217\'20\'19s the truth because it is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The conversation between Christie and Brzezinski continued to get heated and culminated when Christie said, \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t mess with me on the law, Mika.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response, Brzezinski said, \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t mess with me on how women feel about using the ninth month argument on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This post was amended on 10 November 2023. An earlier version incorrectly referred to \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  as a former New Jersey mayor. He is a former governor of the state.\par \par \uc2 enltr2024 GOP candidate \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/morningmika?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @morningmika}}}\uc2  get into an intense back-and-forth on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Christie: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t mess with me on the law, Mika.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brzezinski: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t mess with me on how women feel about using the ninth month argument on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VPWNtXEkBu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VPWNtXEkBu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722627691428581501?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some key takeaways from last night\u8217\'20\'19s Republican presidential debate:\par \par \uc2 1. The Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war was top of mind \u8211\'20\'13 and the rhetoric turned ugly:\par \par \uc2 The candidates largely tried to one-up each other on their unequivocal support for Israel and its military response to the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks on 7 October, with the exception of \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who said the US should not be as actively involved in regional wars.\par \par \uc2 2. Haley and DeSantis continued to battle for second place:\par \par \uc2 While neither Haley nor DeSantis are polling anywhere close to Trump, they stood out in the pack throughout the debate.\par \par \uc2 Haley focused on her experience in the \uc2 UN\uc2  and on foreign policy issues, and DeSantis on his tenure as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  governor. Both seemed to try to remain more composed than usual, with Haley only reacting to barbs from \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For the full takeaways, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/08/key-takeaways-republican-presidential-debate-miami"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Calls to \u8216\'20\'18finish\u8217\'20\'19 Hamas and \u8216\'20\'18you\u8217\'20\'19re just scum\u8217\'20\'19: key Republican debate takeaways}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In an interview on Thursday with CNN, Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 JB Pritzker\uc2  criticized GOP presidential candidates after their debate, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we saw last night were, of course, the same old right-wing, Maga talking points. These are folks that want to take away people\u8217\'20\'19s rights. They want to lower wages, not raise them. They aren\u8217\'20\'19t for working people and they demonstrated that throughout the entire debate, one after another. They\u8217\'20\'19re going to take away a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose and each one of them, in turn, essentially, doubled down on it.\par \par \uc2 I think what we saw last night was an ignorance of what happened on Tuesday night which was an affirmation of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agenda for America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden-Harris 2024 National Advisory Board member Gov. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JBPritzker?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JBPritzker}}}\uc2  on last night's GOP debate: "These are folks who want to take away people's rights. They'd like to lower wages, not raise them. They aren't for working people and they demonstrated it throughout the entire debate." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VrUdx9cDRw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VrUdx9cDRw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brooke Goren (@BrookeGoren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BrookeGoren/status/1722617077578813933?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 JB Pritzker\uc2  has vowed to continue protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in his state following last night\u8217\'20\'19s GOP presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve said it loud and clear: Illinois will be a sanctuary for reproductive rights as long as I\u8217\'20\'19m governor.\par \par \uc2 While the GOP presidential hopefuls debate how to take away your rights nationwide, I stand firm in my commitment to protect your freedoms.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI've said it loud and clear: Illinois will be a sanctuary for reproductive rights as long as I'm governor.\par \par \uc2 While the GOP presidential hopefuls debate how to take away your rights nationwide, I stand firm in my commitment to protect your freedoms.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 JB Pritzker (@JBPritzker) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JBPritzker/status/1722452789740089774?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, voters in Ohio successfully {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the state constitution.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/11/09/democrats-abortion-election-plan-2023?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  a new Axios report, Pritzker\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights group, Think Big America, has donated $1 million to an effort to put a measure similar to Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s on Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s ballot in 2024 and is also in talks with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups across Arizona and Florida.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  on GOP presidential candidates: 'They continue to push their lies'\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest provider of reproductive rights organization, has slammed Republican presidential candidates over their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views following last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDid the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GOPDebate?src=hashtag_click"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GOPDebate}}}\uc2  presidential candidates miss the election results last night? They continue to push their lies about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but we know the truth: \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is safe, normal, and WINS ELECTIONS,\u8221\'20\'1D the group tweeted.\par \par \uc2 enltrDid the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GOPDebate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GOPDebate}}}\uc2  presidential candidates miss the election results last night? They continue to push their lies about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but we know the truth: \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is safe, normal, and WINS ELECTIONS.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Planned Parenthood Action (@PPact) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPact/status/1722448745319522670?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  also criticized Nikki Haley\u8217\'20\'19s calls for a consensus surrounding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNikki Haley, we already have a \u8216\'20\'18consensus:\u8217\'20\'19 Most Americans agree that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be safe, legal, and not in the hands of politicians.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr?? Nikki Haley, we already have a \u8216\'20\'18consensus:\u8217\'20\'19 Most Americans agree that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be safe, legal, and not in the hands of politicians. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GOPDebate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GOPDebate}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Planned Parenthood Action (@PPact) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPact/status/1722445367306768450?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Following the series of Democratic wins this week surrounding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  urged voters to \u8220\'20\'1Ckeep organizing, keep voting and keep making our voices heard\u8221\'20\'1D as the country heads into 2024.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnce again, voters made it clear that they believe women should have the right to make decisions about their own bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said.\par \par \uc2 enltrOnce again, voters made it clear that they believe women should have the right to make decisions about their own bodies.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, voters chose to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into their state constitution. And in Kentucky, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndyBeshearKY?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AndyBeshearKY}}}\uc2  won a second term as governor after standing\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1722378826221547715?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is more from the memo sent to Congress\u8217\'20\'19s Republican lawmakers from Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe GOP already tried the \u8216\'20\'18ostrich strategy\u8217\'20\'19 in 2022 of ignoring the issue and hoping it would go away. It didn\u8217\'20\'19t work, and tonight\u8217\'20\'19s results show that the issue is still salient with voters. It is long past due for the GOP to define where it stands on the issue nationally \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The GOP should contrast this stance of clarity and compassion with the Democrats, who do not support a single limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , celebrate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and have long moved past the \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D position.\par \par \uc2 Referencing to Democrats gaining control of Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s state legislature on Tuesday, Dannenfelser said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s election in Virginia also shows is that having a clear position and contrasting it isn\u8217\'20\'19t enough \u8211\'20\'13 campaigns and the party must put real advertising dollars behind it, going toe-to-toe with the Democrats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats rush to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on ballots after victory in Ohio \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Good morning,\par \par \uc2 Following a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wins for Democrats across the country on Tuesday, Democrats are reportedly rushing to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot in swing states while Republican leaders struggle to figure out vote-winning stance.\par \par \uc2 With Ohio voting on Tuesday to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution, there is \u8220\'20\'1Cnow added urgency\u8221\'20\'1D to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on ballots in Arizona, Nevada, Florida, Nebraska and South Dakota, a new Axios report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/11/09/democrats-abortion-election-plan-2023?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reveals.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWinning in red states is inspiring. Ohio really has taken this ballot measure strategy to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the next level ,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelly Hall, executive director of progressive non-profit The Fairness Project, told Axios.\par \par \uc2 According to the report, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups are also trying to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s state constitution. Moreover, Think Big America, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights group launched by Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, JB Pritzker, has donated $1m to an effort to put a measure similar to Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s on Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s ballot in 2024. The group is also in discussions with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups in Arizona and Florida, a senior staffer told the outlet.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sbaprolife.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/SBA-Ohio-Virginia-Results-Memo.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told }}}\uc2  Congress in an internal memo on Wednesday: \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be an issue in every race in 2024, so the GOP must lean in and define this issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  president Shawn Fain in Illinois today to highlight the details from the tentative deal with Detroit automakers\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US Senate Democrats are set to vote on Supreme Court ethics probe subpeonas involving GOP billionaire donor \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2  and legal activist \uc2 Leonard Leo\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231109ejb900237\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
