\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Seth Meyers: \u8216\'20\'18Standing up for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights and bodily autonomy wins elections\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 725 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2023\par 17:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Late-night hosts discuss the Republican primary debate, \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s testimony in her father\u8217\'20\'19s fraud trial and big election wins for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Seth Meyers\par \par \uc2 Late-night hosts recapped the testimony of \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  during her father\u8217\'20\'19s New York civil fraud trial on Wednesday, a scenario Trump was reportedly \u8220\'20\'1Cdesperate\u8221\'20\'1D to avoid. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m assuming because Ivanka is, in his eyes, the most competent and thus the most knowledgable member of the family,\u8221\'20\'1D Seth Meyers speculated on Late Night. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no way Trump trusted his two bearded, oblong bozos\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 Eric and Don Jr \u8211\'20\'13 with any real information, but Ivanka could get him in trouble.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She could, for instance, explain why Trump, during his own testimony on Tuesday, presented a piece of paper from his jacket pocket that he claimed would clear his name.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m honestly dying to know what that document was, because it was no doubt incredibly stupid,\u8221\'20\'1D said Meyers, imagining its contents: \u8220\'20\'1CYour honor, I have in my possession the fortune of a cookie, obtained last night at Mr Chang\u8217\'20\'19s on 58th street.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, new polling on the likely 2024 presidential matchup between Trump and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  shows Trump near-even with the current president in several battleground states, which baffled Meyers. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re telling me that Trump, the guy who stocked the bsupreme court with 80s movie villains with the explicit goal of overturning Roe v Wade, is leading the polls in Ohio, where voters just overwhelmingly approved a ballot measure to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights?\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis shit makes so little sense, even Steve Kornacki\u8217\'20\'19s big board last night said, \u8216\'20\'18I give up.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne thing\u8217\'20\'19s for sure: standing up for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and bodily autonomy wins elections,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CVoters are clearly furious about losing Roe and even in supposedly red states like Kentucky and Ohio, they\u8217\'20\'19ve been turning out in large numbers to protect reproductive rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was also evident in the way they were coping last night that Republicans are having a hard time coming to terms with the fact that their position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is deeply unpopular with the majority of voters,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, pointing to a clip of Fox News host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  trying to make sense of the election in Ohio, the seventh state to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enshrine \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  by ballot measure since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year.\par \par \uc2 According to Hannity, \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats are trying to scare women into thinking Republicans don\u8217\'20\'19t want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal under any circumstances.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, I wonder where voters could possibly have gotten the notion that Republicans want to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , aside from all the GOP-led states that have outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or the GOP politicians who say they want to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or the new speaker of the House who sponsored a bill to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Meyers retorted.\par \par \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel\par \par \uc2 And in Los Angeles, Jimmy Kimmel opened with a look at the Republican debate, which featured five candidates who \u8220\'20\'1Clook like they\u8217\'20\'19re complaining to the manager at a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The lineup \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , Nikki Haley, Tim Scott, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 notably did not include frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a who\u8217\'20\'19s who of who has no chance to beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimmel joked. But for these five Republicans, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe stakes were higher than lifts in a pair of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s boots.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is ridiculous to have these debates without the frontrunner, the guy they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to beat,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, you know things have gone sideways when you\u8217\'20\'19re watching something and you\u8217\'20\'19re thinking god, I wish \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kimmel then turned to \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s testimony in New York. \u8220\'20\'1COnly in the Trump family does take your daughter to work day mean she\u8217\'20\'19s forced to testify in court,\u8221\'20\'1D he joked.\par \par \uc2 Like her brothers, Ivanka pleaded ignorance, frequently answering with \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t recall\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cwhich is a phrase she picked up from her father when Eric asked when his birthday was,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimmel quipped.\par \par \uc2 And in election news, Ohio became the 24th state to legalize cannabis for recreational use. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about time,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kimmel. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Wright brothers are from Ohio, Neil Armstrong is from Ohio \u8211\'20\'13 people from Ohio know how to get high.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231109ejb9002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
