\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Republicans beware: hostility to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  stands to haunt Trump\u8217\'20\'19s party in 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 Lloyd Green \par \uc2 934 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2023\par 15:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The party-induced demise of Roe v Wade may keep the Republicans from returning to power for another four years\par \par \uc2 Republicans beware \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  retains its saliency. As a corollary, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is down but not out.\par \par \uc2 On election day this week, voters in Ohio, Virginia and Kentucky embraced individual autonomy and reproductive rights. Looking forward, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision in the Dobbs case and the Trumpian majority\u8217\'20\'19s rejection of privacy as a fundamental constitutional right stand to haunt Trump and his party as they enter the 2024 election season.\par \par \uc2 Buckeye voters enshrined \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in their state after having twice backed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Meanwhile, in the purplish Old Dominion, both houses of the legislature swung Democratic, a rebuff to the efforts of Glenn Youngkin, the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, to enact a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Safe to say, he will not be running for president any time soon.\par \par \uc2 In Kentucky, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic and pro-choice governor, handily defeated \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general. Last Saturday, Trump figuratively embraced Cameron as Maga-approved. On Wednesday, Trump trashed Cameron as a \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  swamp creature.\par \par \uc2 Practically speaking, the Republican party-induced demise of Roe may keep the Republicans from returning to power for another four years. The personal really is the political.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Democrats have an issue to be wielded. It unites the party. By the numbers, 83% of Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Black voters, more three-quarters of its youngest voters, 73% of the state\u8217\'20\'19s Latinos and five-of-eight of its college graduates identified as pro-choice, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/11/07/ohio-issue-1-exit-poll-results/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to exit polls}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, little more than one in six Republicans supported the measure. With Trump having repeatedly bragged about his supreme court picks, the Republican party owns the issue.\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  reports that nearly 65% of the 72.2 million women aged 15\u8211\'20\'1349 in the US currently use contraception. That figure appears to have left little to no mark on the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 collective psyche.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://clerk.house.gov/Votes/2022385"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 195 House Republicans voted against the Right to Contraception Act}}}\uc2 , including Mike Johnson, the current speaker; Kevin McCarthy, his predecessor; Steve Scalise, the present majority leader: and \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , the chair of the conference. Conveniently, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/nov/08/mike-johnson-house-speaker-republican?CMP=share_btn_tw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Johnson no longer recalls how he voted}}}\uc2 . As a lawyer for the rightwing \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , he argued that hormonal birth control was tantamount to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and should be banned.\par \par \uc2 Also last year, Matt DePerno, Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s failed Republican attorney general, openly mused about restricting accessibility to contraception. At a Republican debate, he questioned the validity of Griswold, the pertinent 1965 supreme court ruling.\par \par \uc2 For good measure, DePerno also spearheaded efforts to undo Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 150,000-vote win in Michigan. These days, he faces four felony election interference charges. Pro-tip: everything Trump touches comes to pain.\par \par \uc2 Democrats cannot afford to gloat. They too face headwinds of their own \u8211\'20\'13 crime and immigration\par \par \uc2 As Republicans lick their wounds, they ought to ponder {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jpitney/status/1722240912951234574"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what Ray Collins said to Orson Welles in Citizen Kane}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIf it was anybody else, I\u8217\'20\'19d say what\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen to you would be a lesson to you. Only you\u8217\'20\'19re going to need more than one lesson. And you\u8217\'20\'19re going to get more than one lesson.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Still, Democrats cannot afford to gloat. They too face headwinds of their own \u8211\'20\'13 crime and immigration. One only needs to look at New York to see their impact.\par \par \uc2 There, residents of the Bronx, a majority-minority New York City outer borough, ousted an incumbent Democrat and elected a Republican to the city\u8217\'20\'19s council after a decades-long drought. On eastern Long Island, Republicans wrested control of the Suffolk county executive\u8217\'20\'19s office after a similar dry spell. Even as crime recedes in the Big \uc2 Apple\uc2 , immigration and housing pose new crises.\par \par \uc2 To put things into perspective, when the mayor and the president are clashing about immigrants, it is no longer a theoretical or another Republican talking point. On that score, if Senator McConnell gets his way, aid to Israel and Ukraine will be linked to an immigration overhaul.\par \par \uc2 Turning to the map, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely play a key role in swing states. In Arizona, Michigan, Pennsylvania, Virginia and Wisconsin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/religious-landscape-study/compare/views-about-abortion/by/state/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more voters favor \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights than not}}}\uc2 . In Georgia, there is a 48-49 split, according to data from \uc2 Pew Research\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican hostility to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also save endangered Democratic incumbents in Ohio (Senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 ) and Montana (Senator John Tester). Earlier this year, Montana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/05/05/politics/montana-abortion-restrictions-greg-gianforte/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed legislation}}}\uc2  restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Days later, the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court struck down the legislation as violating the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution. Said differently, in Ohio and Montana, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a live issue.\par \par \uc2 Right now, President Biden is the underdog. He trails Trump in most electoral battlegrounds. The president also ages before us, and lacks the manic energy of his predecessor. Biden will not get any younger. The clock runs.\par \par \uc2 The 2024 elections are now less than 365 days away. Against this backdrop, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely emerge as a go-to issue if for no other reason than it gets people to the polls, older suburban women and college students alike.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Green is an attorney in New York and served in the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  during the George HW Bush administration\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 9 November 2023 to correct the list of states in which voters strengthened individual autonomy and reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231109ejb9001mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
