\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republican hopefuls sharpen critique of Trump as election losses hang in the air\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 932 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2023\par 12:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Candidates barrel through substantive but hostile debate in Miami amid warning that Republicans have become \u8216\'20\'18a party of losers\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A day after Republicans suffered a string of off-year election defeats, five of the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential hopefuls barreled through a substantive yet hostile primary debate on Wednesday, clashing over policy and with each other in a competition for second place behind the absentee frontrunner, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On stage in Miami, the debate was dominated by foreign questions about the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war, immigration and China. But the contenders also decried the losses in Ohio, Kentucky and Virginia, warning that 2024 could end with the re-election of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  if they were unsuccessful in breaking Trump\u8217\'20\'19s dominance of the Republican primary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve become a party of losers,\u8221\'20\'1D said businessman \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , noting that Republicans lost the US House in 2018, and the Senate and the White House in 2020. He decried the \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave that never came\u8221\'20\'1D in 2022. And on Tuesday night, Ramaswamy said the party again \u8220\'20\'1Cgot trounced\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 With just over two months until the Iowa caucuses, which officially launch the Republican nominating contest, the window for denting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lead is closing. On Wednesday, his leading rival for the nomination, the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , sharpened his case against the former president.\par \par \uc2 Taking the stage in his home state, DeSantis recalled that Trump often said \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans were gonna get tired of winning\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, we saw last night \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m sick of Republicans losing,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, before touting his re-election rout last year, a bright spot in an otherwise disappointing midterm election for the party. \u8220\'20\'1CI will be a nominee that can win the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump, who became a resident of Florida after leaving the White House, again skipped the debate and instead held a dueling rally in Hialeah, a heavily Latino Miami suburb.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley, who served as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the United Nations, sought to build on her campaign\u8217\'20\'19s momentum, presenting herself as in the vanguard of the next generation of Republican leaders and distinguishing herself from Trump as an unambiguous foreign policy hawk.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe world is on fire,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said. In 2016, Trump, she said, was the \u8220\'20\'1Cright president at the right time. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19s the right president now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the candidates confronted their most immediate challenge \u8211\'20\'13 beating Trump in a primary \u8211\'20\'13 they were well into the second hour of the debate when it came time to discuss the issue that has powered Democratic wins in conservative states despite Biden\u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Ohio voted to enshrine a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into their state constitution, the Democrats took control of both chambers of the Virginia general assembly, and held on to the governorship in beet-red Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 When finally asked about their position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the candidates offered a range of positions underscoring the lack of consensus within the party since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year.\par \par \uc2 Senator Tim Scott of South Carolina again committed to supporting a national ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy. He argued that 15 weeks was a reasonable limit, and called on Haley and DeSantis to support one, too.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, who signed a six-week ban in Florida, emphasized his support for \u8220\'20\'1Ca culture of life\u8221\'20\'1D and lamented that the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement had been \u8220\'20\'1Ccaught flat-footed\u8221\'20\'1D after Roe.\par \par \uc2 Haley sidestepped Scott\u8217\'20\'19s challenge, arguing that Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Cshould be honest with the American people\u8221\'20\'1D that they do not have the votes in the Senate to enact such a ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs much as I\u8217\'20\'19m pro-life, I don\u8217\'20\'19t judge anyone for being pro-choice, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t want them to judge me for being pro-life,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that the decision to restrict or expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights should be left up to the states. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are some states that are going more on the pro-choice side. I wish that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the case, but the people decide it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has continued to dominate the field in Iowa and nationally, despite facing four criminal indictments and a civil fraud case involving his businesses for which he took the stand in New York this week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll say this about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , whose anti-Trump candidacy has struggled to gain traction. \u8220\'20\'1CAnybody who\u8217\'20\'19s going to be spending the next year and a half of their life focusing on keeping themselves out of jail and courtrooms cannot lead this party or this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Substantive discussion over America\u8217\'20\'19s role in the world pervaded the debate, the first since Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza after the attack by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  that left 1,400 people dead. The candidates were largely united in their support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s retaliatory offensive, which has killed more than 10,000 Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 It also drew some of the sharpest attacks. Ramaswamy, an isolationist, derided Haley and DeSantis as \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  in three-inch heels\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a jab that immediately drew accusations of sexism. DeSantis ignored the barb, but Haley responded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re five-inch heels, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t wear them unless you can run in them,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. She added: \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re not a fashion statement. They\u8217\'20\'19re for ammunition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy went after Haley again later in the debate, noting that her daughter was on TikTok. \u8220\'20\'1CLeave my daughter out of your voice,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley shot back, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re just scum.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231109ejb9001e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
