\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Calls to \u8216\'20\'18finish\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and \u8216\'20\'18you\u8217\'20\'19re just scum\u8217\'20\'19: key Republican debate takeaways\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 852 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2023\par 09:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Candidates showed unequivocal support for Israel on a night when Nikki Haley shot back at \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s criticism\par \par \uc2 The third Republican debate was held in Miami on Wednesday, with frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  once again foregoing the debate for his own rally nearby.\par \par \uc2 The pool has dwindled since the last debate, and Ron DeSantis, Nikki Haley, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , Tim Scott and \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  seemed to be more serious and focused this time around as they answered questions on the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war, immigration, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the federal budget. Even so, the debate had moments where it devolved into a shouting match, with petty barbs and personal attacks.\par \par \uc2 Here are the main things to know about the debate.\par \par \uc2 1. The Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war was top of mind \u8211\'20\'13 and the rhetoric turned ugly\par \par \uc2 The candidates largely tried to one-up each other on their unequivocal support for Israel and its military response to the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks on October 7, with the exception of \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who said the US should not be as actively involved in regional wars.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe first thing I said when it happened was, I said, finish them. Finish them,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said about \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , touting her former position as special envoy to the United Nations under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . DeSantis, meanwhile, focused on the flights he chartered for Floridians in Israel before overstating his aid to the Israeli government.\par \par \uc2 When asked about how the impact of the war was playing out on college campuses in the US, however, DeSantis seemingly denied the existence of Islamophobia, and said he would quash some pro-Palestine student groups.\par \par \uc2 The candidates did not address the estimated 10,000 Palestinian civilians killed by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s strikes and its ground invasion in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 2. After Republican election losses, candidates tried to regain ground, especially on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The day before the debate, the Republican party saw major losses across the country, from the Virginia state legislature to Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s governorship. The candidates addressed that head on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve become a party of losers,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy said in his opening statements. \u8220\'20\'1CWe got trounced last night in 2023. And I think that we have to have accountability in our party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many of the election losses were in states where Republicans were trying to enact stricter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws after Roe v Wade was overturned last year. DeSantis, Christie and Haley tried to address that issue by backing away from rightwing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric and focusing on states\u8217\'20\'19 rights to choose.\par \par \uc2 Haley, in particular, took the most measured stance, saying she did not judge those who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban was politically untenable.\par \par \uc2 3. Haley and DeSantis continued to battle for second place\par \par \uc2 While neither Haley nor DeSantis are polling anywhere close to Trump, they stood out in the pack throughout the debate.\par \par \uc2 Haley focused on her experience in the \uc2 UN\uc2  and on foreign policy issues, and DeSantis on his tenure as Florida governor. Both seemed to try to remain more composed than usual, with Haley only reacting to barbs from Ramaswamy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur world is on fire,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said in her closing remarks. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t win the fights of the 21st century with politicians from the 20th century.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Not far from the debate hall, Trump held a campaign rally. But fellow Florida man DeSantis avoided many direct attacks on the former president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not about me, this is about you,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in his opening and closing remarks.\par \par \uc2 4. There were personal attacks \u8211\'20\'13 particularly involving Ramaswamy\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy started his debate by attacking the media, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  chairwoman \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 , and even the NBC moderators, seemingly as part of his attempt to portray himself as the anti-establishment candidate.\par \par \uc2 He then turned his focus to Haley. \u8220\'20\'1CDo you want a leader from a different generation who is going to put this country first, or do you want \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  in three-inch heels?\u8221\'20\'1D he said, criticizing her hawkish foreign policy positions.\par \par \uc2 And when it came the entrepreneur\u8217\'20\'19s turn to talk about his policy on TikTok, Ramaswamy referred to Haley and said: \u8220\'20\'1CIn the last debate, she made fun of me for actually joining TikTok while her own daughter was actually using the app for a long time. So you might want to take care of your family first.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLeave my daughter out of your voice,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley shot back. When Ramaswamy went on, she dismissed him, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CYou are just scum.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 5. Candidates were more serious and focused than in past debates\par \par \uc2 The earlier debates, with larger candidate pools, have tended to be circus-like in their atmosphere, with more riffs and off-topic detours. From the opening statements, the debate seemed to be more focused on the issues Americans are grappling with, from war in the Middle East and in Ukraine, and kitchen-table issues such as social security.\par \par \uc2 The seriousness of the candidates seemed to reflect that the primary season was just around the corner, and that positioning themselves strategically around Trump would mean building more trust with American voters.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231109ejb9000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
