\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  views, name-calling and foreign policy cap wide-ranging third Republican debate \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein and Maanvi Singh \par \uc2 6,391 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2023\par 04:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. Read our latest coverage of the Republican debate here:DeSantis and Haley rip into absent Trump at Republican debate\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 In Miami, NBC News hosted the most sober and restrained of the three Republican presidential debates thus far. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Tim Scott, Nikki Haley, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  feuded and found common ground over a variety of topics, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c47128f08098a8706fe2e#block-654c47128f08098a8706fe2e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 border security}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c48598f0898cc3cb03ef0#block-654c48598f0898cc3cb03ef0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c41fa8f0898cc3cb03ec7#block-654c41fa8f0898cc3cb03ec7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social security reforms}}}\uc2 . But there was drama nonetheless, particularly between Haley and Ramaswamy, who the former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador at one point called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c3dd88f0898cc3cb03ea0#block-654c3dd88f0898cc3cb03ea0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cscum\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has an overwhelming lead among polls for the nomination, once again skipped the get-together, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c4e7b8f081362db4f9d54#block-654c4e7b8f081362db4f9d54"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  will not attend the fourth debate set for next month in Alabama.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of some of the biggest moments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c45e58f0898cc3cb03ee0#block-654c45e58f0898cc3cb03ee0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again called}}}\uc2  for gunning down drug traffickers who cross into the US over the southern border with Mexico.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Christie{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c3cdd8f0898cc3cb03e9c#block-654c3cdd8f0898cc3cb03e9c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  TikTok of \u8220\'20\'1Cpolluting the minds of American young people all throughout this country\u8221\'20\'1D, and said he would ban it on his first day in the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Scott{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c37a08f08098a8706fdd8#block-654c37a08f08098a8706fdd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Cterrorist sleeper cells\u8221\'20\'1D in America, while demanding more accountability for aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c4acf8f081362db4f9d45#block-654c4acf8f081362db4f9d45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for}}}\uc2 Joe Biden to drop his re-election campaign, and accused him of not really being the president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Haley {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c388a8f081362db4f9cd8#block-654c388a8f081362db4f9cd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 Vladimir Putin and Xi Jinping would love to see Ramaswamy in the White House. She did not mean it as a compliment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign says debate showed Republicans 'embracing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s losing and extreme Maga agenda'\par \par \uc2 The manager of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign Julie Chavez Rodriguez released a statement lumping the five Republicans who participated in tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , saying there is no daylight between their policies:\par \par \uc2 Normally, after you lose, you take a moment to reflect and course correct. But in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s MAGA Republican Party, apparently you double down on the same extreme agenda that was soundly rejected last night in elections across the country. That\u8217\'20\'19s what we witnessed tonight: the entire Republican field once again embracing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s losing and extreme MAGA agenda of banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , cutting Social Security and Medicare, and rigging the economy for the ultra-wealthy at the expense of working Americans. In fact, the only thing that the American people agree with these MAGA Republicans on is that their extreme agenda has left them reeling as \u8216\'20\'18a party of losers.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A year from now, Americans will face a clear choice \u8212\'20\'14 between President Biden, who is focused on the issues impacting you, and MAGA Republicans, whose policy platform is to make things worse for you by taking away your freedoms. We\u8217\'20\'19ll spend the next year making sure every American knows just that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Noted Republican pollster Frank Luntz complimented Nikki Haley\u8217\'20\'19s stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The GOP has been suffering at the ballot box ever since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year. Just yesterday, voters in Ohio, a state that has voted Republican in the last two presidential elections, approved a constitutional amendment to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while in Virginia, Democrats took control of the general assembly, preventing Republican governor Glenn Youngkin \u8217\'20\'19s plan to pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of Haley\u8217\'20\'19s remarks. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if the policy does her any good in her race for the nomination, or if other Republicans follow suit:\par \par \uc2 enltrNikki Haley has the best Republican answer on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GOP}}}\uc2  would be stronger if they used her language. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gaXStT7gmG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gaXStT7gmG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Frank Luntz (@FrankLuntz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FrankLuntz/status/1722446456832029092?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump plans to skip fourth Republican presidential debate in Alabama - report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did not attend tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate of Republican presidential candidates, nor the two that came before it, and CBS News reports he will not participate in the fourth debate set for next month:\par \par \uc2 enltrNewsy \u8212\'20\'14 Trump advisor Chris LaCavita tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @edokeefe}}}\uc2  that Trump will not attend the fourth debate next month in Tuscaloosa, Alabama\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Rinaldi (@olivialarinaldi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/olivialarinaldi/status/1722450228140241168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 That debate is set for 6 December in Tuscaloosa, Alabama.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Tonight was the first debate without \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , the North Dakota governor and presidential aspirant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/?ex_cid=abcpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who is basically nowhere}}}\uc2  in the polls.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after it wrapped up, he posted some sour grapes on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrTonight, voters learned why a career politician shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be the next president, and why party insiders have no business artificially shrinking the Republican field. Career politicians can\u8217\'20\'19t fix what\u8217\'20\'19s wrong in Washington. They\u8217\'20\'19re why we\u8217\'20\'19re in this mess in the first place!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  (Text "DOUG" to 70177) (@DougBurgum) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DougBurgum/status/1722450037806911530?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03am GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that Republicans pushed for have become a liability for the party. As the candidates search for new ways to discuss the topic, they have been softening their tones and regurgitating anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  myths.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  said he stands \u8220\'20\'1Cculture of life\u8221\'20\'1D but noted that different states may want different things. He did not emphasize the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban he signed into law. Nikki Haley, who once touted her stanchly pro-life views and suggested federal action taken to limit abortions tonight said it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely that a federal ban would have support in Congress.\par \par \uc2 She also brought back misinformation about \u8220\'20\'1Clate term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, which doctors emphasize is not a medical term, and does not carry medical relevance.\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott also said that California and New York allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cuntil the day of birth\u8221\'20\'1D which is false. Those states ban almost all abortions after fetal viability, around 24 weeks into pregnancy. Seven states and the District of Columbia have no restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Nonetheless, less than 1% of abortions in the US are performed past 21 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more context, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/27/abortion-myths-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  myths Republicans are recycling to reframe a losing issue}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy demands Biden 'end his candidacy now'\par \par \uc2 As the debate concluded, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  leveled an attack on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , arguing he isn\u8217\'20\'19t really the president and demanding he end his re-election campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI also want to close with one message to the Democrat Party: End this farce that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is going to be your nominee. We know he\u8217\'20\'19s not even the president of the United States \u8211\'20\'13 he\u8217\'20\'19s a puppet for the managerial class,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo have the guts to step up and be honest about who you\u8217\'20\'19re actually going to put up, so we can have an honest debate. Biden should step aside and end his candidacy now, so we can see whether it\u8217\'20\'19s Newsom or \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  or whoever else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 'I don't judge anyone for being pro-choice', Haley says, arguing, 'We don't need to divide America over this issue anymore'\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate is taking place in the wake of yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s election, where Republican attempts to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were turned down by voters in Ohio and Virginia. Indeed, the GOP has been on a losing streak at the ballot box on the issue ever since Roe v Wade was struck down in June 2022, and in response to a question on her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, Nikki Haley called for something of a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you is, as much as I\u8217\'20\'19m pro-life, I don\u8217\'20\'19t judge anyone for being pro-choice, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t want them to judge me for being pro-life. So when we\u8217\'20\'19re looking at this, there are some states that are going more on the pro-life side, I welcome that. There are some states that are going more on the pro-choice side. I wish that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the case, but the people decided,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said.\par \par \uc2 She also noted the long odds any nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restriction would face getting through Congress and signed by the president, and concluded by appealing for politicians to back off the issue:\par \par \uc2 So let\u8217\'20\'19s find consensus. Let\u8217\'20\'19s agree on \u8230\'20\'26 how we can ban late-term abortions. Let\u8217\'20\'19s make sure we encourage adoptions and good quality adoptions. Let\u8217\'20\'19s make sure we make contraception accessible. Let\u8217\'20\'19s make sure that none of these state laws put a woman in jail or give her the death penalty for getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Let\u8217\'20\'19s focus on how to save as many babies as we can, and support as many moms as we can and stop judgment. We don\u8217\'20\'19t need to divide America over this issue anymore.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  said he wants to impose sanctions on Mexican cartels, a move that the Biden administration made yesterday.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration imposed sanctions on 13 members of the Sinaloa cartel, and four of the Sonora cartel, accusing them of trafficking fentanyl.\par \par \uc2 The sanctions cut them off from the US banking system, and blocked their US assets.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy supports walls on borders with both Mexico and Canada\par \par \uc2 Like many Republicans, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  said he wanted to build a wall on the southern border. But he didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop there.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy says he also wants to build a wall on the northern border with Canada, arguing it\u8217\'20\'19s also a source of fentanyl trafficking. From his remarks:\par \par \uc2 What we need to do is stop using our military to protect somebody else\u8217\'20\'19s border halfway around the world, when we\u8217\'20\'19re short right here at home.\par \par \uc2 Get serious about protecting this border and then the other thing that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been discussed as the northern border, I\u8217\'20\'19m the only candidate on this stage, as far as I\u8217\'20\'19m aware, who has actually visited the northern border. There was enough fentanyl that was captured just on the northern border last year to kill 3 million Americans. So we got to just skate to where the puck is going, not just where the puck is. Don\u8217\'20\'19t just build the wall, build both walls.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, again, calls for shooting drug smugglers 'stone cold dead'\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  once again proposed hardline, legally dubious methods to improve security on the US border with Mexico, including shooting drug smugglers \u8220\'20\'1Cstone cold dead\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He had made a similar remark at a previous debate, and repeated it just now:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll build a wall, but we\u8217\'20\'19re going to designate the cartels to be foreign terrorist organizations or something similar to that. And we\u8217\'20\'19re going to authorize the use of deadly force. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to have maritime operations to interdict precursor chemicals going into Mexico, but I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you this, if someone in the drug cartels is sneaking fentanyl across the border, when I\u8217\'20\'19m president, that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be the last thing they do. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to shoot him stone cold dead.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 Scott joins calls to 'close our southern border'\par \par \uc2 The debaters are debating again, and one thing\u8217\'20\'19s for sure: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates?page=with:block-654c3dd88f0898cc3cb03ea0#block-654c3dd88f0898cc3cb03ea0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the salvoes}}}\uc2  between \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and Nikki Haley notwithstanding, this faceoff is a much more sober affair than the previous two.\par \par \uc2 The candidates were asked how they would handle border security and fentanyl smuggled across the border. Tim Scott responded first, and called for deploying technology to secure the border.\par \par \uc2 We should close our southern border. For $10 billion, we can close our southern border. For an additional $5 billion, we could use the currently available military technology to surveil our southern border to stop fentanyl from crossing our border.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 The debate is now taking another commercial break!\par \par \uc2 Shortly before it did so, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  earned himself some chuckles by making light of his state\u8217\'20\'19s place as a destination for many retirees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, look, as governor of Florida, I know a few people on Social Security and I know it\u8217\'20\'19s important,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis remarked.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 The debate has entered wonky territory, as the candidates weigh in on whether they would reform the Social Security old-age benefit.\par \par \uc2 Reforming the program is considered one of the most perilous topics in Washington, so much so that it\u8217\'20\'19s often referred to as the \u8220\'20\'1Cthird rail\u8221\'20\'1D of US politics. But Social Security is projected to be heading towards insolvency, and \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  proposed raising the retirement age and cutting off high-earners from accessing it:\par \par \uc2 The fact is on Social Security, remember why it was established. It was established as a safety net program to make sure that no one would grow old in this country in poverty. That\u8217\'20\'19s what we got to get back to \u8211\'20\'13 rich people should not be collecting Social Security.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley made a similar argument, while saying the retirement age, currently 65, should be recalibrated to \u8220\'20\'1Creflect more of life expectancy. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t do that now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Most candidates seemed to agree that TikTok is bad, and they all want to ban it. Both Republicans and Democrats in the Capitol seem to agree on this as well.\par \par \uc2 Montana became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/tiktok-ban-montana-325a33578a2bbfbe53e9c251d528c5fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first state}}}\uc2  in the US to completely ban the app in May, based on the argument that the Chinese government could gain access to user information from TikTok. But in legal proceedings challenging the ban, a federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/oct/12/judge-questions-montana-tiktok-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed}}}\uc2  skepticism, saying that Montana had not provided evidence to debunk TikTok\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that it does not share US user data.\par \par \uc2 More than half of US states and the federal government have banned the app on official devices.\par \par \uc2 Content creators have said that total bans would harm businesses and violate free speech rights.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 The snit between Nikki Haley and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  is better watched than read.\par \par \uc2 Thus, you can see the exchange, and hear the audience\u8217\'20\'19s gasps, below:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CLeave my daughter out of your voice... You\u8217\'20\'19re just scum.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nikki Haley hits \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  after he brings up the fact that her daughter, like him, uses TikTok. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3CKUupHaD1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3CKUupHaD1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722435285567340717?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott said that Biden had sent \u8216\'20\'18billions to Iran\u8217\'20\'19, which is misleading.\par \par \uc2 Scott appears to be referring to a prisoner swap, wherein the Biden administration $6bn (\u163\'00\'A34.8bn) of Iranian oil money in exchange for the release of five American detainees. The money was not US money, but rather money owed to Iran and frozen by the Trump administration in 2018 when the US left the Iran nuclear deal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Haley calls Ramaswamy 'scum' after he invokes daughter in debate\par \par \uc2 It just gets worse and worse between Nikki Haley and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 . When it came the entrepreneur\u8217\'20\'19s turn to talk about his policy on TikTok, Ramaswamy referred to Haley and said, \u8220\'20\'1CIn the last debate, she made fun of me for actually joining TikTok while her own daughter was actually using the app for a long time, so you might want to take care of your family first.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haley shot back. \u8220\'20\'1CLeave my daughter out of your voice,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. And as Ramaswamy went on, she dismissed him, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cyou are just scum.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Christie backs TikTok ban, accuses app of 'polluting the minds of American young people'\par \par \uc2 The debate has resumed with the first question about TikTok, the much-maligned social media network that\u8217\'20\'19s owned by a Chinese firm and beloved by many young people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me say this: TikTok is not only spyware, it is polluting the minds of American young people all throughout this country, and they\u8217\'20\'19re doing it intentionally,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn my first week as president, we would ban TikTok.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 The debate is now taking a brief break.\par \par \uc2 Shortly before the pause, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who is no stranger to over-the-top, attention-grabbing remarks, appeared to call Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1CNazi\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 See the moment here:\par \par \uc2 enltrAnswering a question on Ukraine funding, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  seems to call \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1CNazi.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Yy1l6k539V"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Yy1l6k539V}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722429697517146520?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Multiple candidates conflated pro-Palestine activism with antisemitism, mischaracterizing the global protest movement against Israel\u8217\'20\'19s killing of more than 10,000 civilians in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley compared pro-Palestinian protesters to the K.K.K., while DeSantis said he would quash student groups and questioned the existence of Islamophobia. Most pro-Palestine movements have condemned the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  killings in Israel alongside the growing casualties in Gaza. The candidates, however, did not speak to civilian deaths in Gaza on stage.\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/wilfred-chan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wilfred Chan}}}\uc2  recently reported, this sort of rhetoric builds on \u8220\'20\'1Cdecades of organized efforts\u8221\'20\'1D to paint pro-Palestine advocates as antisemitic and pro-terrorist:\par \par \uc2 In 2015, CCR and Palestine Legal published a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://palestinelegal.org/the-palestine-exception#exec-summary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  on the tactics used by pro-Israel lobbying groups, school administrators and public officials to shut down Palestinian rights activists. They included false accusations of antisemitism or support for terrorism, legal threats and criminal investigations, and they often succeeded in \u8220\'20\'1Cintimidating or deterring Palestinian solidarity activists from speaking out\u8221\'20\'1D, the report found.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/01/palestine-us-activism-firings-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The Palestine exception\u8217\'20\'19: why pro-Palestinian voices are suppressed in the US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Haley says Putin and Xi 'salivating' at Ramaswamy's candidacy\par \par \uc2 The bad blood between Nikki Haley and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  was apparent as the former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador responded to comments he made criticizing aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPutin and President Xi are salivating at the thought that someone like that could become president,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said.\par \par \uc2 She then strenuously defended assisting Kyiv in its defense against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion:\par \par \uc2 No, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think we should give them cash. I think we should give them the equipment, the ammunition to win. And I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you if Biden had done it when they first asked for it, this war would be over. But let\u8217\'20\'19s also remember this \u8211\'20\'13 when you left Afghanistan in shambles and left them with a ton of weapons and money, it\u8217\'20\'19s not that we left it\u8217\'20\'19s how we left.\par \par \uc2 When you look at Ukraine, don\u8217\'20\'19t think for a second now everybody wants to move away from Ukraine. They\u8217\'20\'19ll want to move away from Israel a year from now. America can never be so arrogant to think we don\u8217\'20\'19t need friends. After 9/11, we needed a lot of friends. Now is the time to get partnerships.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 'I believe that we have sleeper terrorist cells in America' - Scott\par \par \uc2 Responding to a question on how he would assist Ukraine in its battle against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion, senator Tim Scott pivoted to criticizing the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s border policies, and then warned that \u8220\'20\'1Cterrorist cells\u8221\'20\'1D are entering the country from Mexico:\par \par \uc2 The American people are frustrated that they do not have a president who reminds us and tells us where\u8217\'20\'19s the accountability. Where are those dollars? How are those dollars being spent? We need those answers for us to continue to see the support for Ukraine and at the same time I would say that the package \u8230\'20\'26 that\u8217\'20\'19s been offered by the president for Ukraine and Israel, that\u8217\'20\'19s a wrong approach. We need to focus specifically on providing Israel with the $14 billion that they need so that we show the world that we are 100% undeniably standing shoulder-to-shoulder with Israel. And then, as we turn away from that direct support for Israel, we should go to our southern border and close our southern border with the resources necessary.\par \par \uc2 I believe that we have sleeper terrorist cells in America. Thousands of people have come from Yemen, Iran, Syria and Iraq. If we\u8217\'20\'19re going to deal with the national security emergency at our border, we have to do it now.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Initially, DeSantis had exaggerated his intervention after \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacked Israel. He received pushback from Israeli diplomats after he falsely claimed credit for aid to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military operations in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  governor claimed he had worked with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s consul general in Miami to send military equipment, including drones, body armor and helmets, though private parties. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://embassies.gov.il/miami/AboutTheEmbassy/Pages/The%20Consul%20General.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maor Elbaz-Starinsky}}}\uc2  , Israel\u8217\'20\'19s consul general, said Israel had not asked for DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s help, and that the governor\u8217\'20\'19s involvement was limited to smoothing paperwork requirements for a previously arranged shipment of \u8220\'20\'1Crifle parts\u8221\'20\'1D ordered by his government.\par \par \uc2 US exporters seeking to provide support for Israel would need to first get federal authorizations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 DeSantis questions existence of Islamophobia as he vows to protect Jewish students\par \par \uc2 Responding to a question about what he would do to make Jewish students feel comfortable on college campuses, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  appeared to imply that Islamophobia does not exist.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd what is Biden doing? Not only is he not helping the Jewish students who are being persecuted, he is launching an initiative to combat so-called Islamophobia,\u8221\'20\'1D the Florida governor said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo, it\u8217\'20\'19s the antisemitism that is spiraling out of control. That is what we have to confront. And as president, I can tell you this, we are not going to stand for this on college campuses any longer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  attacked the Biden administration for leaving Americans \u8220\'20\'1Cstranded\u8221\'20\'1D in Israel. \u8220\'20\'1CThere could have been more hostages, if we hadn\u8217\'20\'19t acted,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s true that DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s administration chartered flights to bring Floridians in Israel back to the US, but the rest of what he said is false.\par \par \uc2 The hostages were taken before DeSantis took any action to charter flights. \uc2 Hamas\uc2  took about 240 hostages when it attacked on 7 October. The group has not appeared to take any further hostages since its initial attack. It is unclear that DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 chartered planes to Israel would have any impact on \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 actions.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is also sending flights to Israel to evacuate Americans. DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 administration said that Floridians coming back would not be charged for the flights, whereas the State Department is asking passengers for a refund.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 A few minutes later, Nikki Haley responded to \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d first like to say I wear five-inch heels, and don\u8217\'20\'19t wear them unless you can run on them,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI wear heels not for a fashion statement \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re for ammunition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Asked about his policies towards Israel, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  attacked Nikki Haley for pursuing policies he said fueled wars \u8211\'20\'13 and compared her to \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  in three-inch heels\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Cheney is the former vice-president under \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  who was seen as fueling that administration\u8217\'20\'19s hawkish actions. From Ramaswamy\u8217\'20\'19s response:\par \par \uc2 The fact of the matter is the Republican Party is not that much better. You have the likes of Nikki Haley who stepped down from her time at the \uc2 UN\uc2 , bankrupt or in debt \u8230\'20\'26 Then she becomes a military contractor. She joins the board of \uc2 Boeing\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 and is now a multimillionaire. So I think that that\u8217\'20\'19s wrong when Republicans do it or Democrats do it. That\u8217\'20\'19s the choice we face. Do you want a leader from a different generation who is going to put this country first or do you want \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  in three-inch heels?\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 GOP candidates call to 'finish' \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , back hardline Israel response to attacks\par \par \uc2 The next question put to the candidates concerned Israel. \u8220\'20\'1CAs President of the United States, what would you be urging Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  to do at this moment?\u8221\'20\'1D asked Lester Holt.\par \par \uc2 All the candidates said they would support Israel in its conflict with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , and backed hardline policies to rout the group from the Gaza Strip.\par \par \uc2 As Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  put it:\par \par \uc2 I will be telling Bibi finish the job once and for all with these butchers \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . They\u8217\'20\'19re terrorists. They\u8217\'20\'19re massacring innocent people. They would wipe every Jew off the globe if they could. He cannot live with that threat right by his country, that \uc2 Hamas\uc2  should release every hostage and they should unconditionally surrender. I\u8217\'20\'19m sick of hearing the media, I\u8217\'20\'19m sick of hearing other people blame Israel just for defending itself.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley said much the same:\par \par \uc2 The first thing I said to him when it happened was, I said, finish them. Finish them. And the reason is, I worked on this every day when I was at the United Nations. And we have to remember that they have to one, eliminate \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , two, support Israel with whatever they need whenever they need it, and three, make sure we bring our hostages home.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 The question was then put to \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , a wealthy entrepreneur and first-time presidential contender who is essentially running as the candidate who is even more conservative than Trump.\par \par \uc2 He started with harsh words for the GOP and its poor performance in recent elections, including yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s. \u8220\'20\'1CI think there\u8217\'20\'19s something deeper going on in the Republican Party, here and I am upset about what happened last night. We become a party of losers,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy said, adding \u8220\'20\'1CWe got trounced last night in 2023. And I think that we have to have accountability in our party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then he took the unusual decision to attack the moderators:\par \par \uc2 Think about who\u8217\'20\'19s moderating this debate. This should be \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , Joe Rogan and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , we\u8217\'20\'19d have 10 times the viewership asking questions that GOP primary voters actually care about bringing more people into our party, getting the Democrats and we\u8217\'20\'19ve got Kristen Welker here. Do you think Democrats would actually hire Greg Gutfeld toasted democratic debate? They wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t do it. And so the fact of the matter is him and Kristen I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna use this talk because it\u8217\'20\'19s actually about you in the media and the corrupt media establishment.\par \par \uc2 Gutfeld is a conservative Fox News personality, while Welker is one of the NBC moderators handling tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Next up to answer the question was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador Nikki Haley.\par \par \uc2 She harkened back to her time working in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration, while arguing the time was right for \u8220\'20\'1Can accountant in the White House\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 From her answer:\par \par \uc2 You know, everybody wants to talk about President Trump. Well, I can talk about President Trump. I can tell you that I think he was the right president at the right time. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19s the right president now. I think that he put us $8 trillion in debt, and our kids are never gonna forgive us for that. I think the fact that he used to be right on Ukraine and foreign issues, now he\u8217\'20\'19s getting weak in the knees and trying to be friendly again. I think that we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to go back to the fact that we can\u8217\'20\'19t live in the past. We can\u8217\'20\'19t live in other headlines. We\u8217\'20\'19ve got to start focusing on what\u8217\'20\'19s going to make America strong and proud. And that\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19m focused on doing. Let\u8217\'20\'19s make sure we pay down our debt. I think we need an accountant in the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t even in attendance, but moderator Lester Holt made him the subject of the first question, which was addressed to all five candidates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the first ex-president in more than 100 years to run for the White House again and he remains popular among Republican primary voters as his legal challenges mount,\u8221\'20\'1D Holt said.\par \par \uc2 Addressing Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Holt asked, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhy should you and not him be the Republican nominee to face \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a year from now?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis said, in part:\par \par \uc2 This country is in trouble and the elites that have put us here, they don\u8217\'20\'19t care about you. They don\u8217\'20\'19t care that you\u8217\'20\'19re having to grapple with higher grocery prices or have higher gas prices. They don\u8217\'20\'19t care that your family is less secure because of the open border that\u8217\'20\'19s allowed drugs and even terrorists to come into this country.\par \par \uc2 Well, I care. I am not going to sit idly by and let this country continue its downward spiral. We need leadership, and we need it now. I\u8217\'20\'19ll take the hits, I\u8217\'20\'19ll take the arrows, I\u8217\'20\'19ll take the slings, because ultimately it\u8217\'20\'19s not about me \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s about you. I will fight for you. I will make sure to lead this country\u8217\'20\'19s revival, and I will win for you and your family. Actions speak louder than words. We don\u8217\'20\'19t have time for excuses.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Third Republican presidential debate begins in Miami\par \par \uc2 The third debate of the 2024 Republican presidential primary has kicked off in Miami.\par \par \uc2 Hosted by NBC News, tonight\u8217\'20\'19s event features Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , former United Nations ambassador Nikki Haley, entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , senator Tim Scott and former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Polls show that none of these candidates are leading the race, or even close to it. The frontrunner is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has maintained his lead all year, but has not attended any debates \u8211\'20\'13 tonight\u8217\'20\'19s included.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate audience of about 1,700 people consists mostly of Republican party members and officials from many states. No public tickets were made available.\par \par \uc2 Several of those heading for the debate hall spoke of the need for unity among the candidates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter the disappointing results in Kentucky and Virginia, we have to get back to talking about the issues and policies,\u8221\'20\'1D Rafael Garcia, a \u8220\'20\'1Cprobable\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  supporter from Miami, said. \u8220\'20\'1CEverything we hear is about Trump, or DeSantis, and how they\u8217\'20\'19re fighting with each other. We want to hear what plans they have for us, not tearing each other down all the time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Garcia said he believed either Christie, or Nikki Haley, would represent the best chance for Republicans to oust \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from the White House next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t really think \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  can win the nomination, there are too many Trump people who are against him. But Haley has been doing well. I\u8217\'20\'19d want it to be her if it\u8217\'20\'19s between her and Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sandy Anderson, from Delray Beach, Florida, is a supporter of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s done such a good job as our governor, he deserves the chance to lead the country,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t understand why people don\u8217\'20\'19t like him. He\u8217\'20\'19s the strongest of all the candidates.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 A handful of protestors, some Republican supporters, some Democratic, have shown up outside Miami\u8217\'20\'19s Adrienne Arsht performing arts center, where Republican presidential hopefuls (minus frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ) will face off in the third primary debate a little later this evening.\par \par \uc2 Miami native Bob Kunst is a regular attendee at political events in the city. Tonight he\u8217\'20\'19s here calling on the candidates to declare their support for Israel, and denounce antisemitism. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a Democrat, but \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t getting it done, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t think any of the Republicans here tonight have the balls,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 Kunst worries that members of his synagogue who planned to protest with him won\u8217\'20\'19t be able to find him. \u8220\'20\'1CThe police have moved me twice,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom the front of the building to the side and now out back where there\u8217\'20\'19s nobody around. It\u8217\'20\'19s wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporter Chauncey O\u8217\'20\'19Connor said he thought about attending the former president\u8217\'20\'19s rival rally tonight a short distance away in Hialeah, but instead wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cshake the hand of friendship\u8221\'20\'1D with those rooting for the challengers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been flipped off a few times,\u8221\'20\'1D he admits. \u8220\'20\'1CI just show them the peace sign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrA few protesters are beginning to gather at Miami\u8217\'20\'19s Adrienne Arsht center where Republican presidential candidates debate tonight. Trump supporter Chauncey O\u8217\'20\'19Connor says he\u8217\'20\'19s missing the former president\u8217\'20\'19s rally nearby to be here. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been flipped off a few times,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ja56EyZmhA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ja56EyZmhA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Richard Luscombe (@richlusc) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/richlusc/status/1722381430557204847?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  on the campaign trail in Iowa yesterday. Photograph: Scott Olson/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 However tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate goes for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely to touch the heights of exactly one year ago, when Florida\u8217\'20\'19s hard right governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/ron-desantis-trump-2024-florida-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soared to re-election}}}\uc2  by a 20 point margin, a fact he has been keen to brag about on the presidential campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s possible, of course, that 8 November 2022 marked the pinnacle of DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s political career. There\u8217\'20\'19s evidence his extremist agenda as governor since, which includes passing a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, restricting Black voters\u8217\'20\'19 rights, attacking the LGBTQ+ community and going after the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest private employer, \uc2 Disney\uc2 , in a feud over his \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t Say Gay\u8221\'20\'1D law, has alienated voters both in Florida and nationally.\par \par \uc2 A poll released Tuesday showed DeSantis has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ron-desantis-trump-florida-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fallen even further behind}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Florida, mirroring his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cratering support across the country}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That, and the shortening window to stage a comeback before January\u8217\'20\'19s first primary contest in Iowa, is why he needs a stellar performance this evening here in Miami. Polling suggests Nikki Haley has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/iowa-poll/caucus/2023/10/30/iowa-poll-donald-trump-leads-ron-desantis-nikki-haley-tied-presidential-candidates-gop-caucus/71342485007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tied him for second place}}}\uc2  to Trump in Iowa, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/21/ron-desantis-fifth-new-hampshire-trump-ramaswamy-haley-christie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left him for dust}}}\uc2  in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 Expect DeSantis to face some searching questions tonight from Haley, particularly over the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war, and his record in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Instead of attending debate, Trump to hold rally near Miami to court Hispanic voters\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is skipping this evening\u8217\'20\'19s debate of Republican presidential candidates, but won\u8217\'20\'19t be far from its Miami venue, the Knight Concert Hall at the Adrienne Arsht Center for Performing Arts.\par \par \uc2 The former president is instead scheduled to hold a rally in the suburb of Hialeah, where he is looking to court Hispanic voters in a state that supported his candidacy both in 2016 and 2020, and will be crucial in his campaign for the White House next year.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally is scheduled to begin at 7pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 NBC News the host of third GOP presidential debate\par \par \uc2 NBC News is hosting this evening\u8217\'20\'19s Republican debate, which begins at 8pm in Miami.\par \par \uc2 The five-candidate showdown will be moderated by Lester Holt, anchor of NBC Nightly News, Kristen Welker, moderator of Meet the Press, and \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2 , a prominent conservative radio host.\par \par \uc2 NBC will show the debate live {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/now"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , as well as on major streaming platforms.\par \par \uc2 Fox News hosted the first debate in Milwaukee, while the second debate in Simi Valley, California was co-hosted by Fox News, \uc2 Fox Business Network\uc2  and Univision.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, Haley, Ramaswamy, Scott, Christie set for Florida faceoff\par \par \uc2 Good evening, US politics blog readers, and thank you for joining us as we cover the third debate of the Republican presidential nomination process. This evening at 8pm eastern time in Miami, five candidates \u8211\'20\'13 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , former United Nations ambassador Nikki Haley, entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , senator Tim Scott and former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 will take the stage for yet another unusual debate among the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential aspirants. What makes tonight\u8217\'20\'19s faceoff, and the two others that came before, so strange is the absence of the far-and-away frontrunner for the nomination, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He wasn\u8217\'20\'19t there for the first debate in Milwaukee, nor for the second debate in Simi Valley, California, and won\u8217\'20\'19t be in Miami for tonight\u8217\'20\'19s showdown, and paid no apparent penalty for it \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll after poll}}}\uc2  shows him with a massive lead for the nomination.\par \par \uc2 But no ballots have been cast yet and nothing is decided, meaning there is plenty of reason to pay attention to what these five Republicans have to say. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a few things we will be looking out for:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  proved once again to be the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s Achilles heel in off-year elections held yesterday. Voters in Virginia handed the state legislature to Democrats in a rebuke of Republican governor Glenn Youngkin \u8217\'20\'19s push to restrict the procedure, while red-leaning Ohio voted to protect the right in the state constitution. What will the five candidates, all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes of various stripes, have to say about that?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Haley has seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/iowa-poll-republicans-trump-nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a pop}}}\uc2  in recent polling, coming in striking distance of the second-place position currently held by DeSantis. Will that intensify the rivalry between the two candidates, or expose Haley, who served under Trump, to new attacks?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel \u8217\'20\'19s place as a cause celebre for Republicans has been renewed ever since \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deadly 7 October attack. What will the candidates say about their policy towards the country, particularly when it comes to the ongoing and controversial invasion of Gaza?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231109ejb800003\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
