\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 White House decries \u8216\'20\'18nasty personal smears\u8217\'20\'19 after House Republicans subpoena Biden family \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 6,577 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2023\par 00:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can follow the action of the third GOP debate here:Latest updates: Five Republican candidates face off in third GOP presidential debate\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can follow the action of the third Republican debate with us here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/republican-third-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-miami-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Five Republican candidates face off in third GOP presidential debate \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/election-results-abortion-rights-democrats-biden-trump-polls-politics-latest?page=with:block-654b9b2b8f08098a8706f5e2#block-654b9b2b8f08098a8706f5e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 basked}}}\uc2  in the glow of several victories in off-year elections held yesterday, both for their candidates and their causes. Among the triumphs was Democratic governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election in deep-red Kentucky, Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s vote to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution and a slew of wins in Virginia legislative races that will prevent Republican governor Glenn Youngkin from enacting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. But trouble loomed elsewhere. The House last night voted to censure progressive Democrat \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  for her use of a controversial pro-Palestine slogan, which was today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/election-results-abortion-rights-democrats-biden-trump-polls-politics-latest?page=with:block-654bda8a8f08098a8706fa8b#block-654bda8a8f08098a8706fa8b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also condemned}}}\uc2  by the White House. Meanwhile, election analysts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/election-results-abortion-rights-democrats-biden-trump-polls-politics-latest?page=with:block-654bf3478f08098a8706fb94#block-654bf3478f08098a8706fb94"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 say}}}\uc2  that despite Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 recent successes, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not out of the woods yet.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration once again {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/election-results-abortion-rights-democrats-biden-trump-polls-politics-latest?page=with:block-654bd7e18f081362db4f9957#block-654bd7e18f081362db4f9957"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  it does not support a ceasefire in Gaza, despite growing calls on the left for Israel to cease its hostilities.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/election-results-abortion-rights-democrats-biden-trump-polls-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-654c0e458f081362db4f9b8d#block-654c0e458f081362db4f9b8d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  an attempt to keep \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  off next year\u8217\'20\'19s primary ballot for his plot to overturn his 2020 election loss.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans sent subpoenas to two members of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s family and a business associate, and demanded testimony from five others, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/election-results-abortion-rights-democrats-biden-trump-polls-politics-latest?page=with:block-654bf9008f081362db4f9aba#block-654bf9008f081362db4f9aba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawing fury}}}\uc2  from the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ivanka Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/election-results-abortion-rights-democrats-biden-trump-polls-politics-latest?page=with:block-654bfdf88f0898cc3cb03c5b#block-654bfdf88f0898cc3cb03c5b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took the stand}}}\uc2  at her family business\u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial in New York City, and could not remember many things.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Progressives including senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/election-results-abortion-rights-democrats-biden-trump-polls-politics-latest?page=with:block-654bcb778f081362db4f9888#block-654bcb778f081362db4f9888"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders}}}\uc2  and congresswoman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/election-results-abortion-rights-democrats-biden-trump-polls-politics-latest?page=with:block-654bc3e28f081362db4f97fc#block-654bc3e28f081362db4f97fc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alexandria}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/election-results-abortion-rights-democrats-biden-trump-polls-politics-latest?page=with:block-654bc3e28f081362db4f97fc#block-654bc3e28f081362db4f97fc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez}}}\uc2  decried the decision to censure Tlaib.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 DeSantis and Haley to clash as Republicans prepare for Miami debate\par \par \uc2 With the race\u8217\'20\'19s runaway leader appearing at his own private rally just across town, five survivors of an already bruising race for the Republican 2024 presidential nomination will gather in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/miami"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miami}}}\uc2  on Wednesday night to argue why they are the better choice for the White House than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The third Republican primary debate is expected to be a more bitter affair than its predecessors in Wisconsin and California, with sparring over global conflicts in Gaza and Ukraine likely to dominate.\par \par \uc2 From left to right: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Nikki Haley, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , Tim Scott and \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  Composite: Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/08/republican-debate-miami-ron-desantis-nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis and Haley to clash as Republicans prepare for Miami debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Minnesota supreme court rejects challenge to Trump's appearance on primary ballot over 2020 plot\par \par \uc2 Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court has turned down a challenge to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appearing on next year\u8217\'20\'19s primary ballot due to his involvement in attempts to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-insurrection-election-president-f6b72c94bb351c1b870d4884e54f6a75"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Plaintiffs in the case had argued Trump disqualified himself from holding office by participating in an \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection\u8221\'20\'1D, but the state supreme court did not agree, though it left open the possibility he could be barred from the ballot in the general election scheduled for November 2024.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the AP:\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota Supreme Court on Wednesday dismissed a lawsuit seeking to bar former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from the 2024 primary ballot under a constitutional provision that forbids those who \u8220\'20\'1Cengaged in insurrection\u8221\'20\'1D from holding office.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s high court declined to become the first in history to use Section Three of the 14th Amendment to prevent someone from running for the presidency. However, it said in its ruling the decision applied only to the state\u8217\'20\'19s primary and left open the possibility that plaintiffs could try again to knock Trump off the general election ballot in November.\par \par \uc2 The ruling is the first to come in a series of lawsuits filed by liberal groups that are seeking to use Section Three to end the candidacy of the frontrunner in the Republican presidential primary by citing his role in the violent Jan. 6, 2021, assault on the U.S. Capitol that was intended to halt certification of Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory.\par \par \uc2 Trump has attacked the lawsuits as \u8216\'20\'18frivolous\u8217\'20\'19 attempts by \u8216\'20\'18radical Democrat dark money groups\u8217\'20\'19 to short-circuit democracy by interfering with his attempt to regain the White House.\par \par \uc2 The provision at issue bars from office anyone who swore an oath to the constitution and then \u8216\'20\'18engaged in insurrection\u8217\'20\'19 against it. It was mainly used to prevent former Confederates from taking over state and federal government positions after the Civil War.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs in the cases contend that Section Three is simply another qualification for the presidency, just like the Constitution\u8217\'20\'19s requirement that a president be at least 35 years old. They filed in Minnesota because the state has a quick process to challenge ballot qualifications, with the case heard directly by the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court.\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s more from earlier this month, when arguments in the case were first heard:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/02/minnesota-supreme-court-case-trump-2024-ballot-eligibility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump should be blocked from state ballot, Minnesota supreme court hears}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  spent today trying to find the answer to the biggest question of last night\u8217\'20\'19s off-year election results: how did it turn out so well for Democrats and their causes, even in states where Republicans have lately been dominant? Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he found:\par \par \uc2 Nowhere was there a bigger sigh of relief on Tuesday night than at the White House.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-poll-democrats-swing-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brutal opinion polls}}}\uc2  for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the weekend had revived murmurs over his viability as the Democratic standard bearer in next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election. But then came sweeping victories for Democrats at the ballot box in general elections that offered a reminder of two key Republican liabilities: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and democracy.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights supporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won big}}}\uc2  in an Ohio ballot measure. The Democratic governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , was re-elected in Kentucky by campaigning on reproductive rights while his challenger, the state attorney general, \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 , touted his endorsement by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . A Democrat won an open seat on the Pennsylvania supreme court after campaigning on his pledge to uphold \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/08/democrat-biden-poll-election-virginia-kentucky-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Real people, real votes boost Biden\u8217\'20\'19s hopes on night of Democratic wins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has been keeping a live blog running ever since \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 7 October terrorist attack against Israel, covering the fallout from the bloody incursion and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s retaliatory invasion of the Gaza Strip.\par \par \uc2 Follow along below for the latest developments in the conflict:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/08/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-biden-netanyahu-gaza-occupation-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Hamas war live: situation in West Bank \u8216\'20\'18increasingly dire\u8217\'20\'19, UN chief warns; Netanyahu dismisses \u8216\'20\'18idle rumours\u8217\'20\'19 of ceasefire for hostages deal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to meet with bipartisan group of senators who visited Israel, Saudi Arabia, Egypt\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet this evening with a group of Democratic and Republican senators who just returned from a trip to the Middle East, Punchbowl News reports, as his administration navigates the ongoing fallout from Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza following \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s terrorist attack last month:\par \par \uc2 enltrSCOOP \u8212\'20\'14 Senators who recently traveled to Israel, Saudi Arabia & Egypt are heading to the White House tonight to meet with President Biden, per multiple sources.\par \par \uc2 This CODEL was led by Graham and Cardin. Included Thune, Reed, others.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Desiderio (@AndrewDesiderio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1722367065619562498?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden traveled to Israel shortly after the 7 October terrorist attack, and his secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  in recent days visited the country, including the West Bank, as well as Iraq. However the president\u8217\'20\'19s policy has attracted criticism from some Democrats as well as many Arab American voters, who see Biden as enabling the thousands of civilian deaths reported in Gaza since Israel\u8217\'20\'19s counterattack against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  began.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  concludes testimony in civil fraud trial\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a big news day in New York City, where \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  just departed the witness stand in the ongoing civil fraud trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his family.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s daughter kept her testimony in line with that of two of her brothers, who already testified, while repeatedly saying she did not recall details of correspondences about loans \u8211\'20\'13 a plank of the case against the family, which centers on a judge\u8217\'20\'19s finding that the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  for years inflated the value of its assets to secure better loan terms and other benefits.\par \par \uc2 We have a separate live blog that will tell you all about Ivanka\u8217\'20\'19s time on the witness stand today, and you can read it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/08/ivanka-trump-testimony-civil-fraud-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ivanka Trump describes Deutsche Bank\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18positive feelings\u8217\'20\'19 towards her family in fraud trial testimony \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House blasts Republican move to subpoena Biden family\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led House oversight committee today sent subpoenas to the president\u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s brother James Biden and family associate Rob Walker, prompting a furious response from the White House.\par \par \uc2 The subpoenas, which compel the three men to appear for depositions, come as House Republicans press forward with an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that centers on unproven allegations that he benefited from corrupt business dealings by his family members.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe House Oversight Committee has followed the money and built a record of evidence revealing how \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  knew, was involved, and benefited from his family\u8217\'20\'19s influence peddling schemes. Now, the House Oversight Committee is going to bring in members of the Biden family and their associates to question them on this record of evidence,\u8221\'20\'1D the committee\u8217\'20\'19s chair James Comer said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the three subpoenas, Comer requested that five other members of the Biden family and their associates appear for interviews.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, White House spokesperson Ian Sams condemned the GOP for dragging the president\u8217\'20\'19s relatives into their long-running investigations:\par \par \uc2 enltrHallie Biden is the widow of the President's deceased son Beau\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Secundy is her sister\par \par \uc2 Melissa Cohen is the President's daughter-in-law\par \par \uc2 They're all private citizens\par \par \uc2 He won't be, but Comer should be ashamed of desperately resorting to nasty personal smears like this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zmvwSvSFHZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zmvwSvSFHZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ian Sams (@IanSams46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IanSams46/status/1722341551760625728?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Indeed, what to make of yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s off-year election victories by Democrats and their causes, particularly if you are somebody worried about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s poll numbers?\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election came just days after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/05/us/politics/biden-trump-2024-poll.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times and Siena College}}}\uc2  released a survey that found Biden was trailing the Republican presidential frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in five of the six swing states expected to decide the winner. Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 strong electoral performance yesterday seems to contradict that grim conclusion, but, in an analysis, the University of Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Politics says the result is actually not as surprising as it appears.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COff-year elections feature smaller electorates and don\u8217\'20\'19t feature presidential candidates at the top of the ballot,\u8221\'20\'1D the center writes.\par \par \uc2 All signs point to next year\u8217\'20\'19s race being a close contest between Biden and Trump. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/articles/elections-2023-democrats-enjoy-a-strong-night/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Center for Politics\u8217\'20\'19s piece}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Last night\u8217\'20\'19s results have given Democrats a shot in the arm and have confounded the recent narrative about Democrats being in deep trouble next year. But it\u8217\'20\'19s also true that these races in many respects differ from the election coming up next year. It may be the case that President Biden is in fact uniquely vulnerable, and that even former President Trump \u8211\'20\'13 himself dragged down by plenty of vulnerabilities that likely are not getting the kind of attention now that they will if he is renominated \u8211\'20\'13 could beat Biden. It may also be the case that polling a year out from an election is not predictive (and it often is not). Maybe the Democrats do just have an advantage now in smaller turnout, off-year elections as their base has absorbed many higher-turnout, college-educated voters while shedding lower-turnout voters who don\u8217\'20\'19t have a four-year degree. Maybe the presidential year turnout will bring out more Trump voters and give the Republicans a clearer shot. About all we feel comfortable saying is that we should continue to expect the presidential race to be close and competitive \u8211\'20\'13 a boring statement, we know, but probably true.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kentucky has not supported a Democratic president in more than 25 years, but last night, voters in the Bluegrass State decided to give Democratic governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  a second term.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN, Beshear was asked if his victory in the strongly Republican state offered any lessons for beleaguered Democrats elsewhere. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  (D), when asked if his reelection in deep-red Kentucky is a blueprint for Democratic campaigns:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur blueprint was... show up, work hard, get results, and care about everybody. And don't get distracted by whatever the issue of the day is in Washington, D.C.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EZZcEb3TQ0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EZZcEb3TQ0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722298480587133110?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the White House, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  told reporters yesterday was a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood night\u8221\'20\'1D after voters in Ohio and Virginia handed victories to advocates of reproductive rights:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CVoters have been clear, regardless of whether they're in a so-called red or blue state, that one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree that government should not be telling a woman what to do with her body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 VP \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Election Night {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CAlW3ICgOs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CAlW3ICgOs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722338211135959301?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The bigger question that is undoubtedly on her mind \u8211\'20\'13 and, of course, on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 is whether the momentum Democrats have seen at the state-level since Roe v Wade was overturned will remain in a year, when the presidential elections are held.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Council on American-Islamic Relations\uc2  has denounced the Republican-led House of Representatives\u8217\'20\'19 decision to censure \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  over her criticisms of Israel.\par \par \uc2 In a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cair.com/press_releases/cair-slams-houses-hypocritical-and-racist-censure-of-palestinian-american-muslim-congresswoman-rashida-tlaib/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  on Wednesday, \uc2 CAIR\uc2  national executive director \uc2 Nihad Awad\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 The American Muslim community stands against this hypocritical and racist targeting of representative \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , whose voice is indispensable in representing the concerns of millions of Americans who are horrified by the war crimes our government supports against the Palestinian people. She should wear this cowardly censure as a badge of honor. We will not be cowed by those attempting to muzzle our voices.\par \par \uc2 Both Republicans and Democrats in the House of Representatives who orchestrated the suppression and censure of the only Muslim Palestinian voice in Congress under the cover of darkness while ignoring the openly racist, bigoted and violent remarks that members of Congress have made about Muslims and Palestinians, should be deeply ashamed of their actions. They are on the wrong side of history.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  called last night\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic victories across the country an \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant night for the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey rejected these extreme, extreme policies that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing from the Republican party and they also lifted up the president\u8217\'20\'19s agenda, the president\u8217\'20\'19s values.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response to a follow-up question on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings, Jean-Pierre said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to take these polls with a grain of salt\u8230\'20\'26 I talked about 2020\u8230\'20\'26what we saw is a president that was able to bring an incredibly strong, diverse coalition to win in 2020. We saw the same thing in 2022\u8230\'20\'26 we kept on hearing about a \u8216\'20\'18Red Wave\u8217\'20\'19 that didn\u8217\'20\'19t materialize\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t put much stock in polls. The president\u8217\'20\'19s going to focus on delivering for the American people. He has an agenda that is incredibly popular and that matters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House denounces Tlaib's use of controversial pro-Palestinian slogan\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe strongly disagree\u8221\'20\'1D with Democratic representative \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s support for the controversial pro-Palestinian phrase \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom the river to the sea\u8221\'20\'1D, for which the sole Palestinian congresswoman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/08/rashida-tlaib-censure-vote-palestine-support-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was censured}}}\uc2  by the Republican-controlled House on Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe strongly disagree with using that phrase \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s been said by many people at the White House. I do not have any conversations to read out to you with the congresswomen,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said after being asked if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has spoken to Tlaib about the matter.\par \par \uc2 But Jean-Pierre added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been very, very clear how it is important to be mindful about the language that we use at this time, and we will continue to speak out on that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/rashida-tlaib"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tlaib}}}\uc2 , who is the only Palestinian American in the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 , on Tuesday defended her criticism of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s actions in Gaza and urged US lawmakers to join in calling for a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/rashida-tlaib-censure-israel-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I will not be silenced\u8217\'20\'19: Rashida Tlaib hits back at congressional censure motion}}}\par \par \uc2 Tlaib has long criticized \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s support of Israel, but received intense backlash after her defense of the slogan \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom the river to the sea\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a social media post on Friday, Tlaib {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RashidaTlaib/status/1720574880557539763?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1720574880557539763%7Ctwgr%5E4097e55233a549413e95b7f6b36e190b90a31568%7Ctwcon%5Es1_c10&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmichiganadvance.com%2F2023%2F11%2F06%2Ftlaib-stands-by-her-defense-of-pro-palestinanian-slogan-from-the-river-to-the-sea%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended the phrase}}}\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Can aspirational call for freedom, human rights, and peaceful coexistence, not death, destruction, or hate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/31/from-the-river-to-the-sea-where-does-the-slogan-come-from-and-what-does-it-mean-israel-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The full slogan}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the river to the sea, Palestine will be free\u8221\'20\'1D, references the land that sits between the Jordan River and the Mediterranean Sea. While many recognize the slogan as a call for Palestinian liberation, others argue that the term has been used to call for the destruction of Israel and the persecution of Jewish people.\par \par \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  appeared before Congress before she was censured, with Minnesota congresswoman \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  to her left. Photograph: CSPAN\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House reiterates that it does not support ceasefire in Gaza\par \par \uc2 White House national security spokesman John Kirby was just asked at the daily press briefing how long is a humanitarian pause \u8211\'20\'13 in the sense of something being characterized as such.\par \par \uc2 Is, for example, a 72-hour humanitarian pause different from a ceasefire, Kirby was asked by one of the gathered journalists.\par \par \uc2 Kirby said a humanitarian pause was \u8220\'20\'1Cas long as it needed to be\u8221\'20\'1D, eg to get aid in to Gaza or people out of the Palestinian territory, and was something different from \u8220\'20\'1Ca general ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D that stands as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccessation of hostilities\u8221\'20\'1D between both sides as they seek to negotiate towards an end game in a war, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do not support that at this time,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby said. He said the White House regarded at ceasefire as currently being to the benefit of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , as opposed to Israel, in military and propaganda terms.\par \par \uc2 A humanitarian pause, in contrast, is something \u8220\'20\'1Ctemporary, localized and for specific purposes,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby said.\par \par \uc2 John Kirby arrives for the White House press briefing today. Photograph: Chris Kleponis/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House national security spokesman John Kirby adds, at the press briefing now ongoing in the west wing, that it could take \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than one pause\u8221\'20\'1D in the fighting in Gaza to get all hostages out of the territory.\par \par \uc2 That is not to say there is any sign today that an opportunity has yet been created for them to be released.\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military is currently reiterating that there will be no ceasefire in Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 but the military will allow for \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian pauses,\u8221\'20\'1D Reuters notes.\par \par \uc2 The White House reckons such pauses could \u8220\'20\'1Clast hours or days.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kirby says the US continues to urge Israel to minimize civilian deaths in Gaza, especially putting people who are currently trying to flee to the south of the territory or out of it altogether \u8220\'20\'1Cin harm\u8217\'20\'19s way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He acknowledged that \u8220\'20\'1Cmost Palestinians don\u8217\'20\'19t want to leave\u8221\'20\'1D and there are around a million people internally displaced within Gaza right now.\par \par \uc2 National Security Council Coordinator for Strategic Communications John Kirby speaks during the daily briefing in the Brady Briefing Room of the White House in Washington today. Photograph: Andrew Caballero-Reynolds/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House is holding its press briefing and national security spokesman John Kirby is reiterating a point he made yesterday, that the notion of Israel occupying Gaza is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a long term solution to post-conflict governance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This follows Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s declaration earlier this week that Israel would take control of security in Gaza for an indefinite period, adding to the sense of uncertainty over the future of the Palestinian territory even as it is currently gripped by war and humanitarian crisis.\par \par \uc2 Kirby said, meanwhile, that there are still between 500 and 600 Americans that the US is trying to get out of Gaza. And, asked by journalists about what the militant group \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , that controls Gaza, is demanding to release the more than 200 hostages that its fighters snatched when they attacked southern Israel on October 7 and killed at least 1,400 people, Kirby would not give details. The hostages include Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a way to communicate with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , we are using that way. We are doing everything we can to get those folks back with their families,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders on House's censure of \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 : 'Pathetic and shameful'\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders has also hit back at the Republican-led House\u8217\'20\'19s decision to censure \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  over her criticisms of Israel amid its deadly bombing campaign that has killed over 10,000 Palestinians, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe House should pass desperately needed aid for Gaza, work to stop the conflict in the Middle East, and address the pressing needs of the American people.\par \par \uc2 Instead they voted to censure my friend \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , the only Palestinian-American in Congress. Pathetic and shameful!\u8221\'20\'1D the Independent Vermont senator said.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House should pass desperately needed aid for Gaza, work to stop the conflict in the Middle East, and address the pressing needs of the American people. Instead they voted to censure my friend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RashidaTlaib?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RashidaTlaib}}}\uc2 , the only Palestinian-American in Congress. Pathetic and shameful!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bernie Sanders (@SenSanders) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSanders/status/1722274281391112667?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 MPower Change, a Muslim-led grassroots organization, has thrown its support behind \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  following her censure by the Republican-led House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 In a post on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , the group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CzXvD1YregV/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShame on those who voted to silence the only Palestinian voice in Congress. Rep. \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  has been censured for defending the rights of Palestinians to live free of Israeli occupation and siege and for demanding an end to the bloodshed in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Rashida has always been on the side of humanity and she will continue to do that regardless of those who try to stop her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  speaks out against \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  censure\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  has spoken out against the House\u8217\'20\'19s censure of \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  over her criticisms of Israel amid its deadly bombing campaign across Gaza that has killed over 10,000 Palestinians in reponse to the October 7 \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks on Israel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not lost on anyone how many offensive, violent, and racist things people regularly hear members of Congress say, yet virtually the only one that gets censured for her political speech also happens to be the only Palestinian American.\par \par \uc2 It does not reflect well. At all,\u8221\'20\'1D the New York Democratic representative said.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt is not lost on anyone how many offensive, violent, and racist things people regularly hear members of Congress say, yet virtually the only one that gets censured for her political speech also happens to be the only Palestinian American.\par \par \uc2 It does not reflect well. At all. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LzQUtg2WbU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/LzQUtg2WbU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1722253102248755218?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led House of Representatives has voted to censure \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic representative and Congress\u8217\'20\'19s only Palestinian-American.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Chris Stein reports:\par \par \uc2 The 234-188 tally came after enough {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  joined with Republicans to censure Tlaib, a punishment one step below expulsion from the House. The three-term congresswoman has long been a target of criticism for her views on the decades-long conflict in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The debate on the censure resolution on Tuesday afternoon was emotional and intense. The Republican representative Rich McCormick of Georgia pushed the censure measure in response to what he called Tlaib\u8217\'20\'19s promotion of antisemitic rhetoric. He said she had \u8220\'20\'1Clevied unbelievable falsehoods about our greatest ally, Israel, and the attack on October 7\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Tlaib provoked criticism last week by defending the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/31/from-the-river-to-the-sea-where-does-the-slogan-come-from-and-what-does-it-mean-israel-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial slogan}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom the river to the sea\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In remarks on the House floor, Tlaib defended her criticism of the country and urged lawmakers to join in calling for a ceasefire in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will not be silenced and I will not let you distort my words,\u8221\'20\'1D Tlaib said. \u8220\'20\'1CNo government is beyond criticism. The idea that criticizing the government of Israel is antisemitic sets a very dangerous precedent, and it\u8217\'20\'19s been used to silence diverse voices speaking up for human rights across our nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also said she had condemned the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks on Israeli citizens several times.\par \par \uc2 For further details, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/house-vote-censure-rashida-tlaib-palestine-criticize-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House votes to censure Rashida Tlaib over her criticism of Israel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 : 'It's time to recognize Maga extremism is the wrong answer'\par \par \uc2 Following a series of Democratic wins across the country, Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said that \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s time to recognize Maga extremism is the wrong answer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In an address on Wednesday, the New York senator said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no possible takeaway from last night other than this: Americans fiercely opposed Maga extremism, fiercely opposed total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and want bipartisan leaders who can put America\u8217\'20\'19s needs first.\par \par \uc2 After last night\u8217\'20\'19s results, I have a message to my Republican colleagues:\par \par \uc2 When the Maga agenda can\u8217\'20\'19t win in deep-red Kentucky or in Ohio or help you in Virginia, it\u8217\'20\'19s time to recognize Maga extremism is the wrong answer, not just for the country but even for the GOP.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CWhen the MAGA agenda can't win in deep-red Kentucky, or in Ohio, or help you in Virginia, it's time to recognize MAGA extremism is the wrong answer, not just for the country but even for the GOP.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Majority Leader Schumer (D-NY) on Democrats' wins on Election Night {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dOT5RGS34m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dOT5RGS34m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1722287173620080845?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is more from the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s staff and agencies on Yusef Salaam, one of the exonerated '\u8220\'20\'1CCentral Park Five\u8221\'20\'1D members who won a New York City council seat following yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s election:\par \par \uc2 Salaam, a Democrat, will represent a central Harlem district on the city council, having run unopposed for the seat in one of many local elections playing out across New York state on Tuesday. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/salaam-central-park-new-york-council-primary-508d317b9dce37fd5635ae6128ceec2d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won his primary election}}}\uc2  in a landslide.\par \par \uc2 The victory comes more than two decades after DNA evidence was used to overturn the convictions of Salaam and four other Black and Latino men in the 1989 rape and beating of a white jogger in Central Park. Salaam was imprisoned for almost seven years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor me, this means that we can really become our ancestors\u8217\'20\'19 wildest dreams,\u8221\'20\'1D Salaam said in an interview before the election.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  City, voters were deciding whether to re-elect the Queens district attorney and cast ballots in other city council races. The council, which passes legislation and has some oversight powers over city agencies, has long been dominated by Democrats and the party is certain to retain firm control after the election.\par \par \uc2 Local elections on Long Island could offer clues about how the city\u8217\'20\'19s suburbs could vote in next year\u8217\'20\'19s congressional elections.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/yusef-salaam-nyc-council-seat-central-park-five"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Exonerated \u8216\'20\'18Central Park Five\u8217\'20\'19 member wins New York City council seat}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Philadephia has elected Cherelle Parker, the first female mayor to lead the city.\par \par \uc2 Following her victory, Parker, who served 10 years as a state representative for northwest Philadelphia, said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you Philly. We did it. We made history, or \u8220\'20\'1Cher\u8221\'20\'1D story. As a little girl, I never dreamed that this moment would arrive but it\u8217\'20\'19s here now\u8230\'20\'26 From the bottom of my heart, thank you for believing in me and in my vision for a safer, cleaner greener city with economic oppurtunity for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThank you, Philly!! Stay tuned for more announcements and updates coming soon right here! Our journey doesn't end here\u8212\'20\'14it's just the beginning of the work we'll do together. Keep an eye on social media for exciting news to come! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wfEKYFPzXY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wfEKYFPzXY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cherelle Parker (@PeopleforParker) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PeopleforParker/status/1722237540034367861?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Brandon Presley\uc2 , the Democrat who lost to Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s incumbent Republican governor, \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2  said that although the result \u8220\'20\'1Cwasn\u8217\'20\'19t what we wanted, I\u8217\'20\'19m more confident than ever in our people \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMay God bless Gov Reeves in his victory and this great state,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, following his defeat in yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial election.\par \par \uc2 enltrMississippi is a wonderful state that welcomed me and Katelyn into all 82 counties over this campaign. While tonight\u8217\'20\'19s result wasn\u8217\'20\'19t what we wanted, I\u8217\'20\'19m more confident than ever in our people. May God bless Gov. Reeves in his victory and this great state. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uCaxzhIq3Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uCaxzhIq3Y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Brandon Presley\uc2  (@BrandonPresley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BrandonPresley/status/1722127216736112827?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Maine voters have rejected a utilities initiative to establish the state\u8217\'20\'19s first public power company backed by climate groups.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Aliya Uteuova reports:\par \par \uc2 Maine voters turned down an attempt on Tuesday to oust the state\u8217\'20\'19s corporate-owned electric utilities and replace them with a non-profit backed by climate advocacy groups.\par \par \uc2 In one of several ballot initiatives, Maine voters rejected the proposed takeover of the two investor-owned utilities that distribute 97% of electricity in the state.\par \par \uc2 Voters opted for the status quo rather than a move that would have marked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/maine-electric-utility-referendum-9bdf113f345c3b93de0f5fc59f791c19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first time a state with existing private utilities discarded them all at the same time}}}\uc2 . The proposal had called for dismantling \uc2 Central Maine Power\uc2  and \uc2 Versant Power\uc2  and creating a non-profit utility called Pine Tree Power to govern the grid.\par \par \uc2 Supporters had said there was little to lose because of the utilities\u8217\'20\'19 poor performance.\par \par \uc2 Critics, though, argued there was no guarantee the non-profit utility would perform any better, while the move could spark lawsuits and buying out the existing utilities could cost as much as $13.5bn.\par \par \uc2 For further details, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/08/maine-voters-reject-electric-utilities-proposal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maine voters reject plan for non-profit power utility backed by climate groups}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is video of Ohio voters celebrating their victory after securing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the state:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Rhode Island has elected its first Black representative to Congress, Democratic Gabe Amo.\par \par \uc2 Following his win, Amo, who worked under the \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  administrations, said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI went to vote with my mom earlier today. When I was 8 years old helping my mother study for the citizenship test, I never could have imagined that I would go with her to cast her ballot to vote for her son for the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The journey of so many Rhode Islanders and their familes is one of grit, hard work, determination and resilience. I stand on the shoulders of so many who came before me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrGabe Amo will be the first person of color to represent Rhode Island in Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I was 8 years old helping my mother study for the citizenship test, I never could have imagined that I would go with her to cast her ballot to vote for her son.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aGSDLLQ4xK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aGSDLLQ4xK}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YkmmpMVXTu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YkmmpMVXTu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 POLITICO (@politico) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/politico/status/1722103780613792235?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Campaigners hail voters for rejecting Republican 'false narrative' on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 ParentsTogether Action, a national family advocacy group, has hailed voters, including parents, for \u8220\'20\'1Crejecting the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to win their votes\u8221\'20\'1D in multiple states.\par \par \uc2 The organization\u8217\'20\'19s executive director Ailen Arreaza said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis election season, we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s strategy on full display: target parent voters with a false narrative about \u8216\'20\'18parental rights\u8217\'20\'19 that hinges on a manufactured sense of distrust, chaos, and loss of control that Republicans themselves have created to stoke fear in parents - and last night we saw that agenda fail.\par \par \uc2 From Ohio to Virginia to Kentucky and beyond, voters saw the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s emphasis on education and parental rights as exactly what it is: an attempt to distract from their extreme and unpopular agenda. Let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear: the real GOP agenda aims to obliterate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, undermine access to an honest education, ban books, all while attempting to cut benefits that actually help families thrive like the expanded Child Tax Credit and accessible child care.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake though\u8211\'20\'13 Republicans see parents as a key voting bloc who they can persuade by creating a false sense that their rights are being threatened..\par \par \uc2 Like yesterday showed us, parents will continue to see through the rhetorical noise and vote for who will really support what families want and need to succeed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is an excerpt from a poll report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/11/07/politics/cnn-poll-trump-biden-matchup/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  released}}}\uc2  by CNN on Tuesday that showed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  leading \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  by 4% in a hypothetical rematch:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C One year out from Election Day 2024, former President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/president-donald-trump-45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  narrowly leads President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2 , 49% to 45% among registered voters, in a hypothetical rematch in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/24131320/cnn-poll-on-2024.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest CNN poll}}}\uc2  conducted by SSRS\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 All told, 51% of voters nationwide say there is no chance at all that they would vote for Biden, and just 4% are not currently supporting him but say there is a chance they will. Nearly half, 48%, say there is no chance they will vote for Trump, and only 2% that they aren\u8217\'20\'19t currently backing him but would consider it\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Among voters younger than 35, 48% support Trump, 47% Biden. Political independents break 45% Trump to 41% Biden. Black voters favor Biden, 73%vs. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 23%, while Latino voters split 50% Biden to 46% Trump. And among voters of color generally, women divide 63% Biden to 31% Trump, while men split about evenly, 49% Trump to 46% Biden.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  thanks voters for re-electing him\par \par \uc2 Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  has thanked his voters after winning a second term, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our chance to turn these four years of progress into decades of prosperity for your kids and mine. Let\u8217\'20\'19s make it happen together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrTo my fellow Kentuckians: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 This is our chance to turn these four years of progress into decades of prosperity for your kids and mine. Let's make it happen together. ^AB {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/isjH0CNRdZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/isjH0CNRdZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  (@GovAndyBeshear) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovAndyBeshear/status/1722089413017006393?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hails Ohio's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights victory: 'Democracy won'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has hailed the victory secured by Ohio voters to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released on Tuesday, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/11/07/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-ohio-issue-1-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmericans once again voted to protect their fundamental freedoms \u8211\'20\'13 and democracy won. In Ohio, voters protected access to reproductive health in their state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Ohioans and voters across the country rejected attempts by MAGA Republican elected officials to impose extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that put the health and lives of women in jeopardy, force women to travel hundreds of miles for care, and threaten to criminalize doctors and nurses for providing the health care that their patients need and that they are trained to provide.\par \par \uc2 This extreme and dangerous agenda is out-of-step with the vast majority of Americans. My administration will continue to protect access to reproductive health care and call on Congress to restore the protections of Roe v. Wade in federal law once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats secure victories in Virginia, Ohio and Kentucky\par \par \uc2 Democrats have secured victories in multiple states including Virginia, Ohio and Kentucky in yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s elections, while Mississippi saw its Republican incumbent governor beat out his Democratic opponent.\par \par \uc2 In Virginia, Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/virginia-election-voting-results-house-delegates-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gained}}}\uc2  full control of the state legislature, a win that will allow them to block Republican governor Glenn Youngkin\u8217\'20\'19s conservative agenda \u8211\'20\'13 which includes a 15-week ban on abortions.\par \par \uc2 Ohio also saw a win for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights with voters overwhelming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deciding}}}\uc2  to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections to the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 In Kentucky, the predominantly conservative state saw its Democratic incumbent governor \uc2 Andy Beshear{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/kentucky-governor-election-results-andy-beshear-democrat-wins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retain}}}\uc2  his seat. Beshear beat his Republican opponent \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 , also the state\u8217\'20\'19s first Black attorney general.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Mississippi, \uc2 Brandon Presley\uc2 , a Democrat and relative of Elvis Presley, conceded to the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican incumbent governor \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2  following a heated race that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/mississippi-governor-election-results-tate-reeves-republican-wins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 included}}}\uc2  verbal blows exchanged on both sides.\par \par \uc2 Despite yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic victories, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is trailing behind \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in five swing states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/05/biden-trails-trump-five-swing-states-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including}}}\uc2  Nevada, Arizona, Georgia, Pennsylvania and Michigan. A new CNN poll released on Tuesday also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/11/07/politics/cnn-poll-trump-biden-matchup/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed }}}\uc2  Trump leading Biden 49% to 45% in a hypothetical rematch.\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led House voted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/house-vote-censure-rashida-tlaib-palestine-criticize-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 censure Rashida Tlaib, Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic representative}}}\uc2  and Congress\u8217\'20\'19s only Palestinian American over her criticism of Israel.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/yusef-salaam-nyc-council-seat-central-park-five"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yusef Salaam,}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/yusef-salaam-nyc-council-seat-central-park-five"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  one of the exonerated Central Park Five members, has won a New York City council seat.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is set to attend a rountable with climate leaders, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/playbook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231108ejb800264\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
