\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18 \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  is a winning issue\u8217\'20\'19: rights victories in 2023 US elections raise hopes for 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,011 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par 19:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 23\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats will almost certainly use the issue to buoy their party in races, while Republican voters may be abandoning their party over it\par \par \uc2 More than a year after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, handing states the power to decide if and how to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , voters have again overwhelmingly rejected attempts to curtail access to the procedure. A string of successes for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups on Tuesday are raising hopes among Democrats that, despite recent dismal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-poll-democrats-swing-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2 , the issue will lift their odds in 2024.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, the only state to hold an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot referendum in 2023, more than 56% of voters agreed to enshrine the right to the procedure into the state constitution. In Virginia, Democrats won back full control of the state legislature after Republicans campaigned on the promise of a \u8220\'20\'1Csensible limit\u8221\'20\'1D that would ban most abortions past 15 weeks of pregnancy. In Kentucky, the incumbent Democratic governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , bested his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republican opponent. And in Pennsylvania, in a race dominated by talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Democrats won a seat on the state supreme court.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday evening in downtown Columbus, Ohio, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates crowded into a hotel ballroom to watch as results streamed in. Once the vote was called in their favor, the conversation in the room immediately turned to the topic on everyone\u8217\'20\'19s minds: what does the victory mean for next year?\par \par \uc2 In 2024, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related referendums may be on the ballot in roughly a dozen states, including in critical swing states like Nevada, Florida, Pennsylvania, Arizona and Iowa. Democrats will almost certainly lean on the issue to buoy their party in races for Congress and the White House. And Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s results in Ohio raise hopes that they might be able to pluck voters from the other side. While Joe Biden lost Ohio in 2020, garnering only about 45% of the vote, Issue 1, the proposal to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution, won with an estimated 56% of the vote on Tuesday. That sweep indicates that Republican voters are abandoning their party on this issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a winning issue, including in states that are considered red,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Kimberly Inez McGuire\uc2 , executive director of Urge: Unite for Reproductive & Gender Equity. \u8220\'20\'1CYoung people, black voters, rural voters \u8211\'20\'13 voters all across the state came out and we saw support in every single corner of the state. The lesson for other states is: don\u8217\'20\'19t take anyone for granted. Don\u8217\'20\'19t assume they\u8217\'20\'19re gonna support you, but also don\u8217\'20\'19t assume that they\u8217\'20\'19re gonna oppose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The issue turns voters out in high numbers, which could also prove a boon for Biden at a time of low enthusiasm: nearly 4 million people voted this year on Issue 1, according to early data from Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state office. That\u8217\'20\'19s only slightly less than the 4.2 million people who turned out to vote in Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial race last year \u8211\'20\'13 even though 2023 was considered an \u8220\'20\'1Coff-off\u8221\'20\'1D election year.\par \par \uc2 The failures in Ohio and Virginia also leave Republicans without a clear roadmap for messaging on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 an issue that led them to underperform in the 2022 midterms. In Ohio, opponents of the ballot initiative, Issue 1, focused much of their message not on the morality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but on the idea that Issue 1 threatened parents\u8217\'20\'19 rights to know if their children underwent an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or gender-affirming care. (That claim is dubious, legal experts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/ohio-abortion-vote-misinformation-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2 .) In Virginia, Republicans tried to take advantage of Americans\u8217\'20\'19 lack of support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the second and third trimester by proposing to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks with exceptions for rape, incest and medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 Both efforts were viewed as tests for next year \u8211\'20\'13 had either message won over voters, Republicans across the country may have adopted them in their own races in 2024. Now, their strategy is in question, and any course they choose risks alienating key constituencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the GOP moves to the center on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they\u8217\'20\'19re afraid that they\u8217\'20\'19ll lose conservative donors and base voters \u8211\'20\'13 who are the ones who tend to be the most passionate Republican voters, the ones who turn out the most reliably and also people who donate a lot of money,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a University of California, Davis School of Law professor who studies the legal history of reproduction. \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans have been trying to finesse that, with pretty much no success to date.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite being directly responsible for overturning Roe v Wade through his appointments to the supreme court, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has attempted to stem the damage by distancing himself from much of his party, coming out against a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. But polling shows that voters don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily trust Republicans who say they will not totally ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That may be in part due to their decades-long partnership with an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement that would like to eliminate the procedure entirely.\par \par \uc2 Hours before polls closed on Tuesday, Jamie Curry, Ohio regional coordinator for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Students for Life, tried to convince passing \uc2 Ohio State University\uc2  students that Issue 1 was too extreme. \u8220\'20\'1CYou seem to be in favor of a commonsense, middle of the road, but there\u8217\'20\'19s plenty of people who align more pro-choice and are voting no on this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D Curry told one student.\par \par \uc2 But Curry\u8217\'20\'19s message of moderation and compromise were contrasted by her group\u8217\'20\'19s nearby poster board , which read: \u8220\'20\'1CAll human beings are valuable persons, no matter their stage in life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans can spend their money saying that, \u8216\'20\'18We are the moderates on this,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Joey Teitelbaum, vice-president of research for Global Strategy Group, a Democratic polling firm. \u8220\'20\'1CBut in voting for Democrats in Virginia and voting for \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a major part of that race and the communications, voters are clearly saying, \u8216\'20\'18We do not trust Republicans on this.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231108ejb80035x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
