\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Real people, real votes boost Biden\u8217\'20\'19s hopes on night of Democratic wins\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,244 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par 19:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 22\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Election victories in Virginia and Kentucky and an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  vote in Ohio give welcome boost to president after bruising opinion pollsUS politics \u8211\'20\'13 live updates\par \par \uc2 Nowhere was there a bigger sigh of relief on Tuesday night than at the White House.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-poll-democrats-swing-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brutal opinion polls}}}\uc2  for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the weekend had revived murmurs over his viability as the Democratic standard bearer in next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election. But then came sweeping victories for Democrats at the ballot box in general elections that offered a reminder of two key Republican liabilities: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and democracy.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights supporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won big}}}\uc2  in an Ohio ballot measure. The Democratic governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , was re-elected in Kentucky by campaigning on reproductive rights while his challenger, the state attorney general, \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 , touted his endorsement by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . A Democrat won an open seat on the Pennsylvania supreme court after campaigning on his pledge to uphold \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the biggest pre-2024 barometer was Virginia, where the Republican governor, Glenn Youngkin, who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/01/youngkin-virginia-election-voters-removed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assailed voting rights}}}\uc2 , poured tens of millions of dollars into an effort to gain full control of the statehouse and impose a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Instead Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/virginia-election-voting-results-house-delegates-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secured both chambers}}}\uc2 , simultaneously killing off rumours of a last-minute Youngkin presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 If things had gone the other way, the whispering campaign for 80-year-old Biden to step aside would have become a roar. Instead, in the cold light of day, white hair and an unsteady gait look like small offences compared with a messianic mission to end American democracy and reproductive autonomy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is an incredible amount of whiplash over the course of the last 72 hours,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://indivisible.org/ezra-levin-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ezra Levin}}}\uc2 , co-founder and co-executive director of the progressive grassroots movement Indivisible. \u8220\'20\'1CAs of Sunday night, Democrats were destined to lose badly both on Tuesday and also a year from Tuesday. It was written in the stars, foregone conclusion that Biden was going to lead his party to defeat and he would deserve it. Just look at the terrible series of polls that came out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think polls are meaningless but I do think they are given more power than they deserve. What the poll says is right now here is what a group of voters think they will do a year from now. We can take that at face value and believe that is the case and also we should pay attention to the other data that we have coming in, namely the election results that tell us when the choice is given to voters about whether they are going to push the button for the Republicans, for the Maga [Make America great again] supporters, for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  zealots or a Democrat or a Democratic proposal like protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, it\u8217\'20\'19s very clear what they choose .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The outcomes indicate the staying power and potency of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an issue since a conservative majority of the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-supreme-court-decision-854f60302f21c2c35129e58cf8d8a7b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned the federal right to the procedure last year}}}\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measures have passed in several states as some other Republican-run states have instituted new bans. Joe Scarborough, a cable news TV host and former Republican congressman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Morning_Joe/status/1722212687227375938?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commented on Wednesday}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe overturning of Roe has got to be the most devastating single event for the Republican party since Watergate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One man who understands this is Trump himself. Although he likes to remind religious conservatives that his supreme court appointments made the overturning of Roe v Wade possible, he has also used 2024 election campaign speeches to urge pragmatism and warn his base that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are a vote loser. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own past, more liberal views on the topic might lend credence to the idea that he would not seek a national ban.\par \par \uc2 The former president also pushes election denialism less than he used to. His speeches typically dwell briefly on his false claim that the 2020 election was stolen; he devotes far more time to security at the US-Mexico border, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/StephenM/status/1722265254393184294?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his allies said}}}\uc2  Republican candidates should have done more to exploit. But his numerous criminal indictments and looming trials will make his anti-democracy extremism millstone hard to escape.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, the evidence of the past seven years is that, with Trump at the head of the party, Republicans repeatedly lose or underperform expectations. \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , who is challenging Trump for the nomination, cited Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s result in deep-red Kentucky. \u8220\'20\'1CCameron was a rising star in the Republican party until he decided to throw his lot in with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D he told CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s face it, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is political and electoral poison down ballot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump effect may have damaged Republicans in Virginia. The results may also indicate the limitations of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/02/parents-right-movement-virginia-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cparents\u8217\'20\'19 rights\u8221\'20\'1D movement}}}\uc2  seen as pivotal to Youngkin\u8217\'20\'19s election as governor two years ago. The movement arose from grievance over schools\u8217\'20\'19 handling of the coronavirus pandemic, including long closures and mask mandates, all of which may have faded from memory. It then morphed into divides around instruction of hot-button topics related to race, sexual orientation and gender identity, with flashpoints over book bans and school bathrooms.\par \par \uc2 But just as the \u8220\'20\'1Cwar on woke\u8221\'20\'1D pushed by the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , has a hit a ceiling in the Republican primary, Republicans appear to have run out of road in Virginia. Democrats held the state senate and flipped control of the house of delegates. Among the winners was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/nbc-out/out-politics-and-policy/danica-roem-become-virginias-1st-transgender-state-senator-rcna124175"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Danica Roem}}}\uc2 , who became the first transgender person elected to Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s state senate after a campaign that emphasised practical concerns such as fixing roads and feeding kids. Liberals won a majority on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/liberals-win-loudoun-county-schools_n_65440037e4b06bc01e238d10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 school board in Loudoun county}}}\uc2 , which had become a frontline in the culture wars.\par \par \uc2 Levin of Indivisible commented: \u8220\'20\'1CIt turns out voters actually like teachers. It turns out voters actually like their schools. It turns out voters don\u8217\'20\'19t actually want to pick vicious fights with trans kids. It just doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work for them. Now, I would like the Republicans to drop those attacks because they do quite a bit of harm, even though they lose elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 All of it is good news for Biden, who has shown a Houdini-like ability to escape the doubters and bounce back just in the nick of time. Still, his name was not on the ballot and the polls offer some nagging doubts about whether Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 down-ballot success will translate to the president, who faces {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-approval-economy-poll-survey-b6ec307d15e65ad37b69ff1dc1a0dca8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widespread scepticism about his job performance}}}\uc2  and internal dissent over his staunch embrace of Israel.\par \par \uc2 Cenk Uygur {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/cenkuygur?s=43"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ??}}}\uc2 , a political commentator and media host who has launched a long-shot primary campaign against Biden, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/cenkuygur/status/1722266785620386087?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on X}}}\uc2 , the platform formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CLast night showed that Democratic policies are strong everywhere, from Ohio to Kentucky. Yet the leading Democratic nominee for president is trailing the most unpopular politician of all time by five points. Biden never makes the Democratic case. Extraordinarily weak candidate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Others, however, contend that Tuesday was a blue wave and now is not the time to change the captain of a winning team. Jim Messina, a Democratic strategist, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Messina2012/status/1722235811528348095?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWhat if \u8211\'20\'13 and just hear me out for a second \u8211\'20\'13 the Democratic brand *and* \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  have policies people actually like? And the way people voted last night is a reflection of both those things?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231108ejb8002xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
