\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats gain control of Virginia state legislature in blow to Republican plans\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve \par \uc2 833 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par 16:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In a rebuke to Glenn Youngkin, the governor, voters rejected stricter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits and conservative school policies\par \par \uc2 Democrats have secured full control of the Virginia state legislature, winning a majority in the house of delegates and depriving the Republican governor, Glenn Youngkin, of the opportunity to enact a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Democrats maintained their majority in the state senate and flipped control of the house of delegates, where Republicans previously held a narrow advantage. Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 victories quashed Youngkin\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of securing a Republican-controlled legislature that would be able to advance his policy agenda, casting doubt upon his prospects as a potential presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor Youngkin and Virginia Republicans did everything they could to take total control of state government, but the people of the Commonwealth rejected them,\u8221\'20\'1D Susan Swecker, chair of the Democratic party of Virginia, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CVirginians won\u8217\'20\'19t go backwards. Instead of extremism and culture wars, people voted for commonsense leadership and problem solvers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As one of the only states holding off-year elections, the Virginia results could serve as a bellwether for the presidential race next year. Democrats also secured key victories on Tuesday in Kentucky, where the incumbent governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , won re-election, and Ohio, where voters approved a measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Virginia Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 success will spell doom for Youngkin\u8217\'20\'19s proposed 15-week \u8220\'20\'1Climit\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would ban the procedure after 15 weeks with exceptions for rape, incest and medical emergencies. Democratic legislators in Virginia have previously used their senate majority to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-virginia-state-government-42791ab80e24a3c6944819ac820273a6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 block bills}}}\uc2  restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and they had promised to do so again if they maintained control of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 The possibility of curtailing access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had become a galvanizing issue in Virginia, which is now the last remaining state in the US south without severe restrictions on the procedure. Virginia Democrats correctly predicted that voters\u8217\'20\'19 continued displeasure with the reversal of Roe v Wade would help them flip control of the house of delegates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Republicans] called their plan to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Virginia a plan to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in the state and claimed it was just a \u8216\'20\'18limit\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Mini Timmaraju, president and CEO of \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2 , said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWell, tonight, Virginians showed the GOP and Glenn Youngkin exactly what voters have to say about it: we don\u8217\'20\'19t want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, and we don\u8217\'20\'19t want leaders who do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Virginia results may serve as an indication of where swing voters in battleground states stand ahead of the 2024 presidential election. Virginia has been trending toward Democrats in recent years, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  carried the state by 10 points in 2020. But Youngkin\u8217\'20\'19s victory in 2021 proved Virginia remains a battleground state, and Republicans had hoped the governor\u8217\'20\'19s success would deliver them a legislative trifecta in Richmond, but that failed to materialize.\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign reveled in Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 wins on Tuesday, pointing to them as evidence that the president would similarly succeed when he is on the ballot again next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVoters across the political spectrum once again showed up and voted for our agenda and rejected the dangerous Maga extremism that has come to define today\u8217\'20\'19s Republican Party at every level,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Chavez Rodriguez, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager. \u8220\'20\'1CThat same choice will be before voters again next November and we are confident the American people will send President Biden and Vice-President Harris back to the White House to keep working for them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 failure to take full control of the legislature may throw cold water on speculation over Youngkin\u8217\'20\'19s national ambitions, as the governor had been named as a potential presidential candidate for 2024. As polls closed on Tuesday, Youngkin deflected questions over his future plans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been asked this so much, so many times over the course of the last year,\u8221\'20\'1D Youngkin told CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m humbled by it. I\u8217\'20\'19m focused on Virginia; we\u8217\'20\'19ve got a lot of work to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With Democrats in control of the state senate and able to block much of Youngkin\u8217\'20\'19s agenda, it will be much harder for the governor to make a pitch for the White House. Given that Virginia governors cannot serve consecutive terms, Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 victories on Tuesday guarantee that Youngkin will not have the opportunity to govern with a Republican-controlled legislature before he leaves office in 2026.\par \par \uc2 Youngkin\u8217\'20\'19s critics celebrated his party\u8217\'20\'19s defeats, suggesting the disappointing performance would bring an end to any presidential aspirations.\par \par \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2 , director of the University of Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Politics, joked on X: \u8220\'20\'1CCLEARANCE SALE: all \u8216\'20\'18Youngkin for President 2024\u8217\'20\'19 merchandise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 8 November 2023. A previous version said that Virginia governors are limited to serving a single term. In fact, governors may serve more than one term, but they cannot serve consecutive terms.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231108ejb700002\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
