\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Families flee past tanks as Israel begins to storm Gaza City\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,550 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par 12:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Civilians given four-hour window to leave encircled capital but fears many are still trapped. Plus, Salman Rushdie on peace, Barbie and what freedom cost himDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Waving white flags and holding their hands above their heads, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/07/we-saw-death-families-flee-past-tanks-as-israel-prepares-to-storm-gaza-city"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Palestinian families fled past tanks waiting to storm Gaza City}}}\uc2  in the next stage of the war that the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , has said will give Israel \u8220\'20\'1Cindefinite\u8221\'20\'1D control over the besieged territory.\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military gave civilians inside the encircled city a four-hour window to leave on Tuesday, as its forces prepared to retake the biggest city in the strip.\par \par \uc2 Men, women and children, some carrying their belongings on donkeys, fled their homes past Israeli troops out of the city.\par \par \uc2 In an Arabic-language message, the \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (\uc2 IDF\uc2 ) said they would allow people to leave from 10am until 2pm local time, and published a video of dozens of people along a main road.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What have the Israeli military said about the latest developments? \uc2 Jonathan Conricus\uc2 , the acting spokesperson for the Israeli military, has called the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leadership inside and outside Gaza {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/08/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-biden-netanyahu-gaza-occupation-palestine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-654b3c608f08a667a2c2735c#block-654b3c608f08a667a2c2735c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdead men walking\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in an interview with Sky News in Australia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Israel and Palestine? Here is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/03/israel-and-palestine-a-complete-guide-to-the-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a complete guide to the crisis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Ohio spoke tonight\u8217\'20\'19: voters add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to state constitution\par \par \uc2 Ohio voters resoundingly voted to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to their state constitution, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a major victory for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights supporters}}}\uc2  in the only state where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on the ballot this November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIssue 1\u8221\'20\'1D passed with more than 57% of the vote, according to results shortly after the outcome was declared.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access has been in contention in Ohio since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade last year, sending the issue back to the states, which led to 16 states banning nearly all abortions. Ohio has a six-week ban on the books, which briefly took effect until a court paused it. Yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s results should prevent it from being reinstated.\par \par \uc2 After polls closed yesterday, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters gathered in downtown Columbus at a watch party hosted by Ohioans United for Reproductive Rights, the coalition backing Issue 1. Each time an agency or news organization declared that Issue 1 had passed, cheers erupted \u8211\'20\'13 culminating in an ear-splitting roar when CNN, which was playing on a widescreen TV, aired footage of the watch party itself.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else happened with the elections across the country yesterday? Voters across the US went to the polls on Tuesday for an array of key races that may set the tone for the general election next year. The night produced some historic wins and some surprise outcomes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/08/us-elections-2023-abortion-rights-virginia-kentucky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here is a roundup of the notable races called so far}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What happened in Virginia? Democrats have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/virginia-election-voting-results-house-delegates-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secured full control of the Virginia state legislature}}}\uc2 , winning a majority in the house of delegates and depriving the Republican governor, Glenn Youngkin, of the opportunity to enact a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 This year on track to be the hottest\par \par \uc2 on record, say scientists\par \par \uc2 The world is set to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/nov/08/2023-on-track-to-be-the-hottest-year-on-record-say-scientists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hotter in 2023 than in any other year on record}}}\uc2 , scientists have said, before a landmark climate summit this month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can say with near certainty that 2023 will be the warmest year on record, and is currently 1.43C above the pre-industrial average,\u8221\'20\'1D said Samantha Burgess, the deputy director of the Copernicus Climate Change Service. \u8220\'20\'1CThe sense of urgency for ambitious climate action going into Cop28 has never been higher.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Copernicus scientists found that last month was the hottest October on record globally, with temperatures 1.7C above what they were thought to have been during the average October in the late 1800s.\par \par \uc2 By burning fossil fuels and destroying nature, humans have pumped heat-trapping gases into the atmosphere that have raised the temperature of the planet by 1.2C since the industrial revolution. The global temperature anomaly for October 2023 was the second highest across all months in their dataset, the scientists found, behind only the month before.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? The world\u8217\'20\'19s fossil fuel producers are planning expansions that would blow the planet\u8217\'20\'19s carbon budget twice over, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/nov/08/insanity-petrostates-planning-huge-expansion-of-fossil-fuels-says-un-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a UN report has found}}}\uc2 . Experts called the plans \u8220\'20\'1Cinsanity\u8221\'20\'1D and said they \u8220\'20\'1Cthrow humanity\u8217\'20\'19s future into question\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Is there any good climate news? China has published a long-awaited methane reduction plan, a sign it is moving closer towards a new climate agreement with the US. The two countries {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/08/china-methane-plan-climate-agreement-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may soon break ground}}}\uc2  on the new agreement before a presidential meeting next week and the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s climate conference, Cop28.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican-controlled House of Representatives voted last night to censure the Democratic representative\par \par \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  of Michigan, the only Palestinian American in Congress, in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/house-vote-censure-rashida-tlaib-palestine-criticize-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extraordinary rebuke of her rhetoric about the Israel-Hamas war}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  is\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/08/ivanka-trump-testify-fraud-trial-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to appear on the witness stand today}}}\uc2  at her father\u8217\'20\'19s New York $250m fraud trial. She will be the last family member and final witness to testify before the prosecution rests its case.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Russian security council secretary,\par \par \uc2 Nikolai Patrushev\par \par \uc2 , said on Wednesday that the \u8220\'20\'1Cdestructive\u8221\'20\'1D policies of the US and its allies were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/08/russia-ukraine-war-kyiv-avdiivka-zelenskiy-putin?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-654b37378f08a667a2c2732f#block-654b37378f08a667a2c2732f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasing the risk that nuclear, chemical or biological weapons would be used}}}\uc2 . Patrushev said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe international arms control regime has been undermined.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Amid growing outrage\par \par \uc2 at the death of a Jewish man\par \par \uc2 after an altercation\par \par \uc2 during a protest over the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war, southern California police {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/california-police-man-death-protests-israel-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for calm}}}\uc2  as they investigated\par \par \uc2 . Paul Kessler, 69, died on Monday from a head injury sustained at pro-Israel and pro-Palestinian demonstrations.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day:\par \par \uc2 one in four homes with gas cookers breach\par \par \uc2 hourly pollution levels and pump out toxic particles linked to childhood asthma\par \par \uc2 Gas cookers are pumping toxic particles linked to childhood asthma into kitchens, living rooms and bedrooms across Europe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/nov/08/gas-cookers-pump-out-toxic-particles-linked-to-childhood-asthma-report-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a report has found}}}\uc2 . Dutch scientists measured the air quality in 247 homes and found average levels of nitrogen dioxide (NO 2) were almost twice as high in those cooking with gas as in those cooking without. One in four homes with gas cookers breached hourly pollution levels set by the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2 , while none of the homes in the control group, which used electric cookers, broke the limits. Burning gas to cook food releases pollutants such as NO 2 that hurt lungs and inflame airways.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: \u8216\'20\'18The good guys don\u8217\'20\'19t always win\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 Salman Rushdie on peace, Barbie and what freedom cost him\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe live in a time I did not think I would see, a time when freedom \u8211\'20\'13 and in particular, freedom of expression, without which the world of books could not exist \u8211\'20\'13 is everywhere under attack from reactionary, authoritarian, populist, demagogic, half-educated, narcissistic, careless voices; when places of education and libraries are subject to hostility and censorship; and when extremist religion and bigoted ideologies have begun to intrude in areas of life in which they do not belong,\u8221\'20\'1D writes Salman Rushdie. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd there are also progressive voices being raised in favour of a new kind of bien-pensant censorship, one that appears virtuous, and which many people, especially young people, have begun to see as a virtue \u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/nov/08/salman-rushdie-peace-freedom-barbie-myths-fables"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What do we do about free speech when it is so widely abused?}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 plastic waste \u8216\'20\'18spiralling out of control\u8217\'20\'19 across Africa, analysis shows\par \par \uc2 Plastic waste is \u8220\'20\'1Cspiralling out of control\u8221\'20\'1D across Africa, where it is growing faster than any other region, new analysis has shown. At current levels, enough plastic waste to cover a football pitch is openly dumped or burned in sub-Saharan Africa every minute, according to the charity \uc2 Tearfund\uc2 . If the trend continues unabated, the region is projected to end up with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/nov/08/plastic-waste-spiralling-out-of-control-across-africa-analysis-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 116m tonnes of plastic waste annually by 2060}}}\uc2 , six times more than the 18m tonnes of waste produced in 2019. The main reason for the increasing plastic consumption in sub-Saharan Africa, where 70% of the population is under 30, is demand for vehicles and other products because of rising income and population growth. Overall, plastic use worldwide is projected to almost triple by 2060.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing:\par \par \uc2 singing by boys\u8217\'20\'19 choir \u8216\'20\'18sounds more brilliant\u8217\'20\'19 when girls in audience\par \par \uc2 Behind the rousing song of an all-male choir lies an evolutionary force that is better known for shaping the sex lives of hopeful frogs and crickets, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2023/nov/08/singing-by-boys-choir-sounds-more-brilliant-when-girls-in-audience"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research suggests}}}\uc2 . Recordings of an elite boys\u8217\'20\'19 choir once directed by Johann Sebastian Bach in Leipzig, Germany, reveal that the more physically mature boys in the group boosted their vocals with an appealing ring when girls were in the audience. The effect, seen only among the older bass singers, aged 16 to 19, is thought to be the choral equivalent of behaviour more often observed in frogs and crickets, which alter their individual calls to stand out from the crowd during mate-enticing choruses.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231108ejb8001pa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
