\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  providers brace themselves ahead of Ohio vote: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s just terrifying\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman in Cleveland, Ohio \par \uc2 1,016 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par 01:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 If Issue 1 fails, supporters of the proposal believe the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court will reinstate a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 When Annie Boyle picked up the phone, the woman at the other end of the line wanted to know: what\u8217\'20\'19s going on with Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum?\par \par \uc2 As a patient advocate at Preterm, a sprawling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Cleveland, Ohio, Boyle is used to confusion over Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which took effect shortly after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, but is now on hold. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m old, I don\u8217\'20\'19t need an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the woman on the phone said, but she sounded disturbed by the ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSix weeks?\u8221\'20\'1D the woman exclaimed, according to Boyle, who recounted the call. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat if I was raped?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Ohioans will head to the polls to vote on Issue 1, a proposal to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution. The stakes are high: if Issue 1 fails, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters suspect that the Ohio supreme court will reinstate the six-week ban. It does not include exceptions for pregnancies resulting from rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just really terrifying to think about. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know anyone who\u8217\'20\'19s not scared,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sri Thakkilapati, the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s executive director. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a kind of moral injury that comes with fighting so hard to provide this care, because you think it\u8217\'20\'19s the right thing \u8211\'20\'13 and then not being able to do it and having to turn literally hundreds of people away each week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Staffers at Preterm are haunted by memories of the six-week ban, which was in effect for just under three months before a state court blocked it. The day Roe fell, they had just a few hours before Ohio moved to implement it. They rushed to squeeze in as many procedures as possible; at one point, a doctor performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on his knees because he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t grab a stool quickly enough, one Preterm staffer recalled. The clinic\u8217\'20\'19s senior staff stayed late into the night to call patients and cancel their upcoming appointments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome people were completely devastated \u8211\'20\'13 screaming, crying on the phone,\u8221\'20\'1D recalled Kelsey Bowman, Preterm\u8217\'20\'19s director of operations. \u8220\'20\'1CAs empathetic human beings, you\u8217\'20\'19re just like: \u8216\'20\'18This is awful. This is the worst. I\u8217\'20\'19m having to tell somebody that they can\u8217\'20\'19t receive their care here and they have to go out of state.\u8217\'20\'19 And then so many people were saying: \u8216\'20\'18I can\u8217\'20\'19t possibly do that.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A court paused the ban in September 2022. A year later, the Ohio supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/27/ohio-supreme-court-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heard arguments in the case}}}\uc2 , but the justices have not yet ruled.\par \par \uc2 Over the months that the ban was in effect, abortions fell by 60% at Preterm, Thakkilapati said. After the courts froze the ban, Preterm employees called the patients who were still early enough in their pregnancy to get abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany of them had gone out of state, and the people who didn\u8217\'20\'19t came back and had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  here,\u8221\'20\'1D Thakkilapati said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey hadn\u8217\'20\'19t changed their mind. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to continue their pregnancy. They just were being forced to be pregnant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a kind of moral injury that comes with fighting so hard to provide this care\par \par \uc2 Sri Thakkilapati\par \par \uc2 Preterm is among the first legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in the United States: a group of women opened the clinic in March 1974, months before US women gained the right to open credit cards in their own name. Now, Preterm normally performs abortions up to 21 weeks of pregnancy and accounts for somewhere between a fifth and a fourth of all abortions in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, just days before the vote, Preterm appeared back to business as usual. Staffers in scrubs worked briskly, bringing ginger ale to patients who had just undergone abortions and helping patients who were preparing for the procedure stretch out on top of couches and under heating pads. Others manned the phone lines in the call center, softly answering questions about morning-after pills, ultrasounds and periods.\par \par \uc2 However, reminders of the referendum were everywhere. The street outside Preterm was littered with at least a dozen signs urging people to vote either for and against Issue 1. A handful of protesters milled amongst the Issue 1 signs and carried signs of their own. One woman stood near the clinic driveway with a sign that read, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s Not Too Late to Change Your Mind.\u8221\'20\'1D Bright yellow posters that read \u8220\'20\'1CSTOP KILLING BABIES HERE\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CMOMMY LET ME LIVE\u8221\'20\'1D were propped up near the clinic.\par \par \uc2 Bellamy Morales, a Preterm patient advocate, accessorized their bright blue Taylor Swift cardigan with a shirt bearing the words \u8220\'20\'1COhioans for Reproductive Freedom\u8221\'20\'1D, a name of the coalition backing Issue 1. The stress of the ban \u8211\'20\'13 and the chance that it may cost them their job \u8211\'20\'13 had led Morales, whose pronouns are they/she, to check into a mental health center in summer 2022.\par \par \uc2 Now, Morales said that they are \u8220\'20\'1Ccautiously excited\u8221\'20\'1D about the vote on Tuesday. Polling looks good for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters: in an October {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bw.edu/assets/community-research-institute/october_ohio_issues_poll-final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2 , 58% of Ohio residents said they would vote in favor of Issue 1. But Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s surprise victory in 2016 tempered her optimism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want so much for it to be OK and to pass and to be able to celebrate with everyone,\u8221\'20\'1D Morales said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I think, at least for me, 2016 has shown you don\u8217\'20\'19t really know for sure \u8211\'20\'13 you can make all the projections and think it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna pass, but you\u8217\'20\'19re never 100% sure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Preterm staffers are preparing, both logistically and emotionally, for the possibility that the ban will snap back into effect. They are ready to provide patients with the resources they need to potentially go out of state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very nerve-racking to have to wait,\u8221\'20\'1D Bowman said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut having to make those phone calls again \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s just a nightmare scenario.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231106ejb6001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
