\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Elections from Virginia to New Jersey could offer early referendum on Biden\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 901 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2023\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Voters could strike blow for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Ohio and choose governors, legislators and mayors in off-year elections across US\par \par \uc2 Millions of Americans go to the polls on Tuesday to vote in elections and ballot measures that could offer an interim verdict on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency a year out from his bid to retain the White House.\par \par \uc2 Voters will choose governors in Kentucky and Mississippi, decide legislative control in New Jersey and Virginia and determine whether the Ohio state constitution should protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 All 40 seats in Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s senate and all 100 seats in the state\u8217\'20\'19s house of delegates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/virginia-votes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are in play}}}\uc2 . Democrats are aiming to hold or widen their 22-18 advantage in the senate and win a majority in the House, where Republicans currently have a 52-48 edge.\par \par \uc2 Voters\u8217\'20\'19 decisions could be affected by events on the national political stage, ranging from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings to the recent chaos in the House of Representatives as Republicans struggled for three weeks to elect a speaker.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople say, oh, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter because it\u8217\'20\'19s national but people don\u8217\'20\'19t make those distinctions,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/staff/larry-j-sabato/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Larry Sabato}}}\uc2 , director of the Center for Politics at the \uc2 University of Virginia in Charlottesville\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CNational is state and state is local. They\u8217\'20\'19re measuring the worth of the parties, one against the other. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if there\u8217\'20\'19s any way we can measure it but surely this Republican dysfunction in the US House is having some effect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Virginia is the only state in the south that has not imposed further limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/divided-america-roe-v-wade-supreme-court-cold-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court overturned}}}\uc2  the landmark Roe v Wade ruling last year. But Republicans have pledged to pass a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 supported by the Republican governor, Glenn Youngkin \u8211\'20\'13 if they gain control of the legislature.\par \par \uc2 Youngkin, who upset Democrats in 2021 by making \u8220\'20\'1Cparents\u8217\'20\'19 rights\u8221\'20\'1D his signature issue, is not on the ballot this time but the elections will be watched closely for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/hes-pretty-smooth-glenn-youngkin-of-virginia-may-be-a-challenger-for-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clues to his future political prospects}}}\uc2 . Republican donors opposed to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could yet try to persuade Youngkin to make a last-minute entry into the 2024 presidential primary.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are also pursuing control of either legislative chamber in solidly Democratic New Jersey, where all seats in the general assembly and senate are up for grabs. Republicans have made headway since 2021, when they flipped seven seats, and are pushing issues ranging from the economy to parental rights in K-12 education.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in conservative Kentucky, the Democratic governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/12/kentucky-ex-felons-vote-democratic-governor-andy-beshear"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andy Beshear}}}\uc2 , is running for re-election against the Republican state attorney general, \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 . Beshear\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is touting his record of bringing jobs to Kentucky, backing public schools, expanding healthcare access and setting strict policies to curb the spread of the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Cameron, who is African American, has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/meetthepressblog/kentuckys-daniel-cameron-touts-trump-backing-home-stretch-governors-ra-rcna121081"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touting his endorsement}}}\uc2  by Trump. He is focusing on public safety, learning loss from school closures during the pandemic and culture war issues championed by Republicans nationally, such as opposing gender-affirming care for transgender children.\par \par \uc2 In Mississippi, the Republican governor, \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2 , is running for re-election against the Democrat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/29/brandon-presley-elvis-presley-mississippi-governor-tate-reeves"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brandon Presley}}}\uc2 , a former small-town mayor who is the second cousin of singer Elvis Presley. While Reeves is leading in the polls in the deeply conservative southern state, Presley has raised more money over the course of the campaign.\par \par \uc2 In political ads, Reeves has accused Presley of being backed by out-of-state liberals and opposing bans on gender-affirming care for transgender youth like the one Reeves signed into law in February. Presley has said he does not support gender-affirming care for minors, or transgender girls playing girls\u8217\'20\'19 sports, and is running on the promise of tax cuts and expanding Medicaid.\par \par \uc2 A debate between the candidates last week proved {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mississippi-governor-election-debate-reeves-presley-f157476d126399736bdb856d1c4cff85"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an ill-tempered affair}}}\uc2  with Reeves and Presley trading insults and talking over one another.\par \par \uc2 A ballot question in Ohio asks voters whether to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution, a move that would render moot a six-week limit signed into law by the Republican governor, \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 . That law is on hold pending litigation at the state supreme court. The vote is being closely watched as Democrats across the country hope to add to their string of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/democrats-abortion-rights-victory-kansas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wins in 2022}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ohio voters will also answer a ballot question about whether the state should legalise marijuana for recreational use. If approved, the statute would legalise, regulate and tax marijuana for adults over 21, expanding on the currently legal medicinal use of cannabis.\par \par \uc2 Cities across the country will elect mayors on Tuesday. In Philadelphia, Democrat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/election/david-oh-cherelle-parker-mayor-election-20231101.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cherelle Parker and Republican David Oh}}}\uc2 , both former city council members, are competing for an open seat as Democrat \uc2 Jim Kenney\uc2  reaches the limit of his mayoral term. In Houston, a crowded field of candidates led by the US congresswoman \uc2 Sheila Jackson Lee\uc2  and state senator John Whitmire, both Democrats, are competing to succeed the term-limited mayor, \uc2 Sylvester Turner\uc2 , also a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 A bad night for Democrats might been seen as a grim reflection on Biden, who approval rating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/513305/democrats-ratings-biden-slip-overall-approval.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stood at just 37%}}}\uc2  in a Gallup opinion poll last week. Surveys suggest he is running neck and neck with Trump in a hypothetical rematch.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231107ejb7001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
