\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Nikki Haley and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  potent challengers to Biden in swing states, poll shows \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,015 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2023\par 21:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For our reporting on politics polling, read our latest article:Biden faces calls not to seek re-election as shock poll rattles senior Democrats\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Democrats are grappling with a New York Times/Siena College {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6548e6ed8f08af73b5ca99af#block-6548e6ed8f08af73b5ca99af"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll  }}}\uc2  released over the weekend that showed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in five of the six swing states that will be crucial to deciding next year\u8217\'20\'19s election. Worse still, it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-65490baf8f08226b7ac67a3c#block-65490baf8f08226b7ac67a3c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed  }}}\uc2  in five of the six swing states that will be crucial to deciding next year\u8217\'20\'19s election. Worse still, it \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and Nikki Haley, two Republicans who polls show are less popular with the party\u8217\'20\'19s voters than Trump, also beating the president in a general election match-up. David Axelrod, an ex- \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  adviser, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-654904a48f0888d3e2106bde#block-654904a48f0888d3e2106bde"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said  }}}\uc2  the survey should give the president pause, while Dan Pfeiffer, also formerly of the Obama White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-654917fc8f0832f412179db3#block-654917fc8f0832f412179db3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believes  }}}\uc2  the Democrats still have a path to victory.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-654949258f0832f412179fcc#block-654949258f0832f412179fcc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will try again  }}}\uc2  to censure progressive Democrat \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  for her comments about Israel, with two separate resolutions targeting her.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump took the witness stand in his civil fraud trial in New York City, and things quickly took a turn for the worse. Our live blog recounts the day\u8217\'20\'19s events {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6548f5b68f0888d3e2106b0e#block-6548f5b68f0888d3e2106b0e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel \u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6549218b8f081e24ac48a368#block-6549218b8f081e24ac48a368"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues  }}}\uc2 , with the Palestinian health ministry announcing the death toll has crossed 10,000.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ohio is gearing up to vote tomorrow on whether to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state constitution. Polls indicate the effort may succeed, but reproductive rights advocates are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-654925328f081391dc01aa45#block-654925328f081391dc01aa45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nonetheless anxious  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Another poll shows Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-65493e2f8f081e24ac48a49a#block-65493e2f8f081e24ac48a49a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmingly believe  }}}\uc2  the country is headed in the wrong direction, and confirms that both Biden and Trump remain unpopular.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Republicans gear up to again attempt Tlaib censure over Israel-Palestine remarks\par \par \uc2 Days after a resolution to censure progressive Democrat \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  was voted down in the House by a bipartisan group of lawmakers, Republicans have introduced two more resolutions to punish her for her comments regarding Israel.\par \par \uc2 Rightwing Republican \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  was the author of the original resolution to censure Tlaib, and is making a new attempt:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepMTG  }}}\uc2  (R-GA) introduces a revised resolution to censure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRashida?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepRashida  }}}\uc2  (D-MI) for "antisemitic activity and sympathizing with terrorist organizations."\par \par \uc2 Her previous censure resolution was defeated last week after 23 Republicans voted with Democrats to table (kill) the measure. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/joNBxb1dVN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/joNBxb1dVN  }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1721623818920145267?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 Also jumping into the fray is Georgia Republican Rich McCormick, who voted against Greene\u8217\'20\'19s original resolution to censure Tlaib, and has now introduced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1721620345331863620"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his own  }}}\uc2 . In a video posted on X (formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2  ), he says his problem with the first attempt was that it accused Tlaib of \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection\u8221\'20\'1D, which, if passed, could have had implications for a \u8220\'20\'1Cformer president\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a reference to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrMy resolution to censure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRashida?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepRashida  }}}\uc2  is an honest one that protects free speech while still holding her to account for her reckless behavior. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mK367M0c6f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mK367M0c6f  }}}\uc2  is an honest one that protects free speech while still holding her to account for her reckless behavior.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congressman Rich McCormick, MBA MD (@RepMcCormick) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMcCormick/status/1720224802420507075?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, Tlaib stirred up controversy by accusing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  of supporting \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocide of the Palestinian people\u8221\'20\'1D and warning his assistance to Israel as it invades Gaza will hurt his standing in next year\u8217\'20\'19s election:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/04/rashida-tlaib-video-biden-palestine-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rashida Tlaib claims in video that Biden supports Palestinian genocide  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in New York City, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just concluded a tumultuous day of testimony in his civil fraud trial.\par \par \uc2 His time on the stand was marked by repeated clashes with judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  , who is deciding what penalties to level on the former president and his family after finding that they are liable for committing fraud.\par \par \uc2 Check out our live blog for more on what happened in today\u8217\'20\'19s hearing:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/donald-trump-testify-civil-fraud-trial-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump rails against judge in testimony: \u8216\'20\'18the fraud is on behalf of the court\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The New York Times /Siena College poll finding \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in key swing states is raising concerns among Democrats nationwide, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith  }}}\uc2  reports, but there\u8217\'20\'19s no sign of the president changing his decision to run for re-election:\par \par \uc2 Senior Democrats have sounded the alarm after an opinion poll showed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  trailing the Republican frontrunner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump  }}}\uc2  in five out of six battleground states exactly a year before the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Trump leads in Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, Nevada and Pennsylvania, with Biden ahead in Wisconsin, according to a survey {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/11/06/us/elections/times-siena-battlegrounds-registered-voters.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published on Sunday  }}}\uc2  by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Siena College. Biden beat Trump in all six states in 2020 but the former president now leads by an average of 48% to 44% across these states in a hypothetical rematch.\par \par \uc2 Additional findings released on Monday, however, showed that if Trump were to be convicted of criminal charges against him, some of his support in some swing states would erode by about 6%, which could be enough to tip the electoral college in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s favour.\par \par \uc2 Even so, the survey is in line with a series of recent polls that show the race too close for comfort for many Trump foes as voters express doubts about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age \u8211\'20\'13 the oldest US president in history turns 81 later this month \u8211\'20\'13 and handling of the economy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/cenkuygur/status/1721257059226886537?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prompting renewed debate  }}}\uc2  over whether he should step aside to make way for a younger nominee.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-poll-democrats-swing-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden faces calls not to seek re-election as shock poll rattles senior Democrats  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The latest ABC/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll shows that 76% of Americans believe the country is headed in the wrong direction, on top of that daunting New York Times/Siena poll.\par \par \uc2 The ABC poll also shows that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings among voters is just 33% \u8211\'20\'13 but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s is even lower at 29%.\par \par \uc2 enltrOne year out to the 2024 election, new polls show former Pres. Trump is gaining ground in key battleground states. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelvscott?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @rachelvscott  }}}\uc2  has more details. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yHdTArJPAN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yHdTArJPAN  }}}\uc2  has more details.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Good Morning America (@GMA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GMA/status/1721504340500734282?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 ABC political heavyweights \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2  and George Stephanopoulos then discussed the outlook, with Karl saying many GOP voters don\u8217\'20\'19t know the extremist things that the former president plans to do if he gets back into the White House, including prosecuting former senior aides and unleashing US troops on US streets.\par \par \uc2 enltr"This is a wake-up call. This is frightening for not just the Biden White House, not just for Democrats, but for anybody who fears what a return to a Trump presidency would mean. He can win. " \u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jonkarl?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @jonkarl  }}}\uc2  on polls showing former Pres. Trump gaining support in battleground states. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9hxL17tAjI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9hxL17tAjI  }}}\uc2  on polls showing former Pres. Trump gaining support in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Good Morning America (@GMA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GMA/status/1721505168355717566?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Diplomats at the US state department have sent a \u8220\'20\'1C blistering critique\u8221\'20\'1D of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the Israel-Gaza crisis, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/11/06/u-s-diplomats-slam-israel-policy-in-leaked-memo-00125538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a report  }}}\uc2  published by Politico a little earlier.\par \par \uc2 The outlet obtained what it termed a dissent memo, which features two requests, first that the US back the idea of a ceasefire between Israel and Gaza (not the \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian pause\u8221\'20\'1D the White House has been talking about) and that it air more of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s private criticisms of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military actions and the effects on Palestinian civilians.\par \par \uc2 The leaked memo notes that the disconnect \u8220\'20\'1Ccontributes to regional public perceptions that the United States is a biased and dishonest actor, which at best does not advance, and at worst harms, US interests worldwide\u8221\'20\'1D and noting that the US \u8220\'20\'1Cmust publicly criticize Israel\u8217\'20\'19s violations of international norms such as failure to limit offensive operations to legitimate military targets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It adds: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Israel supports settler violence and illegal land seizures or employs excessive use of force against Palestinians, we must communicate publicly that this goes against our American values so that Israel does not act with impunity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSCOOP: I obtained a copy of one of the dissent memos circulated in the State Department in which U.S. diplomats are furious over the Biden admin\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the story: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Kh8nW6f1L5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Kh8nW6f1L5  }}}\uc2  war. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the story:\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nahal Toosi (@nahaltoosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nahaltoosi/status/1721588636091613271?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Democrats are grappling with a New York Times/Siena College {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6548e6ed8f08af73b5ca99af#block-6548e6ed8f08af73b5ca99af"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll  }}}\uc2  released over the weekend that showed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in five of the six swing states that will be crucial to deciding next year\u8217\'20\'19s election. Worse still, it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-65490baf8f08226b7ac67a3c#block-65490baf8f08226b7ac67a3c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed  }}}\uc2  in five of the six swing states that will be crucial to deciding next year\u8217\'20\'19s election. Worse still, it \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and Nikki Haley, two Republicans who are down in the polls against Trump, also beating the president in a general election match-up. David Axelrod, an ex- \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  adviser, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-654904a48f0888d3e2106bde#block-654904a48f0888d3e2106bde"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said  }}}\uc2  the survey should give the president pause, while Dan Pfeiffer, also formerly of the Obama White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-654917fc8f0832f412179db3#block-654917fc8f0832f412179db3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believes  }}}\uc2  the Democrats still have a path to victory.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has been going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump took the witness stand in his civil fraud trial in New York City, and things quickly took a turn for the worse. Read our live blog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6548f5b68f0888d3e2106b0e#block-6548f5b68f0888d3e2106b0e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel \u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6549218b8f081e24ac48a368#block-6549218b8f081e24ac48a368"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues  }}}\uc2 , with the health ministry in the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  -controlled territory announcing the death toll among Palestinians has crossed 10,000.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ohio is gearing up to vote tomorrow on whether to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state constitution. Polls indicate the effort may succeed, but reproductive rights advocates are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/biden-trump-polls-2024-election-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-654925328f081391dc01aa45#block-654925328f081391dc01aa45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nonetheless anxious  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It isn\u8217\'20\'19t just in general election polls that Nikki Haley is showing strength. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino  }}}\uc2  reports, the former South Carolina governor and United Nations ambassador under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is also rising in polls of Republican presidential contenders, though the former president remains far-and-away the frontrunner:\par \par \uc2 On Monday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley  }}}\uc2  returned to the building where her political career began to formally submit the paperwork to appear on the Republican presidential primary ballot in her home state of South Carolina. Haley held up her filing for the cameras. In loopy writing she had scrawled: \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s do this!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The exclamation punctuated Haley\u8217\'20\'19s emergence as a viable alternative to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump  }}}\uc2 . It comes nearly 20 years after Haley\u8217\'20\'19s election to the South Carolina statehouse, having bested a 30-year Republican incumbent in a come-from-behind victory that stunned her party and began her unlikely ascent to the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion and then to become \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the United Nations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve always been the underdog,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said in remarks at the statehouse on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CI enjoy that. It\u8217\'20\'19s what makes me scrappy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a Republican primary still thoroughly dominated by Trump, Haley is enjoying, for now, the next best thing: an unexpected rise to second place.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/04/nikki-haley-republican-presidential-primary-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley\u8217\'20\'19s unexpected rise from \u8216\'20\'18scrappy\u8217\'20\'19 underdog to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s closest rival  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow is election day in states with off-year races, including Ohio, where voters will decide whether to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state constitution. The state leans Republicans, but as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman  }}}\uc2  reports, polling shows voters appear in favor of the measure:\par \par \uc2 When Annie Boyle picked up the phone, the woman at the other end of the line wanted to know: what\u8217\'20\'19s going on with Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum?\par \par \uc2 As a patient advocate at Preterm, a sprawling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Cleveland, Ohio, Boyle is used to confusion over Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which took effect shortly after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, but is now on hold. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m old, I don\u8217\'20\'19t need an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the woman on the phone said, but she sounded disturbed by the ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSix weeks?\u8221\'20\'1D the woman exclaimed, according to Boyle, who recounted the call. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat if I was raped?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Ohioans will head to the polls to vote on Issue 1, a proposal to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution. The stakes are high: if Issue 1 fails, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters suspect that the Ohio supreme court will reinstate the six-week ban. It does not include exceptions for pregnancies resulting from rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just really terrifying to think about. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know anyone who\u8217\'20\'19s not scared,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sri Thakkilapati, the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s executive director. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a kind of moral injury that comes with fighting so hard to provide this care, because you think it\u8217\'20\'19s the right thing \u8211\'20\'13 and then not being able to do it and having to turn literally hundreds of people away each week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/06/ohio-abortion-vote-issue-1-six-week-ban-clinics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers brace themselves ahead of Ohio vote: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s just terrifying\u8217\'20\'19  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry in the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  -controlled territory says more than 10,000 Palestinians have been killed there since 7 October.\par \par \uc2 We have a separate live blog covering the conflict, and you can follow it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/06/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-jordan-airdrops-medical-supplies-gaza-blinken-turkey-push-contain-conflict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Hamas war live: more than 10,000 Palestinians killed in Gaza since 7 October, says health authority; Rafah crossing reopens  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Another issue that may be on voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds next year, particularly among Democrats, is Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza. Last week, several Democratic senators publicly endorsed the idea of a \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian pause\u8221\'20\'1D in the incursion, and the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington  }}}\uc2  reports that \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  , a progressive independent who caucuses with the Democrats, is also calling for a break in the fighting:\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  has stepped up his calls for a humanitarian pause in Gaza, demanding an immediate stop to Israeli bombing and an end to the killing of thousands of \u8220\'20\'1Cinnocent men, women and children\u8221\'20\'1D in the enclave.\par \par \uc2 In some of his strongest words in the 30-day war, the independent US senator from Vermont decried the 7 October \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack inside {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel  }}}\uc2 . He labelled \uc2 Hamas\uc2  as an \u8220\'20\'1Cawful terrorist organization\u8221\'20\'1D that had \u8220\'20\'1Cslaughtered 1,400 people in cold blood\u8221\'20\'1D, reiterating his belief that Israel had the right to defend itself.\par \par \uc2 But speaking on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union on Sunday, Sanders said the death of civilians had to stop. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat Israel does not, in my view, have a right to do is to kill thousands of thousands of innocent men, women and children who had nothing to do with that attack,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The senator added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s not enough food, there\u8217\'20\'19s not enough water, medicine, fuel. You\u8217\'20\'19ve got a humanitarian disaster, it has to be dealt with right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/05/bernie-sanders-israeli-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders calls for end to Israeli strikes and killing of thousands  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Another former advis er to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  has weighed in on the New York Times /Siena poll, and agreed it\u8217\'20\'19s a warning sign for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am still processing this poll and will have more to say in the coming days. But I do not want to sugarcoat it. While some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s gains among Black, Hispanic, and young voters may be hard to believe, numbers like these are broadly consistent with the trendlines in recent polls. This poll shows that not only can Trump win, he might now be a slight favorite to do so. Even if we don\u8217\'20\'19t take the results literally, we should take them very, very seriously,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.messageboxnews.com/p/a-constructive-response-to-the-new"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes  }}}\uc2  Dan Pfeiffer.\par \par \uc2 But Pfeiffer sees a way for Democrats to turn around their fortunes by targeting what he calls \u8220\'20\'1CDouble Haters\u8221\'20\'1D, or voters who disapprove of both Biden and Trump. The key to reaching this group will be reminding it of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s legislative accomplishments that polling shows are broadly popular with the public, such as the 2021 infrastructure bill that will pour billions of dollars into roads and bridges, or the provisions of last year\u8217\'20\'19s Inflation Reduction Act that allows Medicare to negotiate lower prescription drug prices.\par \par \uc2 Pfeiffer writes:\par \par \uc2 This finding is important for a couple of reasons. It means that the path to persuading these \u8220\'20\'1CDouble Haters\u8221\'20\'1D is relatively simple in conception, if not execution. Reaching these voters is not easy. They are skeptical of the media and politicians. Most of them do not consume political news. So it will take a lot of time and even more effort.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign and Super PACs like \uc2 Unite\uc2  the Country cannot do everything. We all have a role to play. I am confident you have \u8220\'20\'1CDouble Haters\u8221\'20\'1D among your friends and family. I certainly do. The research shows voters are more likely to be persuaded by people they know. Let\u8217\'20\'19s work to educate people about everything Biden has done to grow the economy, create jobs, and lower costs. The best language to use is in the Navigator Poll.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://navigatorresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/Navigator-Update-10.24.2023.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a link  }}}\uc2  to said poll from Navigator Research, which Pfeiffer bases his findings on.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Beyond the Republicans who hope to beat him in a general election, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  also has a primary challenger in the form of Minnesota congressman \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  . Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang  }}}\uc2  with more on why Phillips thinks he can triumph over the sitting president:\par \par \uc2 For people who know the Democratic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota  }}}\uc2  congressman \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  , his run for presidency is perplexing. For some of them, it\u8217\'20\'19s also disappointing, maybe even enraging. But they also think he\u8217\'20\'19s genuine in his quest to go up against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the Democratic primary, despite how it might affect his own political career and how it could damage Biden in one of the most consequential elections in recent US history.\par \par \uc2 Phillips {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/27/democratic-congressman-dean-phillips-launches-primary-challenge-against-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced his run  }}}\uc2  for the presidency in New Hampshire last week, saying it was time for the next generation to lead in a pointed reference to concerns about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age. He says he is a fan of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s and a supporter of his policies, but he is 54, while Biden is 80. Phillips, the heir to a distilling empire who also co-owned a gelato company, is injecting his own wealth into his presidential campaign \u8211\'20\'13 solving any problem of raising funds.\par \par \uc2 In Minnesota, where Phillips represents a purple district filled with wealthier suburbs of Minneapolis, Phillips first ran for Congress in the state\u8217\'20\'19s third congressional district and flipped a longtime Republican seat blue. In his next two elections, he won more and more voters to his side, preaching pragmatic politics and driving a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J2kdZIIzEUg&themeRefresh=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 government repair truck  }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ann Gavin helped him. She knocked on doors, delivered campaign signs. The 70-year-old Democratic voter from Plymouth, Minnesota, admires the congressman and the work he\u8217\'20\'19s done for the district. She thinks he would be a great president someday, too, with his business savvy and political skills.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/04/who-is-dean-phillips-views-running-president-2024-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who is Democratic congressman Dean Phillips \u8211\'20\'13 and why is he taking on Biden?  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Haley, DeSantis also potent challengers to Biden in swing states \u8211\'20\'13 poll\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has for months led polls of Republican presidential contenders, giving him a clear edge heading into next year\u8217\'20\'19s primaries. But let\u8217\'20\'19s say something happens to knock him out of contention, and his former United Nations ambassador Nikki Haley wins the nomination. How might she do against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Siena College asked voters that question in the six swing states it polled, and found she would be an even more potent challenger to Biden than Trump:\par \par \uc2 filtr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NEW?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NEW  }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SienaResearch?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SienaResearch  }}}\uc2  / {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytimes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nytimes  }}}\uc2  Polls:\par \par \uc2 WISCONSIN\par \par \uc2 Haley 53% (+14)\par \par \uc2 Biden 39%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 Haley 46% (+10)\par \par \uc2 Biden 36%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 PENNSYLVANIA\par \par \uc2 Haley 49% (+10)\par \par \uc2 Biden 39%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NEVADA\par \par \uc2 Haley 46% (+9)\par \par \uc2 Biden 37%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 Haley 46% (+9)\par \par \uc2 Biden 37%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GEORGIA\par \par \uc2 Haley 45% (+5)\par \par \uc2 Biden 40%\par \par \uc2 3,662 LV, 10/22-11/3 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Jwojz4luQ3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Jwojz4luQ3  }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Political Polls (@Politics_Polls) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Politics_Polls/status/1721551250808783179?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 Or what about \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  ? While headlines have lately focused on why the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s once-promising presidential campaign has floundered among Republicans, the NYT/Siena poll he would best Biden in five of the six swing states, if he somehow clinched the nomination:\par \par \uc2 inltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NEW?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NEW  }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SienaResearch?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SienaResearch  }}}\uc2  / {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytimes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nytimes  }}}\uc2  Polls:\par \par \uc2 WISCONSIN\par \par \uc2 DeSantis 48% (+4)\par \par \uc2 Biden 44%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 PENNSYLVANIA\par \par \uc2 DeSantis 47% (+4)\par \par \uc2 Biden 43%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NEVADA\par \par \uc2 DeSantis 45% (+4)\par \par \uc2 Biden 41%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 DeSantis 46% (+4)\par \par \uc2 Biden 42%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GEORGIA\par \par \uc2 DeSantis 45% (+1)\par \par \uc2 Biden 44%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 Biden 44% (+1)\par \par \uc2 DeSantis 43%\par \par \uc2 3,662 LV,\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Jwojz4luQ3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Jwojz4luQ3  }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Political Polls (@Politics_Polls) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Politics_Polls/status/1721552181109637196?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 You can find the survey\u8217\'20\'19s full data {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/11/06/us/elections/times-siena-battlegrounds-registered-voters.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former top Obama adviser says Biden needs to decide if re-election campaign 'is wise' after grim polls\par \par \uc2 David Axelrod helped Barack Obama win the White House twice, and after looking at the New York Times /Siena College poll released yesterday that found \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  leading in five of the six major swing states, he says \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  needs to decide if pressing on with his re-election campaign is a good idea.\par \par \uc2 The president announced his campaign earlier this year and has shown no signs of wavering, despite persistently low approval ratings and a succession of polls indicating Trump, the frontrunner for the Republican nomination, would be a strong challenger.\par \par \uc2 On X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2  , Axelrod says he is particularly worried about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s ability to address concerns about his age:\par \par \uc2 enltrIt's very late to change horses; a lot will happen in the next year that no one can predict & Biden's team says his resolve to run is firm.\par \par \uc2 He's defied CW before but this will send tremors of doubt thru the party--not "bed-wetting," but legitimate concern. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/g6zeWF0T87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/g6zeWF0T87  }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Axelrod (@davidaxelrod) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidaxelrod/status/1721187586268389858?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe greatest concern is that his biggest liability is the one thing he can't change. Among all the unpredictables there is one thing that is sure: the age arrow only points in one direction.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Axelrod (@davidaxelrod) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidaxelrod/status/1721187789071409279?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS  }}}\uc2  is justly proud of his accomplishments. Trump is a dangerous, unhinged demagogue whose brazen disdain for the rules, norms, laws and institutions or democracy should be disqualifying. But the stakes of miscalculation here are too dramatic to ignore.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Axelrod (@davidaxelrod) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidaxelrod/status/1721189100986806558?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 enltrOnly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JoeBiden  }}}\uc2  can make this decision. If he continues to run, he will be the nominee of the Democratic Party. What he needs to decide is whether that is wise; whether it's in HIS best interest or the country's?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Axelrod (@davidaxelrod) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidaxelrod/status/1721189538880516252?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2023  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats are chewing over the New York Times /Siena College poll released this weekend that shows \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in several key swing states. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what one senator had to say, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/markoliver"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Oliver  }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Democratic senator Richard Blumenthal said on Sunday that the party had \u8220\'20\'1Cits work cut out for us\u8221\'20\'1D in response to new polling that shows President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  trailing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump  }}}\uc2  in five of six swing states.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/05/us/politics/biden-trump-2024-poll.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey  }}}\uc2  by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Siena College of voters in six battleground states, was released with 365 days to go until the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Biden is ahead in Wisconsin, but Trump topped the survey in Nevada, Arizona, Georgia, Pennsylvania and Michigan. The margins ranged from three to 10 percentage points, and reflected an erosion of support among the fragile, multiracial coalition that elected Biden over Trump in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union, Blumenthal of Connecticut, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI was concerned before these polls, and I\u8217\'20\'19m concerned now. These presidential races over the last couple of terms have been very tight. No one is going to have a runaway election here. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to take a lot of hard work, concentration, resources. And so we have our work cut out for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, Blumenthal praised Biden\u8217\'20\'19s record, pointing to his diplomacy on the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war \u8211\'20\'13 which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/28/democrats-biden-reelection-israel-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismayed  }}}\uc2  some on the progressive side of the party \u8211\'20\'13 saying the president\u8217\'20\'19s leadership \u8220\'20\'1Chas been critical \u8230\'20\'26 where he\u8217\'20\'19s forged a bipartisan consensus in favor of a peaceful outcome with a Palestinian state as the goal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/05/biden-trails-trump-five-swing-states-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blumenthal: Democrats have \u8216\'20\'18work cut out\u8217\'20\'19 as Biden trails Trump in five swing states  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 How is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  coping with the scrutiny and pressure of his ongoing civil fraud trial? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell  }}}\uc2  looked into it, and here\u8217\'20\'19s what he found:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has appeared at times angrily under siege as he stews over his predicament in the New York civil fraud case, according to people close to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former president  }}}\uc2 , particularly furious in recent weeks with the witness testimony that could result in the end of the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  empire.\par \par \uc2 The rulings from the presiding New York state supreme court justice \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  , who found that Trump and co-defendants were liable for fraud and ordered all of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s adult children to testify at the ongoing trial, for instance, have taken a toll.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo sad to see my sons being PERSECUTED in a political Witch Hunt by this out of control, publicity seeking, New York State Judge, on a case that should have NEVER been brought,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump partially {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/111342342174353964"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in one Truth Social post  }}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CLegal Scholars Scream Disgrace!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And Trump was furious when the judge imposed a gag order against him in the New York case, as well as when the judge enforced $15,000 in fines last week after deciding that Trump violated its prohibitions by assailing the judge\u8217\'20\'19s law clerk.\par \par \uc2 But Trump appears to have been otherwise content with his legal situation, including with the multiple criminal cases that are marching towards trial, the people said \u8211\'20\'13 an observation that the playbook he reverts to when feeling threatened, to attack and delay, has lately been successful.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/05/trump-trials-attack-delay-strategy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump angry over trials but happy with attack and delay strategy, insiders say  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  set to appear on witness stand in civil fraud trial\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected this morning to make a rare appearance on the witness stand in the civil fraud trial of his family business.\par \par \uc2 The trial in New York City is one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the many  }}}\uc2  civil and criminal legal entanglements the president is caught up in. At stake here is his family business, the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  , which a judge could levy major penalties against, depending on the outcome of the trial.\par \par \uc2 Follow our live blog for the latest on his testimony:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/donald-trump-testify-civil-fraud-trial-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump fraud trial: former US president due to testify in New York court \u8211\'20\'13 live  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden trails Trump in five of six swing states, poll shows, but conviction could change the game\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Democrats were rattled yesterday when the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Siena College published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/05/us/politics/biden-trump-2024-poll.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a poll  }}}\uc2  showing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in five of the six swing states that are expected to decide the election next year. Voters surveyed thought the former president was a better bet to handle the economy, immigration and national security, all issues Biden has made priorities of his administration, while a massive 71% thought he was \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo old\u8221\'20\'1D to continue doing the job. We are still a year away from election day and voter sentiment could change dramatically, but the poll was a high-quality one and exactly the sort an incumbent does not want to receive as they kick off their re-election bid.\par \par \uc2 But next year\u8217\'20\'19s election will be like no other because Trump \u8211\'20\'13 the presumptive nominee \u8211\'20\'13 is facing four separate criminal indictments, and the Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/06/us/politics/trump-biden-times-siena-poll.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said today  }}}\uc2  that if he is convicted and sentenced, that could swing voter sentiment by about six percentage points, enough to deliver key states to Biden. The trial most likely to be resolved before election day is the politically potent proceedings against Trump for trying to overturn the 2020 election, which will take place in Washington DC and currently has a start date of 4 March.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we are watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to take the stand in the civil fraud trial of his family business, where he will face hostile questioning about his business empire in open court. We have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/06/donald-trump-testify-civil-fraud-trial-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a live blog  }}}\uc2  on that.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  is in Turkey, the latest stop on a tour of the Middle East this weekend that included visits to Iraq and the West Bank, all aimed at dealing with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/06/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-jordan-airdrops-medical-supplies-gaza-blinken-turkey-push-contain-conflict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Follow our live blog  }}}\uc2  for the latest news on the conflict.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  will get its moment in the spotlight when Biden pays a visit to the passenger railway\u8217\'20\'19s employees today in Delaware and touts \u8220\'20\'1CBidenomics\u8221\'20\'1D, the term his administration has dubbed for his economic accomplishments that is not exactly catching on with voters. The president makes public remarks at 1.15pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231106ejb6001xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
