\par\par \uc2 Television & radio\par \b \uc2 John Oliver on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights: \u8216\'20\'18A case where voting can have an immediate and lasting effect\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Adrian Horton \par \uc2 966 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2023\par 16:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Last Week Tonight host surveys the bleak state of US reproductive rights ahead of several key state elections\par \par \uc2 Ahead of statewide elections in the US, John Oliver looked at the state of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which is a \u8220\'20\'1Chuge issue\u8221\'20\'1D in a number of races, including the Kentucky governor\u8217\'20\'19s race, Virginia state senate races, and a measure to enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization overturned Roe v Wade last June, \u8220\'20\'1Cthings are bleak\u8221\'20\'1D, the Last Week Tonight host said on Sunday evening. Fourteen states have enacted near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, and two have proposed six-week bans.\par \par \uc2 The hostile landscape has led to some creative ideas; one Californian proposed a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic that would operate in international waters. \u8220\'20\'1CLawless territory, no rules, anything goes. It\u8217\'20\'19s not only a foolproof plan, but it\u8217\'20\'19s also the literal premise for the movie Money Plane,\u8221\'20\'1D said Oliver. \u8220\'20\'1CYou didn\u8217\'20\'19t hallucinate that during peak Covid \u8211\'20\'13 there really was a film about a casino in the sky full of thieves, cartels and arms dealers who can never be arrested because the money plane is always moving in international airspace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Oliver advocated for watching the movie \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cif you pop an edible immediately, it should start to kick in right around when you meet the film\u8217\'20\'19s villain, Darius Emanuel Grouch III, AKA \u8216\'20\'18The Rumble\u8217\'20\'19, played by Kelsey Grammer,\u8221\'20\'1D who says in one clip: \u8220\'20\'1CWhatever you want to wager on, the money plane has you covered. You wanna bet on a dude fucking an alligator? Money plane.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the Frasier reboot that we deserved,\u8221\'20\'1D Oliver quipped.\par \par \uc2 Jokes aside, mobile clinics or out-of-state options just aren\u8217\'20\'19t practical for many women. \u8220\'20\'1CFor many, traveling across state lines isn\u8217\'20\'19t feasible, even before you consider that, in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal, it\u8217\'20\'19s not like they\u8217\'20\'19ve had a sudden surge in providers to handle out-of-state patients,\u8221\'20\'1D Oliver explained. \u8220\'20\'1CSo there are now significant backlogs, meaning that women who travel to another state may have more difficulty getting appointments, and it may even become hard for those living in some states where it remains legal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Between bans, onerous restrictions and confusing criminalization, such as in Texas, which deputized citizens to report those aiding and abetting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in America is currently a complete clusterfuck, with many confused and others considering drinking bleach,\u8221\'20\'1D said Oliver.\par \par \uc2 And yet, lawmakers \u8211\'20\'13 mostly men \u8211\'20\'13 have argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans make healthcare safer; one Texas legislator declared the state \u8220\'20\'1Csafe for little babies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are, objectively, not safe for women, and can needlessly put them through absolute hell,\u8221\'20\'1D Oliver countered, before sharing a video of a Texas woman who was forced to give birth to her baby, at great risk to her, even though it would suffocate to death within an hour. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a truly horrible thing to have to add to the list of things pregnant women are not safe to do \u8230\'20\'26 ride a rollercoaster, eat sushi, dye your roots and simply exist in the state of Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D Oliver joked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMedical professionals are now finding themselves caught in the middle between trying to do what they know is medically right for their patients while also not running afoul of the law, or having their license revoked,\u8221\'20\'1D he explained.\par \par \uc2 And health exemptions are so scarce that there are instances of women waiting for their conditions to deteriorate to be legally eligible for healthcare; in another clip, a Texas woman explained how she waited for days to become sick enough for doctors to legally be able to induce her doomed pregnancy. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we say that these laws take away people\u8217\'20\'19s right to control their own body, this is what we\u8217\'20\'19re talking about,\u8221\'20\'1D Oliver said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe had to wait from Tuesday till Friday to get close enough to dying to be saved. Pre-emptively choosing to save her own life was illegal in her state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s no wonder,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued, that women in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are nearly three times more likely to die due to pregnancy, childbirth or soon after.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe rhetoric around the Dobbs decision was that it simply \u8216\'20\'18returned decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the states\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Oliver noted. \u8220\'20\'1CWhich is a very nice way of saying it removed decisions from individuals and their doctors, and placed them in the hands of state legislators. And those politicians are now legislating medicine without even a modicum of medical understanding.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What do we do now? Oliver advised, first, screaming. \u8220\'20\'1CBut the most important thing for you to do right now is \u8211\'20\'13 and I apologize for even saying this \u8211\'20\'13 to vote. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are, for all the attacks on them, still widely popular.\u8221\'20\'1D In all six instances that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have been on the ballot since Dobbs, voters have decided to preserve them. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is genuinely a case where voting can have an immediate and lasting effect,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a medical decision between a patient and their doctor, full stop. And it is maddening to see some push to make their states safe for \u8216\'20\'18little babies\u8217\'20\'19, while also making it far more dangerous for the people they grow up to be,\u8221\'20\'1D Oliver concluded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHopefully, one day, we can eventually get to a place where people who want to end a pregnancy, save their own life or make any other medical or reproductive decision about their own body will not have to seek out the same legal loopholes that the money plane provides for those who want to bet on a dude fucking an alligator in front of Frasier.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231106ejb6002ec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
