\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 High stakes for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights as Pennsylvania votes on key judge pick\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 906 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2023\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican Carolyn Carluccio, running for supreme court, has drawn ire over apparent opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania voters will select a new member of the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court on Tuesday in a judicial election that has become the unlikely focus of Republican billionaire donors, political action committees and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates.\par \par \uc2 Democrat Daniel McCaffery is facing off against Carolyn Carluccio, a conservative judge whose apparent opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access has drawn the ire of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and other reproductive justice groups.\par \par \uc2 As McCaffery and Carluccio compete for a seat on the Pennsylvania supreme court, total spending in the race surpassed $17m, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/pennsylvania-supreme-court-election-campaign-3676cdc368faf25dc0cfc567608b42fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 an unusually high price tag for an election that typically sees low voter turnout. But Democrats and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates hope Pennsylvania voters view Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ballot as a proxy for reproductive freedom in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis election, Pennsylvania voters have a choice between Carolyn Carluccio, who has tried to hide her anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions and dodge questions about the judiciary\u8217\'20\'19s role in protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and Daniel McCaffery, a proven champion of reproductive freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D said Breana Ross, campaigns director of Planned Parenthood Votes Pennsylvania.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates hope to energize Pennsylvania voters by casting Carluccio as an existential threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. This strategy delivered liberals a resounding victory in the Wisconsin supreme court race earlier this year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-turnout-record-bac438d1d79e32f0bacdc7d5966adf75"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when record numbers of voters turned out to elect Janet Protasiewicz}}}\uc2 , a Democrat who pledged to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-turnout-record-bac438d1d79e32f0bacdc7d5966adf75"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Protasiewicz}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s conservative opponent, Dan Kelly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/03/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refrained from voicing his opinion on voting rights.}}}\par \par \uc2 Carluccio\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, taking its cues from Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s unsuccessful playbook, has avoided sharing her views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . After winning the primary election in May, Carluccio removed information about her opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from her campaign website, according to a May report from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://keystonenewsroom.com/story/republican-nominee-for-pennsylvania-supreme-court-wiped-anti-abortion-language-from-website/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Keystone}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Carluccio\u8217\'20\'19s campaign site previously vowed to defend \u8220\'20\'1Call life under the law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we redesigned our website, we chose to no longer include a r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9 link. Judge Carluccio listed on her r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9 that she would \u8216\'20\'18defend all life under the law\u8217\'20\'19, and she meant just that: under the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Rob Brooks, a spokesman for Carluccio\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Carluccio has frequently branded herself as a non-political actor who operates outside the bounds of traditional partisanship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI reject calls to rule based on partisan or ideological grounds and instead rule according to our laws,\u8221\'20\'1D Carluccio wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pennlive.com/opinion/2023/08/why-im-running-for-pennsylvania-supreme-court-opinion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an August op-ed}}}\uc2  about her candidacy.\par \par \uc2 Despite Carluccio\u8217\'20\'19s insistence on her own ideological neutrality, her campaign has invited the support of distinctly rightwing groups. In a February letter to the Pennsylvania Coalition for Civil Justice Reform, Carluccio {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://paforciviljusticereform.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Carluccio-Questionnaire-Response.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disclosed}}}\uc2  that her candidacy was endorsed by the Pennsylvania Pro-Life Federation, a leading anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group in the state.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.campaignfinanceonline.pa.gov/pages/CFAnnualTotals.aspx?Filer=20220629"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to campaign finance reports}}}\uc2 , her campaign received over $4m from Commonwealth Leaders Fund, a political organization funded by the billionaire GOP donor Jeffrey Yass.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania Democrats said Carluccio is hiding her ties to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement in a disingenuous bid for primary voters. The general electorate is supportive of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access \u8211\'20\'13 64% of all Pennsylvania voters in the 2022 midterms said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in most or all cases, according to polling from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-pennsylvania-supreme-court-274a476c66e2ea3f9dace25a4cff546a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHer campaign is clearly trying to portray her as acceptable to a primary audience,\u8221\'20\'1D said JJ Abbott, executive director of Commonwealth Communications, a progressive political consulting firm. \u8220\'20\'1CThey know \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a motivator for voters, since the Dobbs decision, voters are more likely to engage in elections because of what is at stake for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the stakes of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election are not straightforward. Unlike Wisconsin, where the threat of the 1849 near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban loomed overhead, the outcome of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court race will not directly affect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state. Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s race will not change the composition of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s high court \u8211\'20\'13 four of the seven seats on the current bench are held by Democrat-affiliated justices. Carluccio is operating in what appears to be a much less dire political environment than Kelly, whose campaign struggled to avoid the topic of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  while Wisconsin was feeling the effects of the 1849 ban.\par \par \uc2 Still, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and other reproductive justice advocates said the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement needs to look ahead to the 2025 election, when three of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic justices will appear on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The long-term maintenance of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s liberal supreme court majority is a priority for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates. In September, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  Votes launched a seven-figure advertisement campaign against Carluccio, the largest ad buy in the group\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 As anxieties mount, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters are hopeful that Pennsylvania voters, as in Wisconsin, will heed the warnings offered by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  on the long-term consequences of Carluccio\u8217\'20\'19s candidacy.\par \par \uc2 Dr Benjamin Abella, a medical professor and emergency physician in Philadelphia, said voters like him are \u8220\'20\'1Cpaying attention\u8221\'20\'1D to Carluccio\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to hide her campaign\u8217\'20\'19s ties to rightwing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe public understands that we should not be lulled into a false sense of security on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, especially if a judge is keeping quiet on their intentions and positions,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no such thing as a safe state any more and that any and every election poses a risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231104ejb40012z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
