\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats grow nervous over Israel\u8217\'20\'19s conduct in Gaza as Senate leader vows not to consider House security bill \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,796 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 November 2023\par 20:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest reporting on US politics\u8217\'20\'19 involvement with the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war, read our latest report:Leftwing Democrats try to block Biden Israel aid by using human rights law\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 There appears to be a shift in sentiment towards Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza in Washington DC, particularly among Senate Democrats. A group of 13 lawmakers has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-654500bf8f08293ffae5253f#block-654500bf8f08293ffae5253f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed on to}}}\uc2  a joint statement calling for a humanitarian pause in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to root out \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , and in a visit to Tel Aviv, secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-6544f26d8f08293ffae5243e#block-6544f26d8f08293ffae5243e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a similar request}}}\uc2 . The Senate now seems to be on a collision course with the House, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-654514bf8f08d1827a66b786#block-654514bf8f08d1827a66b786"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last night passed}}}\uc2  a bill to send Israel military assistance while also slashing funding to the \uc2 IRS\uc2  tax authority. That\u8217\'20\'19s a nonstarter for Democrats, and their Senate leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , says the measure won\u8217\'20\'19t be considered in the chamber, while minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-65451bc48f08293ffae52727#block-65451bc48f08293ffae52727"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seems}}}\uc2  uncomfortable with it.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Next Tuesday is election day for off-year contests, including in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-6545207e8f08af73b5ca7f5b#block-6545207e8f08af73b5ca7f5b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , where voters will be asked to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state constitution, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-654524db8f08af73b5ca7fb2#block-654524db8f08af73b5ca7fb2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2 , where Democrats hope to defang Republican governor Glenn Youngkin.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Democrats are also expressing concerns publicly over the number of civilians killed in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-65454f2c8f08293ffae529ba#block-65454f2c8f08293ffae529ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including}}}\uc2  California progressive \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 George Santos will run for re-election next year, even if he is expelled from the House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-65452e0f8f08d1827a66b944#block-65452e0f8f08d1827a66b944"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he told CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , the transportation secretary and first openly gay person to serve in a president\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-6545495e8f08d1827a66ba7a#block-6545495e8f08d1827a66ba7a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  Republican House speaker Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s history of anti-LGBTQ+ statements.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Got questions about Israel and Palestine? \uc2 The Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-65450fe38f08af73b5ca7e28#block-65450fe38f08af73b5ca7e28"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has answers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just Senate Democrats who are questioning Israel\u8217\'20\'19s handling of its invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 House Democrats are also publicly worrying over the mounting civilian death toll. Here\u8217\'20\'19s California progressive \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2  telling CNN that while he supports Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself, he believes too many civilians are dying in its invasion:\par \par \uc2 enltrLet me be clear: The bombing of innocent women and children must stop. Today. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EOFaDHdBzD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EOFaDHdBzD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2  (@RepRoKhanna) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRoKhanna/status/1720452360684667380?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 3, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has arrived in Lewiston, Maine, site of a mass shooting last week that left 18 people dead.\par \par \uc2 He is currently visiting Schemengees Bar and Grille, one of two locations where army reservist Robert Card opened fire:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn Lewiston, Maine, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  leave flowers and pay their respects at a memorial outside the Schemengees Bar & Grille, one of the sites where a gunman killed 18 people last month. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5D3HWJkHjs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5D3HWJkHjs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Toluse Olorunnipa (@ToluseO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ToluseO/status/1720525167703535747?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 3, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to meet with first responders in Lewiston, as well as survivors of the attack and family members of the victims, before heading to Rehoboth Beach, Delaware for the weekend.\par \par \uc2 In the weeks since the killings, reports have emerged that people who knew Card tried to sound the alarm about his behavior. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/01/maine-shootings-texts-letter-robert-card"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texts and letter show concerns Maine suspect would carry out shooting}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 First openly gay cabinet secretary Buttigieg condemns House speaker Johnson's anti-LGBTQ+ statements\par \par \uc2 Transportation secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , the first openly gay man to serve in a US president\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet, condemned Republican House speaker Mike Johnson for his history of making anti-LGBTQ+ statements.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN, Buttigieg said, \u8220\'20\'1CI will admit it\u8217\'20\'19s a little bit difficult driving the family minivan to drop our kids off at daycare, passing the dome of the Capitol knowing the speaker of the House, sitting under that dome, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t even think our family ought to exist.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Buttigieg:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CIt's a little bit difficult\u8230\'20\'26to drop our kids off at daycare, passing the dome of the Capitol, knowing that the Speaker of the House...doesn't even think our family ought to exist.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Transportation Sec. \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  condemns Speaker Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s anti-LGBTQ comments and views {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HAGkX5U8kK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HAGkX5U8kK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1720498594283717052?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 3, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Johnson has a long history of disparaging same-sex couples, including in 2004, when he wrote a newspaper op-ed saying homosexuality was \u8220\'20\'1Cinherently unnatural\u8221\'20\'1D. Since being elected speaker last month, he has avoided making similar statements, telling Fox News commentator \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  in an interview that he \u8220\'20\'1Cgenuinely love[d] all people regardless of their lifestyle choices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGo pick up a Bible off your shelf and read it \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s my worldview\u8221\'20\'1D, he added. Here\u8217\'20\'19s some further reading on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/27/mike-johnson-christian-bible-lgbtq-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Go pick up a Bible\u8217\'20\'19: Speaker Mike Johnson defends anti-LGBTQ+ views}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  saying he will ignore a House Republican bill to give Israel military assistance while cutting funding to the \uc2 IRS\uc2 , it seems likely Senate Democrats will soon propose a measure that lines up with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s demands.\par \par \uc2 The president last month asked lawmakers to approve aid to both Israel and Ukraine, and money for border security. At a press conference earlier today, the Democratic House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  said that proposal would be welcomed by his lawmakers:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CWe'll look at any bipartisan product that comes out of the Senate in good faith.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Minority Leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  (D-NY), when asked how House Democrats would respond to a Senate Israel aid bill that includes changes to border policy and asylum laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yhuaJVoL4k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yhuaJVoL4k}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1720479855517553081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 3, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The bigger question is what Republican House speaker Mike Johnson will do with it, and whether it would have the votes to pass Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber, where a growing faction of GOP members are opposed to aiding Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 There appears to be a shift in sentiment towards Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza in Washington DC, particularly among Senate Democrats. A group of 13 lawmakers has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-654500bf8f08293ffae5253f#block-654500bf8f08293ffae5253f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed on to}}}\uc2  a joint statement calling for a humanitarian pause in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing invasion to root out \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , and in a visit to Tel Aviv, secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-6544f26d8f08293ffae5243e#block-6544f26d8f08293ffae5243e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a similar request}}}\uc2 . The Senate now seems to be on a collision course with the House, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-654514bf8f08d1827a66b786#block-654514bf8f08d1827a66b786"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last night passed}}}\uc2  a bill to send Israel military assistance while also slashing funding to the \uc2 IRS\uc2  tax authority. That\u8217\'20\'19s a nonstarter for Democrats, and their Senate leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  says the measure won\u8217\'20\'19t be considered in the chamber, while minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-65451bc48f08293ffae52727#block-65451bc48f08293ffae52727"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seems}}}\uc2  uncomfortable with it.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Next Tuesday is election day for off-year contests, including in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-6545207e8f08af73b5ca7f5b#block-6545207e8f08af73b5ca7f5b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , where voters will be asked to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state constitution, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-654524db8f08af73b5ca7fb2#block-654524db8f08af73b5ca7fb2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2 , where Democrats hope to defang Republican governor Glenn Youngkin.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 George Santos will run for re-election next year, even if he is expelled from the House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-65452e0f8f08d1827a66b944#block-65452e0f8f08d1827a66b944"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he told CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Got questions about Israel and Palestine? \uc2 The Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/03/democrats-israel-hamas-war-ceasefire-biden-aid-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-65450fe38f08af73b5ca7e28#block-65450fe38f08af73b5ca7e28"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has answers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Proceedings are done for the day in the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  civil fraud trial in New York, where \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  testified again.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a taste of Lauren Aratani\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/eric-trump-testimony-fraud-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2 , one of the two sons trusted to run \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s real estate empire, testified on Friday that he was not involved with the financial documents a judge has ruled to be fraudulent, in a trial that threatens to hobble his family\u8217\'20\'19s business.\par \par \uc2 In a second day on the witness stand, the former US president\u8217\'20\'19s second son said he relied on outside accountants and lawyers to check financial documents. His older brother \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  made the same argument in his testimony earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors presented evidence that showed \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  had signed off on documents that estimated the value of trophy properties such as the Trump Seven Springs estate north of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  City and the Trump National Doral golf club in Florida.\par \par \uc2 That undercut his testimony on Thursday that he knew nothing about those estimates, which Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  found were fraudulently inflated to win favorable terms from lenders and insurers.\par \par \uc2 And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/eric-trump-testimony-fraud-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  Lauren\u8217\'20\'19s report in full.\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s some further reading, by me, about the Trump boys\u8217\'20\'19 tactics in court:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/donald-trump-jr-eric-trump-testimony-fraud-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ring any bells? Trump boys show less than total recall at family fraud trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Thirty-one Democrats voted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/01/us-house-vote-republican-george-santos-expel-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not to expel}}}\uc2  the Republican lawmaker George Santos from the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  because he has not been convicted of any crime and to eject him would set a dangerous precedent for Republicans to expel their ideological opponents, a leading congressman said.\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 . Photograph: Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Maga\u241\'00\'F1a/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor me this was an easy call,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  of Maryland, a law professor and influential progressive who sat on the January 6 committee and was lead manager in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s impeachment for inciting the attack on Congress.\par \par \uc2 Santos \u8220\'20\'1Chasn\u8217\'20\'19t been convicted of anything yet, and he has not been convicted of anything in our ethics process\u8221\'20\'1D, Raskin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2023/11/jamie-raskin-explains-why-he-voted-to-keep-george-santos-in-congressfor-now/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2023/11/jamie-raskin-explains-why-he-voted-to-keep-george-santos-in-congressfor-now/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mother Jones}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe history is very telling. We\u8217\'20\'19ve expelled five people in the history of the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2 . Three of them were Confederate traitors and the other two had other federal criminal convictions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 James A Traficant, an Ohio Democrat, was the last House member to be expelled, in 2002 and after being convicted of crimes including conspiracy to commit bribery, obstruction of justice and racketeering. After seven years in jail, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/id/wbna38106529"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted}}}\uc2  to run for re-election.\par \par \uc2 Raskin continued: \u8220\'20\'1CFor us to take the step of expelling someone who had not been convicted of anything would be a really dangerous manoeuvre, especially with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  in control of the House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read on:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/george-santos-expel-vote-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat says voting to expel Santos would have set dangerous precedent}}}\par \par \uc2 And also, as a footnote, some recommended reading, in the form of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/news-desk/out-of-jail-back-to-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the great David Grann on the curious case of James A Traficant}}}\uc2 , for the New Yorker. This is just a taste \u8211\'20\'13 you really owe it to yourself to buy Grann\u8217\'20\'19s book of New Yorker pieces, The Devil and Sherlock Holmes: Tales of Murder, Madness and Obsession, before today is through\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 George Santos, the New York fabulist, part-time {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/nbc-out/out-politics-and-policy/rep-george-santos-denies-ever-drag-queen-rcna66414"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drag enthusiast}}}\uc2 , accused fraudster and congressman, told CNN earlier he would \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely\u8221\'20\'1D run for re-election next year even if he is expelled from Congress over his criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 George Santos. Photograph: Drew Angerer/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Santos {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/george-santos-expel-vote-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survived an expulsion vote}}}\uc2 , over 23 federal criminal charges to which he pleaded not guilty, on a motion brought by members of his own party this week. He could face another such vote after a House ethics committee investigation concludes later this month.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s his conversation with the great corridor-haunter himself, Manu Raju, CNN chief congressional correspondent:\par \par \uc2 Raju: \u8220\'20\'1CSo, if they expel you, and then they put someone else in the seat, you\u8217\'20\'19re going to run in 2024?\par \par \uc2 Santos: \u8220\'20\'1CAbsolutely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Raju: \u8220\'20\'1CUh-huh. Can you win a primary, given of all these things that are lined up against you\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Santos: \u8220\'20\'1CYes. Yes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Raju: \u8220\'20\'1C\u8230\'20\'26 and the general election?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Santos: \u8220\'20\'1CWell\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Raju: This is a Biden-leaning district. And you have all these issues against you.\par \par \uc2 Santos: \u8220\'20\'1CCould I have won the general election last time? Nobody said I could. But I survived.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Raju: \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a different situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Santos: \u8220\'20\'1CNo, I understand. But elections are tricky. There\u8217\'20\'19s no predetermined outcome.\par \par \uc2 Raju: \u8220\'20\'1CYour voters thought they were electing one person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Santos: \u8220\'20\'1CManu, nobody elected me\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Raju: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t true.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Santos: \u8220\'20\'1CNobody elected me because I played volleyball or not. Nobody elected me because I graduated college or not.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople elected me because I said I\u8217\'20\'19d come here to fight the swamp, I\u8217\'20\'19d come here to lower inflation, create more jobs, make life more affordable, and the commitment to America. That\u8217\'20\'19s why people voted for anybody. To say that they voted based on anybody\u8217\'20\'19s biography, I can beg you this. Nobody knew my biography. Nobody opened my biography who voted for me in the campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately for Santos, once he got to Congress, lots of reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/22/george-santos-lies-republican-party-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did open his biography}}}\uc2 . And, explaining the volleyball reference, a lot of it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/22/george-santos-lies-republican-party-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned out not to be true}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And that was before the criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Shifting back to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing invasion of Gaza, here\u8217\'20\'19s Connecticut\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  on why he is now calling for a temporary pause in the fighting.\par \par \uc2 Murphy and 12 other Democratic senators signed onto a statement advocating for a \u8220\'20\'1Cshort-term cessation of hostilities\u8221\'20\'1D to get hostages out of Gaza and humanitarian aid in. He elaborates on the call, in an interview with MSNBC:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  (D-CT) explains why he\u8217\'20\'19s calling for a \u8220\'20\'1Cshort-term cessation of hostilities\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI simply believe that the current level of civilian casualties inside Gaza is too high, both from a moral perspective and a strategic perspective.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6rMgr3cfjU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6rMgr3cfjU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1720486981296144436?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 3, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Also happening next Tuesday are legislative elections in Virginia, where Republicans hope to take full control of Senate and empower GOP governor Glenn Youngkin to enact his agenda unimpeded. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  reports on how a Democratic congresswoman who conquered new territory for the party five years ago is working to help state-level candidates do the same:\par \par \uc2 As two dozen volunteers prepared to knock doors on an unseasonably warm afternoon in late October, Congresswoman \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2  reminded them that their work helped flip her battleground House seat in 2018. She predicted it would pay off again for Virginia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is how we have won in hard races across {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2  and across the country, and it is certainly why I feel confident that we are on the right path headed towards November 7,\u8221\'20\'1D Spanberger said, speaking to campaign volunteers in a sunny parking lot in Manassas.\par \par \uc2 Spanberger has played an active role in boosting Virginia Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes for election day, as the party looks to flip control of the house of delegates and maintain their majority in the state senate. The stakes are high: Republicans would achieve a legislative trifecta in Richmond if they take control of the state senate, allowing them to enact controversial policies like banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks and limiting access to the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 With her carefully crafted political persona as a centrist Democrat, Spanberger may be the right person to deliver her party\u8217\'20\'19s closing message in the final stretch of the campaign. In Manassas, Spanberger laid out her vision for how Virginia Democrats would succeed on 7 November, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is nothing more important than helping people believe that the policies and the government \u8211\'20\'13 whether it be in Richmond or on Capitol Hill \u8211\'20\'13 that they want is possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The results on Tuesday could affect Spanberger\u8217\'20\'19s own future as well; the congresswoman has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/28/spanberger-future-00108756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  told multiple people that she intends to run for governor in the battleground state. If she is successful, her victory would allow Democrats to take back the Virginia governorship, which is now held by Republican Glenn Youngkin, in 2025.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/who-is-abigail-spanberger-virginia-congress-democrat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Abigail Spanberger flexes her political power in a battleground state: \u8216\'20\'18I could see her as president\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not 2024 yet, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean there aren\u8217\'20\'19t any important elections happening this year. Indeed, next Tuesday is election day in several states nationwide for off-year contests over ballot initiatives, governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansions and other key questions. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman}}}\uc2  with some troubling news out of Ohio, where voters will decide on whether to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state constitution:\par \par \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Republican secretary of state quietly canceled the voter registrations of more than 26,000 voters in late September, less than two weeks before the deadline to register to vote in next week\u8217\'20\'19s hotly contested \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum in the state.\par \par \uc2 Voting rights advocates say the process lacked transparency and departed from \uc2 Frank LaRose\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s usual practice of alerting groups before removing registrations from the rolls. And it comes as LaRose campaigns hard against the 7 November constitutional amendment vote \u8211\'20\'13 when Ohio voters will decide whether to enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution \u8211\'20\'13 as well as a vote on a separate measure to legalize marijuana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are disappointed in the secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office\u8217\'20\'19s authorization of the voter purge while voting for the November election was already (and still is) under way,\u8221\'20\'1D Kayla Griffin, of the voting rights group All Voting is Local, said.\par \par \uc2 Voter list maintenance is a standard, legally required part of the election process, and many if not most of these registrations are for people who have moved away, died or long since stopped voting. The state issues alerts by mail to voters whose registration is flagged for removal, leaving the chance to update or confirm their registration before being kicked off the rolls.\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s unusual to remove voter registrations this close to an election given the risk of disenfranchising people who intend to vote but simply missed the memo that they had been flagged for removal. In fact, if this was a national election rather than a state-level contest, what LaRose\u8217\'20\'19s office has done would have been illegal. The National Voter Registration Act prohibits elections offices from systematically removing voters from the rolls within 90 days of a federal election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/ohio-republican-election-secretary-of-state-voter-purge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio purged 26,000 voters days before \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  referendum deadline}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 One minute after the House approved an Israel aid package that excluded providing similar assistance to Ukraine, the top Republican in the Senate, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , tweeted this:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe U.S. has global interests and global responsibilities. Our support for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s fight is leading the free world to make historic commitments to defense. Allies\u8217\'20\'19 investments are helping grow the U.S. industrial base to meet future threats. But America has to lead by example.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Leader McConnell (@LeaderMcConnell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell/status/1720195428254204168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 This what some would call a \u8220\'20\'1Csubtweet\u8221\'20\'1D: McConnell does not mention the House proposal at all nor its architect, Republican speaker Mike Johnson, but he is clearly referring to the just-passed bill. While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/14/republican-house-ukraine-support-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some Republicans}}}\uc2  are ready to cut off aid to Kyiv, McConnell remains a steadfast backer of the country\u8217\'20\'19s defense against Russia.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Democratic senator who calls the shots in the chamber, said he would not even consider the House bill:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House is scheduled to vote today on the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s unserious and inadequate aid package.\par \par \uc2 The nonpartisan \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  reported that this package will add billions to the deficit.\par \par \uc2 I'm glad {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  issued a veto threat over this stunningly unserious proposal.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1720129717267837142?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrLet me be clear: The Senate will not take up the House GOP's deeply flawed proposal\par \par \uc2 Instead we will work on our own bipartisan emergency aid package that includes funding for aid to Israel, Ukraine, humanitarian aid including for Gaza, and competition with the Chinese Government\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1720134873841623374?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House passes Israel security bill, but its prospects are grim\par \par \uc2 Yesterday evening, the Republican-led House of Representatives passed a bill to provide Israel with security assistance as it presses on with its invasion of Gaza and conflict with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . But the measure is not expected to be considered by the Senate, and has attracted a veto threat from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over provisions rescinding money from the \uc2 IRS\uc2  tax authority and driving up the US budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are instead holding out for a larger package that would, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/31/biden-administration-republicans-israel-ukraine-emergency-military-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as Biden has requested}}}\uc2 , pay for more military aid to Ukraine and improved border security in addition to aiding Israel, while also avoiding cuts to White House priorities like improving the \uc2 IRS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ability to crack down on tax cheats. Such a measure is expected to attract some support from Senate Republicans, most notably \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , who has remained a champion of Ukraine even as polls show many other Republicans are growing wary of paying for the country\u8217\'20\'19s defense against Russia.\par \par \uc2 Back to the House vote, it was 226 to 196 in favor of passage, with all but two Republicans present voting yes and all but 12 Democrats in attendance voting against it. Several of the Democrats who voted for the bill had previously attacked it as inappropriately partisan, including Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Debbie Wasserman Schultz\uc2 , who said she nonetheless decided to support it due to her connection to Israel:\par \par \uc2 enltrI urged many of my colleagues to vote against this bill because of the horrendous precedent it set and the urgent need to pass the full emergency supplemental proposed by President Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Debbie Wasserman Schultz\uc2  (@RepDWStweets) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepDWStweets/status/1720226163551834384?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFor me, as a Jew, as a Zionist and as the representative of a large Jewish community, I personally needed to cast my vote to stand by Israel, the homeland of the Jewish people, in this moment of crisis.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Debbie Wasserman Schultz\uc2  (@RepDWStweets) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepDWStweets/status/1720226390157508955?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrI will continue to work closely with the White House, the Senate and bipartisan colleagues in the House to ensure America provides vital humanitarian aid and security assistance for our allies in Israel, Ukraine, and Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Debbie Wasserman Schultz\uc2  (@RepDWStweets) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepDWStweets/status/1720226592335532433?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s staff has put together a comprehensive look at the conflict between Israel and Palestine, which is experiencing of one of its worst spasms of violence in years after \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s terrorist attack, which killed 1,400 people last month.\par \par \uc2 The hostilities in the heart of the Middle East is one of the few wars with implications that are felt worldwide, and particularly in Washington DC, where successive presidential administrations, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s included, have made Israel a top foreign policy priority. Read more about it below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/03/israel-and-palestine-a-complete-guide-to-the-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel and Palestine: a complete guide to the crisis}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There are those who talk about Middle East policy, and there are those who carry it out \u8211\'20\'13 regardless of if they have they ability or authority to actually do so. Case in point: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor whose campaign for the Republican presidential nomination appears to be going nowhere. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  reports, he\u8217\'20\'19s been trying to use his powers in the Sunshine State to respond to \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attack on Israel, or at least make voters think he is:\par \par \uc2 His pathway to the presidency looks more forbidding than ever, but tanking poll numbers and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/iowa-poll-republicans-trump-nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stalled campaign}}}\uc2  have not dissuaded \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  from running foreign policy as if he was the incumbent in the White House.\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor has raised eyebrows and hackles by using state resources for a series of actions and operations since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Hamas war}}}\uc2  began that come under the purview of the federal government.\par \par \uc2 They include \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/desantis-touts-role-organizing-flights-israel-details-murky/story?id=104045514"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 evacuating}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D hundreds of US citizens from Israel on charter flights; exporting humanitarian aid and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/27/ron-desantis-sending-weapons-israel-military-fake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claiming to have procured weapons}}}\uc2  ; as well as activating Florida\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/15/ron-desantis-florida-state-guard-militia-veterans-quit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 militarized state guard}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cas needed, to respond\u8221\'20\'1D to an overseas conflict.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, he has summoned Florida\u8217\'20\'19s legislature for an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/florida-iran-sanctions-desantis-israel-hamas-dcdc2edb781fa384369111d5268f9fd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emergency session next week}}}\uc2  that will, among other issues, seek to impose more state sanctions on Iran, a key ally of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , replicating measures already in place at federal level for decades.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/ron-desantis-israel-hamas-foreign-policy-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis plays at being president with his own Israel-Hamas foreign policy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just senators who are weighing in on the war in Gaza, it\u8217\'20\'19s also people who want to be senators. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  reports that the conflict has exposed one of the few differences separating the three leading candidates to fill California\u8217\'20\'19s open Senate seat next year:\par \par \uc2 As three leading {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2  Democrats vie for a rare opening in the Senate, the Israeli offensive in Gaza has exposed rare fault lines in the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 otherwise aligned platforms.\par \par \uc2 Following \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attack on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  last month, all three leading candidates in the race to fill \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s seat \u8211\'20\'13 representatives Barbara Lee, Adam Schiff and \uc2 Katie Porter\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 condemned the group\u8217\'20\'19s actions. But as Israel ramped up its attacks on Gaza in retaliation, their divergent approaches to foreign policy became clear.\par \par \uc2 The fissures between the candidates are a reflection of debates within the broader Democratic party. But in California\u8217\'20\'19s open primary, where voters will choose between leading Democratic candidates with nearly identical platforms, the issue could be a deciding factor for some voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese candidates have regularly identified themselves as progressive candidates on a host of domestic policy issues \u8211\'20\'13 you can hardly tell the difference between them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sara Sadhwani, a professor of American politics at Pomona College. But when it comes to Israel and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom the get-go, we began to see some of these real distinctions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lee, who was the sole member of Congress to vote against the authorization for the use of military force after 9/11 that gave the president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govtrack.us/congress/bills/107/hjres64/text/ath"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broad power}}}\uc2  to wage war, has maintained her position as an unwavering anti-war progressive. She is the only leading candidate to have called for a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI absolutely condemn all violence against civilians \u8211\'20\'13 including the horrific terrorist attacks by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Nothing is more valuable than human life,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the Guardian in an emailed statement . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the surest way to mitigate the suffering in both Israel and Palestine is through a ceasefire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/california-senate-election-democrats-israel-gaza-lee-schiff-porter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 View on Israel-Gaza emerges as rare divide for California\u8217\'20\'19s Senate hopefuls}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic senators say 'much more must be done to protect civilian life' in Gaza war\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, 13 Democratic senators released a joint statement calling for \u8220\'20\'1Ca short-term cessation of hostilities\u8221\'20\'1D in the Gaza Strip, with the goal of getting aid to civilians and releasing hostages taken by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warner.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/pressreleases?ID=B2A2A8CF-ED79-4D6C-9D38-ABC4635DA24F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The letter}}}\uc2  was signed by Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Mark Warner and Tim Kaine, Dick Durbin and Tammy Duckworth of Illinois, \uc2 Jeff Merkley\uc2  of Oregon, Peter Welch of Vermont, Elizabeth Warren and \uc2 Ed Markey\uc2  of Massachusetts, \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  of New Jersey, \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\uc2  of Maryland, Tina Smith of Minnesota, \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  of Connecticut and Jeanne Shaheen of New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what is said, in part:\par \par \uc2 As Senators, we have been closely monitoring the war in Gaza and believe that much more must be done to protect civilian life. We have been in ongoing dialogue with government officials in the United States, Israel and other nations in the region. We have communicated extensively with international aid officials doing work in Gaza, including those working together with the \uc2 U.S. Agency for International Development\uc2 . And we have talked at length with our own constituents who have family and friends in the region.\par \par \uc2 The failure to adequately protect non-combatant civilians risks dramatic escalation of the conflict in the region and imposes severe damage on prospects for peaceful coexistence between Israelis and Palestinians. Based on the consensus opinion of U.S. and international aid officials, it is nearly impossible to deliver sufficient humanitarian aid to protect civilian life under current conditions.\par \par \uc2 Thus, we join President Biden in his call for a short-term cessation of hostilities that pose high-risk to civilians, aid workers or humanitarian aid delivery in Gaza, in order to accomplish three goals:\par \par \uc2 Successful delivery of needed humanitarian aid to civilians under strict and necessary oversight\par \par \uc2 Increased focus on the release of all hostages kidnapped on October 7\par \par \uc2 Opportunity for broader discussion amongst Israeli and Palestinian leadership, together with regional and global partners, about long-term strategies to reduce decades-long conflict in the region.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In addition to US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Israel, the other big news in the Gaza conflict today is a speech by \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s secretary general \uc2 Hassan Nasrallah\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Lebanon-based militia group is widely seen as considering entering the war by attacking Israel from the north. We have a separate live blog covering the latest in the conflict, and you can follow it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/03/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-un-blinken-expected-call-for-pauses-fighting-allow-aid-gaza-tel-aviv-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Israel-Hamas war live: US tells Israel that civilians caught in crossfire must be protected}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just Senate Democrats that are concerned about how Israel is carrying out its invasion of Gaza, and how that might reflect on the United States.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/biden-officials-voice-new-concerns-warnings-israels-war-hamas-rcna123445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reported}}}\uc2  some Biden administration officials are also privately uneasy, despite the president\u8217\'20\'19s embrace of Israel following \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 7 October attack.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from their piece:\par \par \uc2 As the humanitarian crisis in Gaza worsens and the death toll among Palestinian civilians continues to rise, there is growing concern among top Biden administration officials about how the Israelis are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/Israel-Hamas-war-Gaza-Strip-conflict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 carrying out the war}}}\uc2  and uncertainty about whether they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/will-israel-hamas-gaza-conflict-spark-wider-war-united-states-rcna122991"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can be reined in}}}\uc2 , according to two current and two former senior U.S. officials familiar with the internal discussions.\par \par \uc2 Some administration officials also are worried that the U.S. could become more and more isolated on the world stage over President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s close alignment with Israel \u8212\'20\'14 and that he will be blamed for some of the Israeli military\u8217\'20\'19s actions, according to three current and former officials.\par \par \uc2 Biden and his top aides have in the past week adjusted the administration\u8217\'20\'19s public message to emphasize concern for Palestinian civilians and U.S. efforts to get them humanitarian relief. The shift follows growing criticism at home and abroad of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision to swiftly and staunchly back Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military response to \uc2 Hamas\uc2  while initially speaking less forcefully about protecting Palestinians; meanwhile, images of civilian casualties in Gaza continue to ricochet around the world.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf this really goes bad, we want to be able to point to our past statements,\u8221\'20\'1D a senior U.S. official said. The official said the administration is particularly worried about a narrative taking hold that Biden supports all Israeli military actions and that U.S.-provided weapons have been used to kill Palestinian civilians, many of them women and children. The Defense Department has said the U.S. is not putting any limits or restrictions on the weapons it\u8217\'20\'19s providing Israel.\par \par \uc2 Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  delivered a planned, more strident message Thursday before he boarded his plane for a trip to Israel. \u8220\'20\'1CAs we\u8217\'20\'19ve said from the start, Israel has not only the right but the obligation to defend itself,\u8221\'20\'1D he told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve also said very clearly and repeatedly that how Israel does this matters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said his discussions with the Israelis would focus on \u8220\'20\'1Cconcrete steps\u8221\'20\'1D they can take to better protect civilians. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen in recent days Palestinian civilians continuing to bear the brunt of this action, and it\u8217\'20\'19s important that the United States is committed to making sure everything possible is done to protect civilians.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top US diplomat arrives in Tel Aviv to urge humanitarian pauses, aid\par \par \uc2 Secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  arrived in Tel Aviv earlier today with the goal of convincing Israel to ease the suffering of civilians caught up in its campaign against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Before arriving, Blinken said he would seek \u8220\'20\'1Cconcrete measures\u8221\'20\'1D from Israel intended to reduce civilian casualties, including allowing more aid into Gaza and the implementation of humanitarian pauses in the fighting. Blinken will simultaneously be looking to avoid saying anything that casts doubt on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the United States supports.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Blinken\u8217\'20\'19s visit, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/patrickwintour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Patrick Wintour}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/03/blinken-flies-in-to-israel-to-meet-netanyahu-as-idf-pushes-further-into-gaza-city"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blinken to urge Israel to show restraint in campaign to destroy Hamas}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats grow nervous over Israel conduct in war with \uc2 Hamas\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Ever since \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 7 October attack against Israel, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has projected steadfast support of the longtime US ally. But with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of the Gaza Strip under way, the president\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic allies are growing uneasy with the increasing toll of civilians killed or wounded. Dick Durbin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/dick-durbin-gaza-ceasefire-israel-hamas-war/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became}}}\uc2  the first senator to call for a ceasefire yesterday, and later joined 12 other Democratic lawmakers in signing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warner.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/pressreleases?ID=B2A2A8CF-ED79-4D6C-9D38-ABC4635DA24F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  asking for \u8220\'20\'1Ca short-term cessation of hostilities\u8221\'20\'1D to facilitate the release of hostages taken by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  last month, and the delivery of humanitarian aid. Meanwhile, secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  arrived in Tel Aviv today to urge Israel\u8217\'20\'19s leadership {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/03/blinken-flies-in-to-israel-to-meet-netanyahu-as-idf-pushes-further-into-gaza-city"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to show more restraint}}}\uc2  in its campaign in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The shift in sentiment comes as Israel awaits a new infusion of military aid Biden requested after visiting the country last month, but which is currently caught up in Capitol Hill\u8217\'20\'19s partisan meat grinder. The Republican-led House of Representatives yesterday approved $14b in aid to Israel while simultaneously cutting the budget of the \uc2 IRS\uc2  tax authority \u8211\'20\'13 a proposition unpalatable to most Democrats. The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  says his chamber won\u8217\'20\'19t consider the bill, and is instead working on its own broader package that will include aid to Ukraine and pay for increased security on the southern border. All these will be stories to watch today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is this afternoon traveling to Lewiston, Maine, site of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/01/maine-shootings-texts-letter-robert-card"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a mass shooting}}}\uc2  last week that killed 18 people. He will meet with first responders, as well as relatives of the victims.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  is expected to return to the witness stand today to testify in the civil fraud trial of the family business, the head of which is, of course, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US economy added 150,000 jobs last month, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just-released data}}}\uc2  that was weaker than months prior but also reflected the impact of the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  strike.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231103ejb3002bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
